h-priest-is-released.html', 'snippet': 'Georges Vandenbeusch, 42, who was reported to have been held in Nigeria by Boko Haram, a group with ties to Al Qaeda, was released on Tuesday, according to French authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A French priest kidnapped in November by Islamist militants in northern Cameroon was released on Tuesday, according to French authorities. The priest, Georges Vandenbeusch, 42, was reported to have been held in Nigeria by Boko Haram, a group with ties to Al Qaeda. He described his captivity as “terribly boring,” according to Reuters. He paced circles under a tent beneath a tree, he said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cameroon: Kidnapped French Priest Is Released', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cameroon: Kidnapped French Priest Is Released', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vandenbeusch, Georges', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cameroon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T00:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2268600-57a1-52f1-b671-c4d271817c2f', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2268600-57a1-52f1-b671-c4d271817c2f'}, {'abstract': 'Hamas lawmakers on Tuesday approved a 2014 budget totaling $589 million for the Gaza Strip that included a staggering 75 percent deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/world/middleeast/gaza-hamas-lawmakers-approve-large-budget-deficit.html', 'snippet': 'Hamas lawmakers on Tuesday approved a 2014 budget totaling $589 million for the Gaza Strip that included a staggering 75 percent deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Hamas lawmakers on Tuesday approved a 2014 budget totaling $589 million for the Gaza Strip that included a staggering 75 percent deficit. The Islamist Hamas movement has said that Egypt’s closing of hundreds of smuggling tunnels beneath its border this summer had cost the strip $460 million in taxes and broader productivity. Gaza gets significant funding from the Palestinian Authority and donor nations, but Hamas has rarely made budgetary specifics public. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Hamas Lawmakers Approve Large Budget Deficit', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaza: Hamas Lawmakers Approve Large Budget Deficit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akram, Fares', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T00:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}]