, {'abstract': 'A combination of Sprint and T-Mobile could raise prices and hurt consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/opinion/preserving-wireless-competition.html', 'snippet': 'A combination of Sprint and T-Mobile could raise prices and hurt consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The corporation that controls Sprint, the third-biggest cellphone company in the country after Verizon and AT&T, is reportedly planning to make an offer to buy the smaller rival T-Mobile in a move that would reduce competition in an important industry that already has too little of it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preserving Wireless Competition', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preserving Wireless Competition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile US Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sprint Nextel Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SOFTBANK Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T01:06:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt: