haring patterns that echo the movements of scavenging birds, flocking insects and gliding sharks.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/navigating-our-world-like-birds-and-bees/', 'snippet': 'How we move around in our world is deeply hard-wired, a new study suggests, sharing patterns that echo the movements of scavenging birds, flocking insects and gliding sharks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'African tribesmen walk through their landscape in a pattern that eerily echoes the movements of scavenging birds, flocking insects, gliding sharks and visitors to Disneyland, a new study finds, suggesting that aspects of how we choose to move around in our world are deeply hard-wired.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/health/01well-physed/01well-physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/01/health/01well-physed/01well-physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/health/01well-physed/01well-physed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/health/01well-physed/01well-physed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1404, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/health/01well-physed/01well-physed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/01/health/01well-physed/01well-physed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/health/01well-physed/01well-physed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Navigating Our World Like Birds and Bees', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Navigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Walking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T05:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08bb1a75-2c2d-5a07-9ca9-f2ec1ea386a1', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08bb1a75-2c2d-5a07-9ca9-f2ec1ea386a1'}, {'abstract': 'More employees are likely to be working shorter workweeks in 2014, as government policies nudge them and employers in that direction, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/shorter-workweeks-are-likely-in-new-year/', 'snippet': 'More employees are likely to be working shorter workweeks in 2014, as government policies nudge them and employers in that direction, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago. He is the author of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shorter Workweeks Are Likely in New Year', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T05:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc4a04d-94dd-575f-9b50-021ecc46f9d7', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc4a04d-94dd-575f-9b50-021ecc46f9d7'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11 A.M. (HGTV) ROSE PARADE 2014 The new year is once again coming up roses for HGTV, which heralds 2014 from its traditional perch at the 125th annual parade. Vin Scully, the hall of fame sports broadcaster and grand marshal, will lead nearly 50 floats, centered on the theme “Dreams Come True” and adorned with more botanical elements — including orchids (above), black lichen, Spanish moss, safflower blossoms, coconut flakes and even chive and onion seed — than the average florist might go through in five years, down Colorado Avenue in Pasadena, Calif. The “Property Brothers” — Drew and Jonathan Scott — and Nancy O’Dell will provide a play-by-play of the nuptials of Danny Leclair and Aubrey Loots on the AIDS Healthcare Foundation’s wedding cake float with the tagline “Love Is the Best Protection.” And eight former Women Airforce Service Pilots from World War II are expected to ride atop a float titled “Our Eyes Are on the Stars.” (Stanford will take on Michigan State in the Rose Bowl game at 5 p.m. on ESPN.) The HGTV programming moves into prime time at 8 with a tour of the latest “Dream Home” giveaway: a three-bedroom modern mountain house with soaring ceilings and wilderness views near Lake Tahoe. The winner also gets a GMC Yukon Denali and $250,000.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2dc2202-3791-5f37-b5fb-9e9f5b33d42b', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2dc2202-3791-5f37-b5fb-9e9f5b33d42b'}, {'abstract': 'The oath of office was administered by Eric T. Schneiderman, the attorney general of New York, in a brief ceremony inside the front yard of the mayor’s rowhouse in Park Slope, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/nyregion/de-blasio-sworn-in-as-new-york-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'The oath of office was administered by Eric T. Schneiderman, the attorney general of New York, in a brief ceremony inside the front yard of the mayor’s rowhouse in Park Slope, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill de Blasio was sworn in as the 109th mayor of New York City early Wednesday, at two minutes past the stroke of midnight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio Sworn In as New York Mayor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Chiara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCray, Chirlane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Dante', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T06:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edcf337f-cd84-5336-9364-6c5e3c452f14', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edcf337f-cd84-5336-9364-6c5e3c452f14'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. O’Connor, a veteran war correspondent, became an advocate for threatened journalists in Mexico, one of the world’s most dangerous countries for the press.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/world/americas/mike-oconnor-advocate-for-mexican-journalists-dies-at-67.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. O’Connor, a veteran war correspondent, became an advocate for threatened journalists in Mexico, one of the world’s most dangerous countries for the press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike O’Connor, a longtime foreign correspondent who had worked in recent years to protect journalists in Mexico, died on Sunday in Mexico City. He was 67.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N