', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05eat3/05eat3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05eat3/05eat3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05eat3/05eat3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Need Some Greens? Then Eat This Pork Belly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'High on the Hog', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pork', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bittman, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St John (London, England, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a9a0b31-d1a9-5c5c-9c89-f5dbbe86cdb0', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a9a0b31-d1a9-5c5c-9c89-f5dbbe86cdb0'}, {'abstract': 'Why is it so hard to make a low-cal soda that actually tastes good?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/magazine/the-quest-for-a-natural-sugar-substitute.html', 'snippet': 'Why is it so hard to make a low-cal soda that actually tastes good?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a Sunday evening last September, stevia became famous. In the final episode of “Breaking Bad,” an image of the sweetener filled the TV screen. Lydia emptied the packet into her mug of camomile tea, not knowing that Walt, her former partner, had poisoned it. “How are you feeling?” he later asked. “Kind of under the weather, like you’ve got the flu? That would be the ricin I gave you. I slipped it into that stevia crap that you’re always putting in your tea.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05lowcal1/mag-05Low-Cal-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05lowcal1/mag-05Low-Cal-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 712}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05lowcal1/mag-05Low-Cal-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 863, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05lowcal1/mag-05Low-Cal-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1726, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05lowcal1/mag-05Low-Cal-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05lowcal1/mag-05Low-Cal-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05lowcal1/mag-05Low-Cal-t_C