’ve come up with a useful way to summarize what has been happening in the euro area. In the figure below I compare the ratio of government debt to GDP (from the IMF — year-end number) with the 10-year interest rate (from the ECB) for a number of euro nations; I show two dates, the peak of the euro crisis in 2011 and a relatively recent observation:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of the Euro, In One Graph', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T15:17:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/690d0191-a71a-574c-b67b-67e208673c6a', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/690d0191-a71a-574c-b67b-67e208673c6a'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of tourists and residents across Colorado eagerly took part in the country’s first-ever sales of state-regulated recreational marijuana.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/us/colorado-stores-throw-open-their-doors-to-pot-buyers.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of tourists and residents across Colorado eagerly took part in the country’s first-ever sales of state-regulated recreational marijuana.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — They lined up before dawn and in the snow on Wednesday, baby boomers from Nebraska, retirees from Denver and a young man who had driven all day from Ohio. Some were longtime marijuana users. Some had been arrested for marijuana possession.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Up Early and in Line for a Marijuana Milestone in Colorado', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Line Early for Milestone on Marijuana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T15:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/268d39b6-b831-58d0-a8ae-5ad0bf865caa', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/268d39b6-b831-58d0-a8ae-5ad0bf865caa'}, {'abstract': 'The French chanteuse and style icon shares her beauty secrets, tips for winter dressing and more.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/rules-of-style-lou-doillon-on-looking-kooky-and-staying-true-to-yourself/', 'snippet': 'The French chanteuse and style icon shares her beauty secrets, tips for winter dressing and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The model and actress Lou Doillon recorded her first album “Places,” which came out last summer, in just 10 days with no money and zero expectations. Half the songs were written over the previous seven years just sitting around the house. “I always lived with guitarists,” she said over a cappuccino last fall in the lobby of the Dream Downtown hotel in New York, the morning after a show at the Highline Ballroom. “When they would leave, I would just pick up their acoustic guitars and start doing finger picking and write.” When she decided to record the album, she told her producer, “Let’s do it petite. If it works out, good.” And if it doesn’t? “Then I can die in a corner without anyone noticing.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/t-magazine/03doillon-beddie/03doillon-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/t-magazine/03doillon-beddie/03doillon-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 500}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/t-magazine/03doillon-beddie/03doillon-beddie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/t-magazine/03doillon-beddie/03doillon-beddie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1707, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/t-magazine/03doillon-beddie/03doillon-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/03/t-magazine/03doillon-beddie/03doillon-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/t-magazine/03doillon-beddie/03doillon-beddie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rules of Style | Lou Doillon on Looking Kooky and Staying True to Yourself', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rules Of Style: Her Own Path, Her Own Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T16:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68fae201-67e0-53df-bd5c-3b9677c9e488', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68fae201-67e0-53df-bd5c-3b9677c9e488'}, {'abstract': 'The Met’s traditional New Year’s Eve “Die Fledermaus” is heavy on shtick and good humor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/arts/music/die-fledermaus-at-the-met-via-douglas-carter-beane.html', 'snippet': 'The Met’s traditional New Year’s Eve “Die Fledermaus” is heavy on shtick and good humor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Real Champagne tends to provoke sticker shock in cash-strapped young people hoping to drink their way through New Year’s Eve. A popular solution is André, the saccharine, mass-produced sparkling wine that sells for about $4 or $5 a bottle.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/FLEDERMAUS/FLEDERMAUS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/FLEDERMAUS/FLEDERMAUS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/FLEDERMAUS/FLEDERMAUS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image