rd_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52437ecb-6f57-5a12-96b1-f870efee764d'}, {'abstract': 'The space agency said that the Challenger space shuttle explosion should “never be trivialized.” Beyoncé included a NASA audio sample in her new song “XO.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/nasa-responds-to-beyonces-use-of-challenger-audio/', 'snippet': 'The space agency said that the Challenger space shuttle explosion should “never be trivialized.” Beyoncé included a NASA audio sample in her new song “XO.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beyoncé’s new self-titled album has won raves from critics and fans, but now it has come under indirect fire from an unexpected authority: NASA.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NASA Responds to Beyoncé’s Use of Challenger Audio', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Challenger (Space Shuttle)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-01T16:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/213c3074-2cb1-581f-94e6-c11b43a74ea6', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/213c3074-2cb1-581f-94e6-c11b43a74ea6'}, {'abstract': '“Outside Mullingar” is the 10th John Patrick Shanley play to be produced by the Manhattan Theater Club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/theater/a-10th-play-is-the-charm.html', 'snippet': '“Outside Mullingar” is the 10th John Patrick Shanley play to be produced by the Manhattan Theater Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an impressive and unusually enduring relationship spanning three decades, the Manhattan Theater Club has produced nine plays by John Patrick Shanley, none of which started on Broadway. But with the 10th, the romantic comedy “Outside Mullingar,” which is in previews at the Samuel J. Friedman Theater, that streak will change. This show, about two neighboring misfits whose families are in a land dispute in rural Ireland, reunites some of the same Tony-winning artists who worked on Mr. Shanley’s only drama to transfer to Broadway, the celebrated “Doubt”: the superb actor Brian F. O’Byrne, here playing an introvert living on a cattle farm, and the veteran director Doug Hughes. Debra Messing, who played the scarf-favoring lyricist in the NBC series “Smash,” makes her Broadway debut as Mr. O’Byrne’s love interest. (261 West 47th Street, Manhattan; 212-239-6200, manhattantheatreclub.com.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/arts/05GUIDE2/05GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/arts/05GUIDE2/05GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/arts/05GUIDE2/05GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 430, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/arts/05GUIDE2/05GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 859, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 