will to tease Todd Gross’s theme out of today’s puzzle. When I finally found out what it was, however, I thought it was brilliant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burning the Midnight Oil', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T03:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/308d0c41-df42-5b48-81a4-548882d39456', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/308d0c41-df42-5b48-81a4-548882d39456'}, {'abstract': 'Even a little more dressed up than usual, as the de Blasios were Wednesday, it was still clear that his election marked a departure from the Bloomberg years in more ways than one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/nyregion/at-inauguration-seeing-another-sign-of-change-in-what-the-first-family-wore.html', 'snippet': 'Even a little more dressed up than usual, as the de Blasios were Wednesday, it was still clear that his election marked a departure from the Bloomberg years in more ways than one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill de Blasio was dressed in a suit that seemed to basically fit. His wife, Chirlane McCray, wore a tailored, aubergine coat, his daughter, Chiara, had on a leopard-print overcoat, and his son, Dante, was in a suit and a plaid scarf, but no tie.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/nyregion/fashion/fashion-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 