name': 'Ito', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31114212-d810-53af-adb9-c36be416a13c', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31114212-d810-53af-adb9-c36be416a13c'}, {'abstract': 'With portraits, landscapes and found objects, Zoe Strauss shows the history and socioeconomic topography of Homestead, Pa., site of a fabled Carnegie-owned steel mill.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/portraits-of-a-rust-belt-mill-town/', 'snippet': 'With portraits, landscapes and found objects, Zoe Strauss shows the history and socioeconomic topography of Homestead, Pa., site of a fabled Carnegie-owned steel mill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zoe Strauss loves monumental undertakings. She embarked on her first photographic project, “Under I-95” — spanning a decade and encompassing “literally everything” — without knowing anything about making pictures. Her new project, “Homesteading,” is similarly all-encompassing, tracing the history and socioeconomic topography of Homestead, Pa., the site of a fabled Carnegie-owned steel mill that closed in 1986.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/blogs/20140102-lens-strauss-slide-QR8I/20140102-lens-strauss-slide-QR8I-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/02/blogs/20140102-lens-strauss-slide-QR8I/20140102-lens-strauss-slide-QR8I-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/blogs/20140102-lens-strauss-slide-QR8I/20140102-lens-strauss-slide-QR8I-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumb