ppet': 'Video and images shared on social media show the long-awaited rescue of the 52 passengers of a Russian ship, the Akademik Shokalskiy, which has been trapped in ice off the coast of Antarctica since Dec. 24.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 10:01 a.m. The red-and-white Chinese helicopter with dual rotors hovered over the ice, then settled gently on a flat patch at one of the earth’s southernmost points. At least seven men in puffy orange jackets clambered out and onto the Antarctic polar cap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complex Effort for Antarctic Rescue', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora Australis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Icebreakers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turney, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T10:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84d3b07b-5a46-5f23-9c61-e8fc6f102162', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84d3b07b-5a46-5f23-9c61-e8fc6f102162'}, {'abstract': 'On t