 had already made several prize-winning documentaries about Egypt when massive protests against the dictatorship of Hosni Mubarak erupted in Cairo in January 2011. She knew she had to remain there to chronicle the uprising, and spent the next two and a half years filming “The Square,” which has won awards at festivals from Sundance to Dubai and has been shortlisted for the Oscar for best documentary feature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jehane Noujaim on Filming History as It Happens', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noujaim, Jehane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T14:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/367944d0-ad6e-5b9e-9de5-edf2e52bc9cf', 'word_count': 1364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/367944d0-ad6e-5b9e-9de5-edf2e52bc9cf'}, {'abstract': 'Affordable lodging is just one of the advantages of hitting this stretch of Long Island when temperatures are low.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/travel/a-winter-weekend-in-the-north-fork.html', 'snippet': 'Affordable lodging is just one of the advantages of hitting this stretch of Long Island when temperatures are low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s free to watch the sun set over the wetlands that fringe the causeway connecting East Marion and Orient, near the eastern tip of Long Island’s North Fork. If the weather has been dry enough in this wine country just across the bay from the Hamptons, there’s a good perch on the marshy land near Latham Farms, by a little cabin on stilts known locally as the crab shack. The wine is also free, if your friend Jeanny Pak happens to have brought along a bottle of malbec and some plastic cups without telling you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/travel/02-frugal-span/02-frugal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/02/travel/02-frugal-span/02-frugal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/travel/02-frugal-span/02-frugal-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/travel/02-frugal-span/02-frugal-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/travel/02-frugal-span/02-frugal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/02/travel/02-frugal-span/02-frugal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/travel/02-frugal-span/02-frugal-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Winter Weekend in the North Fork', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Fork (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T14:18:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98a29771-29dd-52aa-ab86-8d4f247d545b', 'word_count': 1571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98a29771-29dd-52aa-ab86-8d4f247d545b'}, {'abstract': 'The writer Robert Macfarlane talks about the transformative power of seeing the world one step at at time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/travel/why-walk.html', 'snippet': 'The writer Robert Macfarlane talks about the transformative power of seeing the world one step at at time.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Old Ways: A Journey on Foot” by Robert Macfarlane caps off a trilogy of books that examine the subtle links between landscape, history and the imagination. Having already ventured into wilds, high and low, this third book focuses on the ancient routes and countless communal pathways that mark the world, connecting people to places, one another and the landscapes they inhabit.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05QNA2_SPAN/05QNA2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05QNA2_SPAN/05QNA2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'su