_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d513a22d-d55a-570c-9631-7c1995eda337', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d513a22d-d55a-570c-9631-7c1995eda337'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/the-gun-report-january-2-2014/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today we return from our holiday break. Here are some notable shootings that occurred while we were gone:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: January 2, 2014', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T18:34:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9225d40f-edd8-55ec-aefa-4b6029e14bac', 'word_count': 2573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9225d40f-edd8-55ec-aefa-4b6029e14bac'}, {'abstract': 'No argument is ever taken off the table.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/bodyguard-of-zombies-counterattack-by-cockroaches/', 'snippet': 'No argument is ever taken off the table.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bit about the WSJ’s continuing denialism on rising inequality brings to mind a point I think I’ve made before, but which seems especially appropriate for recent debates. It is this: Today’s right wing never gives up on a politically convenient argument, no matter how thoroughly it may have been refuted by analysis and evidence. It may downplay that argument for a while — though often even that doesn’t happen — but it always comes back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bodyguard of Zombies, Counterattack by Cockroaches', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T18:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef720a01-d8f3-57dd-9b10-5aee2ab86345', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef720a01-d8f3-57dd-9b10-5aee2ab86345'}, {'abstract': 'The Earl Scruggs Center, which celebrates the late bluegrass star, is scheduled to open this month in Shelby, N.C.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/in-north-carolina-an-earl-scruggs-museum/', 'snippet': 'The Earl Scruggs Center, which celebrates the late bluegrass star, is scheduled to open this month in Shelby, N.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bluegrass legend Earl Scruggs, whose three-finger banjo-picking technique became known as “Scruggs style,” is celebrated at a new museum near his childhood home of Flint Hill, N.C., in the foothills of the Blue Ridge mountains. The Earl Scruggs Center, in the restored 1907 Cleveland County courthouse in downtown Shelby, covers the life, time and community of the musical innovator, who died in 2012 at the age of 88.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/travel/03scruggs/03scruggs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/travel/03scruggs/03scruggs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2