01/02/alicia-keys-loses-job-with-blackberry/', 'snippet': 'Alicia Keys has lost her job as BlackBerry’s global creative director. She got the job last year in connection with the company’s introduction of the BlackBerry 10 line of phones. But she continued to use an iPhone to post on Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While grappling with a $4.4 billion loss in its last quarter, the smartphone maker BlackBerry has fired several senior executives, including its chief executive, and is in the midst of laying off about 40 percent on its employees. On Thursday, the musician Alicia Keys also left the company, where she had been global creative director.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/technology/02bits/02bits-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/02/technology/02bits/02bits-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/technology/02bits/02bits-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/technology/02bits/02bits-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/technology/02bits/02bits-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/02/technology/02bits/02bits-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/technology/02bits/02bits-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alicia Keys Leaves Job With BlackBerry', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Alicia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackBerry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T19:59:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbe4568c-059b-58ea-b56c-adfb2a0cd1b7', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbe4568c-059b-58ea-b56c-adfb2a0cd1b7'}, {'abstract': 'A bill passed by the Ugandan Parliament could have dire consequences for a shortlisted documentary about the role of American evangelicals in stirring up homophobia there.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/ugandas-antigay-bill-vs-a-documentary-on-homophobia/', 'snippet': 'A bill passed by the Ugandan Parliament could have dire consequences for a shortlisted documentary about the role of American evangelicals in stirring up homophobia there.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Square” and “Pussy Riot: A Punk Prayer” are not the only Oscar-shortlisted international documentaries that have run into trouble at home. “God Loves Uganda,” about the role of American evangelicals in stirring up homophobia in that African country, has suffered an arguably even more difficult fate. On Dec. 20, the nation’s Parliament passed a strict antigay bill, which mandates life in jail for engaging in “aggravated homosexuality,” as well prohibiting any form of same-sex contact. Though it has yet to be signed into law by the country’s president, it also carries harsh penalties for anyone promoting or even discussing gay material like that covered by the film, and demands that Ugandans inform on gay people or risk jail themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/ugandafilm/ugandafilm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/ugandafilm/ugandafilm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 769}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/ugandafilm/ugandafilm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/ugandafilm/ugandafilm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/ugandafilm/ugandafilm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/ugandafilm/ugandafilm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/02/arts/ugandafilm/ugandafilm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Uganda’s Antigay Bill vs. a Documentary on Homophobia', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Roger Ross', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T20:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5625495-1e72-52c2-903a-3f859e6331b8', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5625495-1e72-52c2-903a-3f859e6331b8'}, {'abstract': 'Beyoncé’s new album is No. 1 on the Billboard chart again, and was one of the top sellers of 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/02/beyonc-closes-out-year-on-a-high-note/', 'snippet': 'Beyoncé’s new album is No. 1 on the Billboard chart again, and was one of the top sellers of 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of the year the music charts belonged to Beyoncé.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyoncé Closes Out Year on a High Note', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eminem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'One Direction (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T20:21:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, '