rs that relations would be damaged if Afghanistan released prisoners accused of attacking American forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — American senators visiting Kabul on Thursday intensified pressure on President Hamid Karzai to sign a long-term security deal with the United States. And responding to a new crisis between the allies this week, they warned the Afghan government away from plans to summarily release dozens of detainees accused of attacking American forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/world/afghanistan2/afghanistan2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/world/afghanistan2/afghanistan2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/world/afghanistan2/afghanistan2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/world/afghanistan2/afghanistan2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/world/afghanistan2/afghanistan2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/world/afghanistan2/afghanistan2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/world/afghanistan2/afghanistan2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Karzai Is Warned Over Release of Detainees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawmakers Warn Karzai Over Release of Detainees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrasso, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T21:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/474f48e8-1750-5b4b-ad6f-537f66eb5cd7', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/474f48e8-1750-5b4b-ad6f-537f66eb5cd7'}, {'abstract': '“Images of an Infinite Film,” at the Museum of Modern Art, is a showcase of 16-millimeter works mainly from the Conceptual 1970s onward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/arts/design/conceptual-works-in-images-of-an-infinite-film-at-moma.html', 'snippet': '“Images of an Infinite Film,” at the Museum of Modern Art, is a showcase of 16-millimeter works mainly from the Conceptual 1970s onward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re of a certain age and reading this, you probably grew up watching educational filmstrips and going to the movies, where you would witness the occasional projector malfunction or celluloid meltdown. The rise of digital technology and the waning of analog film — which wasn’t even called “analog” until digital came along — made these problems largely disappear. But at the very onset of film’s decline, artists embraced it as a medium — particularly 16-millimeter film.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03FILMMOMA_SPAN/03FILMMOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03FILMMOMA_SPAN/03FILMMOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03FILMMOMA_SPAN/03FILMMOMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03FILMMOMA_SPAN/03FILMMOMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03FILMMOMA_SPAN/03FILMMOMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03FILMMOMA_SPAN/03FILMMOMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumb