rest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abd El Fattah, Alaa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okasha, Tawfik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T22:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93a51751-edb3-5fd9-9575-babd4b205c54', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93a51751-edb3-5fd9-9575-babd4b205c54'}, {'abstract': '“William Kent: Designing Georgian Britain” brings to mind the social, political and power elements of an 18th-century era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/arts/design/william-kent-designing-georgian-britain-at-bard.html', 'snippet': '“William Kent: Designing Georgian Britain” brings to mind the social, political and power elements of an 18th-century era.', 'lead_paragraph': '“William Kent: Designing Georgian Britain,” at the Bard Graduate Center Gallery, should thrill Anglophiles as least as much as the return of “Downton Abbey.” Brimming with art and antiques from some of Britain’s most storied estates, it surveys an important but underappreciated 18th-century artist, adviser, designer, illustrator and architect of buildings and landscapes through his work over four decades (1709-48). And it brings to life the social and political machinations of the Georgian era, most of all the new elite’s cementing of power and status through Italianate country houses filled with Grand Tour souvenirs. Britain fancied itself a New Rome, and Kent aspired to be its “Raphael Secundus,” or second Raphael.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03KENT/03KENT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03KENT/03KENT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03KENT/03KENT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03KENT/03KENT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03KENT/03KENT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03KENT/03KENT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03KENT/03KENT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting His Stamp on England', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting His Stamp on England', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'ran