Steven Bernstein and the Hot 9 at Jazz Standard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The time machine was set on shuffle for Henry Butler with Steven Bernstein and the Hot 9 on Wednesday night at Jazz Standard, where they are performing together through Sunday. Their collaboration is both historically aware and fully prepared to cut loose.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03SUBBUTLER_SPAN/SUBBUTLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03SUBBUTLER_SPAN/SUBBUTLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03SUBBUTLER_SPAN/SUBBUTLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03SUBBUTLER_SPAN/SUBBUTLER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03SUBBUTLER_SPAN/SUBBUTLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03SUBBUTLER_SPAN/SUBBUTLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03SUBBUTLER_SPAN/SUBBUTLER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Orleans and New York, Onstage', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Orleans and New York, Onstage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butler, Henry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Steven (1961- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T22:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/98aa1c3b-4345-568a-9323-b2f877297f7b', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98aa1c3b-4345-568a-9323-b2f877297f7b'}, {'abstract': 'Billy Joel is making an effort at concerts to generate new value from his extensive catalog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/arts/music/billy-joels-new-years-eve-concert-at-barclays-center.html', 'snippet': 'Billy Joel is making an effort at concerts to generate new value from his extensive catalog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before midnight on New Year’s Eve at Barclays Center, in his first Brooklyn concert since he played in a Long Island garage band, Billy Joel sat at a Steinway grand between two guitarists. He wore a dark suit and tie, sang clearly and evenly, and spoke to the audience by announcing the name of a song, the album it came from, the year it was released. About a third of those songs, going back to his first record from 1971, were not hits, and he hadn’t performed some of them much or at all in recent decades. At least for the first hour — before the concert grew looser and more obvious — he seemed consumed by the task of generating new value, and he was formidable, no joke at all.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BILLY_SPAN/BILLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BILLY_SPAN/BILLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BILLY_SPAN/BILLY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BILLY_SPAN/BILLY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BILLY_SPAN/BILLY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BILLY_SPAN/BILLY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BILLY_SPAN/BILLY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Blender of Genres Squeezes More Juice', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Blender of Genres Squeezes More Juice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joel, Billy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-02T22:33:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67db1a60-dcd0-5604-8fc4-52cecebd61fc', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67db1a60-dcd0-5604-8fc4-52cecebd61fc'}, {'abstract': 'Beat Takeshi is back with “Beyond Outrage,” a sequel to the 2011 “Outrage.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/movies/beyond-outrage-mobsters-are-back-with-beat-takeshi.html', 'snippet': 'Beat Takeshi is back with “Beyond Outrage,” a sequel to the 2011 “Outrage.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The men in Takeshi Kitano’s latest yakuza drama, “Beyond Outrage,” are not ones for closure. While professionals in less bloody careers try to move from strength to strength, these mobsters in suits tend to move from outrage to outrage as part of their daily business. In this relentless, insular sequel to Mr. Kitano’s 2011 hit, “Outrage,” actual physical violence is often less shocking than the scheming and betrayal that routinely shake up the traditional hierarchies behind these criminal enterprises.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BEYOND1_SPAN/BEYOND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BEYOND1_SPAN/BEYOND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03BEYOND1_SPAN/BEYOND1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,