zie Borden endures, is about to get a bump in attention thanks to a new movie about the notorious murder case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 50 to 300 visitors a day descend on the Lizzie Borden Bed & Breakfast Museum in Fall River, Mass., a three-story Victorian with dark green shutters and the site of one of America’s most infamous — and most aggressively researched and marketed — murder cases. At times, tourists arrive by the busloads, from “all over the world,” said the house’s co-owner, Lee-Ann Wilber.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05HEADSUP1_SPAN/05HEADSUP1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05HEADSUP1_SPAN/05HEADSUP1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05HEADSUP1_SPAN/05HEADSUP1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05HEADSUP1_SPAN/05HEADSUP1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1524, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05HEADSUP1_SPAN/05HEADSUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/05/travel/05HEADSUP1_SPAN/05HEADSUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i