35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b44f1a2-f432-5f18-9ad7-a276d2cef620'}, {'abstract': 'An overdue step toward inclusion of gays and lesbians in the Boy Scouts that went into effect on New Year’s Day was welcome but did not go far enough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/opinion/scoutings-incomplete-evolution.html', 'snippet': 'An overdue step toward inclusion of gays and lesbians in the Boy Scouts that went into effect on New Year’s Day was welcome but did not go far enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new year brings a positive change in the membership practices of the Boy Scouts of America. In May, delegates attending the Boy Scouts’ national convention voted to allow openly gay boys to participate in the group’s activities. That overdue step toward inclusion went into effect on New Year’s Day, a welcome — though incomplete — turn for an organization that until quite recently rejected any change in its discriminatory ways. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scouting’s Incomplete Evolution', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scouting’s Incomplete Evolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T01:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d19daa8-38ac-58b7-8235-c82dba4fc070', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d19daa8-38ac-58b7-8235-c82