, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/nyregion/mayor/mayor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/nyregion/mayor/mayor-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/nyregion/mayor/mayor-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/nyregion/mayor/mayor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Work, de Blasio Finds Full Plate of Headaches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Work, Mayor Finds Full Plate Of Headaches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T02:11:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1d979fd-1c82-5a43-9cae-0e4f49cce617', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1d979fd-1c82-5a43-9cae-0e4f49cce617'}, {'abstract': 'Doctors Without Borders said it had drastically scaled back operations at an airport encampment in Bangui, the capital, because of a growing political and sectarian crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/world/africa/central-african-republic-violence-forces-aid-group-to-curtail-work.html', 'snippet': 'Doctors Without Borders said it had drastically scaled back operations at an airport encampment in Bangui, the capital, because of a growing political and sectarian crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Doctors Without Borders, the international medical charity known for its resilience in some of the world’s most inhospitable crisis zones, said Thursday that it had drastically curtailed operations at an airport encampment in the Central African Republic, where violence has imperiled about 100,000 displaced people taking refuge. The group said in a statement that its clinic at the airport in Bangui, the capital, which had been treating more than 100 wounded people a day, would now treat “only the most severe cases” with an emergency crew. It was an unusual but not unprecedented retreat for the group, which has remained active in the country throughout a growing political and sectarian crisis, and will continue to work in two hospitals and two other camps in Bangui. Last August the organization completely withdrew from Somalia after having worked there for 22 years, attributing the decision to repeated attacks on its staff. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Central African Republic: Violence Forces Aid Group to Curtail Work', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Central African Republic: Violence Forces Aid Group to Curtail Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangui (Central African Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central African Republic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T02:12:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b849acf-a84d-50e5-b872-40d968937c93', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b849acf-a84d-50e5-b872-40d968937c93'}, {'abstract': 'The approval process for elevating the deck of the Bayonne Bridge is a case study, critics say, in environmental bureaucracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/nyregion/long-review-of-bayonne-bridge-project-is-assailed.html', 'snippet': 'The approval process for elevating the deck of the Bayonne Bridge is a case study, critics say, in environmental bureaucracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seemed ingenious at the time: Elevate the deck of the existing Bayonne Bridge to accommodate the giant cargo ships that will begin passing through the Panama Canal in 2015 after the project to widen and deepen it is scheduled to be finished. Building a new bridge or tunneling under Kill Van Kull would have been much more expensive and would have required years of regulatory reviews.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/nyregion/Bayonne-1/Bayonne-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, '