cumulate in the city, New Jersey and Westchester County by Friday. The mix of wind and snowfall will create limited visibility throughout the region, and motorists can expect slippery, snow-covered roads. Winds of up to 35 miles an hour are expected to create a windchill as cold as 20 degrees below zero. Residents were urged to stay indoors, but those who must go outside were advised to dress warmly, carry emergency supplies and use public transportation. The Red Cross has advice for staying safe in such weather.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Need to Know About the Snowstorm', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T03:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bf5fe06-e925-5542-a590-7586c6c51e06', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf5fe06-e925-5542-a590-7586c6c51e06'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Kluwe, a punter for the Minnesota Vikings for eight seasons, wrote a first-person article alleging that team officials asked him to stop speaking about gay rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/sports/football/support-for-gay-rights-drew-harassment-ex-viking-says.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Kluwe, a punter for the Minnesota Vikings for eight seasons, wrote a first-person article alleging that team officials asked him to stop speaking about gay rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The free-agent punter Chris Kluwe, whose outspoken views on gay rights and other issues of equality have drawn widespread attention, accused a Minnesota Vikings assistant of harassment and homophobia in a first-person account published Thursday on the website Deadspin.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Support for Gay Rights Led to Harassment, Ex-Viking Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Support for Gay Rights Drew Harassment, Ex-Viking Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kluwe, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Vikings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deadspin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T03:35:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e5f789a-22d5-5d3a-95c1-0b5cc85f9ff2', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e5f789a-22d5-5d3a-95c1-0b5cc85f9ff2'}, {'abstract': 'The entire process, which officials said they hoped would begin within the next two weeks, would take roughly 90 days to complete, allowing for weather and other factors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/us/us-military-ship-readied-for-mission-to-destroy-syrias-chemical-weapons.html', 'snippet': 'The enti