ty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/johnson-beats-buzzer-and-nets-pull-off-a-stunner.html', 'snippet': 'Deron Williams’s season-high 29 points and Joe Johnson’s last-second jumper helped the Nets begin 2014 with a victory at Oklahoma City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OKLAHOMA CITY — Paul Pierce was in his late-game flow. Deron Williams showed a swagger he had lacked all season. But when the game was on the line Thursday night, it was clear who would get the ball.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/03nets-1/03nets-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/03nets-1/03nets-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/03nets-1/03nets-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/03nets-1/03nets-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1488, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/03nets-1/03nets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/03nets-1/03nets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/sports/basketball/03nets-1/03nets-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Johnson Beats Buzzer, and Nets Pull Off a Stunner', 'kicker': 'Nets 95, Thunder 93', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Johnson Beats Buzzer, and Nets Pull Off a Stunner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T05:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/840542a8-e185-59de-b828-08f13b677338', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/840542a8-e185-59de-b828-08f13b677338'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:15 P.M. (TCM) A BEAUTIFUL MIND (2001) Russell Crowe, above, in a role for which he received an Oscar nomination, portrays John Forbes Nash Jr., the gifted mathematician who battled schizophrenia for decades before going on to win the Nobel in economic science. Jennifer Connelly won for best supporting actress as Alicia Larde, the M.I.T. student who became Nash’s wife. And Ed Harris plays Nash’s contact for a government project. The paradox of this film (which won for best picture), directed by Ron Howard from a script by Akiva Goldsman, and the emotions it elicits is that the story “is almost entirely counterfeit,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. Still, “Mr. Crowe, with his superhuman powers of concentration, shows us a man who dwells almost entirely in an inner world, and he dramatizes that inwardness as if nobody were watching.” In the end, Mr. Scott added, “the governing dynamic of ‘A Beautiful Mind’ is sentimentality of a familiar and not altogether unwelcome kind. The movie can — indeed, should — be intellectually rejected, but you can’t quite banish it from your mind.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T06:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d13c90c-64e6-57fe-bc7d-df0a14b03c11', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d13c90c-64e6-57fe-bc7d-df0a14b03c11'}, {'abstract': 'In 2012, people in the northeastern state killed about 150,000 federally protected Amur falcons. In 2013, the number dropped to zero, after a campaign by the state and nonprofit groups to promote the value of wildlife.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/a-hunting-community-in-nagaland-takes-steps-toward-conservation/', 'snippet': 'In 2012, people in the northeastern state killed about 150,000 federally protected Amur falcons. In 2013, the number dropped to zero, after a campaign by the state and nonprofit groups to promote the value of wildlife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOYANG, Nagaland — In the fall of 2012, the people in this northeastern state, which is known for its hunting traditions, killed about 150,000 fede