word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36b96073-5b35-5db7-9e2a-3d45e3491ee2'}, {'abstract': 'C.T. Hsia, who died in New York on Dec. 29 aged 92, was a cosmopolitan scholar who established a Chinese literary canon in the West, said his friend and colleague David Der-wei Wang.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/q-a-david-der-wei-wang-on-c-t-hsia-chinese-literary-critic/', 'snippet': 'C.T. Hsia, who died in New York on Dec. 29 aged 92, was a cosmopolitan scholar who established a Chinese literary canon in the West, said his friend and colleague David Der-wei Wang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'C.T. Hsia, the Chinese literary critic who died in New York on Dec. 29, aged 92, had a “legendary career” as “a true cosmopolitan, shrewd, critical and brilliant,” says David Der-wei Wang, the Edward C. Henderson Professor of Chinese Literature at Harvard University, in an interview on the significance of the life and work of his mentor and friend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. & A.: David Der-wei Wang on C.T. Hsia, Chinese Literary Critic', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kafka, Franz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Ang', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mansfield, Katherine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date'