le for Christie’s. Is there a bubble in the art market?  We used to see high prices for our old-master paintings. We sold Van Gogh’s “Sunflowers” here in London in 1987 for $40 million, which was a record at the time. Really, over the last five years we have seen a steady march toward high prices in postwar art. At the same time, new buyers are entering the market from the Middle East, Asia, Russia and elsewhere.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05talk/mag-05Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1817, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05talk/mag-05Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1817}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05talk/mag-05Talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 339, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05talk/mag-05Talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05talk/mag-05Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05talk/mag-05Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/magazine/05talk/mag-05Talk-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_na