5/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE TRIP TO ECHO SPRING: On Writers and Drinking,  by Olivia Laing. (Picador, $26.) A charming and gusto-driven look at the alcoholic insanity of six famous authors, among them Hemingway, Fitzgerald and Cheever.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice | Recent books of particular interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T16:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/45eb50c1-5d95-539f-8cb3-3aaf69320cce', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45eb50c1-5d95-539f-8cb3-3aaf69320cce'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOMBSTONE: The Great Chinese Famine, 1958-1962,  by Yang Jisheng. Translated by Stacy Mosher and Guo Jian. (Farrar, Straus & Giroux, $17.) Yang, a historian and veteran journalist in Beijing, estimates that 36 million Chinese starved to death during the Great Leap Forward. A landmark study of the disaster and the delusions and cruelties of Communist Party leaders, “Tombstone” is also a memorial for the uncle who raised Yang like a son and died of starvation in 1959.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': N