rom a value of 4.2 to the dollar in 1914 to over 4 trillion). The monetary crisis was so traumatic that to this day, it renders the German people thoroughly allergic to price increases.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RAMPELL/05RAMPELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 255, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RAMPELL/05RAMPELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 255}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RAMPELL/05RAMPELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RAMPELL/05RAMPELL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 872, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RAMPELL/05RAMPELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RAMPELL/05RAMPELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RAMPELL/05RAMPELL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Marks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Marks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Frederick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Weimar (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T16:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfdcbb50-0d7c-5d98-a9c7-8102dd7aebf2', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfdcbb50-0d7c-5d98-a9c7-8102dd7aebf2'}, {'abstract': 'Darrin M. McMahon explores the concept of genius.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/books/review/divine-fury-by-darrin-m-mcmahon.html', 'snippet': 'Darrin M. McMahon explores the concept of genius.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does the genius have that the rest of us lack? What is that special “something” that sets him apart? That’s easy. It’s a little spirit, or daimonion, that takes over his mind, like the one that possessed Socrates. Or perhaps it has something to do with the birthday god that shapes a man’s personality, like the genius (from the Latin for “to beget”) who watched over Augustus Caesar. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RYERSON/05RYERSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RYERSON/05RYERSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RYERSON/05RYERSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RYERSON/05RYERSON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2003, 'width': 2003, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RYERSON/05RYERSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RYERSON/05RYERSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05RYERSON/05RYERSON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beautiful Minds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beautiful Minds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, Darrin M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T16:17:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Ryerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8614029f-f92f-5a1e-9e86-95e6d6ba44e0', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8614029f-f92f-5a1e-9e86-95e6d6ba44e0'}, {'abstract': 'A former C.I.A. lawyer is full of praise for the agency and its staff.', 'web_url': 'ht