, 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T17:48:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48a33acd-d542-57ff-8b0e-a2cfad441f46', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48a33acd-d542-57ff-8b0e-a2cfad441f46'}, {'abstract': 'You might want to reach for this tea if you feel a sore throat coming on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/health/meyer-lemon-and-ginger-infusion-with-turmeric-and-cayenne.html', 'snippet': 'You might want to reach for this tea if you feel a sore throat coming on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a lot going on in this lovely infusion, with the tart lemon and pungent ginger. Turmeric contributes beautiful color, along with its nutritional benefits – it has been shown to have powerful anti-inflammatory and antioxidant attributes — and the tiny pinch of cayenne packs a small punch. If you feel a sore throat coming on I highly recommend this tea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/health/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/08/health/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/health/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/hea