person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/204f3fb9-580d-519c-aeeb-84a1a5f58f66', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/204f3fb9-580d-519c-aeeb-84a1a5f58f66'}, {'abstract': 'More people are adopting Internet-connected home devices, according to holiday gift trends and the news expected at the consumer electronics show next week, but analysts say they are still far from mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/is-2014-the-year-of-the-connected-home/', 'snippet': 'More people are adopting Internet-connected home devices, according to holiday gift trends and the news expected at the consumer electronics show next week, but analysts say they are still far from mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tech companies have been talking for years about the so-called connected home, in which home appliances and accessories connect to the Internet. Judging from Christmas with my family — as well as the news expected at the International Consumer Electronics Show next week — this year it might become a reality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/technology/03bits-nest/03bits-nest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/technology/03bits-nest/03bits-nest-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/technology/03bits-nest/03bits-nest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/technology/03bits-nest/03bits-nest-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/technology/03bits-nest/03bits-nest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/technology/03bits-nest/03bits-nest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/technology/03bits-nest/03bits-nest-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is 2014 the Year of the Connected Home?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Appliances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T18:02:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b1c35a9-228f-52ec-acee-dd9cd581cab8', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b1c35a9-228f-52ec-acee-dd9cd581cab8'}, {'abstract': 'Justin Timberlake’s album “The 20/20 Experience” was the top seller in 2013, a year in which album sales continued to fall.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/justin-timberlake-album-was-the-top-seller-in-a-diminished-market/', 'snippet': 'Justin Timberlake’s album “The 20/20 Experience” was the top seller in 2013, a year in which album sales continued to fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The year-end chart news is mixed for Justin Timberlake. On the bright side, “The 20/20 Experience” (RCA), the comeback album he released in March, was the top selling album of 2013, according to Nielsen SoundScan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03artsbeat-jt/03artsbeat-jt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03artsbeat-jt/03artsbeat-jt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03artsbeat-jt/03artsbeat-jt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03artsbeat-jt/03artsbeat-jt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03artsbeat-jt/03artsbeat-jt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03artsbeat-jt/03artsbeat-jt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/arts/03artsbeat-jt/03artsbeat-jt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Justin Timberlake Album Was the Top Seller in a Diminished Market', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Timberlake, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T18:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e20c062e-c21a-5c8a-a585-25757ffc2aa0', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e20c062e-c21a-5c8a-a585-25757ffc2aa0'}, {'abstract': 'An appreciation of the architect Oscar Niemeyer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/magazine/back-to-the-future-in-algeria.html', 'snippet': 'An appreciation of the architect Oscar Niemeyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The legacy of Oscar Niemeyer, the Brazilian architect who died in 2012 at the age of 104, is most familiarly seen in the Modernist buildings he designed for Brasilia, the planned city that became the country’s capital in 1960. But his work in Algeria — not nearly so well known — has also enhanced his reputation as one of the 20th century’s great architects. Niemeyer, a Communist who fled to France following the military takeover of Brazil in 1964, designed several buildings in Algeria in the late 1960s (as well as a library in recent years that is still being built). The plan for one, La Coupole, a sports arena in Algiers, which can be seen in the slide show here, was made on a napkin. Mekki Damerdji, an architect and professor in Algiers, says Mentouri University (shown here), in the city of Constantine, is a favorite of his for its stark contrast to the more traditional buildings that dominate the country’s landscape. “We’re not used to seeing this shape in our country,” Damerdji says. “We haven’t anything like this in Algeria. It’s very beautiful. It’s like a bird.”\xa0Julie Bosman', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back to the Future in Algeria', 'kicker': 'Look', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back to the Future in Algeria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niemeyer, Oscar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T18:09:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dde1014-a254-51b0-b6d0-95da1384785e', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dde1014-a254-51b0-b6d0-95da1384785e'}, {'abstract': 'The couple’s 25-foot-wide townhouse on the Upper East Side boasts six fireplaces and an indoor basketball court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/01/05/realestate/20140105-LOVE.html', 'snippet': 'The couple’s 25-foot-wide townhouse on the Upper East Side boasts six fireplaces and an indoor basketball court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The couple’s 25-foot-wide townhouse on the Upper East Side boasts six fireplaces and an indoor basketball court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/realestate/20140105-LOVE-slide-SGL0/20140105-LOVE-slide-SGL0-articleLarge.jpg', 'he