'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T18:56:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Cottrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cottrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/17ee4902-b1ba-5afc-9953-bc11ab56cad7', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17ee4902-b1ba-5afc-9953-bc11ab56cad7'}, {'abstract': 'The Writers Guild nominees fleshed out the picture for awards watchers, with only “American Hustle” and “Dallas Buyers Clubs” among the contenders with nods from three guilds. Meanwhile, “Inside Llewyn Davis” was left off all three lists.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/momentum-builds-for-hustle-and-dallas-as-llewyn-lags/', 'snippet': 'The Writers Guild nominees fleshed out the picture for awards watchers, with only “American Hustle” and “Dallas Buyers Clubs” among the contenders with nods from three guilds. Meanwhile, “Inside Llewyn Davis” was left off all three lists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not all Oscar-hopeful screenplays are eligible for the Writers Guild Awards: heavy hitters like “12 Years a Slave” and “Philomena” didn’t qualify (for lack of membership or other bureaucratic reasons), along with the indies “Short Term 12” and “Fruitvale Station.” But several of the top contenders for the Little Golden Guy got nods today from the guild. There were surprises like the inclusion of “Lone Survivor,” the director Peter Berg’s adaptation of a true story of a Navy SEAL mission gone terribly awry; and the omission of “Inside Llewyn Davis,” from the Coen brothers, whom the Writers Guild has favored before. (Perhaps the members were bothered by what the Coens themselves described as the film’s lack of a plot.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Momentum Builds for ‘Hustle’ and ‘Dallas’ as ‘Llewyn’ Lags', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berg, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellison, Megan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winter, Terence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Writers Guild of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T18:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd5edba-0614-5f63-a3e0-c70ebf4bb7db', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd5edba-0614-5f63-a3e0-c70ebf4bb7db'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals court, endorsing a broad conception of executive branch secrecy, said the White House could withhold a Justice Department memo about the handing over of telephone records.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/us/court-backs-shielding-of-legal-memo-on-phone-records.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court, endorsing a broad conception of executive branch secrecy, said the White House could withhold a Justice Department memo about the handing over of telephone records.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A federal appeals court on Friday ruled that the Obam