 won a postseason road game, even in the previous seven years as one of the N.F.L.’s strongest teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — The New Orleans Saints’ victory over the Tampa Bay Buccaneers in their final regular-season game Sunday featured their trademark passing game, key defensive stops and 70,000 rollicking fans fueled by brass bands and beer.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/sports/SAINTS/SAINTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/04/sports/SAINTS/SAINTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/sports/SAINTS/SAINTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/sports/SAINTS/SAINTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1228, 'width': 1804, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/sports/SAINTS/SAINTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/04/sports/SAINTS/SAINTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/sports/SAINTS/SAINTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dominant in Dome, Saints Face Tough Road as They Try to Defy Trends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dominant in Dome, Saints Face Tough Road As They Try to Defy Trends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payton, Sean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-03T21:07:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a2ed981-1e56-54dd-92b3-c4c907edbc83', 'word_count': 1285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a2ed981-1e56-54dd-92b3-c4c907edbc83'}, {'abstract': 'After two combat tours in Afghanistan, an infantry rifleman readjusts to civilian life — and the paternal role he left behind.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/03/reclaiming-fatherhood-after-afghanistan/', 'snippet': 'After two combat tours in Afghanistan, an infantry rifleman readjusts to civilian life — and the paternal role he left behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During my enlistment, I had the privilege to serve as an infantry rifleman, the primary infantry job in the United States Marine Corps. My role was to locate, close with and destroy or repel the enemy, by fire and close combat. As I advanced through my career, I learned valuable teamwork, communication and leadership skills that I continue to use. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reclaiming Fatherhood After Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'ran