ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/700a34aa-293b-529c-b054-3357ab77fad1', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/700a34aa-293b-529c-b054-3357ab77fad1'}, {'abstract': 'A lawyer writes about forced arbitration for employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/opinion/employees-and-arbitration.html', 'snippet': 'A lawyer writes about forced arbitration for employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Employees and Arbitration', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Employees and Arbitration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T00:51:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c454d25-d6de-57ff-95ec-d29ad3f7d3fb', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c454d25-d6de-57ff-95ec-d29ad3f7d3fb'}, {'abstract': 'A concertgoer says most audience members are trying hard to avoid causing a distraction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/opinion/coughing-at-concerts.html', 'snippet': 'A concertgoer says most audience members are trying hard to avoid causing a distraction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coughing at Concerts', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coughing at Concerts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coughs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T00:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae5dd28a-793e-59df-a25b-06f7cf7357b5', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae5dd28a-793e-59df-a25b-06f7cf7357b5'}, {'abstract': 'The most vulnerable suffer when technology contracts are bungled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/opinion/an-error-message-for-the-poor.html', 'snippet': 'The most vulnerable suffer when technology contracts are bungled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — MORE than two million people have signed up for health insurance coverage under the Affordable Care Act, a tribute to the effectiveness of the “tech surge” the Obama administration deployed to overcome the highly publicized problems with HealthCare.gov that emerged in October. The website’s initial rollout will long stand as a monument to how badly technology contracting can go wrong. But the remarkable recovery also demonstrates what a determined response to such bungling can achieve.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Error Message for the Poor', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Error Message For the Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Super, David A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T01:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David A. Super', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Super', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a29ae7-acdc-5bed-a722-847f3589ed21', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a29ae7-acdc-5bed-a722-847f3589ed21'}, {'abstract': 'On a visit to Rio de Janeiro, asylum was the question of the hour. Could South America be his next stop after Russia?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/opinion/nocera-brazil-is-abuzz-about-snowden.html', 'snippet': 'On a visit to Rio de Janeiro, asylum was the question of the hour. Could South America be his next stop after Russia?', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — When I visited China in June, my trip happened to coincide with the discovery that Edward Snowden was hiding out in Hong Kong. By then, Snowden’s revelations about the voracious data-collection operation by the National Security Agency was front-page news all over the world. Snowden hadn’t yet been charged for the leak of tens of thousands of pages of classified N.S.A. documents, but it was clear that it was coming. So it was only natural to ask — as many journalists did — would Hong Kong give Snowden asylum if he requested it? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil Is Abuzz About Snowden', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil Is Abuzz About Snowden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T01:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4360525b-0b7c-530b-acb9-07e5144a97c0', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4360525b-0b7c-530b-acb9-07e5144a97c0'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s annual holiday trips to Hawaii include bonding time with the high school friends who have come to be known collectively as the Choom Gang.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/us/politics/visits-with-school-pals-are-a-touchstone-on-presidents-trips-to-hawaii.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s annual holiday trips to Hawaii include bonding time with the high school friends who have come to be known collectively as the Choom Gang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama has called Hawaii his refuge, and so it has been throughout his political life. In 2006, Mr. Obama used the family Christmas holiday there to decide whether to run for president. For the past two weeks, he has been recharging on Oahu after an unpleasant year in the job.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/us/CHOOM/CHOOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/04/us/CHOOM/CHOOM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/us/CHOOM/CHOOM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/us/CHOOM/CHOOM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/04/us/CHOOM/CHOOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/04/us/CHOOM/CHOOM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'th