0th trip to the region to get the two sides to stick the timetable he set forth when he started new negotiations last July. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ticking Mideast Clock', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Ticking Mideast Clock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T02:18:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e253083-9916-5f3e-866b-6a6b09b391b0', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e253083-9916-5f3e-866b-6a6b09b391b0'}, {'abstract': 'A video produced by a safety agency warned of the dangers of a chemistry experiment that went awry at a Manhattan school this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/nyregion/school-experiment-that-burned-boy-was-focus-of-federal-warning.html', 'snippet': 'A video produced by a safety agency warned of the dangers of a chemistry experiment that went awry at a Manhattan school this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only weeks before a chemistry experiment sent a plume of fire across a Manhattan high school science lab, engulfing two students and leaving one with life-threatening burns, a federal safety agency issued a video warning of the dangers of the very same experiment, a common one across the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'School Experiment That Burned Boy Was Focus of Federal Warning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'School Experiment That Critically Burned Boy Was Focus of Federal Warning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemistry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beacon School (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York-Presbyterian Hospital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanes, Alonzo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poole, Anna', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T02:24:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73d86fbc-47e4-51bc-adf3-e6fd445c9a88', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73d86fbc-47e4-51bc-adf3-e6fd445c9a88'}, {'abstract': 'Taxpayers pay too much for federal contractors, and they get too little in return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/opinion/not-getting-their-moneys-worth.html', 'snippet': 'Taxpayers pay too much for federal contractors, and they get too little in return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, two recent crises to hit the White House — the revelations about unlawful surveillance and the botched health care rollout — have nothing in common. But each is a reminder of the increasing extent to which government work has been contracted out to private-sector companies. Currently, Washington spends about $500 billion a year on private-sector contracts, more than twice the amount in 2000.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Getting Their Money’s Worth', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Getting Their Money’s Worth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Procurement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T02:29:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/508d1987-0c29-5327-92a2-ece27182d351', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/508d1987-0c29-5327-92a2-ece27182d351'}, {'abstract': 'Two Obama proposals offer a promise of at least some relief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/opinion/stopping-mentally-ill-gun-buyers.html', 'snippet': 'Two Obama proposals offer a promise of at least some relief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rebuffed by Congress on stronger gun safety laws, President Obama is wisely using use his executive powers in a more focused attempt to bar mentally ill people from eluding federal watch lists and purchasing firearms. Two sensible changes proposed for the background check system would allow states and mental health providers more discretion than they have now in reporting information about potentially violent people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stopping Mentally Ill Gun Buyers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stopping Mentally Ill Gun Buyers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T02:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf14973d-334c-5a21-a8b8-811e460cb0ad', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf14973d-334c-5a21-a8b8-811e460cb0ad'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-jan-3-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 3, 2014', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Lottery Numbers for Jan. 3, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T02:33:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8db8167-6d92-5df8-a381-1004e34fc42c', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8db8167-6d92-5df8-a381-1004e34fc42c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cuomo exercised his clemency power for the first time since taking office in 2011, pardoning just three men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/opinion/governor-cuomos-stingy-pardons.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cuomo exercised his clemency power for the first time since taking office in 2011, pardoning just three men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The power to grant clemency is a critical function of the executive branch. It serves as a last, case-by-case resort to remedy an unjustly long sentence, erase a wrongful conviction or show forgiveness where it is merited. But New Yorkers seeking clemency from Gov. Andrew Cuomo, either from within prison or after their release, have found virtually no consolation during the three years of his tenure.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Governor Cuomo’s Stingy Pardons', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Governor Cuomo’s Stingy Pardons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T02:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd8171a2-64d0-5ef9-b854-1fffc1dd955b', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://articl