'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/04/business/how-the-auto-industry-fared-in-december-1388811090031/how-the-auto-industry-fared-in-december-1388811090031-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Auto Industry Fared in December', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T04:57:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4802e711-d646-58e9-975b-878f15e6d6e8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4802e711-d646-58e9-975b-878f15e6d6e8'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) ADMISSION (2013) Tina Fey (above, seated) portrays Portia Nathan, a Princeton admissions officer who seems to take a special kind of glee in controlling the fate of applicants aspiring to the university’s ivy-covered halls. She also has a goal of her own: to succeed the retiring dean of admissions (Wallace Shawn) and beat out her office rival (Gloria Reuben) while reclaiming Princeton’s place at the top of the U.S. News & World Report rankings. But just as her smug English-professor boyfriend (Michael Sheen) dumps her for an aggressive Virginia Woolf scholar (Sonya Walger), a fellow Dartmouth alum (Paul Rudd) comes along with an unusual student (Nat Wolff) he wants Portia to consider. “How could anyone make light of the brutal, capricious system by which our young people are judged and sorted?” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about this comedy from Paul Weitz, adapted from the novel by Jean Hanff Korelitz. “And I must confess that I don’t know whether to be relieved or disappointed that ‘Admission,’ which had the potential to be a sharp, satirical jab at the soft belly of middle-class anxiety, chose instead to be a warm and wacky fable of wish fulfillment. Mr. Weitz lines up a target placed at the explosive intersection of class, race, region and every other source of societal anguish, and then does not so much miss as aim in another direction — or several — letting fly a volley of darts that land as lightly as badminton birdies.” Still, Ms. Fey and Mr. Rudd “are fun to watch, though not as much fun as they might have been in a riskier, crazier movie,” he said, adding that “the best scenes belong to Lily Tomlin, brilliantly cast as Portia’s mother, an unbowed second-wave woman warrior with a pair of borzois and a Bella Abzug tattoo.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T06:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/90f7cc83-8b74-539a-965b-dd5cd73cd5c3', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90f7cc83-8b74-539a-965b-dd5cd73cd5c3'}, {'abstract': 'Cambodian police officers on Saturday cleared protesters from a Phnom Penh park that has been the staging ground for antigovernment demonstrations, and organizers canceled a planned Sunday rally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/world/asia/cambodia.html', 'snippet': 'Cambodian police officers on Saturday cleared protesters from a Phnom Penh park that has been the staging ground for antigovernment demonstrations, and organizers canceled a planned Sunday rally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHNOM PENH, Cambodia — Seeking to quash one of the most serious challenges to the nearly 30-year rule of the country’s authoritarian leader, Cambodian authorities evicted antigovernment protesters on Saturday from a public square and banned all public gatherings as a court summoned two opposition leaders for police questioning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cambodia Cracks Down on Protest With Evictions and Ban on Assembly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cambodia Cracks Down on Protest With Evictions and Ban on Assembly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hun Sen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cambodia National Rescue Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T08:02:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/589c7fab-7f40-569e-bf0a-fa0005b0520b', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/589c7fab-7f40-569e-bf0a-fa0005b0520b'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama insisted that lawmakers make restoring unemployment benefits for 1.3 million Americans their “first order of business” in the new year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/us/politics/obama-urges-congress-to-restore-benefits-to-the-long-term-unemployed.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama insisted that lawmakers make restoring unemployment benefits for 1.3 million Americans their “first order of business” in the new year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama, seeking the upper hand with Congress as he heads back from his Hawaiian vacation, insisted on Saturday that lawmakers make restoring unemployment benefits for 1.3 million Americans who are out of work their “first order of business” in the new year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Urges Congress to Restore Unemployment Benefits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Urges Congress to Restore Unemployment Benefits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc495fe-e7d3-51f1-8bef-199caf8e60cd', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc495fe-e7d3-51f1-8bef-199caf8e60cd'}, {'abstract': 'Some animals appear to like sugar but have no response to artificial sweeteners.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/do-animals-have-a-sweet-tooth/', 'snippet': 'Some animals appear to like sugar but have no response to artificial sweeteners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No preference is so quick to form, and none so hard to lose, as a baby’s love for sweets. Give a newborn a drop of sugar water when he’s hours old, and he’ll suckle. At a dental school in Jerusalem in the early 1970s, a scientist named Jacob E. Steiner doled out sucrose to 175 infants before they’d had a drop of mother’s milk and saw clear signs of satisfaction: The babies showed “a marked relaxation of the facial muscle,” he wrote, and “a retraction of the mouth’s angles resembling a ‘smile.’ ” Then he tried the same experiment on several babies born without a cerebral cortex and found the same result. The joy of sugar needs no cogitation; it scarcely needs a brain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/magazine/3-swamp-wallabies/3-swamp-wallabies-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/magazine/3-swamp-wallabies/3-swamp-wallabies-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/magazine/3-swamp-wallabies/3-swamp-wallabies-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/magazine/3-swamp-wallabies/3-swamp-wallabies-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/magazine/3-swamp-wallabies/3-swamp-wallabies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/03/magazine/3-swamp-wallabies/3-swamp-wallabies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/magazine/3-swamp-wallabies/3-swamp-wallabies-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Animals Have a Sweet Tooth?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Sweeteners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taste', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T12:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Engber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Engber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/994366c6-926d-5c2b-ab1d-c8c2b36aa22a', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/994366c6-926d-5c2b-ab1d-c8c2b36aa22a'}, {'abstract': 'I worried that my daughter’s decision to take a gap year would mean she’d never go to college. I shouldn’t have.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/in-fervent-support-of-the-gap-year/', 'snippet': 'I worried that my daughter’s decision to take a gap year would mean she’d never go to college. I shouldn’t have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wasn’t enthusiastic when my daughter first floated her plan to take a “gap year” before college. As someone who couldn’t wait to matriculate, I didn’t see the point of delaying that great intellectual awakening. I felt vaguely disappointed that she wasn’t more eager to embrace all those books and ideas and late-night conversations about the cosmos. And what if her gap year turned into a permanent crevasse and she never earned a degree? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/10/sports/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/10/sports/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/10/sports/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/10/sports/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/10/sports/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/10/sports/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816/0210_SPT_village_ss-slide-1735816-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumb