jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Assn of Machinists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T15:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0764523f-ec56-5a38-9649-7ff8afd12b79', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0764523f-ec56-5a38-9649-7ff8afd12b79'}, {'abstract': 'I hate to say this, but it could happen.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/happy-new-year/', 'snippet': 'I hate to say this, but it could happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s an alarming amount of optimism out there about US economic prospects for 2014. Let me make the situation even more alarming by saying that I basically share that optimism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy New Year?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T15:50:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9a994ec-66cb-5c2b-991b-1976a620bb63', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9a994ec-66cb-5c2b-991b-1976a620bb63'}, {'abstract': '100 years ago The New York Herald reported widespread outrage at the appearance of tango in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/04/1914-amazingly-popular-dance-causes-widespread-social-controversy/', 'snippet': '100 years ago The New York Herald reported widespread outrage at the appearance of tango in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never has a dance been so much discussed, defended and denounced as has the tango, the extraordinary terpsichorean craze which has swept over the whole of Europe and the United States. Society leaders have condemned unsparingly, bishops have shuddered, royalty has expressed uncompromising disapproval, and the tango is still danced with fervor by tens of thousands. It cannot be denied that the tango in its original form would have shocked the most Bohemian society. The very name — tango, “I touch”— has a significance which needs no comment. But it is a far cry from the original as it was danced in the most undesirable cafés of the Argentine to the severely Bowdlerized version tolerated in the modern ballroom. It is believed that the tango is of Spanish origin, and was taken to South America by Spanish settlers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Amazingly Popular Dance Causes Widespread Social Controversy', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tango', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-04T15:55:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9886680c-9411-51ff-9ef3-87a8d43aa5ba', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9886680c-9411-51ff-9ef3-87a8d43aa5ba'}, {'abstract': 'Potential Olympians like Canada’s Steven Stamkos, Slovakia’s Marian Gaborik, Sweden’s Alex Steen and Russia’s Evgeni Malkin are among the N.H.L. players out with injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/sports/hockey/injuries-in-nhl-keep-olympic-rosters-in-flux-worldwide.html', 'snippet': 'Potential Olympians like Canada’s Steven Stamkos, Slovakia’s Marian Gaborik, Sweden’s Alex Steen and Russia’s Evgeni Malkin are among the N.H.L. players out with injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Picking an Olympic roster is tricky enough, but a rash of injuries in the N.H.L. this season is making it harder than ever. Toronto Coach Randy Carlyle noted at the end of December that 108 players were out, 15 percent of the league. That number includes some of the biggest stars among the medal contenders for the Sochi Games, players like Canada’s Steven Stamkos, Slovakia’s Marian Gaborik, Sweden’s Alex Steen and Russia’s Evgeni Malkin.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/sports/DOG-SLAPSHOT/DOG-SLAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/05/sports/DOG-SLAPSHOT/DOG-SLAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/sports/DOG-SLAPSHOT/DOG-SLAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam