ULU — When President Obama departed Hawaii Saturday evening he left behind one notable thing — his wife, Michelle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michelle Obama Extends Her Hawaii Vacation', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-05T13:11:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b34bca6-ff62-5772-8298-f7151bf3ac70', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b34bca6-ff62-5772-8298-f7151bf3ac70'}, {'abstract': 'Is our collective, Internet-driven rage about everything from Miley Cyrus to gun control any more effective than my daughter’s temper tantrums over my insistence that she wear pants?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/my-year-of-mom-rage/', 'snippet': 'Is our collective, Internet-driven rage about everything from Miley Cyrus to gun control any more effective than my daughter’s temper tantrums over my insistence that she wear pants?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s time to put on pants, and my daughter is sprawled on the floor sobbing. “I don’t want them!” she cries. “I don’t wike dem!” My daughter is 2, and she refuses to wear anything except fancy dresses. Today she is wearing a white Easter dress with a green sash and a big pink flower. Never mind that it’s winter and we live in Iowa, where it’s 20 degrees outside. I’ve tried reasoning and pleading with her, and finally we reach a compromise. She can wear the dress as long as she wears pants underneath and a sweater. I get the sweater on her. It’s pink, so that helps. But not the pants.', 'source':