': 'A statement from aides to Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the former oil tycoon, said he has “not yet made any plans about permanent residency in Switzerland or anywhere else.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the former oil tycoon recently freed after a decade in prison in Russia, has left Berlin and arrived by train in Switzerland, where he and his wife will oversee their teenage sons’ return to school, according to a statement from Mr. Khodorkovsky’s aides, who called the trip “a family matter.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freed Russian Oligarch Leaves Germany for Switzerland With Family', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freed Russian Oligarch Leaves Germany for Switzerland With Family', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovsky, Mikhail B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yukos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T00:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e888c460-ea4b-5a32-93f8-e1f75726c444', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e888c460-ea4b-5a32-93f8-e1f75726c444'}, {'abstract': 'Some in Hawaii, eager to claim President Obama as their own, have mounted a well-organized campaign to encourage him to place at least part of his postpresidential operation in the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/us/hawaii-makes-its-case-for-obamas-library-why-not-bring-it-to-the-beach.html', 'snippet': 'Some in Hawaii, eager to claim President Obama as their own, have mounted a well-organized campaign to encourage him to place at least part of his postpresidential operation in the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONOLULU — When Gov. Neil Abercrombie of Hawaii was asked to appear in a video urging President Obama to make the state the home of his presidential library, the governor’s appeal was simple and, he said, reflective of the state’s “Aloha spirit.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/us/LIBRARY-1/LIBRARY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/06/us/LIBRARY-1/LIBRARY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/us/LIBRARY-1/LIBRARY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/us/LIBRARY-1/LIBRARY-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/us/LIBRARY-1/LIBRARY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/06/us/LIBRARY-1/LIBRARY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/us/LIBRARY-1/LIBRARY-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawaii Makes Its Case for Obama’s Library: Why Not Bring It to the Beach?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hawaii Makes Its Case for Obama’s Library: Why Not Bring It to the Beach?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perkinson, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T00:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fffa06f6-f5e8-5435-823b-28b6747b7030', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fffa06f6-f5e8-5435-823b-28b6747b7030'}, {'abstract': 'Although Roger Federer lost in the final of the Brisbane International, he said he was eager for the Australian Open to begin next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/sports/tennis/federer-falls-to-hewitt-but-australian-open-awaits.html', 'snippet': 'Although Roger Federer lost in the final of the Brisbane International, he said he was eager for the Australian Open to begin next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRISBANE, Australia — This stage of Roger Federer’s career will primarily be measured by his success in fending off younger players, but he finished the first week of his 2014 season with a rare loss to an older foe. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federer Falls to Hewitt, but Australian Open Awaits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hewitt Wins Brisbane Final', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothenberg, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hewitt, Lleyton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T01:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8009191e-9e26-54e7-913e-c183c0ce55fd', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8009191e-9e26-54e7-913e-c183c0ce55fd'}, {'abstract': 'Samsung Electronics will report its fourth-quarter earnings estimates, the insider trading trial of Mathew Martoma will begin and the European Central Bank will review its monetary policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/business/economy/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-jan-6.html', 'snippet': 'Samsung Electronics will report its fourth-quarter earnings estimates, the insider trading trial of Mathew Martoma will begin and the European Central Bank will review its monetary policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAMSUNG EARNINGS 2014 will be a tough year for Samsung Electronics, the largest cellphone and television maker in the world. Its stock recently took a beating amid concerns of slowing profit growth from smartphone sales, and the company is under pressure to continue releasing innovative new products to compete with Apple and a crop of handset makers in China. On Tuesday, when the South Korean giant is expected to report earnings estimates for the fourth quarter, investors will keep a close eye on the company’s sales of cellphones, televisions and other items during the holiday shopping season, the most lucrative time of year for electronics manufacturers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week of Jan. 6', 'kicker': 'Looking Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Electronics Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martoma, Mathew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T01:12:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e08aec1f-9e20-572c-abad-c72dbfa9dd1a', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e08aec1f-9e20-572c-abad-c72dbfa9dd1a'}, {'abstract': 'It might sound like a gift to the rich, but eliminating or at least lowering the corporate tax rate would help workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/opinion/abolish-the-corporate-income-tax.html', 'snippet': 'It might sound like a gift to the rich, but eliminating or at least lowering the corporate tax rate would help workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — JOBS don’t grow out of thin air, especially well-paying ones. They require, among other things, companies that are willing to operate where you live. Just ask the Seattle-based District 751 of the machinists’ union, which was worried that Boeing will build its new 777X airliner someplace far away where it is cheaper to produce. Last month the union offered contract concessions, as its president explained, to ensure “the long-term success” of Boeing in Washington State. And on Friday, Boeing machinists approved a contract with concessions to keep assembly of the plane in the area.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/opinion/0106OPEDsergio/0106OPEDsergio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/06/opinion/0106OPEDsergio/0106OPEDsergio-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/opinion/0106OPEDsergio/0106OPEDsergio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/opinion/0106OPEDsergio/0106OPEDsergio-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/opinion/0106OPEDsergio/0106OPEDsergio-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/06/opinion/0106OPEDsergio/0106OPEDsergio-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/opinion/0106OPEDsergio/0106OPEDsergio-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Abolish the Corporate Income Tax', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'conten