cs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T01:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a526465-973f-5dbe-b652-72e6ac056f6f', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a526465-973f-5dbe-b652-72e6ac056f6f'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate will vote on unemployment benefits. But the House? It’s planning another meaningless, symbolic vote on health care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/opinion/republican-disdain-for-the-jobless.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate will vote on unemployment benefits. But the House? It’s planning another meaningless, symbolic vote on health care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the first votes the Senate plans to take when it returns Monday is on restoring unemployment benefits to 1.3 million people who lost them on Dec. 28. It’s hard to imagine a more important action for those who have been out of work the longest and for the economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Disdain for the Jobless', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republican Disdain for the Jobless', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'