151-528e-8b19-dd9800e61e6a'}, {'abstract': 'Schools across the country are reforming a destructive disciplinary policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/opinion/zero-tolerance-reconsidered.html', 'snippet': 'Schools across the country are reforming a destructive disciplinary policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Schools across the country are rethinking “zero tolerance” discipline policies under which children have been suspended, even arrested, for minor offenses like cursing, getting into shoving matches and other garden-variety misbehavior that in years past would have been resolved with detention or meetings with a child’s parents. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zero Tolerance, Reconsidered', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zero Tolerance, Reconsidered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Discipline (Students)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Broward County (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T02:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/97e371e6-e895-5313-aefd-9fcb685e7bf6', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97e371e6-e895-5313-aefd-9fcb685e7bf6'}, {'abstract': 'Phil Dawson kicked a 33-yard field goal as time expired, giving the 49ers a victory at frigid Lambeau Field and sending them to a second-round playoff game at Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/sports/football/49ers-feel-joy-if-not-their-toes.html', 'snippet': 'Phil Dawson kicked a 33-yard field goal as time expired, giving the 49ers a victory at frigid Lambeau Field and sending them to a second-round playoff game at Carolina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREEN BAY, Wis. — The bitterly cold forecast for Sunday’s N.F.C. wild-card game at Lambeau Field concerned San Francisco 49ers Coach Jim Harbaugh. So twice, on Saturday and again before kickoff, he asked his quarterback, Colin Kaepernick, to reconsider his plan to play in short sleeves and without gloves.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/sports/nfc/nfc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/06/sports/nfc/nfc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/sports/nfc/nfc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/sports/nfc/nfc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1174, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/sports/nfc/nfc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/06/sports/nfc/nfc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type