mise an heiress (Myrna Loy) before she can sue for libel, at 1 a.m.; William Dieterle’s “Love Letters” (1945), about a soldier (Cotten, again) who falls for the woman (Jennifer Jones) who may have killed his best friend, at 3 a.m.; and “The Band Wagon” (1953), Vincente Minnelli’s MGM musical with Fred Astaire as an aging star whose Broadway comeback is sabotaged by an overzealous director (Jack Buchanan) and his prima ballerina colleague (Cyd Charisse), at 5 a.m. Arthur Schwartz and Howard Dietz wrote the songs, which include “That’s Entertainment!”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T05:16:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c16af85-04b7-590c-80d5-2f4de8383828', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c16af85-04b7-590c-80d5-2f4de8383828'}, {'abstract': 'Often, fans will use head coverings to vividly declare their loyalties. At other times they merely serve as protection from the elements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/01/06/sports/WeekInPictures.html', 'snippet': 'Often, fans will use head coverings to vividly declare their loyalties. At other times they merely serve as protection from the elements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Often, fans will use head coverings to vividly declare their loyalties. At other times they merely serve as protection from the elements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subt