er story explains his fascination with John Aldridge, who fell off a boat and kept himself alive for several hours before the Coast Guard finally found him.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/behind-the-cover-paul-tough-on-a-tale-of-strategic-survival/', 'snippet': 'The author of this week’s cover story explains his fascination with John Aldridge, who fell off a boat and kept himself alive for several hours before the Coast Guard finally found him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Tough, a contributing writer for the magazine, wrote this week’s cover story about a fisherman named John Aldridge, who fell overboard 40 miles off the eastern end of Long Island last summer and survived nearly 12 hours in the water before being rescued by the Coast Guard. Tough’s most recent book is “How Children Succeed: Grit, Curiosity, and the Hidden Power of Character.”How did you first hear about this extraordinary survival story?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/magazine/20-paul-tough/20-paul-tough-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/20/magazine/20-paul-tough/20-paul-tough-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 835}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/magazine/20-paul-tough/20-paul-tough-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/magazine/20-paul-tough/20-paul-tough-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1530, 'width': 1100, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08