windows for a shrine?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/finkel-2/', 'snippet': 'Can you help a pilgrim design stained glass windows for a shrine?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s puzzle by Daniel Finkel we continue to follow an itinerant nun who most recently made her way to a shrine in the holy town of Duona. We now join her in some construction work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daniel Finkel’s Stained Glass Window Problem', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finkel, Daniel (1979- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T17:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e56cf42-53af-5ce2-bbcf-a2475b537e3a', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e56cf42-53af-5ce2-bbcf-a2475b537e3a'}, {'abstract': 'A reflection on the past year of weekly Numberplay puzzles, including links to the 51 puzzles of 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/2013/', 'snippet': 'A reflection on the past year of weekly Numberplay puzzles, including links to the 51 puzzles of 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happy New Year! We had quite an adventure in 2013, and I’m looking forward to continuing the quantitative fun this coming year (check out this week’s challenge below). Before we get too far\xa0— a short reflection on our recent travels. Numberplay in 2013 featured original problems from many prominent and emerging mathematicians\xa0— problems that served as terrific platforms for our weekly explorations. A connection to an original creator is a powerful experience, and we were fortunate to have had many, including understanding fundamental origami concepts with Barry Hayes; discovering combinatorics with Joel Spencer, Ron Graham and Béla Bollobás; exploring primes with Bernardo Recamán.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay 2013: A Year in Review', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Devlin, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardner, Martin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luck, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Simon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strogatz, Steven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zucker, Joshua', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T17:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e797a039-1518-5927-96be-d29fccc937d2', 'word_count': 3580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e797a039-1518-5927-96be-d29fccc937d2'}, {'abstract': 'As chairwoman, Ms. Yellen will face an arduous task overseeing the gradual unwinding of stimulus measures, despite an uncomfortably high unemployment rate of 7 percent and subdued inflation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/business/economy/Yellen-Senate-Vote.html', 'snippet': 'As chairwoman, Ms. Yellen will face an arduous task overseeing the gradual unwinding of stimulus measures, despite an uncomfortably high unemployment rate of 7 percent and subdued inflation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate confirmed Janet L. Yellen as the chairwoman of the Federal Reserve on Monday, marking the first time that a woman will lead the country’s central bank in its 100-year history.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Fed/Fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Fed/Fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Fed/Fed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Fed/Fed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Fed/Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Fed/Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Fed/Fed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thu