ns for the patient-doctor relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I remember when I first looked up a patient on Google. It was my last day on the bone marrow transplant unit, back when I was an intern. As I stood before the patient, taking her history, she told me she had been a painter and suggested I look up her work on the Internet. I did, and I found her paintings fascinating. Even though our paths crossed fleetingly, she is one of the few patients I vividly remember from that time.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07DOCT/07DOCT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07DOCT/07DOCT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 532}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07DOCT/07DOCT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 907, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07DOCT/07DOCT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1814, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07DOCT/07DOCT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07DOCT/07DOCT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07DOCT/07DOCT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Doctors ‘Google’ Their Patients', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patient Secrets, Found Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T18:59:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haider Javed Warraich, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haider', 'middlename': 'Javed', 'lastname': 'Warraich', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c828047-6a7d-5c7a-9fa1-d9b8a5594ad9', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c828047-6a7d-5c7a-9fa1-d9b8a5594ad9'}, {'abstract': 'During the College Bowl season, the N.C.A.A. allows players to accept gifts.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/tis-the-season-to-compensate-college-athletes/', 'snippet': 'During the College Bowl season, the N.C.A.A. allows players to accept gifts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.C.A.A. classifies Division I football players as amateurs, not professionals, student-athletes, not employees, which is how colleges get away with paying them nothing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tis the Season to Compensate College Athletes', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowl Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinkel, Gary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Ass