': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T19:52:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hana de Goeij', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Goeij', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c954aa2d-4db6-55f2-9d38-be5d0c17ebf5', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c954aa2d-4db6-55f2-9d38-be5d0c17ebf5'}, {'abstract': 'A few thoughts on an unpersuasive defense of scientific materialism.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/the-confidence-of-jerry-coyne/', 'snippet': 'A few thoughts on an unpersuasive defense of scientific materialism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the problems with belonging to a faction that’s convinced it’s on the winning side of intellectual history is that it becomes easy to persuade oneself that one’s own worldview has no weak points whatsoever, no internal contradictions or ragged edges, no cracks through which a critic’s wedge could end up driven.\xa0This kind of overconfidence has been displayed, at various points in the human story, by everyone from millenarians to Marxists, inquisitors to eugenicists. But right now its vices are often found in a certain type of atheistic polemicist, and in a style of anti-religious argument that’s characterized by a peculiar, almost-willed ignorance of why reasonable people might doubt the scientific-materialist worldview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Confidence of Jerry Coyne', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Altruism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atheism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coyne, Jerry A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nagel, Thomas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Republic', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T20:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b27cbf-c92d-51a6-af8d-8f4b9e5d9aef', 'word_count': 1894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b27cbf-c92d-51a6-af8d-8f4b9e5d9aef'}, {'abstract': 'Multiple appliances had been connected to a power strip in an apartment on the 20th floor of the Strand luxury building, according to a Fire Department official.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/nyregion/deadly-hells-kitchen-blaze-traced-to-electrical-wire-fire-dept-says.html', 'snippet': 'Multiple appliances had been connected to a power strip in an apartment on the 20th floor of the Strand luxury building, according to a Fire Department official.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fire that left one man dead and other residents displaced from a high-rise building in Midtown Manhattan over the weekend was traced to an electrical power strip, the Fire Department said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deadly Hell’s Kitchen Blaze Traced to Electrical Wire, Fire Dept. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fatal Midtown Fire Traced to Wire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correal, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClung, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': "Hell's Kitchen (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T20:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/482f1d28-8422-548d-a261-23540ffd4635', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/482f1d28-8422-548d-a261-23540ffd4635'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at gold, home prices and stocks in 2013 confirms some old investment truths.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/your-money/never-mind-the-predictions-what-did-we-learn.html', 'snippet': 'A look back at gold, home prices and stocks in 2013 confirms some old investment truths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m not big on market predictions. In fact, if anyone asks, I’m pretty quick to say that I don’t know what the markets will do in 2014. If you absolutely must have predictions for the next year, then I recommend you check out Barry Ritholtz’s annual list. But if you are interested in something more useful than predictions, I suggest taking a look at what we learned (or had confirmed — again) in 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/business/010614bucks-carl-sketch/010614bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/06/business/010614bucks-carl-sketch/010614bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/business/010614bucks-carl-sketch/010614bucks-carl-sketch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 612, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/business/010614bucks-carl-sketch/010614bucks-carl-sketch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 612, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/business/010614bucks-carl-sketch/010614bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/06/business/010614bucks-carl-sketch/010614bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/06/business/010614bucks-carl-sketch/010614bucks-carl-sketch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Never Mind the Predictions: What Did We Learn?', 'kicker': 'The Sketch Guy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T20:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edbe012c-4175-5630-8288-7453ba413875', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edbe012c-4175-5630-8288-7453ba413875'}, {'abstract': 'It was a long wait for those on a trapped research vessel, and if any of 338 sharks get too close to the Australian beach, they’ll send out tweets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/science/a-long-frozen-rescue-and-sharks-on-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'It was a long wait for those on a trapped research vessel, and if any of 338 sharks get too close to the Australian beach, they’ll send out tweets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nobody had a longer week than the 52 scientists, journalists and tourists waiting to be rescued from a vessel trapped in the frozen waters of East Antarctica. But for fishermen in Maine, where the shrimping season has been canceled because of a dearth of the crustaceans, it will be an even longer winter.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/03/world/03antarctica-1/03antarctica-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/03/world/03antarctica-1/03antarctica-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xla