ead_paragraph': 'Palo Alto Networks has acquired Morta Security, a two-year-old Silicon Valley security start-up run by former employees of the National Security Agency and the United States Air Force.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palo Alto Networks Acquires  Start-Up Morta Security', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Andreessen Horowitz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greylock Partners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Norwest Venture Partners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palo Alto Networks Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T21:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b9bbd00-fb3d-5277-8b00-a5b05cd134c2', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b9bbd00-fb3d-5277-8b00-a5b05cd134c2'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers seeking to document whether running out of food stamps or money for food at the end of the month damaged people’s health found a high correlation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/health/study-finds-more-diabetic-hospital-visits-when-food-budgets-dip.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers seeking to document whether running out of food stamps or money for food at the end of the month damaged people’s health found a high correlation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poor people with diabetes are significantly more likely to go to the hospital for dangerously low blood sugar at the end of the month when food budgets are tight than at the beginning of the month, a new study has found.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Ties Diabetic Crises to Dip in Food Budgets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Ties Diabetic Crises to Dip in Food Budgets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hypoglycemia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health Affairs (Journal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T21:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67aa7f4b-cb07-53cf-8081-6866209bbdfc', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67aa7f4b-cb07-53cf-8081-6866209bbdfc'}, {'abstract': 'Astronomers, using the Hubble Space Telescope, found the atmosphere of a “super-earth” planet so thick that observations of the surface were nearly impossible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/science/space/the-forecast-on-gj-1214b-extremely-cloudy.html', 'snippet': 'Astronomers, using the Hubble Space Telescope, found the atmosphere of a “super-earth” planet so thick that observations of the surface were nearly impossible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Astronomers from the University of Chicago have used the Hubble Space Telescope to observe the weather on a “super-Earth” planet orbiting a distant star for the first time. Conditions on GJ 1214b are cloudy, with an atmosphere so thick with water vapor or some other heavy molecule that observations of the planet’s surface are nearly impossible, they report in the journal Nature. Super-Earth planets, which are larger than Earth but smaller than Neptune, are among the most common planets in the Milky Way. To compile their forecast, the team analyzed 96 hours of telescope time over 11 months.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07FLOA_SPAN/07FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07FLOA_SPAN/07FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07FLOA_SPAN/07FLOA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07FLOA_SPAN/07FLOA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1101, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/science/07FLOA_SPAN/07FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/0