8de0ea77f1'}, {'abstract': 'The Islamic State of Iraq and Syria, a Qaeda affiliate and onetime ally of Syrian insurgents, was routed from the eastern city of Raqqa, antigovernment activists said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/world/middleeast/rebel-infighting-expands-to-eastern-Syrian-city.html', 'snippet': 'The Islamic State of Iraq and Syria, a Qaeda affiliate and onetime ally of Syrian insurgents, was routed from the eastern city of Raqqa, antigovernment activists said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — An internal war between Syrian insurgents and their onetime allies, members of a transnational jihadist group that even some fighters affiliated with Al Qaeda reject as too extreme, widened on Monday from parts of northern Syria into Raqqa, the largest city in eastern Syria that had been under the group’s control, antigovernment activists and fighters said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rebel Infighting Spreads to an Eastern Syrian City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rebel Infighting Spreads to an Eastern Syrian City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Raqqa (Syria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State of Iraq and Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T22:03:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'las