_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0932c629-cd1a-584a-91f6-58fd17fbfcf6', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0932c629-cd1a-584a-91f6-58fd17fbfcf6'}, {'abstract': 'A sensor manufacturer has created a harness that reads a video gamer’s every move and transfers those motions to a character onscreen in a game. But to work with actual games, the software will have to be adapted by a developer.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/a-device-to-put-you-into-a-video-game/', 'snippet': 'A sensor manufacturer has created a harness that reads a video gamer’s every move and transfers those motions to a character onscreen in a game. But to work with actual games, the software will have to be adapted by a developer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the stories behind the stories at the 2014 International Consumer Electronics Show is how the drop in the price of sensors – the parts in phones and devices that read motion, temperature, pressure and such – has made whiz-bang gizmos possible and affordable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Device to Put You Into a Video Game', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sensors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YEI Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-06T23:38:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e8b32a3-2d5d-535d-923c-8d6a9f080fb7', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e8b32a3-2d5d-535d-923c-8d6a9f080fb7'}, {'abstract': 'Activist investors were once thought of as greedy corporate raiders, but their efforts have become more sophisticated and they are often seen as doing good.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/06/no-barbarians-at-the-gate-instead-a-force-for-change/', 'snippet': 'Activist investors were once thought of as greedy corporate raiders, but their efforts have become more sophisticated and they are often seen as doing good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no longer an insult to be called an activist investor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/dbpix-hedge1/dbpix-hedge1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/07/business/dbpix-hedge1/dbpix-hedge1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/dbpix-hedge1/dbpix-hedge1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/dbpix-hedge1/dbpix-hedge1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1337, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/dbpix-hedge1/dbpix-hedge1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/07/business/dbpix-hedge1/dbpix-hedge1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':