, 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a5dafeb-9831-55df-9f7d-9cbabc92b9ce', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a5dafeb-9831-55df-9f7d-9cbabc92b9ce'}, {'abstract': 'The decisions Heinrich Hiesinger makes in the coming years will go a long way in determining the future of one of Europe’s largest businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/business/international/a-delicate-balance-for-the-turnaround-chief-of-thyssenkrupp.html', 'snippet': 'The decisions Heinrich Hiesinger makes in the coming years will go a long way in determining the future of one of Europe’s largest businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heinrich Hiesinger was hired as chief executive of Thyssen-Krupp in 2011 to clean up and modernize the storied German industrial giant after its disastrous attempt to go global during the financial crisis. Since then, he has been pushing through an overhaul plan that includes cutting the losses in steel while beefing up what he considers more promising businesses like elevators and factory design and construction. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Thyssen1/Thyssen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Thyssen1/Thyssen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Thyssen1/Thyssen1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Thyssen1/Thyssen1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Thyssen1/Thyssen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Thyssen1/Thyssen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/business/Thyssen1/Thyssen1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Delicate Balance for the Turnaround Chief of ThyssenKrupp', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Delicate Balance for the Turnaround Chief of ThyssenKrupp', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ThyssenKrupp AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steel and Iron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hiesinger, Heinrich', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T01:41:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b23242c2-63dd-5dda-afde-ff1070991d26', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b23242c2-63dd-5dda-afde-ff1070991d26'}, {'abstract': 'The ambassador to the United Nations from Jordan said he would renew his appeal to the governing body to visit countries that shelter millions of Syrian refugees, including his own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/world/middleeast/jordan-to-renew-appeal-on-syrian-refugees.html', 'snippet': 'The ambassador to the United Nations from Jordan said he would renew his appeal to the governing body to visit countries that shelter millions of Syrian refugees, including his own.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The ambassador to the United Nations from Jordan, the nation thrust into the rotating presidency of a polarized Security Council, said Monday that he would renew his appeal to the 15-member governing body to visit countries that shelter millions of Syrian refugees, including his own, which hosts more than 500,000 Syrians. The ambassador, Prince Zeid Ra’ad Zeid al-Hussein, said he had made the request before to draw attention to the humanitarian crisis facing Syria’s neighbors, but received no response. The Council has been deadlocked on Syria, but he declined to ascribe blame. “Being on the Council hopefully will make a difference,” he said. Jordan took the rotating two-year seat after Saudi Arabia rejected it to protest what it saw as the weak stance of Western powers toward Syria and Iran, the Saudis’ chief regional rivals. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jordan to Renew Appeal on Syrian Refugees', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jordan Renews Appeal on Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'v