ns-1-billion-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'Altice, whose operations include cable businesses and mobile assets in several European countries and the Caribbean, is expected to use the money to reduce debt, which could allow it to potentially bid for new assets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The European cable and cellphone operator Altice announced on Tuesday that it planned to raise up to 750 million euros, or $1 billion, through an initial public offering on the NYSE Euronext stock exchange in Amsterdam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Cable Operator Altice Plans $1 Billion I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Altice SaRL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T12:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/304534a1-10e8-5216-a5ac-6baff0a406b6', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/304534a1-10e8-5216-a5ac-6baff0a406b6'}, {'abstract': 'Danglers in their various forms are one of our most common grammatical lapses. Participle phrases, “like” comparisons, appositives and other modifying constructions generally must be adjacent to the noun or pronoun they refer to. Otherwise, they dangle — and leave a clumsy or confusing sentence.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/danglers-ahead/', 'snippet': 'Danglers in their various forms are one of our most common grammatical lapses. Participle phrases, “like” comparisons, appositives and other modifying constructions generally must be adjacent to the noun or pronoun they refer to. Otherwise, they d...', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I’ve noted ad nauseam — here, here and here, for example — danglers in their various forms are one of our most common grammatical lapses. Participle phrases, “like” comparisons, appositives and other modifying constructions generally must be adjacent to the noun or pronoun they refer to. Otherwise, they dangle — and leave a clumsy or confusing sentence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Danglers Ahead', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T13:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By PHILIP B. CORBETT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f246268-a0a6-5458-b422-0debdb7c0fef', 'word_count': 1928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f246268-a0a6-5458-b422-0debdb7c0fef'}, {'abstract': 'A woman who dresses on the masculine side wants to know if she has to compromise her expression by dressing according to a religious code.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/booming/must-this-lesbian-wear-a-dress-to-an-orthodox-synagogue.html', 'snippet': 'A woman who dresses on the masculine side wants to know if she has to compromise her expression by dressing according to a religious code.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Dear Civil Behavior: I am a gay woman who tends to dress and identify on the masculine side. I’ll soon be attending a religious service at my extended family’s Orthodox synagogue, requiring modest attire, which means that women are not allowed to wear pants and can be denied entry. I think that as long as I dress respectfully and in the spirit of the religious mandates I should not have to compromise on my gender identity and expression. My family says that I’m being difficult and that “when in Rome …” Of course, there is no chance my relatives would dress according to a code I prescribed for an event if it conflicted with their religious identity. So why am I considered “difficult” for not compromising in the expression of my gender identity when they would be considered justified in not compromising their religious expression? — Name withheld', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Must This Lesbian Wear a Dress to an Orthodox Synagogue?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Synagogues', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T13:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Petrow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Petrow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f55e94-0a28-5e45-ae1e-95f7ffcea290', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f55e94-0a28-5e45-ae1e-95f7ffcea290'}, {'abstract': 'The kidnapping of two executives at a Goodyear factory have become one of the most potent symbols of the challenges companies face in France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/business/international/french-workers-hold-goodyear-managers-over-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'The kidnapping of two executives at a Goodyear factory have become one of the most potent symbols of the challenges companies face in France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Negotiations broke down last weekend at a Goodyear tire factory scheduled for closing in northern France, so employees resorted to a brazen tactic: They kidnapped th