Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Premium', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c98195e2-a213-5a82-a53f-b2f8fc5220b8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c98195e2-a213-5a82-a53f-b2f8fc5220b8'}, {'abstract': 'Detail on the nine systemic financial crises the United States has suffered since 1814, taken from a new paper about post-crisis recoveries.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/200-years-of-american-financial-crises/', 'snippet': 'Detail on the nine systemic financial crises the United States has suffered since 1814, taken from a new paper about post-crisis recoveries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shaila Dewan and I had an article on Monday about a study suggesting the American economy was doing reasonably well — at least compared with the aftermath of previous systemic financial crises. Some readers wrote me asking about what the previous crises were and how they’re defined, so here’s some more detail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '200 Years of American Financial Crises', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reinhart, Carmen M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogoff, Kenneth S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T17:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0f8715b-b47b-5ac7-a336-ea53f162affd', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0f8715b-b47b-5ac7-a336-ea53f162affd'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/the-gun-report-january-7-2014/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If more citizens were armed, criminals would think twice about attacking them, Detroit Police Chief James Craig said in a press conference last week. Craig, who served in the L.A.P.D. for 28 years,\xa0attributes a lack of confidence in his police department to the likelihood that someone with a concealed weapons permit will open fire, The Detroit News reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: January 7, 2014', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T17:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67da7766-99d4-559f-aea8-cb6c8b909ee9', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67da7766-99d4-559f-aea8-cb6c8b909ee9'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Wolfram, a scientist and entrepreneur, announced the “Wolfram Connected Devices Project,” an initiative to provide and share knowledge about connected devices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/wolfram-alpha-wants-to-connect-the-internet-of-things/', 'snippet': 'Stephen Wolfram, a scientist and entrepreneur, announced the “Wolfram Connected Devices Project,” an initiative to provide and share knowledge about connected devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If all our gadgets and gizmos are going to be connected to the Internet, and in turn one another, they’ll need to speak the same language.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/technology/bits-wolfram/bits-wolfram-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/technology/bits-wolfram/bits-wolfram-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/technology/bits-wolfram/bits-wolfram-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/07/technology/bits-wolfram/bits-wolfram-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/07/technology/bits-wolfram/bits-wolfram-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wolfram Wants to Connect the Internet of Things', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T17:58:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a54fb95-5b9b-5c7f-a1ff-8246daec2e28', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a54fb95-5b9b-5c7f-a1ff-8246daec2e28'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama faces a challenge as he seeks to advertise the nation’s financial recovery while arguing for action to help a still-besieged middle class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/us/politics/obama.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama faces a challenge as he seeks to advertise the nation’s financial recovery while arguing for action to help a still-besieged middle class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Only moments after the Senate advanced an emergency extension of unemployment insurance benefits on Tuesday, President Obama stood on an East Room stage full of people without jobs and defied the traditional logic of White House strategy that normally emphasizes good news over bad. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Speaks of Better Days for Economy, With Asterisk', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Better Days, With Asterisk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T18:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/315a607d-1ccb-500d-813d-e0546262cfd3', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/315a607d-1ccb-500d-813d-e0546262cfd3'}, {'abstract': 'The tagine’s sweet and savory flavors pair well with a red wine that is fruity yet dry and perhaps slightly bitter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/dining/lamb-tagine-demands-a-red.html', 'snippet': 'The tagine’s sweet and savory flavors pair well with a red wine that is fruity yet dry and perhaps slightly bitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sweet and savory bursts of flavor in this tagine call for a red wine that is fruity yet dry and perhaps slightly bitter. The fruitiness will echo and amplify the sweet spiciness of the dates, pomegranate seeds, cinnamon and ginger, while the dry, bitter flavors will serve to underline the savory elements and refresh the mouth between bites. Italian reds like dolcetto, Valpolicella and Montepulciano d’Abruzzo specialize in the tension between fruity and bitter flavors.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lamb Tagine Demands a Red', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Drink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T18:09:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e9f8075-b40f-5220-bc16-f37336f8e83c', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e9f8075-b40f-5220-bc16-f37336f8e83c'}, {'abstract': 'BYD announces plans to sell cars in the United States; Detroit automakers plan to distribute $800 million to wo