n’t Add Up', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T19:05:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Swann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/914d6243-f072-5083-9959-55695a9736fe', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/914d6243-f072-5083-9959-55695a9736fe'}, {'abstract': 'The deal allows Sandvik, a Swedish company that provides specialized equipment for the mining and construction industries, to enter a new product area.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/sandvik-to-buy-texas-oil-drilling-equipment-company-for-740-million/', 'snippet': 'The deal allows Sandvik, a Swedish company that provides specialized equipment for the mining and construction industries, to enter a new product area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Swedish engineering company Sandvik said on Tuesday that it had reached an agreement to acquire the Texas oil drilling equipment company Varel International Energy Services for about $740 million.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sandvik to Buy Texas Oil Drilling Equipment Company for $740 Million', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growth Area', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sandvik AB', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Varel International Energy Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T19:13:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b75b31b4-0459-5356-a3cc-8e4be51c744a', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b75b31b4-0459-5356-a3cc-8e4be51c744a'}, {'abstract': 'A first-person account of a visit with Mohamed Fahmy, an Al Jazeera English journalist jailed in Cairo for his coverage of the Muslim Brotherhood, provides a rare glimpse into prison conditions in Egypt.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/a-rare-visit-with-a-jailed-journalist-in-egypt/', 'snippet': 'A first-person account of a visit with Mohamed Fahmy, an Al Jazeera English journalist jailed in Cairo for his coverage of the Muslim Brotherhood, provides a rare glimpse into prison conditions in Egypt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A first-person account of a visit with Mohamed Fahmy, part of a team of journalists from Al Jazeera English who were arrested 10 days ago on accusations that their coverage of the Muslim Brotherhood constituted “false news” and “incitement,” has provided a rare glimpse into prison conditions in Egypt as the government cracks down on the Brotherhood and anyone suspected of supporting it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rare Visit With a Jailed Journalist in Egypt', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahmy, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Jazeera English', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T19:18:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'orig