/2fd64f23-793d-5b32-8c96-e6d011d76bbb'}, {'abstract': 'Chelsea Opera, a small Manhattan opera company, has appointed Samuel McCoy as its new music director and principal conductor.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/samuel-mccoy-to-be-chelsea-operas-music-director/', 'snippet': 'Chelsea Opera, a small Manhattan opera company, has appointed Samuel McCoy as its new music director and principal conductor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chelsea Opera — a small Manhattan opera company that calls itself “the little opera company that could” — has appointed Samuel McCoy as its new music director and principal conductor. For his first outing in the position, Mr. McCoy, who has worked on contemporary operas and classics, will conduct a production of Aaron Copland’s “The Tender Land” at Chelsea Opera in June, said Lynne Hayden\xad-Findlay, who formed the company in 2004 with Leonarda Priore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samuel McCoy to Be Chelsea Opera’s Music Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chelsea Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T20:17:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/850b2f56-3b37-5e0b-aea7-51096658778e', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/850b2f56-3b37-5e0b-aea7-51096658778e'}, {'abstract': 'Monthly talks at the Cornelia Street Café will bring musicians together for talks on subjects like the role of music under the rule of the Taliban and music in advertising.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/07/make-music-new-york-to-host-monthly-talks/', 'snippet': 'Monthly talks at the Cornelia Street Café will bring musicians together for talks on subjects like the role of music under the rule of the Taliban and music in advertising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Make Music New York continues to expand. It began in 1989, as a one-day event, held every year on June 21, the summer solstice, with performances by musicians and ensembles of every stylistic stripe at parks, atriums, street corners and concert halls all over New York City, from 10 a.m. to 10 p.m.\xa0 Then, in 2011, inspired by Phil Kline’s annual “Unsilent Night” boombox parade, a winter solstice (Dec. 21) event was added, with composers and performers parading through the streets making music.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Make Music New York to Host Monthly Talks', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Make Music New York (Festival)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornelia Street Cafe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-07T20:22:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5849123d-709e-5fd5-8b1c-e11aea3ede34', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5849123d-709e-5fd5-8b1c-e11aea3ede34'}, {'abstract': 'Biz Stone, who made his