_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe7621a1-cf46-52c3-8ffb-437c8ccce390', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe7621a1-cf46-52c3-8ffb-437c8ccce390'}, {'abstract': 'Reid Farrington splices together video footage and live performance to produce a theoretical matchup of Mike Tyson and Muhammad Ali in “Tyson vs. Ali.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/theater/tyson-vs-ali-at-3ld-art-technology-center.html', 'snippet': 'Reid Farrington splices together video footage and live performance to produce a theoretical matchup of Mike Tyson and Muhammad Ali in “Tyson vs. Ali.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sweat, the combativeness and even the body blows feel mighty real, but the fight itself is pure fantasy in “Tyson vs. Ali,” a sleek mixed-media meditation on a boxing bout that never was, and never could have been. Currently bobbing and weaving around a simulated ring at the 3LD Art & Technology Center in Lower Manhattan, the production is conceived and directed by Reid Farrington, who deftly splices together video footage and live performance to offer a prismatic take on a theoretical matchup of Mike Tyson and Muhammad Ali, two of the great names in boxing history. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/08TYSON/08TYSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/08TYSON/08TYSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 323}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/08TYSON/08TYSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 551, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/08TYSON/08TYSON-