f cocaine, the second-largest drug find in Berlin in 35 years, the police said. The crates were part of a shipment of more than 1,100 boxes from Colombia to a fruit wholesaler in Berlin. Olaf Schremm, a senior police officer, told reporters that drug smugglers had probably made a “logistical error.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: $8.2 Million in Drugs Found Among Fruit', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Drugs Found Amid Fruit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-08T02:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Cottrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cottrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec395020-c5c6-5d50-820c-40c462f3c5ad', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec395020-c5c6-5d50-820c-40c462f3c5ad'}, {'abstract': 'Some players insist the $760 million proposed settlement by the N.F.L. is too small while others say that ailing former players need help now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/sports/football/doubts-linger-over-nfl-concussion-settlement.html', 'snippet': 'Some players insist the $760 million proposed settlement by the N.F.L. is too small while others say that ailing former players need help now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ink on the N.F.L.’s proposed $760 million settlement had barely dried Monday before ex-players and their lawyers started sifting through hundreds of pages for clues about how the payouts and medical benefits will be distributed and whether there will be enough money for the claims brought by some of the 18,000 retirees.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doubts Linger Over N.F.L. Concussion Settlement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doubts Linger Over N.F.L. Settlement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-08T02:22:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c2abc4b-29e2-52ad-aaaa-2dff9301d987', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c2abc4b-29e2-52ad-aaaa-2dff9301d987'}, {'abstract': 'Mónica Spear, a soap opera actress and former Miss Venezuela, and her ex-husband were killed by robbers after their car broke down, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/world/americas/venezuela-death-of-beauty-queen-in-robbery-rattles-country.html', 'snippet': 'Mónica Spear, a soap opera actress and former Miss Venezuela, and her ex-husband were killed by robbers after their car broke down, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A soap opera actress and former Miss Venezuela, Mónica Spear, was shot to death by robbers after her car broke down on a highway, the authorities said Tuesday. Her ex-husband was also killed, and their 5-year-old daughter was wounded. Venezuela has one of the highest rates of violent crime in the region, but the killing of Ms. Spear, 29, provoked a particularly sharp outcry. President Nicolás Maduro called it “a massacre.” Ms. Spear was crowned Miss Venezuela in 2004 and was a soap opera star on the Spanish-language channel Telemundo. A United States citizen, she was in Venezuela on vacation, local media reported. A police official said five suspects had been arrested. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Death of Beauty Queen in Robbery Rattles Country', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Death of Beauty Queen in Robbery Rattles Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spear, Monica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-08T02:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1bed379-2b75-506e-959c-cb79de59b28