her Provinces Against ‘Iranian Occupation’', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Falluja (Iraq)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-08T05:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b263b4e6-6f16-5c27-995c-2bc952a9fd81', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b263b4e6-6f16-5c27-995c-2bc952a9fd81'}, {'abstract': 'The Polish pianist Rafal Blechacz will be announced on Wednesday as the winner of the $300,000 Gilmore Artist Award, given every four years to an unsuspecting pianist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/arts/music/rafal-blechacz-is-chosen-for-gilmore-artist-award.html', 'snippet': 'The Polish pianist Rafal Blechacz will be announced on Wednesday as the winner of the $300,000 Gilmore Artist Award, given every four years to an unsuspecting pianist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Polish pianist Rafal Blechacz suspected nothing when, while preparing for three concerts in Switzerland in late 2012, he was bombarded with questions by the artistic director of the Lucerne Symphony Orchestra. He had no clue that a recital he gave that year in Schenectady, N.Y., was closely scrutinized and discussed and debated by a select few listeners. ', 'print_sectio