N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-08T17:55:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67e1f66e-9ce4-5f7e-b08a-fb531891a216', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67e1f66e-9ce4-5f7e-b08a-fb531891a216'}, {'abstract': 'When people look up your business on a phone, they probably are not just browsing.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/making-sure-your-website-is-ready-for-smartphones/', 'snippet': 'When people look up your business on a phone, they probably are not just browsing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About half of all mobile searches — those done on a smartphone or on a tablet — have “local intent,” meaning the person searching is looking for a nearby business. That number has risen sharply over the last five years, said Todd Leeloy, general manager of OrangeSoda, a digital marketing company in American Fork, Utah, that was bought by Deluxe in 2012.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Sure Your Website Is Ready for Smartphones', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preparing a Business Website For the Mobile Search Wave', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-08T18:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname'