s gay in an interview with the weekly Die Zeit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Thomas Hitzlsperger, a midfielder who made 52 appearances for Germany’s national team, helped Stuttgart capture the Bundesliga championship in 2007 and played for prominent teams in Germany, England and Italy, made perhaps the biggest news of his career on Wednesday by coming out as a homosexual.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/soccer/09soccer/09soccer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 877, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/soccer/09soccer/09soccer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 877}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/soccer/09soccer/09soccer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 701, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/soccer/09soccer/09soccer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1401, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/soccer/09soccer/09soccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/soccer/09soccer/09soccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/soccer/09soccer/09soccer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former German World Cup Player Comes Out as Gay', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Player Says He’s Gay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitzlsperger, Thomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-08T19:19:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/626945a1-ce12-5a4c-9c7e-6f4f3ffc2a60', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/626945a1-ce12-5a4c-9c7e-6f4f3ffc2a60'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks benefited from crisp ball movement and better team play for much of their game against the Pistons on Tuesday, but the Heat will present a tougher test Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/sports/basketball/knicks-make-progress-against-pistons-but-heat-are-a-truer-test.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks benefited from crisp ball movement and better team play for much of their game against the Pistons on Tuesday, but the Heat will present a tougher test Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For perhaps the first time this season, a sane person could argue that things are heading in the right direction for the Knicks. After winning two of three games on a trip to Texas, a swing that is usually brutal, the Knicks handled the Detroit Pistons, 89-85, at Madison Square Garden on Tuesday night, punctuating their best stretch of the season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'r