s of dollars, is selling some of his smaller prints for $100 each.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Larry Clark’s lurid portraits of teenage sex, violence and drug taking hang at the Metropolitan Museum of Art and the Museum of Modern Art, and can sell for tens of thousands of dollars. Now, Mr. Clark, as a kind of thank you to the fans who have made his bleak 1971 photography book, “Tulsa,” and his 1995 movie, “Kids,” cult classics, is offering thousands of his one-of-a-kind color snapshots for purchase at $100 apiece at an East Village art space. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/sale2/sale2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/sale2/sale2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 706}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/sale2/sale2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/sale2/sale2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 1164, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/sale2/sale2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/sale2/sale2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/sale2/sale2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge