d an impassioned attack on the visit to the Yasukuni Shrine. The shrine honors Japan’s war dead, including some convicted war criminals. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Official Criticizes Japanese Shrine Visit', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Official Criticizes Shrine Visit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Jieyi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T01:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1ce2f42-48c3-51a4-baf0-343c56b8cc90', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1ce2f42-48c3-51a4-baf0-343c56b8cc90'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Le Batard, a columnist for The Miami Herald and an ESPN host, agreed to turn his ballot over to the website Deadspin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/sports/baseball/writer-says-baseball-hall-of-fame-vote-he-gave-away-will-be-heard.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Le Batard, a columnist for The Miami Herald and an ESPN host, agreed to turn his ballot over to the website Deadspin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November, the website Deadspin opened its campaign to buy the Baseball Hall of Fame vote of a member of the Baseball Writers’ Association of America and submit its choices under his name. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Writer Gives Away Baseball Hall of Fame Vote to Deadspin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Writer Defends The Hall Vote He Gave Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Batard, Dan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deadspin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Writers Assn of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Herald', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T01:53:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6377a8c9-0349-540e-8b6b-d1382cdee3c2', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6377a8c9-0349-540e-8b6b-d1382cdee3c2'}, {'abstract': 'Deadly attacks against United Nations personnel increased last year, claiming at least 58 lives, according to the United Nations Staff Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/world/deaths-of-united-nations-personnel-rise.html', 'snippet': 'Deadly attacks against United Nations personnel increased last year, claiming at least 58 lives, according to the United Nations Staff Union.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Deadly attacks against United Nations personnel increased last year, claiming at least 58 lives, according to the United Nations Staff Union. The union said 33 of those killed were peacekeepers and 25 were civilians, including contractors working for the organization. In 2012, 37 United Nations personnel were killed, and in 2011, 36 were killed, the union said. The deadliest attack in 2013 was an ambush in Jonglei State, South Sudan, that killed 12 workers for the United Nations. According to the union, the deaths throughout the year included 16 peacekeepers killed in Darfur and seven in South Sudan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deaths of United Nations Personnel Rise', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deaths of U.N. Personnel Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Department of Peacekeeping Operations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Darfur (Sudan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T01:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah C. Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ccaa2d7-1e5c-5114-ab02-b3e0102a3a3b', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ccaa2d7-1e5c-5114-ab02-b3e0102a3a3b'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey is ‘outraged’ to learn of a traffic-jam vendetta. How about ‘accountable’?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/opinion/the-bully-was-a-dupe.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey is ‘outraged’ to learn of a traffic-jam vendetta. How about ‘accountable’?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey has explanations to make, apologies to give and an administrative house to clean now that his top aides and political cronies were shown to have been fully and gleefully aware of the chaos they caused by ordering up lane closings — and a four-day traffic jam — in September at the George Washington Bridge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bully Was a Dupe', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bully Was a Dupe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Bridget Anne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wildstein, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sokolich, Mark J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T01:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/78d46bbf-00ed-56b2-b3f6-cfa14e5a1587', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78d46bbf-00ed-56b2-b3f6-cfa14e5a1587'}, {'abstract': 'IBM says a new division, with 2,500 employees, will be devoted to the supercomputer’s so-called data analysis and recommendation technology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/technology/ibm-is-betting-that-watson-can-earn-its-keep.html', 'snippet': 'IBM says a new division, with 2,500 employees, will be devoted to the supercomputer’s so-called data analysis and recommendation technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IBM wants to build a large and profitable business from what has mostly been a triumph of computing bragging rights, so it is giving Watson $1 billion and a nice office.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IBM Is Betting That Watson Can Earn Its Keep', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'IBM Is Betting That Watson Can Earn Its Keep', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T01:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dec37c30-08b9-5ab5-82b6-97d43332ae0e', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dec37c30-08b9-5ab5-82b6-97d43332ae0e'}, {'abstract': 'An anti-tax package is the keystone of his 2014 legislative package for New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/opinion/gov-cuomo-begins-his-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'An anti-tax package is the keystone of his 2014 legislative package for New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s State of the State address on Wednesday was a campaign speech for re-election in both style and substance. Whether the policies he laid out are good for the people of New York is another matter. Mr. Cuomo proudly recounted his successes — on-time budgets, marriage equality, gun control. But the centerpiece was his plan to cut taxes by $2 billion over the next three years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gov. Cuomo Begins His Campaign', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gov. Cuomo Begins His Campaign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T02:02:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/881758c9-e396-5bb5-b717-919116f3a2ba', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/881758c9-e396-5bb5-b717-919116f3a2ba'}, {'abstract': 'The judge raised concerns that he might have to call in a fresh group of candidates on Thursday, postponing opening statements by a day.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/08/after-2-days-no-jury-for-insider-trading-case/', 'snippet': 'The judge raised concerns that he might have to call in a fresh group of candidates on Thursday, postponing opening statements by a day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a full day of questioning dozens of potential candidates in a federal courtroom in Lower Manhattan on Wednesday, lawyers still had not selected the 12-member