g that dangerous chemicals were being stored unsafely and that safety equipment and practices were lacking in at least three rooms. One was the makeshift lab where two students were engulfed in flames last week when a chemistry demonstration went horribly awry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '8 Violations for School in Wake of Lab Fire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '8 Violations for School in Wake of Lab Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beacon School (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanes, Alonzo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poole, Anna', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T04:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9129503-2e92-5a5d-8c38-6f0b4e7f36eb', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9129503-2e92-5a5d-8c38-6f0b4e7f36eb'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Kidd, who followed Mark Jackson’s footsteps into coaching, led the Nets over the red-hot Warriors Wednesday night, their most impressive victory in a four-game streak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/sports/basketball/nets-kidd-earns-win-against-warriors-and-jackson-a-coach-who-inspired-him.html', 'snippet': 'Jason Kidd, who followed Mark Jackson’s footsteps into coaching, led the Nets over the red-hot Warriors Wednesday night, their most impressive victory in a four-game streak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Golden State Warriors last visited New York, almost a year ago, Jason Kidd, then a Knicks point guard, approached Coach Mark Jackson with a handshake and a simple message: “Thanks.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/CITY-NETS/CITY-NETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/CITY-NETS/CITY-NETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/CITY-NETS/CITY-NETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/CITY-NETS/CITY-NETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/CITY-NETS/CITY-NETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/CITY-NETS/CITY-NETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/sports/CITY-NETS/CITY-NETS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets’ Kidd Earns Win Against Warriors and Jackson, a Coach Who Inspired Him', 'kicker': 'Nets 102, Warriors 98', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nets’ Kidd Earns Victory in Front of, and Against, an Inspiration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden State Warriors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidd, Jason', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Mark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T04:07:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a7daf85-80ab-5c57-a0f1-8cfb0891f032', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a7daf85-80ab-5c57-a0f1-8cfb0891f032'}, {'abstract': 'Accident investigators were unable to approach a train near the border of Maine and New Brunswick, more than 24 hours after several tank cars derailed and burst into flames.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/world/americas/fire-from-latest-derailment-rages-in-canada.html', 'snippet': 'Accident investigators were unable to approach a train near the border of Maine and New Brunswick, more than 24 hours after several tank cars derailed and burst into flames.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Accident investigators were unable to approach a train near the border of Maine and the Canadian province of New Brunswick on Wednesday, more than 24 hours after five tank cars containing crude oil and four cars filled with propane derailed and burst into flames. The accident came about five months after a runaway train carrying crude oil derailed and destroyed the downtown of Lac-Mégantic, Quebec, killing 47 people. Officials decided to let the fire from the latest accident burn itself out. This week’s derailment, on the Canadian National Railway, involved a 122-car train from Toronto and will most likely add to the current debate in Canada about transporting oil and petroleum products by train. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire From Latest Derailment Rages in Canada', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Fire From Latest Derailment Rages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Brunswick (Canada)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian National Railway Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T04:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1029737f-ec15-5420-8660-74ef3378dd73', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1029737f-ec15-5420-8660-74ef3378dd73'}, {'abstract': 'Rescue workers were astonished that Azzura’e Wilson was alive after a brutal car accident that left her paralyzed, and now she is determined to walk again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/nyregion/after-a-brush-with-death-focusing-on-the-next-step.html', 'snippet': 'Rescue workers were astonished that Azzura’e Wilson was alive after a brutal car accident that left her paralyzed, and now she is determined to walk again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The summer before her junior year of high school, Azzura’e Wilson joined her father for a road trip to Baltimore to pick up her grandmother. Like many of her peers, Azzura’e, 17, decided to share the candid moment with her friends and family on Instagram. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/nyregion/neediest/neediest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/nyregion/neediest/neediest-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1396, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/nyregion/neediest/neediest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/nyregion/neediest/neediest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images