ected to be in the hunt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/sports/baseball/masahiro-tanaka-reportedly-arrives-in-us-for-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Masahiro Tanaka, a highly regarded pitcher, has until Jan. 24 to complete a deal with a major league team, and the Yankees are expected to be in the hunt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pursuit of Masahiro Tanaka moved into a new stage as Japanese news media outlets reported that Tanaka had arrived in the United States on Wednesday to begin meeting with teams interested in signing him. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Masahiro Tanaka Reportedly Arrives in U.S. for Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tanaka Ready for Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanaka, Masahiro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tohoku Rakuten Golden Eagles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T04:46:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/797f518f-49e9-55bc-9416-5d5285bd92aa', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/797f518f-49e9-55bc-9416-5d5285bd92aa'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Porcino held the first trumpet chair in bands led by Count Basie, Woody Herman, Stan Kenton, Buddy Rich and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/arts/music/al-porcino-king-of-the-high-notes-on-jazz-trumpet-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Porcino held the first trumpet chair in bands led by Count Basie, Woody Herman, Stan Kenton, Buddy Rich and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Porcino, whose powerful sound and ability to hit the highest of high notes with ease brought him work as the lead trumpeter in some of the most celebrated big bands in jazz, died on Dec. 31 in Munich. He was 88. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/PORCINO-obit-web/PORCINO-obit-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/PORCINO-obit-web/PORCINO-obit-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/PORCINO-obit-web/PORCINO-obit-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/PORCINO-obit-web/PORCINO-obit-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 1336, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/PORCINO-obit-web/PORCINO-obit-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/PORCINO-obit-web/PORCINO-obit-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/arts/PORCINO-obit-web/PORCINO-obit-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Porcino, First Trumpeter With Leading Jazz Bands, Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Al Porcino, 88, Big-Band Trumpet Virtuoso', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keepnews, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porcino, Al (1925-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T04:56:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Keepnews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keepnews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf57e936-6553-5cad-b183-a7fab2cf0b5a', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf57e936-6553-5cad-b183-a7fab2cf0b5a'}, {'abstract': 'The sporty, all-American, college prep look abounds just in time for the Super Bowl next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/t-magazine/varsity-blues-and-reds.html', 'snippet': 'The sporty, all-American, college prep look abounds just in time for the Super Bowl next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A heavy dose of sporty prep is scoring big in resort collections. Oversize varsity letters, all-American shades of blue and red and pleated miniskirts are at the forefront of the trend. From Charlotte Olympia’s “Team Spirit” suede sandals, complete with a shiny pompom and large “CO” monogram, to Equipment’s collegiate sweater similarly emblazoned with the brand’s initial, the alumni-weekend style is not just for nostalgic coeds. And to bring it all together, simple stripes nod to standard-issue cheerleading uniforms and letterman jackets — just in time for the Super Bowl next month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09market-barsamian/09market-barsamian-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09market-barsamian/09market-barsamian-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09market-barsamian/09market-barsamian-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09market-barsamian/09market-barsamian-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09market-barsamian/09market-barsamian-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09market-barsamian/09market-barsamian-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09market-barsamian/09market-barsamian-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Varsity Blues (and Reds)', 'kicker': 'Market Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'na