for minority students and also presents an annual orchestral concert at Carnegie Hall, has received a $4 million gift from an anonymous donor, its executive and artistic director, Afa S. Dworkin, said on Wednesday. The gift is expected to be announced formally on Thursday. Ms. Dworkin said in an email that the gift would allow the organization to augment its “professional, career development and educational pursuits by launching scholarships at pre-college, collegiate and post-graduate levels.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A $4 Million Gift for Sphinx Organization', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sphinx Organization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T05:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4ee3eb9-50e0-5ca2-a9bf-dba512dac61c', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4ee3eb9-50e0-5ca2-a9bf-dba512dac61c'}, {'abstract': 'As the Yellen era at the Federal Reserve approaches, there are signs that top officials are prepared to take a tougher stand on reining in large, complex financial institutions, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/the-fed-shifts-ground-on-big-banks/', 'snippet': 'As the Yellen era at the Federal Reserve approaches, there are signs that top officials are prepared to take a tougher stand on reining in large, complex financial institutions, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, former chief economist of the Internati