ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Dobbs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dobbs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/916d17a8-8052-550c-ab1b-4bafd185ea86', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/916d17a8-8052-550c-ab1b-4bafd185ea86'}, {'abstract': 'BlackRock has agreed to stop pursuing nonpublic views through analyst surveys. | No Jury has been selected yet for the insider trading trial of a former SAC trader. | 2013 was a banner year for boutique and independent investment banks. | @GSElevator is writing a book.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/morning-agenda-blackrock-ends-early-surveys/', 'snippet': 'BlackRock has agreed to stop pursuing nonpublic views through analyst surveys. | No Jury has been selected yet for the insider trading trial of a former SAC trader. | 2013 was a banner year for boutique and independent investment banks. | @GSEleva...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For almost five years, BlackRock, the world’s largest asset manager, has been surveying Wall Street analysts to extract clues about their views on companies before the outlooks were announced publicly. Now, the tactic has been shut down, Gretchen Morgenson reports in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BlackRock Ends Early Surveys', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T12:55:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6211da1a-b09c-5fe5-82a7-5044b93dbb4d', 'word_count': 1787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6211da1a-b09c-5fe5-82a7-5044b93dbb4d'}, {'abstract': 'Flooding theaters isn’t good for filmmakers or filmgoers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/movies/flooding-theaters-isnt-good-for-filmmakers-or-filmgoers.html', 'snippet': 'Flooding theaters isn’t good for filmmakers or filmgoers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 16, some 7,000 entertainment industry professionals and journalists will converge on Park City, Utah, hoping for a miracle. Distributors will push past exhibitors who will hustle past programmers, agents and critics, all of whom will be sifting through 117 features and 66 shorts at the Sundance Film Festival, looking for the next big thing: for the new Jennifer Lawrence (class of 2010 with “Winter’s Bone”) or for another “Beasts of the Southern Wild,""Fruitvale Station” or “Upstream Color,” three of the most talked-about titles from recent festivals. It will be exciting, exhausting and at times exasperating to be in the thick of such coordinated madness.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Indies Explode, an Appeal for Sanity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Indies Explode, An Appeal For Sanity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T13:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b2b2c7f-63f5-5920-9c9a-49e3f9449054', 'word_count': 1926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b2b2c7f-63f5-5920-9c9a-49e3f9449054'}, {'abstract': 'A casual survey of film veterans reveals wide differences in assessments of the state of indie cinema.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/so-many-indie-films-so-many-reasons/', 'snippet': 'A casual survey of film veterans reveals wide differences in assessments of the state of indie cinema.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With nearly 900 films released in New York theaters last year, Manohla Dargis argues that there are too many lackluster, forgettable and just plain bad movies pouring into theaters. Is flooding theaters — especially with indie releases — good for movies and moviegoers alike? With another edition of the Sundance Film Festival about to start next week, she took a casual survey of some 70 film professionals, asking them about the state of indie film. Here is a sampling of their answers, edited and condensed:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/darlings/darlings-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/darlings/darlings-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/darlings/darlings-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/darlings/darlings-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/darlings/darlings-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/darlings/darlings-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/08/arts/darlings/darlings-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Many Indie Films, So Many Reasons', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Karen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deutchman, Ira', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hope, Ted', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powers, Thom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sehring, Jonathan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vachon, Christine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d69bee4-acda-51b6-9f57-3cac2e5f608d', 'word_count': 1416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d69bee4-acda-51b6-9f57-3cac2e5f608d'}, {'abstract': 'The European Central Bank’s president said he would “consider all available instruments” if the threat of deflation persists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/business/international/ecb-holds-rates-at-record-low-as-deflation-fears-persist.html', 'snippet': 'The European Central Bank’s president said he would “consider all availab