m his drama with Judi Dench and Steve Coogan.', 'lead_paragraph': '“If you make a film in Washington, you do what Frank Capra did,” the director Stephen Frears explained. He was talking about a Lincoln Memorial scene in his drama “Philomena,” which received Golden Globe nods for best picture, screenplay and actress in a drama (Judi Dench). Based on a true story, it follows the title character on her search for the son she was forced to give up when she was a teenager living in a Roman Catholic home for unwed mothers in Ireland. In this scene she visits Washington with the journalist Martin Sixsmith (Steve Coogan). Mr. Frears commented on the scene and what was required to shoot in the nation’s capital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene: Video of ‘Philomena’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coogan, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dench, Judi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frears, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T13:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a33650e3-bdbc-5564-a503-e0ea0b51ec5c', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a33650e3-bdbc-5564-a503-e0ea0b51ec5c'}, {'abstract': 'The charismatic frontwoman of the Dap-Kings has lost her trademark braids, but none of her charisma. Here, she reflects on conquering the disease.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/q-a-months-after-beating-cancer-sharon-jones-is-back-on-the-road/', 'snippet': 'The charismatic frontwoman of the Dap-Kings has lost her trademark braids, but none of her charisma. Here, she reflects on conquering the disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sharon Jones is a whirlwind performer. In concert, the energetic soul singer is known for whipping her braids across her face and darting about the stage while her backing band, the Dap-Kings, swings in the shadows. But Jones’s braids are gone now. After the 57-year-old was diagnosed last year with bile duct cancer, chemotherapy claimed her locks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09jones-hyman/09jones-hyman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09jones-hyman/09jones-hyman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09jones-hyman/09jones-hyman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09jones-hyman/09jones-hyman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09jones-hyman/09jones-hyman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/t-magazine/09jones-hyman/09jone