wirling political drama, Gov. Chris Christie tried on Thursday to control the damage from revelations that his administration ordered the revenge-closings of traffic lanes at the George Washington Bridge by firing a top aide, cutting ties with a longtime political adviser and repeatedly apologizing in a nearly two-hour news conference. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/nyregion/Christie/Christie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/10/nyregion/Christie/Christie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/nyregion/Christie/Christie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/nyregion/Christie/Christie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1271, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/nyregion/Christie/Christie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/10/nyregion/Christie/Christie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/nyregion/Christie/Christie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Very Sad’ Chris Christie Extends Apology in Bridge Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Very Sad’ Christie Extends Apology in Bridge Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zernike, Kate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baroni, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Bridget Anne', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wildstein, David', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T14:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike and Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31d24aa0-c0ac-569a-bd01-d2ae650079a4', 'word_count': 1515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31d24aa0-c0ac-569a-bd01-d2ae650079a4'}, {'abstract': 'Delhi residents are enthusiastic about a new initiative to help them catch corrupt government officials, but lawyers have mixed opinions.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/legal-experts-weigh-in-on-citizen-sting-operations/', 'snippet': 'Delhi residents are enthusiastic about a new initiative to help them catch corrupt government officials, but lawyers have mixed opinions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI\xa0 — When Delhi’s chief minister, Arvind Kejriwal, announced on Wednesday evening that he had created a hotline to help citizens use their phones to conduct sting operations on corrupt state officials, the response from the public was immediate: nearly 4,000 calls poured in by 3 p.m. Thursday, Mr. Kejriwal said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 507}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 866, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1731, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/09/world/asia/09-kejriwal-IndiaInk/09-kejr