e said.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/09/no-comment-necessary-whoops-my-gun-fired/', 'snippet': 'A Kentucky lawmaker accidentally fired her gun in her office. “It happens,” she said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kentucky State Rep. Leslie Combs brought her Ruger 380 semi-automatic handgun to her office in the Capitol Annex on Tuesday. Nothing unusual about that: She often carries the weapon in her purse. But here’s the thing: She accidentally fired it. Whoops. “I’m a gun owner. It happens,” she said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Comment Necessary: Whoops, My Gun Fired', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T15:01:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcb0b763-6b90-5fc8-a7db-05d5f8accbf4', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcb0b763-6b90-5fc8-a7db-05d5f8accbf4'}, {'abstract': 'In an age when solitary TV and movie viewing is easier all the time, some couples meet remotely to share their entertainment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/arts/television/for-couples-split-by-distance-two-screens-can-blink-as-one.html', 'snippet': 'In an age when solitary TV and movie viewing is easier all the time, some couples meet remotely to share their entertainment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FAR-FLUNG lovers once took solace in sharing the same big sky. Now they take it in sharing the little screen. They count down — 3, 2, 1 — to begin “Breaking Bad” at the same second. While Facebook-messaging about it on another slice of the laptop screen. While glimpsing each other’s faces on