dd939', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb109c48-1d9e-59ef-b256-f574885dd939'}, {'abstract': 'Sunday afternoon with the funnies: retro comic strips can make a comeback in a digital world, with new collections published as books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/books/sunday-comics-glory-days-from-dark-horse-fantagraphics.html', 'snippet': 'Sunday afternoon with the funnies: retro comic strips can make a comeback in a digital world, with new collections published as books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE of the simple yet durable cultural traditions of the 20th century — a modest rite that transcended barriers of race and class — was the Sunday morning or afternoon spent lost in the newspaper funnies. There was always something for everyone: “Flash Gordon,” “Prince Valiant” and “Terry and the Pirates” for those craving pulpy adventure; “Archie” and “Peanuts” for laughs and chuckles; “Gasoline Alley” and “Blondie” for family life; and “Krazy Kat” and “Pogo” for the comic-strip intelligentsia.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10COMICS2/10COMICS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10COMICS2/10COMICS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10COMICS2/10COMICS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10COMICS2/10COMICS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'cap