 Washington to make a portrait of Google’s founders, Sergey Brin and Larry Page, he elegantly co-opted Google’s own technology for the job.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portraits From Clips and Bytes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Portraits From Clips and Bytes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheets, Hilarie M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DuBois, R Luke', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ringling, John and Mable, Museum of Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T20:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilarie M. Sheets', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/802d8fd5-99ad-58e7-806a-d4f7554f75e5', 'word_count': 1384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/802d8fd5-99ad-58e7-806a-d4f7554f75e5'}, {'abstract': 'The experimental designer and director Jay Scheib is offering audiences two ways to view his raucous contemporary rewrite of an unfinished early Chekhov play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/theater/platonov-or-the-disinherited-at-the-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'The experimental designer and director Jay Scheib is offering audiences two ways to view his raucous contemporary rewrite of an unfinished early Chekhov play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The experimental designer and director Jay Scheib is offering audiences two ways to view his raucous contemporary rewrite of an unfinished early Chekhov play. You can see a live performance at the Kitchen in Chelsea, where it is called “Platonov,” the play’s traditional title, or you can watch a live simulcast of the performance at one of several theaters in New York and elsewhere, where it goes by another name, “The Disinherited.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10SUBPLATO_SPAN/10SUBPLATO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10SUBPLATO_SPAN/10SUBPLATO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10SUBPLATO_SPAN/10SUBPLATO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10SUBPLATO_SPAN/10SUBPLATO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10SUBPLATO_SPAN/10SUBPLATO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10SUBPLATO_SPAN/10SUBPLATO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10SUBPLATO_SPAN/10SUBPLATO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Chekhov, Framed Anew', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_ki