the artist’s work and his relationship with his friend Piet Mondrian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/nyregion/a-review-of-harry-holtzman-and-american-abstraction-at-the-florence-griswold-museum.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition of Harry Holtzman’s paintings, sculptures and drawings tells the story of the artist’s work and his relationship with his friend Piet Mondrian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can tell by the primary colors and rectilinear grids in Harry Holtzman’s paintings and sculptures that the artist was a disciple of Piet Mondrian, the Dutch founder of Neoplasticism, an aesthetic philosophy that sought spiritual balance through simplified formal structure. Mondrian’s legacy in the United States is even owed in large part to Holtzman, who was 40 years younger and became the sole heir to and executor of his estate. The story of Holtzman’s work and their relationship, however, has been largely left untold. “Harry Holtzman and American Abstraction” at the Florence Griswold Museum in Old Lyme, Conn., offers a thorough and thoughtful recounting of that history.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ARTSCT1_SPAN/12ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ARTSCT1_SPAN/12ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ARTSCT1_SPAN/12ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ARTSCT1_SPAN/12ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 