e, 'lastname': 'Nazaryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a644fa6a-7641-5fde-a708-272f57264c92', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a644fa6a-7641-5fde-a708-272f57264c92'}, {'abstract': 'The president said that federal agencies will cut through red tape to give struggling residents a chance at a better life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/us/politics/obama-announces-promise-zones-in-5-stricken-areas.html', 'snippet': 'The president said that federal agencies will cut through red tape to give struggling residents a chance at a better life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A year after promising to direct federal attention and support to needy areas across the country, President Obama said Thursday that the government would begin helping five economically hard-hit communities fight poverty and assist children.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/us/PROMISE/PROMISE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/10/us/PROMISE/PROMISE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/us/PROMISE/PROMISE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/us/PROMISE/PROMISE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/us/PROMISE/PROMISE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/10/us/PROMISE/PROMISE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/us/PROMISE/PROMISE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Announces ‘Promise Zones’ in 5 Poor Areas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Announces ‘Promise Zones’ in 5 Poor Areas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Antonio (Tex)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T22:31:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dcbfc06-8767-5664-b153-7bf093389ad5', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dcbfc06-8767-5664-b153-7bf093389ad5'}, {'abstract': '“Cold Comes the Night” pits a young motel owner against a criminal who takes her and her daughter hostage to recover a fortune in cash.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/movies/cold-comes-the-night-starring-bryan-cranston-and-alice-eve.html', 'snippet': '“Cold Comes the Night” pits a young motel owner against a criminal who takes her and her daughter hostage to recover a fortune in cash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s more mystery in the grammatically anguished title of “Cold Comes the Night” than in this low-voltage thriller, which asks you to guess, if not for long or terribly hard, which is the tougher of two combatants: a young and lovely single mother or a Polish criminal. In one corner is Chloe (Alice Eve), a hardworking, hard-bitten beauty who runs and lives in one of those motels that rent rooms by the hour. In the other corner is Topo (Bryan Cranston), a very bad man who stops at the motel one evening — the presumably cold night of the title (she puts on a parka) — a stopover that leads to a face-off that ends pretty much how you might guess.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s Hard as Nails, He’s Noir and Nasty', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She’s Hard as Nails, He’s Noir and Nasty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cranston, Bryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall-Green, Logan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eve, Alice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chun, Tze', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Cold Comes the Night (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T22:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7106a60b-7344-511e-b2b5-e794f4499831', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7106a60b-7344-511e-b2b5-e794f4499831'}, {'abstract': 'Notable offerings at K60 Japanese Steak House, which has a lively hibachi room and a quiet sushi bar, include steak teriyaki and an arrangement of sliced white tuna.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/nyregion/a-review-of-k60-japanese-steak-house-in-lake-grove.html', 'snippet': 'Notable offerings at K60 Japanese Steak House, which has a lively hibachi room and a quiet sushi bar, include steak teriyaki and an arrangement of sliced white tuna.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing to know about K60 Japanese Steak House is that this sprawling, neon-trimmed restaurant in a Lake Grove strip mall offers two entirely different dining experiences. The most popular, by far, is the raucous hibachi room, where flames leap, diners cheer (or cringe), servers scurry and impassioned chefs jump, juggle, chop and grill, all beneath the nonstop whoosh of overhead exhaust fans. And there is the adjacent, far quieter “sushi room,” as a hostess called it on a recent evening, with its sleek, sparsely populated tables and booths, serene sushi bar and attentive servers.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12DINELI2/12DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12DINELI2/12DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12DINELI2/12DINELI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': '