MW and Bosch. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking for the Hands-Free Driving Experience', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-09T22:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ba536c2-d613-596c-a6c7-2cfb72e2668e', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ba536c2-d613-596c-a6c7-2cfb72e2668e'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Urie and his partner, Ryan Spahn, live on the Far West Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/realestate/the-good-the-bad-and-the-ugly-betty.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Urie and his partner, Ryan Spahn, live on the Far West Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Michael Urie was cast in 2006 as Vanessa Williams’s slavishly devoted assistant on the television series “Ugly Betty,” it meant a move to Los Angeles. Relocating is an actor’s lot, of course, but Mr. Urie desperately missed New York. Clever guy, he came up with an effective treatment for homesickness: the purchase of an apartment in a very tall building. “Anytime friends came over,” he recalled, “they said, ‘This is just like home.’\xa0” ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/realestate/20140112-LOVE-slide-OG17/20140112-LOVE-slide-OG17-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarg