y credibility, he will have to admit that he set a tone of vindictiveness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey issued repeated apologies Thursday for the abuse of office that now threatens to undermine his political future. Though he sounded remorseful — and clearly sorry that this scandal might sink his ambitions for national office — he blamed his staff for making him a victim. Unbeknown to him, he said, they shut down lanes to the George Washington Bridge to create a four-day traffic jam to punish a local mayor who failed to endorse him in last year’s election. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Chris Christie’s Performance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Chris Christie’s Performance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sokolich, Mark J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Bridget Anne', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baroni, Bill', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wildstein, David', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T02:24:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_m