rticle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/830e1a33-9863-5a43-b7fd-4e01244de165', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/830e1a33-9863-5a43-b7fd-4e01244de165'}, {'abstract': 'In December, employers added just 74,000 jobs, the slowest pace of growth in three years and far below the expectations of many economists who had grown convinced that the market was on a more solid footing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/business/economy/us-economy-added-only-74000-jobs-in-december.html', 'snippet': 'In December, employers added just 74,000 jobs, the slowest pace of growth in three years and far below the expectations of many economists who had grown convinced that the market was on a more solid footing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just when it seemed as if the economy was finally accelerating, the latest employment figures once again confounded expectations of better days ahead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/business/11jobspic/11jobspic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/business/11jobspic/11jobspic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/business/11jobspic/11jobspic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/business/11jobspic/11jobspic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/business/11jobspic/11jobspic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/business/11jobspic/11jobspic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/business/11jobspic/11jobspic-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Growth in Jobs Slows Sharply to 3-Year Low', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growth in Jobs Slows Sharply To 3-Year Low', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Nelson D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T13:38:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef884cc5-b945-53a5-a4ac-962eaa67b03e', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef884cc5-b945-53a5-a4ac-962eaa67b03e'}, {'abstract': 'Fines for banks’ role in mortgage crisis could total nearly $50 billion, not including JPMorgan’s settlement. | Ex-SAC trader falsified grades at Harvard. | A storied Washington law firm looks to merge. | Snapchat says sorry.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/morning-agenda-banks-brace-for-reckoning/', 'snippet': 'Fines for banks’ role in mortgage crisis could total nearly $50 billion, not including JPMorgan’s settlement. | Ex-SAC trader falsified grades at Harvard. | A storied Washington law firm looks to merge. | Snapchat says sorry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the dust has settled on investigations into the role of banks in the mortgage crisis, fines could total nearly $50 billion, and that does not include the $13 billion that JPMorgan Chase agreed to pay, Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Peter Eavis report in DealBook. Put into context, the $50 billion would equal roughly half the total annual profit of large American banks in 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Brace for Reckoning', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T13:58:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97f8f2db-b11e-52e9-b7bb-20b25aa1087d', 'word_count': 1708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97f8f2db-b11e-52e9-b7bb-20b25aa1087d'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch artist crafted expressionistic, wearable art inspired by Native American tradition for the performance troupe’s new work, “Cry, Trojans!”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/the-making-of-folkert-de-jongs-synthetic-sculptural-costumes-for-the-wooster-group/', 'snippet': 'The Dutch artist crafted expressionistic, wearable art inspired by Native American tradition for the performance troupe’s new work, “Cry, Trojans!”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past decade, the Dutch artist Folkert de Jong has gained international recognition for eerily beautiful figurative sculptures made from materials like plastic, polyurethane and bronze. He’s shown at biennales in Sydney and Kiev, is in the permanent collection at the\xa0Los Angeles County Museum of Art, has a show through early April at Antwerp’s Middelheim Museum and will have his work on exhibit this year at the Armory Show and at\xa0James Cohan Gallery. He also has upcoming solo shows in Paris, Milan and Wakefield, England.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making Of | Folkert de Jong’s Synthetic, Sculptural Costumes for the Wooster Group', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wooster Group', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T14:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c1eb0b1-c1a1-57c1-8f06-978fc5a91d59', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c1eb0b1-c1a1-57c1-8f06-978fc5a91d59'}, {'abstract': 'As 300,000 people learned that their tap water was unsafe, residents and businesses expressed a mix of anger and anxiety in coping with the industrial accident.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/us/west-virginia-chemical-spill.html', 'snippet': 'As 300,000 people learned that their tap water was unsafe, residents and businesses expressed a mix of anger and anxiety in coping with the industrial accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, W.Va. — As 300,000 people awoke on Friday to learn that their tap water was unsafe for brushing teeth, brewing coffee or showering, residents and businesses expressed a mix of anger and anxiety in coping with an industrial accident with no clear end in sight. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/us/WVIRGINIA-2/WVIRGINIA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/us/WVIRGINIA-2/WVIRGINIA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/us/WVIRGINIA-2/WVIRGINIA-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/us/WVIRGINIA-2/WVIRGINIA-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/us/WVIRGINIA-2/WVIRGINIA-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/us/WVIRGINIA-2/WVIRGINIA-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/us/WVIRGINIA-2/WVIRGINIA-2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thousands Without Water After Spill in West Virginia', 'kicker': None, 'c