icle', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris and Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93202ea5-ab14-5eb3-8270-5a1e92024c3e', 'word_count': 1348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93202ea5-ab14-5eb3-8270-5a1e92024c3e'}, {'abstract': 'Boris Okuliar, recently a managing director at UBS, is joining Carlyle as head of capital markets in the firm’s global market strategies group. Carlyle is best known for private equity deals, but its market strategies business is also a major focus.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/carlyle-hires-ubs-executive-for-market-strategies-group/', 'snippet': 'Boris Okuliar, recently a managing director at UBS, is joining Carlyle as head of capital markets in the firm’s global market strategies group. Carlyle is best known for private equity deals, but its market strategies business is also a major focu...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carlyle Group, the big alternative investment firm based in Washington, has hired a UBS executive to bolster its capital markets expertise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle Hires UBS Executive for Market Strategies Group', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okuliar, Boris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group LP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T14:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dff588b-8784-595d-9a2c-247e5ab9efd8', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dff588b-8784-595d-9a2c-247e5ab9efd8'}, {'abstract': 'Looking for experienced parents who know how to keep a sedentary teenager moving year round.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/how-do-you-motivate-your-teenager-to-get-moving-in-the-cold/', 'snippet': 'Looking for experienced parents who know how to keep a sedentary teenager moving year round.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the polar vortex had you hibernating, how has it affected your teenager? The open discussion on the New Parent, Old Parent collaboration between Motherlode and Booming is how to get a teen who is disinclined toward activity to get moving, especially in the winter when outdoor fun may be less appealing. I asked parents who have successfully nudged a less-than-enthusiastic teenager out of the house and into exercise to weigh in. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Motivate Your Teenager to Get Moving in the Cold?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T14:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a2d32ed-8e87-5d3a-98f7-88a69f15ed58', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a2d32ed-8e87-5d3a-98f7-88a69f15ed58'}, {'abstract': 'Since a big drop after the recession, the share of American with jobs has failed to rebound, and was no higher in 2013 than the previous year.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/the-employment-rates-new-normal/', 'snippet': 'Since a big drop after the recession, the share of American with jobs has failed to rebound, and was no higher in 2013 than the previous year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The share of Americans with jobs did not increase in 2013. The economy added about 182,000 jobs a month, just enough to keep pace with population growth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Employment Rate’s New Normal', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T14:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a29f02-dc23-577e-8e24-1263daa2fd28', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a29f02-dc23-577e-8e24-1263daa2fd28'}, {'abstract': 'The musician says the film lacks the optimism that she recalls from the folk scene.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/suzanne-vega-has-her-own-issues-with-llewyn-davis/', 'snippet': 'The musician says the film lacks the optimism that she recalls from the folk scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The irate folkies – a group that actually exists – will be paying close attention to how “Inside Llewyn Davis” fares at the Golden Globes on Sunday, and on the awards circuit beyond. “My hunch is that if the film gets a bunch of Oscar noms — especially if it gets a nom for best picture — the dust-up won’t go away,” wrote Christine Lavin, the singer-songwriter who has been on a mission to clarify some things about what she believes the Coen brothers’ portrait of the 1960s Greenwich Village folk scene got wrong. “Maybe it will become a haboob?” she added. “Love that word.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/vega/vega-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/vega/vega-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 904}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/vega/vega-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/vega/vega-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/vega/vega-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/vega/vega-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/vega/vega-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 's