l': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2d92e45-bbcf-5296-894f-edeeefb34b81', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2d92e45-bbcf-5296-894f-edeeefb34b81'}, {'abstract': 'In an English-language interview with the British Broadcasting Corporation on Friday, the Egyptian puppet recently accused of acting as a terrorist mouthpiece protested her innocence.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/paranoia-is-the-mother-in-law-of-invention-puppet-accused-of-terror-in-egypt-tells-bbc/', 'snippet': 'In an English-language interview with the British Broadcasting Corporation on Friday, the Egyptian puppet recently accused of acting as a terrorist mouthpiece protested her innocence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an English-language interview with the BBC on Friday, the Egyptian puppet recently accused of acting as a terrorist mouthpiece protested her innocence. The puppet, Abla Fahita, rejected allegations from a pro-military blogger that unseen hands had manipulated her into sending coded instructions to Islamist terrorists during an ad for a phone company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Paranoia Is the Mother-in-Law of Invention,’ Puppet Accused of Terror in Egypt Tells BBC', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puppets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T15:39:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8af306c9-20cc-5a6b-96f9-9738b993d931', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8af306c9-20cc-5a6b-96f9-9738b993d931'}, {'abstract': 'With the share of Americans in the labor force at a low, the challenge is sorting out how many are shuffling into retirement and how many have abandoned hope of finding jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/debating-why-the-work-force-is-shrinking/', 'snippet': 'With the share of Americans in the labor force at a low, the challenge is sorting out how many are shuffling into retirement and how many have abandoned hope of finding jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People keep leaving the labor force. The share of Americans either working or looking for work sank to 62.8 percent in December, tying October for the lowest level since 1977 – an era when women were much less likely to work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debating Why the Work Force Is Shrinking', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T16:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3f7f246-8894-5888-8426-03ac802f2c75', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3f7f246-8894-5888-8426-03ac802f2c75'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KURT VONNEGUT: Letters,  edited by Dan Wakefield. (Dial, $20.) Written over a 60-year period, these letters display all the hallmarks of Vonnegut’s fiction — smart, hilarious and heartbreaking. It includes chilling descriptions of the Allied firebombing of Dresden and Vonnegut’s time as a P.O.W.; wry dispatches from his years as a struggling writer; and words of commiseration and encouragement to contemporaries like Norman Mailer and Bernard Malamud.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T16:10:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fd41e8d-e841-5187-9a8d-0a49234c5034', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fd41e8d-e841-5187-9a8d-0a49234c5034'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON SUCH A FULL SEA,  by Chang-rae Lee. (Riverhead, $27.95.) Lee abandons realist fiction in this marvelous dystopian fantasy, set in an almost familiar future world. But he continues to grapple with themes of hope and betrayal.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Editor's Choice | Recent books of particular interest", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T16:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/89c64c28-4c93-5a8e-b73b-f433ff83751a', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89c64c28-4c93-5a8e-b73b-f433ff83751a'}, {'abstract': 'The International Kite Festival in Dhordo, Gujarat.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/image-of-the-day-january-10-2/', 'snippet': 'The International Kite Festival in Dhordo, Gujarat.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/world/asia/10-pod-kite-IndiaInk/10-pod-kite-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/10/world/asia/10-pod-kite-IndiaInk/10-pod-kite-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/world/asia/10-pod-kite-IndiaInk/10-pod-kite-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0