els.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Len Vlahos’s debut novel, the Scar Boys are a punk band from Yonkers that hits the road riding a rusty van and working out personal problems while playing gigs in college towns as far south as Georgia. “Music to the rescue,” muses Harry, the book’s narrator. Playing and touring demand creativity and commitment, forcing the Scar Boys — actually three guys and a girl — to come of age in this wry, stylish tale.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hitting the Road', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hitting the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohr, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herrndorf, Wolfgang', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vlahos, Len', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T16:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Behrens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Behrens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/15f15e5c-f1b2-5caa-a537-a16ff895546f', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15f15e5c-f1b2-5caa-a537-a16ff895546f'}, {'abstract': 'In poetry and prose, these books shed light on the fascinating, complicated lives of our commanders in chief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/books/review/maira-kalmans-thomas-jefferson-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'In poetry and prose, these books shed light on the fascinating, complicated lives of our commanders in chief.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Away back in my childhood, the earliest days of my being able to read,” Abraham Lincoln nostalgically remembered on the eve of his first inauguration, “I got hold of a small book. . . . Weems’ ‘Life of Washington.’ ” The future president never forgot its vivid accounts of the battles and heroes of the Revolutionary War, not to mention the causes for which the founders fought. “I recollect thinking then, boy even though I was,” he reminisced, “that there must have been something more than common that those men struggled for.” The book’s stories “fixed themselves on my memory,” he proudly added, acknowledging that “these early impressions last longer than any others.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/books/review/0112-bks-Holzer-1/0112-bks-Holzer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/books/review/0112-bks-Holzer-1/0112-bks-Holzer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 732}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/books/review/0112-bks-Holzer-1/0112-bks-Holzer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 840, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/books/review/0112-bks-Holzer-1/0112-bks-Holzer-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/books/review/0112-bks-Holzer-1/0112-bks-Holzer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/books/review/0112-bks-Holzer-1/0112-