re significant new shows than ever this year, starting this weekend with HBO’s “True Detective” and including that network’s “Looking”; Fox’s Greg Kinnear vehicle, “Rake”; Sundance’s “Red Road”; and USA’s “Sirens,” from Denis Leary. But the big news is likely to be made by the shows that are coming back: “The Following” on Fox, “The Americans” on FX, Netflix’s “House of Cards” and, perhaps best of all, the long-awaited third season of “Sherlock” on PBS.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12HALE1_SPAN/12HALE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12HALE1_SPAN/12HALE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12HALE1_SPAN/12HALE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12HALE1_SPAN/12HALE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12HALE1_SPAN/12HALE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12HALE1_SPAN/12HALE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12HALE1_SPAN/12HALE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Detecting a New Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detecting a New Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T16:58:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eda652f-fe9e-53b1-9070-d9034a9dc9d9', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eda652f-fe9e-53b1-9070-d9034a9dc9d9'}, {'abstract': 'The decision furthered President Obama’s self-described evolution on same-sex marriage rights as his administration appeared closer to confronting a state over its refusal to recognize such rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/us/politics/same-sex-marriage-utah.html', 'snippet': 'The decision furthered President Obama’s self-described evolution on same-sex marriage rights as his administration appeared closer to confronting a state over its refusal to recognize such rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration on Friday made the latest contribution to a fast-moving legal battle over same-sex marriage rights as the Justice Department said that the federal government would recognize as lawful the marriages of some 1,300 same-sex couples in Utah even though the state government is largely refusing to do so. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. to Recognize 1,300 Marriages Disputed by Utah', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. to Recognize 1,300 Marriages Disputed by Utah', 'name': None, 'seo'