 design of a new building for the Vancouver Art Gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/husband-and-wife-architecture-firms-compete-for-vancouver-commission/', 'snippet': 'After being at odds of the Museum of Modern Art’s renovation plan, the firms of Diller Scofidio + Renfro and Tod Williams Billie Tsien Architects are finalists for the design of a new building for the Vancouver Art Gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As they find themselves at odds over the Museum of Modern Art’s renovation announced this week, the architecture firms Diller Scofidio + Renfro and Tod Williams Billie Tsien Architects now also find themselves competing over a new commission. (Elizabeth Diller and Ricardo Scofidio are married to each other, as are Mr. Williams and Ms. Tsien.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Husband-and-Wife Architecture Firms Compete for Vancouver Commission', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scofidio, Ricardo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsien, Billie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Tod', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diller Scofidio & Renfro', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herzog & de Meuron', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanaa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Art Gallery', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T17:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/857c1554-e92e-54e9-adec-5c13977377a2', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/857c1554-e92e-54e9-adec-5c13977377a2'}, {'abstract': 'The French council that oversees broadcasting standards has decided that videos by Miley Cyrus and Britney Spears are too racy for daytime viewing.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/on-french-tv-no-twerking-before-10/', 'snippet': 'The French council that oversees broadcasting standards has decided that videos by Miley Cyrus and Britney Spears are too racy for daytime viewing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those French – they can be such prudes. The Conseil Superieur de l’Audiovisuel, the body that oversees French broadcasting standards, has decided that the promotional video clips for Miley Cyrus’s “Wrecking Ball” and Britney Spears’s “Work Bitch” should be effectively banished from daytime and early evening television in France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10artsbeat-miley/10artsbeat-miley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10artsbeat-miley/10artsbeat-miley-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 908}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10artsbeat-miley/10artsbeat-miley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/10/arts/10artsbeat-miley/10artsbeat-miley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1203, 'width': 795, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}},