he Town Hall, in a concert involving roughly 20 ensembles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Zorn, the tirelessly prolific composer, organizer and genre-scrambler, will throw open the doors to yet another wing of his rambling musical estate this spring, with the premiere of “John Zorn’s Masada Book Three: The Book Beriah.” The work will be presented on March 19 at the Town Hall, in a concert involving roughly 20 ensembles, including the Masada String Trio, the Jamie Saft Trio, Fieldwork and Secret Chiefs 3. Mr. Zorn is scheduled to perform on alto saxophone with Aleph Trio, which includes Shanir Blumenkranz on bass and Ches Smith on drums. Tickets will be available on Monday through Ticketmaster and the Town Hall box office.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Zorn to Present Latest Installment in His Masada Project', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zorn to Expand His Masada Project', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caine, Uri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metheny, Pat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zorn, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stone, The (Manhattan, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ticketmaster', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Town Hall (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T17:38:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da3