rson': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea0065e1-49aa-576d-994b-de04f9af470d', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea0065e1-49aa-576d-994b-de04f9af470d'}, {'abstract': 'Half of all capital raised for private equity buyouts in 2013 went to the biggest funds, according to data released on Friday by Preqin, a research firm based in London. It was the first time since 2008 that megafunds have commanded half the market.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/money-flows-to-the-biggest-buyout-funds/', 'snippet': 'Half of all capital raised for private equity buyouts in 2013 went to the biggest funds, according to data released on Friday by Preqin, a research firm based in London. It was the first time since 2008 that megafunds have commanded half the marke...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the world of private equity, it may help to be big.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Money Flows to the Biggest Buyout Funds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T18:05:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7872e52-815d-560b-baf9-f3998fef300d', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7872e52-815d-560b-baf9-f3998fef300d'}, {'abstract': 'Michele Wiles, a former principal with American Ballet Theater, says she’s given up safety by leading her own company, Ballet Next.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/0