ates-skewers-the-ugliest-branch-of-government/', 'snippet': 'The former Defense Secretary says that most members of Congress are uncivil, incompetent and egotistical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What are all those congressional hearing witnesses privately thinking as they face pompous inquisition from phalanxes of ambitious lawmakers tossing gotcha questions like grenades? “Congress is best viewed from a distance — the farther the better — because up close, it is truly ugly,” advises former Defense Secretary Robert Gates, in his new Washington tell-all, “Duty: Memoirs of a Secretary at War.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Gates Skewers the Ugliest Branch of Government', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T18:29:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/889ea561-8d27-51e1-b09b-e3725367df90', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/889ea561-8d27-51e1-b09b-e3725367df90'}, {'abstract': 'A rare cold day in Los Angeles inspires tonics and teas made with ingredients on hand in the kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/tonics-and-teas/', 'snippet': 'A rare cold day in Los Angeles inspires tonics and teas made with ingredients on hand in the kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, in the course of cleaning out my office and downsizing my cookbook library, I came across an interesting book called “Tonics” by Robert