nly child. The other, Ryusei, grew up in humbler circumstances, with siblings and amid carefree chaos. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE9/12GUIDE9-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE9/12GUIDE9-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE9/12GUIDE9-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE9/12GUIDE9-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1036, 'width': 1556, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE9/12GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE9/12GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE9/12GUIDE9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blood Ties and Crossed Wires', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blood Ties And Crossed Wires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T18:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6b0159c-5399-55fe-ad66-7a3b5f22b2da', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6b0159c-5399-55fe-ad66-7a3b5f22b2da'}, {'abstract': 'Many hoped the resignation of President Michel Djotodia would signal an end to the violence in the Central African Republic between the Muslim rebel group, Seleka, and the Christian militia groups who oppose it.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/reaction-to-resignation-of-central-african-republic-president/', 'snippet': 'Many hoped the resignation of President Michel Djotodia would signal an end to the violence in the Central African Republic between the Muslim rebel group, Seleka, and the Christian militia groups who oppose it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Residents in the Central African Republic celebrated the resignation of their president, Michel Djotodia, as a potential turning point in the recent fighting in their country. Many hoped it would signal an end to the violence between Mr. Djotodia’s Muslim rebel group, Seleka, and the Christian militia groups who oppose it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reaction to Resignation of Central African Republic President', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djotodia, Michel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Channel 4', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seleka', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangui (Central African Republic)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central African Republic', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T18:48:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a09f67ce-8229-5979-af84-8b893733969f', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a09f67ce-8229-5979-af84-8b893733969f'}, {'abstract': 'You never know what you’re going to get at the American Realness Festival, running through next Sunday, which Ben Pryor started five years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/arts/dance/leaps-and-bounds-and-discoveries.html', 'snippet': 'You never know what you’re going to get at the American Realness Festival, running through next Sunday, which Ben Pryor started five years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Realness Festival is the kind of event that has descriptions of performances that say things like “Taking inspiration from ballet, psychoanalysis, queer theory and Marxism ... ” (Jillian Peña’s “Polly Pocket”) or, “At a small-town tap studio, four dancers prepare for a competition” (Tina Satter’s “House of Dance”). You never know what you’re going to get at American Realness, running through next Sunday, which Ben Pryor started five years ago. If you are curious about the latest in contemporary dance, then wander through the scheduling madness of American Realness, dipping in and out at will. There are established names like Miguel Gutierrez, Ishmael Houston-Jones and Neal Medlyn; there are names less known to American audiences, like Marten Spangberg and Eszter Salamon; there are exhibitions (Sarah Maxfield, Ian Douglas, Mr. Medlyn and Fawn Krieger, Ann Liv Young); there are parties; there will be discoveries. (At the Abrons Arts Center and other New York City locations; americanrealness.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE5/12GUIDE5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE5/12GUIDE5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE5/12GUIDE5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE5/12GUIDE5-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1320, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE5/12GUIDE5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE5/12GUIDE5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE5/12GUIDE5-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaps and Bounds and Discoveries', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaps and Bounds And Discoveries', 'nam