nic residency, the pianist Yefim Bronfman devotes Monday evening to Contact!, the orchestra’s new-music series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/arts/music/high-culture-in-the-basement.html', 'snippet': 'In town for concerts as part of his New York Philharmonic residency, the pianist Yefim Bronfman devotes Monday evening to Contact!, the orchestra’s new-music series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In town for concerts as part of his New York Philharmonic residency, the pianist Yefim Bronfman devotes Monday evening to Contact!, the orchestra’s new-music series. At the lower-level Greenwich Village space SubCulture, he will give the premiere of “Passions, Reflected,” a Schumann-influenced work for solo piano by Marc Neikrug, who has a long relationship with the Philharmonic. Joined by two of the orchestra’s string players, Mr. Bronfman will also perform Marc-André Dalbavie’s Piano Trio No. 1 (2008); others in the string section will play Poul Ruders’s String Quartet No. 4 (2012). (7:30 p.m., 45 Bleecker Street, at Lafayette Street, 212-875-5030, nyphil.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE4/12GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE4/12GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE4/12GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/arts/12GUIDE4/12GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy':