ght” and “Richard III” will be treated as two separate shows for the purposes of the Tony Awards, and not as a joint production, the committee that oversees Tony award eligibility ruled on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11richard/11richard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11richard/11richard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11richard/11richard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11richard/11richard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1549, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11richard/11richard-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11richard/11richard-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11richard/11richard-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shakespeare Double-Bill to Be Treated as Two Shows for Tony Eligibility', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Plays Are Not One, Tony Committee Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Sonia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-10T19:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d8604a9-f3bd-5dda-baa9-4211ef32dd56', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d8604a9-f3bd-5dda-baa9-4211ef32dd56'}, {'abstract': 'Lucas Bize, 18, a high school senior and the youngest member of the Racers Edge Motorsports auto racing team, spends his Sundays before a race studying the track.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/nyregion/the-racecar-driver-at-rest.html', 'snippet': 'Lucas Bize, 18, a high school senior and the youngest member of the Racers Edge Motorsports auto racing team, spends his Sundays before a race studying the track.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Lucas Bize is not reading J. D. Salinger for his high school literature class, he is speeding around racetracks in his Mustang at up to 170 miles per hour. Mr. Bize, who lives on the Upper West Side, is a senior at the Professional Children’s School, also called P.C.S., and a professional racecar driver. At 18, he is the youngest driver on the Racers Edge Motorsports team. On Sundays before a race, besides sleeping in and then hanging out with friends, he will study as much as he can about a track. Occasionally he will go with his parents, Alex, 56, and Evelyne, 45, to their home in Montauk, N.Y., where he can practice using a racing simulator, a computer with a large monitor and a wheel attached. Mr. Bize learned to race by tagging along to tracks with his father, a former business partner of Jay Z in the clothing line Rocawear, and his brother, Dennis, 22; both race only for fun now. Mr. Bize’s mother works as his manager. His sister, Natasha, 20, recently moved to Charlotte, N.C., for college.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Racecar Driver at Rest', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Racecar Driver 