sion-of-pauls-case.html', 'snippet': '“Paul’s Case,” an operatic adaptation of a Willa Cather story by UrbanArias, focuses on a teenager who longs to escape his working class world in turn-of-the-century Pittsburgh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is something not quite normal about Paul, the teenager at the center of Willa Cather’s 1905 short story “Paul’s Case,” and everyone around him knows it. Cather memorably illuminates the outward manifestations of the boy’s dandyish disaffection: “His eyes were remarkable for a certain hysterical brilliancy, and he continually used them in a conscious, theatrical sort of way, peculiarly offensive in a boy.” Among his trespasses: a red carnation in his threadbare lapel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11SPEARS/11SPEARS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11SPEARS/11SPEARS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11SPEARS/11SPEARS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11SPEARS/11SPEARS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11SPEARS/11SPEARS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11SPEARS/11SPEARS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheigh