e art accented by music and choreography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Realness, a small-scale annual performance festival of the Abrons Arts Center, began just after 7 on Thursday evening with the audience seated onstage at the center’s playhouse. In a 45-minute solo show titled “Wonder,” a naked woman, Michelle Boulé, briskly paced a figure-eight pattern around the space with a fixed smile for several minutes, to some mild rock music. Later she donned dancewear and, at one point, a full-length blue gown and matching wig.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11REALNESS1/11REALNESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11REALNESS1/11REALNESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 592}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11REALNESS1/11REALNESS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1011, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11REALNESS1/11REALNESS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2021, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11REALNESS1/11REALNESS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11REALNESS1/11REALNESS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/arts/11REALNESS1/11REALNE