 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Bank Is Criticized for Honduran Loan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Bank Is Criticized for Honduran Loan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Finance Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corporacion Dinant', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T02:47:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/010174b1-70d9-52d5-91f9-5b311806fa51', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/010174b1-70d9-52d5-91f9-5b311806fa51'}, {'abstract': 'Lt. Gov. Mark Darr said Friday that he would leave office on Feb. 1, giving in to pressure from Democrats and fellow Republicans who said his impeachment was inevitable over ethics violations tied to his campaign and office spending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/us/politics/arkansas-lieutenant-governor-quitting-under-pressure.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Gov. Mark Darr said Friday that he would leave office on Feb. 1, giving in to pressure from Democrats and fellow Republicans who said his impeachment was inevitable over ethics violations tied to his campaign and office spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lt. Gov. Mark Darr, who was facing the threat of impeachment proceedings in the aftermath of a settlement with the state’s Ethics Commission, said on Friday that he would resign on Feb. 1. Although Mr. Darr, a Republican elected in 2010, had resisted bipartisan demands for his resignation, he agreed to quit as lawmakers openly discussed removing him from office. State investigators determined last month that Mr. Darr had repeatedly broken state law by using more than $31,000 in campaign money for personal reasons, accepting improper contributions and maintaining faulty records. Mr. Darr, who abandoned a bid for Congress after an Arkansas political blogger accused him of the misconduct, said his errors were unintentional but agreed to pay $11,000 in fines. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arkansas: Lieutenant Governor Quitting Under Pressure', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arkansas: Lieutenant Governor Quitting Under Pressure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darr, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T02:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dfe9f8b-0734-505c-bd66-f5c4786557dd', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dfe9f8b-0734-505c-bd66-f5c4786557dd'}, {'abstract': 'Three military advisers were deployed to Somalia last month to help provide logistics, planning and communication assistance to forces combating the Islamic militant group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/world/africa/us-advisers-sent-to-help-somalia-fight-the-shabab.html', 'snippet': 'Three military advisers were deployed to Somalia last month to help provide logistics, planning and communication assistance to forces combating the Islamic militant group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Pentagon has sent a small team of uniformed military advisers to Somalia, the first American troops assigned there since 1993, when 18 Americans were killed in the failed “Black Hawk Down” mission.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Advisers Sent to Help Somalia Fight the Shabab', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Advisers Sent to Help Somalia Fight The Shabab', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T02:54:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6ea7540-f071-5316-bda2-83e00971ecb9', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6ea7540-f071-5316-bda2-83e00971ecb9'}, {'abstract': '“The Record,” a dance-theater piece at the Public Theater, part of the Under the Radar Festival, calls reverent attention to the shared experience of the stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/theater/the-record-at-the-public-theater.html', 'snippet': '“The Record,” a dance-theater piece at the Public Theater, part of the Under the Radar Festival, calls reverent attention to the shared experience of the stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stars of “The Record” — all 45 of them — do not really do much. They stand stock still on a bare stage, strike some funny poses then walk around a bit. They do a little running, too, and assemble in groups and sometimes stretch out on the floor. Just now and then, one will extend a hand to touch another, or a young woman will fall backward into a man’s arms, in a moment of connection that registers with soft surprise. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11record/11record-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11record/11record-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11record/11record-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11record/11record-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1556, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11record/11record-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11record/11record-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/theater/11record/11record-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Assembly of Quietly Moving Parts', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Assembly of Quietly Moving Parts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '600 Highwaymen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T02:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a33812a9-c9c6-5574-9bde-7f5eea2399dc', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a33812a9-c9c6-5574-9bde-7f5eea2399dc'}, {'abstract': 'The latest jobs report is a sobering backdrop for the debate on poverty and inequality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/opinion/no-jobs-no-benefits-and-lousy-pay.html', 'snippet': 'The latest jobs report is a sobering backdrop for the debate on poverty and inequality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is nothing good to say about the December employment report, which showed that only 74,000 jobs were added last month. But dismal as it was, the report came at an opportune political moment. The new numbers rebut the Republican arguments that jobless benefits need not be renewed, and that the current minimum wage is adequate. At the same time, they underscore the need, only recently raised to the top of the political agenda, to combat poverty and inequality. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Jobs, No Benefits, and Lousy Pay', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Jobs, No Benefits, and Lousy Pay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T02:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cc324ab-8bef-551c-837e-3e560476b79d', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cc324ab-8bef-551c-837e-3e560476b79d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Conlin was honored by Baseball’s Hall of Fame in 2011, the same year a newspaper article detailed several accounts of sexual abuse he was accused of committing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/sports/bill-conlin-sportswriter-who-quit-after-molestation-claims-dies-at-79.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Conlin was honored by Baseball’s Hall of Fame in 2011, the same year a newspaper article detailed several accounts of sexual abuse he was accused of committing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Conlin, a sports columnist for The Daily News in Philadelphia who was honored by the Baseball Hall of Fame in 2011 but who left his job later that year amid a storm of publicity over child-molestation accusations, died on Thursday in Largo, Fla. He was 79.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/sports/conlin-obit/conlin-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/sports/conlin-obit/conlin-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/sports/conlin-obit/conlin-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/sports/conlin-obit/conlin-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1324, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/sports/conlin-obit/conlin-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/sports/conlin-obit/conlin-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/sports/conlin-obit/conlin-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Conlin, Sportswriter Who Quit After Molestation Claims, Dies at 79', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bill Conlin, Sportswriter, 79; Quit After Molestation Claims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conlin, Bill (1934-2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T02:59:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ce87529-1371-5bec-a88d-8b4d35a2987a', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ce87529-1371-5bec-a88d-8b4d35a2987a'}, {'abstract': 'Four years after the earthquake, humanitarian aid seems to have run its course and development is lagging.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/opinion/haiti-unfinished-and-forsaken.html', 'snippet': 'Four years after the earthquake, humanitarian aid seems to have run its course and development is lagging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years after the earthquake, Haiti is a fragile, largely forgotten country. It’s possible that some natural or man-made crisis this year could push it back into the headlines. But sustained attention, with the kind of support from outside that Haiti still needs to rebuild and become more self-sufficient, is mostly gone. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti, Unfinished and Forsaken', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haiti, Unfinished and Forsaken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T03:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/32c487d7-e67f-5a60-8f46-ca5b3e5d3bf0', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32c487d7-e67f-5a60-8f46-ca5b3e5d3bf0'}, {'abstract': 'Double quad stacks from Martin Ashwood-Smith.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/10/weigh-in-section/', 'snippet': 'Double quad stacks from Martin Ashwood-Smith.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — Oh boy. I like Martin Ashwood-Smith’s puzzles, but this one really wasn’t in my wheelhouse. That doesn’t make it a bad puzzle, I just had a tough time solving it because I didn’t know much about the things in it. You know you’re in trouble when the clue at 1 Across — “It has a close ‘Kentucky’ cousin” — has you thinking about bourbon instead of flora. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weigh-In Section', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T03:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a8e5a82-823f-53e8-bfaf-54a5a1781c17', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a8e5a82-823f-53e8-bfaf-54a5a1781c17'}, {'abstract': 'There has been progress, but at a nuclear summit meeting in March, world leaders can do more to make the world safer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/opinion/increased-security-for-nuclear-materials.html', 'snippet': 'There has been progress, but at a nuclear summit meeting in March, world leaders can do more to make the world safer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is some rare good news on the issue of securing and containing deadly nuclear materials. In the last two years, seven countries have forsaken their uranium and plutonium stockpiles, bringing the number of nations still possessing appreciable quantities of nuclear fuel usable for bomb-making down to 25. In 1991, the number was 52.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Increased Security for Nuclear Materials', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Increased Security for Nuclear Materials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International A