. Thousands are believed to have been killed and 200,000 displaced by the fighting, which has involved the country’s largest two ethnic groups, the Dinka and the Nuer. Peace talks are underway in Ethiopia. The military’s claim that it had regained control of Bentiu in the north could not immediately be confirmed. Colonel Aguer accused the rebels of looting the city and burning buildings. The medical aid group Doctors Without Borders also said that its facilities in Bentiu had been looted. “It is unacceptable that one of the only humanitarian organizations still providing assistance to the population in Bentiu has been looted,” said the group’s general director, Arjan Hehenkamp. The United Nations Security Council on Friday urged the warring parties to stop the fighting, continue negotiations and ensure the protection of the country’s oil fields. The Council also asked Mr. Kiir to release political prisoners and urged Mr. Machar to agree to a cessation of hostilities “without precondition.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Sudan: Army Says Its Soldiers Have Regained Control of Northern City', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Sudan: Army Says Its Soldiers Have Regained Control of Northern City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiir Mayardit, Salva', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Machar, Riek', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T03:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': "By Isma'il Kushkush", 