 is of Croatian descent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the rivers of invective that Gov. Chris Christie’s allies spilled as they plotted to cripple traffic in Fort Lee, N.J., was one bitter drop of bile: The city’s mayor was referred to as a “little Serbian.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/nyregion/croatian/croatian-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/11/nyregion/croatian/croatian-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/nyregion/croatian/croatian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/nyregion/croatian/croatian-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/nyregion/croatian/croatian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/11/nyregion/croatian/croatian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/11/nyregion/croatian/croatian-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bridge Scandal, a Slight Heard Around the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Bridge Scandal, a Slight Heard Around the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sokolich, Mark J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaminer, Ariel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T05:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d031b34-a12f-5917-b34e-603cd1ec0aad', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d031b34-a12f-5917-b34e-603cd1ec0aad'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) THE PLACE BEYOND THE PINES  (2013) An itinerant motorcycle stunt rider (Ryan Gosling) tries to support a former lover (Eva Mendes, above with Mr. Gosling) and their son by robbing banks, leading to an encounter with a rookie cop (Bradley Cooper) that will have consequences neither can fathom at the time. “The most radical aspect of ‘The Place Beyond the Pines’ is its relentless linearity, the way it tells its story without foreshadowing or flashing back or resorting to other conventional shortcuts,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about this three-part drama, directed by Derek Cianfrance (“Blue Valentine”). “Watching it is refreshing and absorbing partly because it is rare for a film to show this kind of confidence in its own narrative momentum, which is also a gesture of faith in the audience’s willingness to pay attention.” He added, “Your attention is especially rewarded by the work of Mr. Gosling and Mr. Cooper, who offer contrasting studies in tragic, shortsighted masculine intensity.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/074717be-2a78-55df-a0f8-8d19b9ca851c', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/074717be-2a78-55df-a0f8-8d19b9ca851c'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo vetoed the legislation regarding an Upper East Side catering hall who lost its previous liquor license because of a law banning sales within 200 feet of a church.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/nyregion/cuomo-blocks-liquor-license-for-caterer-in-upper-east-side-church.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo vetoed the legislation regarding an Upper East Side catering hall who lost its previous liquor license because of a law banning sales within 200 feet of a church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Upper East Side catering hall that has waged a long-running campaign for a liquor license was dealt a major setback on Friday when Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo vetoed legislation tailor-made for the hall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Blocks Liquor License for Caterer in Upper East Side Church', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Blocks Liquor License for Caterer in East Side Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rose Group Park Avenue LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Catering', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krueger, Liz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T06:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4521ec8-dd48-51a3-a5c9-5f5e3c606840', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4521ec8-dd48-51a3-a5c9-5f5e3c606840'}, {'abstract': 'A taxi hit the boy and a private tour bus struck the man on Friday evening on the Upper West Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/nyregion/boy-and-elderly-man-killed-in-separate-traffic-accidents.html', 'snippet': 'A taxi hit the boy and a private tour bus struck the man on Friday evening on the Upper West Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A boy and an elderly man were struck and killed on Friday in separate traffic accide