, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharon, Ariel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T13:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/70a2041a-7f9e-5eba-897b-a27f769801af', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/70a2041a-7f9e-5eba-897b-a27f769801af'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe discusses Janet Yellen, the new Fed chair.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-dec-13-2013-2/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe discusses Janet Yellen, the new Fed chair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Janet Yellen will be the first woman to head the the Federal Reserve when she takes over for Ben Bernanke at the end of January. This week on Money Talking, Joe Nocera and Rana Foroohar from Time magazine discuss the woman who will soon steer the world’s largest economy. Ms. Foroohar said Yellen will focus on how to help ordinary families get back on their feet, while Joe said Yellen is an expert on unemployment who will apply her skills to the nation’s stubborn unemployment problem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s “Money Talking”: January 10, 2014', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T14:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bd64fce-e4bc-5a44-ae7f-ba957733db44', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bd64fce-e4bc-5a44-ae7f-ba957733db44'}, {'abstract': 'Much misery, no gains.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/the-raleigh-experiment/', 'snippet': 'Much misery, no gains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'North Carolina is an interesting place these days, and I mean that in the worst possible way. It’s a southern state, but one with a major technology complex, growing foreign investment, and what seemed until recently to be a moderating, increasingly sophisticated political culture. But then came the Republican wave of 2010, and NC was taken over by right-wing radicals, who have — among other things — taken the nation’s hardest line in cutting benefits to the unemployed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Raleigh Experiment', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T14:33:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f26b854-ee80-5d9c-a462-7786b58caf7f', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f26b854-ee80-5d9c-a462-7786b58caf7f'}, {'abstract': 'A final look at media reactions to the dread polar vortex.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/11/a-last-look-at-the-media-and-the-dreaded-polar-vortex/', 'snippet': 'A final look at media reactions to the dread polar vortex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was invited to explore the feeding frenzy surrounding the dreaded polar vortex on the NPR show On The Media. The segment, “Sucked Into the Polar Vortex,” is fun and brief. Give a listen here (I’ll add a transcript link when there is one):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Last Look at the Media and the Dreaded Polar Vortex', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roker, Al', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Calgary (Alberta)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:37:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06580066-b227-5e9d-9c66-7d029d2caa3d', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06580066-b227-5e9d-9c66-7d029d2caa3d'}, {'abstract': 'Notable quotes from business articles that appeared in The New York Times last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/business/the-chatter-for-sunday-jan-12.html', 'snippet': 'Notable quotes from business articles that appeared in The New York Times last week.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The fines have been manageable in the context of the bank’s earnings capacity.” ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Chatter for Sunday, Jan. 12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Chatter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackRock Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad8375d1-1674-50cc-8aef-cb588992ba8f', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad8375d1-1674-50cc-8aef-cb588992ba8f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to “Help the Working Poor, but Share the Burden” (Economic View, Jan. 5).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/business/the-minimum-wage-whose-burden.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to “Help the Working Poor, but Share the Burden” (Economic View, Jan. 5).', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO THE EDITOR:', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Minimum Wage: Whose Burden?', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whose Wage Burden?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:39:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dcd5f0f-c5d1-54e1-919d-4e48779d5150', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dcd5f0f-c5d1-54e1-919d-4e48779d5150'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to “Can’t Take It With You, but You Want More” (Applied Science, Jan. 5).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/business/that-thirst-to-earn.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to “Can’t Take It With You, but You Want More” (Applied Science, Jan. 5).', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO THE EDITOR:', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Thirst to Earn', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Thirst To Earn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:41:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1807285-790f-5bdd-b55d-264226ed93a7', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1807285-790f-5bdd-b55d-264226ed93a7'}, {'abstract': 'A start-up’s C.E.O. says aspiring entrepreneurs are constantly seeking his advice. He wants to help, but he also wants to have a life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/jobs/sharing-your-wisdom-within-limits.html', 'snippet': 'A start-up’s C.E.O. says aspiring entrepreneurs are constantly seeking his advice. He wants to help, but he also wants to have a life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am the C.E.O. of a technology start-up with a pretty major presence, especially in our home city. Every day I get a request for a meeting from an aspiring or early-stage entrepreneur. They all say, “Can I just pick your brain?” If I agreed to even a fraction of these requests, my head would become a colander. I’m already seriously slammed: We’re growing fast, I travel a lot and, most important, I have lots of young team members who need my time.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/busi