 and Promotion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mentors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:44:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/34a6567a-a64e-5217-a5f3-748e49adf361', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34a6567a-a64e-5217-a5f3-748e49adf361'}, {'abstract': 'A snowplow operator says that even in subzero temperatures, he “drives with the window open so I can hear if the truck makes a funny noise.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/jobs/dont-snow-on-his-parade.html', 'snippet': 'A snowplow operator says that even in subzero temperatures, he “drives with the window open so I can hear if the truck makes a funny noise.”', 'lead_paragraph': '  ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VOCATION/12-VOCATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VOCATION/12-VOCATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VOCATION/12-VOCATION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VOCATION/12-VOCATION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VOCATION/12-VOCATION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VOCATION/12-VOCATION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VOCATION/12-VOCATION-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Snow on His Parade', 'kicker': 'Vocations: The Snowplow Operator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Snow on His Parade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdman, Kelly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:45:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia R. Olsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Olsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a035ba6-7ea8-5364-917d-b1eb5ad3784d', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a035ba6-7ea8-5364-917d-b1eb5ad3784d'}, {'abstract': 'In a turnaround from decades past, money market bank deposits are paying more interest, on average, than money market mutual funds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/business/an-advantage-vanishes-for-money-funds.html', 'snippet': 'In a turnaround from decades past, money market bank deposits are paying more interest, on average, than money market mutual funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When money market mutual funds were invented back in 1971, they offered something new. Investors could earn higher yields than on bank deposits, with nearly the same liquidity and safety. But that has changed. Currently, a money market deposit at Citibank pays about five times as much interest as an investment in the Fidelity Cash Reserves fund — though, in today’s low-rate environment, the yields are minuscule.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/business/mutfund/datapoints/datapoints-jumbo.png', 'height': 473, 'width': 423, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/business/mutfund/datapoints/datapoints-superJumbo.png', 'height': 473, 'width': 423, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/business/mutfund/datapoints/datapoints-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/15/business/mutfund/datapoints/datapoints-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/business/mutfund/datapoints/datapoints-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Advantage Vanishes for Money Funds', 'kicker': 'Datapoints', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Advantage Vanishes for Money Funds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Market Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:48:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Bernasek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernasek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ee4d377-fa4f-572b-a9c3-a4b05345db5d', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ee4d377-fa4f-572b-a9c3-a4b05345db5d'}, {'abstract': 'A two-year pattern turned a bargain-basement stock market into a much more expensive one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/your-money/a-market-streak-has-ended-but-the-echoes-havent.html', 'snippet': 'A two-year pattern turned a bargain-basement stock market into a much more expensive one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two improbable, gravity-defying years, the streak is over. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-STRA/12-STRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-STRA/12-STRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-STRA/12-STRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-STRA/12-STRA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1516, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-STRA/12-STRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-STRA/12-STRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-STRA/12-STRA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Market Streak Has Ended, but the Echoes Haven’t', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Streak Has Ended, but the Echoes Haven’t', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bespoke Investment Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T15:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Sommer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sommer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cbd89de-f2ba-5d41-a497-6bc8fbb12dc9', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cbd89de-f2ba-5d41-a497-6bc8fbb12dc9'}, {'abstract': 'New forces are causing the American income gap to feed on itself, whether in the political process, education or the broader economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/business/the-vicious-circle-of-income-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'New forces are causing the American income gap to feed on itself, whether in the political process, education or the broader economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost every culture has some variation on the saying, “rags to rags in three generations.” Whether it’s “clogs to clogs” or “rice paddy to rice paddy,” the message is essentially the same: Starting with nothing, the first generation builds a successful enterprise, which its profligate offspring then manage poorly, so that by the time the grandchildren take over, little value remains. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VIEW/12-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VIEW/12-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VIEW/12-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VIEW/12-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/business/12-VIEW/12-VIEW-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail