-258fdc3de810'}, {'abstract': 'The sinking floor, not the glass ceiling, is the urgent issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/opinion/sunday/how-can-we-help-men-by-helping-women.html', 'snippet': 'The sinking floor, not the glass ceiling, is the urgent issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS week Maria Shriver brings together a star-studded cast of celebrities, from Hillary Rodham Clinton to Beyoncé, to call attention to the economic plight of American women and demand that women’s needs be put “at the center of policy making.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Can We Help Men? By Helping Women', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Can We Help Men? By Helping Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coontz, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Economic and Policy Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T19:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Coontz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coontz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b06c720c-ff0e-5afd-af85-9f02dea478c1', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b06c720c-ff0e-5afd-af85-9f02dea478c1'}, {'abstract': 'Giving it an extra four years would provide more time for scientific and commercial experiments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/opinion/sunday/a-longer-life-for-the-space-station.html', 'snippet': 'Giving it an extra four years would provide more time for scientific and commercial experiments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration’s decision to extend the international space station’s time in orbit by at least four years makes good sense. Some $100 billion has been invested to build the station, which was completed less than three years ago. The plan had been to allow the station to plunge into the ocean in 2020. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Longer Life for the Space Station', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Longer Life for the Space Station', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Space Station', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T19:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc33a5b-1aa9-570c-8649-facbd1fe91de', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc33a5b-1aa9-570c-8649-facbd1fe91de'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should reaffirm the longstanding practice of recess appointments that keeps government functioning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/opinion/sunday/protect-the-presidents-appointments.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should reaffirm the longstanding practice of recess appointments that keeps government functioning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under the Constitution, the president nominates federal judges, cabinet members and officials for executive agencies, and the Senate votes on their confirmation. But what if the Senate isn’t in session? The answer has always seemed clear: The Constitution gives the president the power to fill “all vacancies that may happen during the recess of the Senate.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protect the President’s Appointments', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protect the President’s Appointments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T19:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/63eaae82-1e3c-5de4-abb1-2cd93c6a91f7', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63eaae82-1e3c-5de4-abb1-2cd93c6a91f7'}, {'abstract': 'After a year of great change, Executive Editor Jill Abramson discusses upcoming challenges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/public-editor/the-times-from-the-top-looking-ahead.html', 'snippet': 'After a year of great change, Executive Editor Jill Abramson discusses upcoming challenges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THESE days, when Jill Abramson surveys the paper’s masthead, she does so with a certain amount of satisfaction. Half of the 10 top-ranking editors in the newsroom, including herself, are women. That’s a long way from a time when women had no presence on the Times masthead; the first on the news side was Carolyn Lee, in 1990 (though Charlotte Curtis preceded her, as an opinion editor, in 1974).', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times, From the Top: Looking Ahead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Times, From the Top: Looking Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Margaret M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMSON, JILL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T19:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, '