aste', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When a Food Writer Can’t Taste', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taste', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smell (Olfaction)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T19:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlena Spieler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spieler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5279fc7-9beb-52ad-88a2-744ec631bb3f', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5279fc7-9beb-52ad-88a2-744ec631bb3f'}, {'abstract': 'The danger of deciding, too late, to be a good neighbor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/opinion/sunday/i-crashed-the-wrong-shiva.html', 'snippet': 'The danger of deciding, too late, to be a good neighbor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU get to know all the old people. This is what no one tells you when you live in New York City and decide to work from home, but it’s true. One generation’s “off-peak hours” is another’s “hours.” There they are, walking their rickety dogs at 10, doing their laundry at noon, checking their mail at 3, asking you if you know how to operate a VCR machine at 6. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/sunday-review/12SHIVA/12SHIVA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/sunday-review/12SHIVA/12SHIVA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, 