merica/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on strategies to tackle sexual violence worldwide', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is from Nairobi, Kenya, about how police corruption and indifference create impunity that allows sexual violence to unchecked. This is a global problem, particularly in poor countries with dubious criminal justice systems but also of course in the United States. As you’ll see, I argue that we have to change attitudes but above all we have to end the impunity. The organization that I followed in Kenya, Shining Hope for Communities, is doing a terrific job trying to do just that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sexual Violence and Impunity, from Kenya to America', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-11T19:48:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79d90c57-ca8a-5aba-8ae2-4cc217067578', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79d90c57-ca8a-5aba-8ae2-4cc217067578'}, {'abstract': 'Philip Rivers’s distinctive choice of neckwear reflects his down-home roots, while his performance this season shows his capacity for remaining cool under pressure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/sports/football/chargers-quarterback-gives-rivals-reasons-to-fear-the-bolo.html', 'snippet': 'Philip Rivers’s distinctive choice of neckwear reflects his down-home roots, while his performance this season shows his capacity for remaining cool under pressure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Gone are the days when a quarterback would stand at his locker after a game, freshly showered