'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Men's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/47f46467-4212-5967-b422-070dc83c9ab5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/47f46467-4212-5967-b422-070dc83c9ab5'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/arts/television/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (NBC) THE 71ST ANNUAL GOLDEN GLOBE AWARDS Tina Fey and Amy Poehler (above right, with Ms. Fey) host these awards — often considered predictors of the Oscars — sponsored by the Hollywood Foreign Press Association and broadcast live. In the motion picture drama division, the nominees are “12 Years a Slave,” “Captain Phillips,” “Gravity,” “Philomena” and “Rush,” for best picture; Cate Blanchett, Sandra Bullock, Judi Dench, Emma Thompson and Kate Winslet, for best actress; and Chiwetel Ejiofor, Idris Elba, Tom Hanks, Matthew McConaughey and Robert Redford, for best actor. In the comedy or musical division, the nominees are “American Hustle,” “Her,” “Inside Llewyn Davis,” “Nebraska” and “The Wolf of Wall Street,” for best picture; Amy Adams, Julie Delpy, Greta Gerwig, Julia Louis-Dreyfus and Meryl Streep, for best actress; and Christian Bale, Bruce Dern, Leonardo DiCaprio, Oscar Isaac and Joaquin Phoenix, for best actor. Woody Allen will receive the Cecil B. DeMille Award, although he is not expected to attend. Awards will also be handed out for television work. A countdown to the ceremony begins at 4 on E!, which moves to red carpet coverage at 6. NBC will report on arrivals, starting at 7. And E! will visit after-parties at 11.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-12T14:43:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8906dbef-1ead-5d95-ae5c-75a7b8544c14', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8906dbef-1ead-5d95-ae5c-75a7b8544c14'}, {'abstract': 'Lupita Nyong’o, Cate Blanchett and Greta Gerwig are among the actresses to look out for on the red carpet during tonight’s Golden Globes.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/what-to-look-for-on-the-globes-red-carpet/', 'snippet': 'Lupita Nyong’o, Cate Blanchett and Greta Gerwig are among the actresses to look out for on the red carpet during tonight’s Golden Globes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This much is clear about this year’s Golden Globes. Whether Lupita Nyong’o wins the award for best supporting actress at Sunday night’s ceremonies (an award for which she is the heavy favorite) or not, the young Kenyan actress will stride the red carpet beforehand as a bona fide star of the fashion world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Look for on the Globes Red Carpet', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchett, Cate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, January', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Jennifer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-12T14:51:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Emmrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emmrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3c5723f-7700-5a5c-a0de-84fcbc0438a7', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3c5723f-7700-5a5c-a0de-84fcbc0438a7'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Sarah Aubel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/the-scene-milan-fashion-week-neil-barrett/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Sarah Aubel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the Milan Fashion Week photo diary of Sarah Aubel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Fashion Week: Neil Barrett Fall/Winter 2014', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-12T15:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Aubel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aubel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2802f334-4a2e-50cd-a359-c5314ac324e1', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2802f334-4a2e-50cd-a359-c5314ac324e1'}, {'abstract': 'Observers are predicting a split among the top contenders on the movies side, while the usual suspects may prevail in the TV categories.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/golden-globes-predictions-and-hopes/', 'snippet': 'Observers are predicting a split among the top contenders on the movies side, while the usual suspects may prevail in the TV categories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES – The Golden Globes are mostly an excuse to drink, laugh and sing off-key along with the hosts Tina Fey and Amy Poehler. But the awards also serve as a warm-up to creaming your officemates in your Oscar pool. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Golden Globes Predictions (and Hopes)', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-12T15:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a43e367-fed8-5083-acd9-bf5351a6f1e8', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a43e367-fed8-5083-acd9-bf5351a6f1e8'}, {'abstract': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/in-our-pages-january-13/', 'snippet': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 1939: Father Kills Son To ‘End Lifetime Suffering’', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Our Pages: January 13', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smok