 Jong-un score propaganda points.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/opinion/12-iht-edhengart/12-iht-edhengart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/opinion/12-iht-edhengart/12-iht-edhengart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/opinion/12-iht-edhengart/12-iht-edhengart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/opinion/12-iht-edhengart/12-iht-edhengart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1492, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/opinion/12-iht-edhengart/12-iht-edhengart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/12/opinion/12-iht-edhengart/12-iht-edhengart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/opinion/12-iht-edhengart/12-iht-edhengart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Editorial Cartoon', 'kicker': 'Heng', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodman, Dennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-12T23:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e08b4f9-3f19-518e-b99a-1adeef679133', 'word_count': 8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e08b4f9-3f19-518e-b99a-1adeef679133'}, {'abstract': 'The Denver Art Museum is announcing Monday that it has received the largest gift of paintings in its history, a group of 22 Impressionist works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/arts/design/denver-art-museum-gets-impressionist-trove.html', 'snippet': 'The Denver Art Museum is announcing Monday that it has received the largest gift of paintings in its history, a group of 22 Impressionist works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Denver Art Museum is announcing Monday that it has received the largest gift of paintings in its history, a group of 22 Impressionist works — by artists including van Gogh, Monet, Cézanne, Manet and Renoir — from the collection of Frederic C. Hamilton, an oil and gas magnate who has been the museum’s chief benefactor for several decades. The works include van Gogh’s 1887 “Edge of a Wheat Field With Poppies,” which will be the first van Gogh in the museum’s collection. Besides European works the donation includes pieces by major American Impressionists like Childe Hassam and William Merritt Chase. The gift has “forever changed the museum’s ability to deliver world-class exhibitions and programs,” said Christoph Heinrich, the museum’s director, and it transforms Denver’s holdings of Impressionism into one of the most important in the Western states. The paintings, mostly landscapes and seascapes, will be given a dedicated home in the museum’s newest addition, by the architect Daniel Libeskind, which opened in 2006. Mr. Hamilton, who served as chairman of the museum’s board from 1994 until last year, led the fund-raising effort for that $110 million expansion, and the building now bears his name.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/arts/arts2/arts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/13/arts/arts2/arts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/arts/arts2/arts2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/arts/arts2/arts2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/13/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Denver Art Museum Gets Impressionist Trove', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Denver Art Museum Gets Impressionist Trove', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Art Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Frederic C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-12T23:35:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c663744-dfed-5a74-a535-4abb9e3665c4', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c663744-dfed-5a74-a535-4abb9e3665c4'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry described his life in hockey, including the way he followed Yale’s run to a national championship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/sports/hockey/q-and-a-with-john-kerry.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry described his life in hockey, including the way he followed Yale’s run to a national championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If President Obama is the nation’s highest-ranking recreational basketball player, then Secretary of State John Kerry is probably the top hockey player. Kerry was awarded several medals for his Vietnam War service, served 28 years as a senator from Massachusetts and ran for president in 2004, but sometimes it seems that his proudest moments have taken place on a rink.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/13kerryqanda1/13kerryqanda1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/13kerryqanda1/13kerryqanda1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 780}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/13kerryqanda1/13kerryqanda1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'