 'The annual NYC Winter Jazzfest went gloriously big for its 10th anniversary, stretching to five days rather than the usual two, and reaching a total audience of 7,500.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s what you could have heard at around 6:45 on Saturday evening, during the earliest shift of that day’s programming for the 10th annual NYC Winter Jazzfest: Extravagantly detailed large-canvas compositions, courtesy of Darcy James Argue’s Secret Society. A deep meld of Afro-Cuban music and modern jazz by Michele Rosewoman’s New Yor-Uba. Acoustic folk singing emulsified into a satiny blend by Tillery. Complex rhythmic calculus refashioned into body blows, by the guitarist Miles Okazaki or by one of two dynamic young drummers, Mark Guiliana and Ted Poor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Favorites and Discoveries Among a Superabundance of Jazz', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Favorites and Discoveries Among a Superabundance of Jazz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter Jazzfest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T00:17:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3ade2d7-94af-5165-8b05-13d1caa4e37c', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3ade2d7-94af-5165-8b05-13d1caa4e37c'}, {'abstract': 'The actor discusses "House of Cards" on the red carpet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/awardsseason/1000000