g', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve McQueen & Bianca Stigter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T00:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Shern Sharma and Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shern', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f13931b5-e56e-596b-9cfa-93c0b80861c0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f13931b5-e56e-596b-9cfa-93c0b80861c0'}, {'abstract': 'The arrests of three politiqueras, or campaign runners, who are often hired to gather votes in contested races, have become a tricky issue for elected officials in the Rio Grande Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/us/politics/texas-vote-buying-case-casts-glare-on-tradition-of-election-day-goads.html', 'snippet': 'The arrests of three politiqueras, or campaign runners, who are often hired to gather votes in contested races, have become a tricky issue for elected officials in the Rio Grande Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONNA, Tex. — In this Rio Grande Valley town of trailer parks and weedy lots eight miles from the Mexico border, people call them runners or politiqueras — the campaign workers who use their network of relatives and friends to deliver votes for their candidates. They travel around town with binders stuffed with the names and addresses of registered voters, driving residents to and from the polls and urging those they bump into at the grocery store to support their candidates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/us/VOTERS/VOTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/13/us/VOTERS/VOTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/us/VOTERS/VOTERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 947, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/us/VOTERS/VOTERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 947, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/us/VOTERS/VOTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/13/us/VOTERS/VOTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/us/VOTERS/VOTERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Vote-Buying Case Casts Glare on Tradition of Election Day Goads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas Vote-Buying Case Casts Glare on Tradition of Election Day Goads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Donna (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio Grande Valley (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T01:06:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b19db8-5d9c-54a0-a7a6-a808c8749c7c', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b19db8-5d9c-54a0-a7a6-a808c8749c7c'}, {'abstract': 'The reverse Robin-Hoodism of the Republicans runs deep.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/opinion/krugman-enemies-of-the-poor.html', 'snippet': 'The reverse Robin-Hoodism of the Republicans runs deep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suddenly it’s O.K., even mandatory, for politicians with national ambitions to talk about helping the poor. This is easy for Democrats, who can go back to being the party of F.D.R. and L.B.J. It’s much more difficult for Republicans, who are having a hard time shaking their reputation for reverse Robin-Hoodism, for being the party that takes from the poor and gives to the rich.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Krugman_New/Krugman_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Krugman_New/Krugman_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Krugman_New/Krugman_New-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Krugman_New/Krugman_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Krugman_New/Krugman_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Krugman_New/Krugman_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Krugman_New/Krugman_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enemies of the Poor', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enemies Of The Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T01:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0543f63c-9ee5-5761-bb0b-a21a7070553d', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0543f63c-9ee5-5761-bb0b-a21a7070553d'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the Milan men’s shows, including Bottega Veneta’s comfortable sweatpants and Donatella Versace’s cowboy-and-biker themed collection.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/12/dudes-and-other-distractions-in-milan/', 'snippet': 'A look at the Milan men’s shows, including Bottega Veneta’s comfortable sweatpants and Donatella Versace’s cowboy-and-biker themed collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This morning I visited Antonio De Matteis, the chief executive of Kiton, in the company’s new offices in Milan — the former Palazzo Ferre — and he told me something that warmed my heart: you should be able to sleep in your clothes. When a garment feels good and is well made, as a Kiton suit or coat certainly is, you should be able to wear it without sense of care, even if your natural inclination is to baby a very expensive, handmade jacket. Mr. De Matteis, from years of experience, from generations of being Italian, wouldn’t dream of such fussiness. He removed his jacket and slipped it on backward, showing how he wears it to sleep on a plane.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/fashion/versace1/versace1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/12/fashion/versace1/versace1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 811}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'cap