ni, SpA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T01:16:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32866148-359b-5a22-9191-c5b422798159', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32866148-359b-5a22-9191-c5b422798159'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets will play Atlanta on Thursday at O2 Arena as the N.B.A. takes its game on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/sports/basketball/its-brooklyn-basketball-and-branding-as-nets-head-to-london.html', 'snippet': 'The Nets will play Atlanta on Thursday at O2 Arena as the N.B.A. takes its game on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After playing five games in eight days, the Nets find themselves with something of a holiday. They were headed to London on Sunday night, preparing to play the Atlanta Hawks at O2 Arena on Thursday night, the only game they are scheduled to play for the next eight days.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/nets-skybox/nets-skybox-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 541, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/nets-skybox/nets-skybox-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 541}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/nets-skybox/nets-skybox-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/nets-skybox/nets-skybox-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1738, 'width': 1928, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/nets-skybox/nets-skybox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/nets-skybox/nets-skybox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/sports/nets-skybox/nets-skybox-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Brooklyn, Basketball and Branding as Nets Head to London', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Brooklyn, Basketball and Branding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Hawks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T01:16:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8fa608d-824f-5232-af86-741491be5529', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8fa608d-824f-5232-af86-741491be5529'}, {'abstract': 'A broad array of factions have turned against the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria, known as ISIS, in a showdown over tactics, power and ideology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/world/middleeast/syria-rebels-turn-against-most-radical-group-tied-to-al-qaeda.html', 'snippet': 'A broad array of factions have turned against the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria, known as ISIS, in a showdown over tactics, power and ideology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — As a government warplane soared over the northern Syrian city of Raqqa recently, a fighter from the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria, the country’s most radical group linked to Al Qaeda, watched from behind an antiaircraft gun mounted on a pickup truck. Fighters and activists from rival insurgent factions urged him to fire. He did not.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Rebels Turn Against Most Radical Group Tied to Al Qaeda', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria Rebels Turn Against Most Radical Group Tied to Al Qaeda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State of Iraq and Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Nusra Front', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T01:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cad42575-2240-533c-bfc8-38eaa3ddf9f3', 'word_count': 1286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cad42575-2240-533c-bfc8-38eaa3ddf9f3'}, {'abstract': 'The online writings of a woman who has been fighting cancer for seven years invite us to think about the different approaches people take.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/opinion/keller-heroic-measures.html', 'snippet': 'The online writings of a woman who has been fighting cancer for seven years invite us to think about the different approaches people take.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LISA BONCHEK ADAMS has spent the last seven years in a fierce and very public cage fight with death. Since a mammogram detected the first toxic seeds of cancer in her left breast when she was 37, she has blogged and tweeted copiously about her contest with the advancing disease. She has tweeted through morphine haze and radiation burn. Even by contemporary standards of social-media self-disclosure, she is a phenomenon. (Last week she tweeted her 165,000th tweet.) A rapt audience of several thousand follows her unsparing narrative of mastectomy, chemotherapy, radiation, biopsies and scans, pumps and drains and catheters, grueling drug trials and grim side effects, along with her posts on how to tell the children, potshots at the breast cancer lobby, poetry and resolute calls to “persevere.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cred