90fe79ac-a1f7-5973-bc86-0f005c383122'}, {'abstract': 'Four decades later, the Media, Pa., burglars come in from the cold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/opinion/a-flashback-to-the-reign-of-j-edgar-hoover.html', 'snippet': 'Four decades later, the Media, Pa., burglars come in from the cold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was a college sophomore in April 1971, still mourning the death of Jimi Hendrix, when I learned that a campus organization to which I belonged was being spied on by the Federal Bureau of Investigation. The news landed in the mailbox of the Black Student Union — at what is now known as Widener University, not far from Philadelphia — in an envelope stuffed with documents that had been stolen from an F.B.I. office in nearby Media, Pa. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Flashback to the Reign of J. Edgar Hoover', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Flashback to the Reign of J. Edgar Hoover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staples, Brent', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoover, J Edgar', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medsger, Betty', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T01:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/42d34182-52be-59c2-8e6a-38d0574d807b', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42d34182-52be-59c2-8e6a-38d0574d807b'}, {'abstract': 'There are some needed policy changes that could be made by presidential orders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/opinion/missing-executive-actions.html', 'snippet': 'There are some needed policy changes that could be made by presidential orders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama has often issued executive orders to get around recalcitrant Republicans in Congress or to clarify existing policy. Yet there are some areas where the president has been too reticent. The start of a new year is a good moment to point out some matters ripe for executive action.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing Executive Actions', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missing Executive Actions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'},