agraph': 'Here comes genomics, Take 2. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/business/genome1/genome1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/13/business/genome1/genome1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/business/genome1/genome1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/business/genome1/genome1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/business/genome1/genome1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/13/business/genome1/genome1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/business/genome1/genome1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aiming to Push Genomics Forward in New Study', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aiming to Push Genomics Forward in New Study', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regeneron Pharmaceuticals Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Geisinger Health System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T05:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e53f029e-9d36-5e83-9eb5-8f1d0b9bc6d3', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e53f029e-9d36-5e83-9eb5-8f1d0b9bc6d3'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (13) AT BERKELEY (2013) Without narration or identifying the people interviewed — from the humblest janitor to the most esteemed professor — Frederick Wiseman chronicles the history and teaching process of the University of California, Berkeley, while mulling the effect of capitalism on state-funded public education. “Mr. Wiseman has made his share of grim documentaries in which people are processed and oppressed by bureaucracy,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times of this four-hour film, presented here by “Independent Lens.” “\xa0‘At Berkeley’ is not one. Its cautiously upbeat attitude is expressed in a director’s note: ‘I think it is just as important for a filmmaker to show people of intelligence, character, tolerance and good will, hard at work, as it is to make movies about the failures, insensitivities and cruelties of others.’ Amen.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T05:16:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/20026cc0-dae8-5270-a46d-2e9e00cddc6a', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20026cc0-dae8-5270-a46d-2e9e00cddc6a'}, {'abstract': 'Trying hard to top their job as hosts last year, Tina Fey and Amy Poehler fell short when aiming to be like the guys. But they were very funny on the subject of women and Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/movies/awardsseason/tina-fey-and-amy-poehler-celebrate-gender-equality.html', 'snippet': 'Trying hard to top their job as hosts last year, Tina Fey and Amy Poehler fell short when aiming to be like the guys. But they were very funny on the subject of women and Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British actress Emma Thompson tossed her shoes across the stage and slurped a martini, Dean Martin-style. Jennifer Lawrence wore her hair almost West Point short, while the actor Jared Leto and the composer Alex Ebert put up their flowing locks in loose chignons.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blending Genders, for Some Laughs at the Golden Globes', 'kicker': 'The TV Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blending Genders, For Some Laughs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Alessandra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T05:27:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb4e2439-e4b3-5a83-b63e-79af87ac87f2', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb4e2439-e4b3-5a83-b63e-79af87ac87f2'}, {'abstract': '“American Hustle” left a messy Golden Globes as the big winner on Sunday, winning three major awards, including best comedy. But voters stayed true to form and spread their love around.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/movies/awardsseason/american-hustle-and-12-years-a-slave-win-at-the-golden-globes.html', 'snippet': '“American Hustle” left a messy Golden Globes as the big winner on Sunday, winning three major awards, including best comedy. But voters stayed true to form and spread their love around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. — “American Hustle” left a messy Golden Globes as the big winner on Sunday, capturing three major awards, including best comedy. But voters stayed true to form and spread their love around, handing best drama to an otherwise ignored “12 Years a Slave” and best director to Alfonso Cuarón, for “Gravity.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bragging Rights to Share at the Golden Globes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bragging Rights to Share at Globes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{