, 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63b483e8-22f7-58d2-9352-044405ecb338', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63b483e8-22f7-58d2-9352-044405ecb338'}, {'abstract': 'The Titanic replica will be a tourist attraction moored at a riverbank and include features that recreate the experience of the ocean liner’s hitting an iceberg.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/plans-for-a-replica-of-titanic-floated-in-china/', 'snippet': 'The Titanic replica will be a tourist attraction moored at a riverbank and include features that recreate the experience of the ocean liner’s hitting an iceberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A company in southwestern China has announced plans to build a full-scale replica of the Titanic, the passenger ship that famously sank in 1912. The Seven Star Energy Investment Group, based in Sichuan Province, said it would spend spend 1 billion renminbi, or about $164 million, to build an ocean liner that would be moored on a river bank as a tourist attraction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plans for a Replica of Titanic Floated in China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models and Replicas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Titanic (Ship)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Clive', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Su Shaojun', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seven Star Energy Invest