value': 'Bencic, Belinda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T10:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d4b90dc-7455-5c1a-b8ec-9c25ddf49262', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d4b90dc-7455-5c1a-b8ec-9c25ddf49262'}, {'abstract': 'Tang Wei, celebrated yet also briefly blacklisted for her role in Ang Lee’s steamy 2007 film “Lust, Caution,” has been the victim of a telephone scam artist who persuaded her to wire about $34,500 from one of her accounts, according to Chinese news reports.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/tang-wei-film-star-reported-victim-of-phone-scam/', 'snippet': 'Tang Wei, celebrated yet also briefly blacklisted for her role in Ang Lee’s steamy 2007 film “Lust, Caution,” has been the victim of a telephone scam artist who persuaded her to wire about $34,500 from one of her accounts, according to Chinese new...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was her graphic onscreen sex scenes with Tony Leung Chiu-Wai in “Lust, Caution,” under the direction of Ang Lee, that placed Tang Wei in the firmament of Chinese stars. She might have become an even bigger household name after the film was released in 2007 if prudish Chinese officials had not put her on an industry blacklist. Producers and directors avoided working with her for years, until at some point she was deemed to have been rehabilitated. She is now acting in films that are shown in mainland Chinese theaters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tang Wei, Film Star, Reported Victim of Phone Scam', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Ang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leung Chiu-Wai, Tony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Variety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T11:27:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7621089a-a23c-5c16-bb24-65a5a961a6f0', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7621089a-a23c-5c16-bb24-65a5a961a6f0'}, {'abstract': 'In the boldest move in two months of protests against Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra’s government, crowds blocked traffic to Thailand’s costliest real estate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/world/asia/thailand-protests.html', 'snippet': 'In the boldest move in two months of protests against Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra’s government, crowds blocked traffic to Thailand’s costliest real estate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Thousands of protesters who had spent the night on the streets of Bangkok’s central commercial district marched to government offices early Tuesday as part of a so-called shutdown of the city, a largely peaceful demonstration aimed at removing the government of Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/THAILAND/THAILAND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters, Angry at Premier, Fill Bangkok’s Central Business District', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters, Angry at Premier, Fill Bangkok’s Central Business District', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yingluck Shinawatra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thaksin Shinawatra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T11:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc570b2c-0ea9-51c0-87d3-a685e06d6699', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc570b2c-0ea9-51c0-87d3-a685e06d6699'}, {'abstract': 'Genzyme, the American biotechnology unit of the French drug maker Sanofi, is buying a 12 percent stake in Alnylam Pharmaceuticals for $700 million as part of an expanded alliance to develop treatments for rare genetic diseases.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/sanofi-unit-to-buy-700-million-stake-in-rare-disease-company/', 'snippet': 'Genzyme, the American biotechnology unit of the French drug maker Sanofi, is buying a 12 percent stake in Alnylam Pharmaceuticals for $700 million as part of an expanded alliance to develop treatments for rare genetic diseases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The biotechnology unit of the French drug maker Sanofi\xa0 agreed on Monday to buy a 12 percent stake in Alnylam Pharmaceuticals for $700 million as part of an expanded alliance to develop treatments for rare genetic diseases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanofi Unit to Buy $700 Million Stake in Rare Disease Company', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alnylam Pharmaceuticals Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genzyme Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanofi SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T11:52:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68a6ec8e-aa6c-579b-9963-ca4f2188f4a7', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68a6ec8e-aa6c-579b-9963-ca4f2188f4a7'}, {'abstract': 'Collegefeed, a California startup, has developed a computerized job matching system that caters to the special needs of college students, recent graduates and employers looking for educated, entry-level workers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/matchmaker-matchmaker-find-me-a-job/', 'snippet': 'Collegefeed, a California startup, has developed a computerized job matching system that caters to the special needs of college students, recent graduates and employers looking for educated, entry-level workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no coincidence that Sanjeev Agrawal, the co-founder and chief executive of Collegefeed, compares finding a job with dating. Finding The One (