, 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Bel Group names Y&R Midwest its agency of record for Bel Brands USA, and Burger King chooses Horizon Media as its media planning and buying agency for the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bel Group, Paris, expanded its relationship with Y&R, part of the Young & Rubicam Group division of WPP, by naming the agency’s Chicago office, known as Y&R Midwest, as agency of record for Bel Brands USA, Chicago, handling duties like brand strategy and social media for cheeses that include the Laughing Cow and Boursin. Spending was estimated at $15 million to $20 million. Y&R already handles Bel Group advertising in markets like Australia, Canada and Europe. The Bel Brands USA account had previously been handled by the Chicago office of Havas Worldwide, part of the Havas Creative unit of Havas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T16:05:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2a2364f-43ac-54be-8614-18dd03e052e0', 'word_count': 1510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2a2364f-43ac-54be-8614-18dd03e052e0'}, {'abstract': 'The orders reflect Airbus’s dominant position in the market for the most expensive aircraft: large wide-bodies with more than 400 seats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/business/international/airbus-led-rival-boeing-in-jets-ordered-last-year.html', 'snippet': 'The orders reflect Airbus’s dominant position in the market for the most expensive aircraft: large wide-bodies with more than 400 seats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOULOUSE, France — In their rivalry as the world’s leading makers of passenger aircraft, Airbus captured the lead in jets ordered last year, but Boeing delivered more planes to customers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/business/Airbus1/Airbus1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/business/Airbus1/Airbus1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/business/Airbus1/Airbus1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/business/Airbus1/Airbus1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/business/Airbus1/Airbus1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/business/Airbus1/Airbus1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 