stitute of Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T17:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/448c87a6-2a29-5fe5-876e-2ea34b6f9871', 'word_count': 3084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/448c87a6-2a29-5fe5-876e-2ea34b6f9871'}, {'abstract': 'The developments dampened hopes of the insurgents opposed to the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria that they could quickly subdue or co-opt the group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/world/middleeast/rebel-infighting-in-Syria.html', 'snippet': 'The developments dampened hopes of the insurgents opposed to the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria that they could quickly subdue or co-opt the group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Making good on threats to contest attacks by former allies on its power and claimed turf, the extremist militant group the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria has retaken significant parts of the territory in northern Syria that rival insurgent groups had wrested away last week, rebel representatives said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Extremist Militant Group in Syria Retakes Ground Lost to Rival Rebels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extremist Militant Group in Syria Retakes Ground Lost to Rival Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State of Iraq and Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T17:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90cada4d-1800-563e-b13d-1bdb3e927c50', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90cada4d-1800-563e-b13d-1bdb3e927c50'}, {'abstract': 'The money, from a group of philanthropic organizations, could also relieve the city-owned Detroit Institute of Arts from having to sell works to pay the city’s debts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/us/300-million-pledged-to-save-detroits-art-collection.html', 'snippet': 'The money, from a group of philanthropic organizations, could also relieve the city-owned Detroit Institute of Arts from having to sell works to pay the city’s debts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'National and local philanthropic foundations have committed $330 million toward a deal to avoid cuts to Detroit retirees’ pensions and to save the Detroit Institute of Arts’ renowned collection, federal mediators involved in the city’s bankruptcy proceedings announced on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/14DETROIT/14DETROIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/0