video/2ec54b43-96e6-5521-ab68-4498a2657868', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2ec54b43-96e6-5521-ab68-4498a2657868'}, {'abstract': 'Prada and Gucci are designed by women — Miuccia Prada and, at Gucci, Frida Giannini — but this scarcely accounts for their remarkable agreement this season at the men’s fall shows.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/for-prada-and-gucci-a-similar-view-of-fall-fashion/', 'snippet': 'Prada and Gucci are designed by women — Miuccia Prada and, at Gucci, Frida Giannini — but this scarcely accounts for their remarkable agreement this season at the men’s fall shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do Prada and Gucci have in common? Milan, fleets of P.R. people. Both brands are also designed by women — Miuccia Prada and, at Gucci, Frida Giannini — but this scarcely accounts for their remarkable agreement this season at the men’s fall shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Prada and Gucci, a Similar View of Fall Fashion', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giannini, Frida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prada, Miuccia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prada SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T17:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfbbde46-bbc1-5805-a72a-662c2d3eab7f', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfbbde46-bbc1-5805-a72a-662c2d3eab7f'}, {'abstract': 'City officials in Helsinki voted to set aside a parcel of land that could be used for a new museum facility.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/guggenheim-will-invite-architects-to-imagine-a-finnish-outpost/', 'snippet': 'City officials in Helsinki voted to set aside a parcel of land that could be used for a new museum facility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The on-again-off-again proposal to build an outpost of the Guggenheim Museum in Helsinki, Finland, appears to be on again. After city officials there shot down the idea of building the $185 million museum in May 2012, it voted on Monday to reserve a parcel of land on the city’s South Harbor waterfront for the prospective institution. This gives the Guggenheim the green light to start an open international architectural competition to determine who would build the museum. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guggenheim Will Invite Architects to Imagine a Finnish Outpost', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T18:02:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4b601fe-55da-57cf-8699-bb754ac4dfc5', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4b601fe-55da-57cf-8699-bb754ac4dfc5'}, {'abstract': 'Justices across the ideological spectrum appeared prepared to rein in the ability of presidents to make appointments without the Senate’s consent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/us/politics/justices-voice-doubts-on-obama-recess-appointments.html', 'snippet': 'Justices across the ideological spectrum appeared prepared to rein in the ability of presidents to make appointments without the Senate’s consent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In an extended argument that contained large doses of constitutional history and practical politics, the Supreme Court on Monday seemed skeptical of the Obama administration’s contention that it could bypass the Senate to appoint officials during short breaks in the Senate’s work.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/us/SCOTUS/SCOTUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight