, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed45687d-1588-5c36-9bb8-e59ff8141d68', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed45687d-1588-5c36-9bb8-e59ff8141d68'}, {'abstract': 'The Selected Shorts event honoring Ms. Munro will also feature Margaret Atwood, Holly Hunter and others.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/alice-munro-to-beam-in-for-night-at-symphony-space/', 'snippet': 'The Selected Shorts event honoring Ms. Munro will also feature Margaret Atwood, Holly Hunter and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Canadian writer Alice Munro couldn’t make it to Stockholm in December for the ceremony commemorating her Nobel Prize because of health concerns, but Ms. Munro will visit New York — virtually, anyway — later this month.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alice Munro to Beam In for Night at Symphony Space', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alice Munro to Beam In For Night in New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atwood, Margaret', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gopnik, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Holly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munro, Alice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Amy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Symphony Space', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T18:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fab5fbd8-79b9-55c5-93be-21da3af00598', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fab5fbd8-79b9-55c5-93be-21da3af00598'}, {'abstract': 'After an awards ceremony marred by accusations that a member yelled abuse at the director of “12 Years a Slave,” the New York Film Critics Circle expelled a member, Armond White of City Arts. Another member, Lou Lumenick of The New York Post, was suspended for a year.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/armond-white-expelled-from-critics-group/', 'snippet': 'After an awards ceremony marred by accusations that a member yelled abuse at the director of “12 Years a Slave,” the New York Film Critics Circle expelled a member, Armond White of City Arts. Another member, Lou Lumenick of The New York Post, was ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 3:25 p.m. |  The New York Film Critics Circle took the rare step Monday of expelling Armond White, the film critic for CityArts, and of suspending the New York Post film critic Lou Lumenick for a year. The group confirmed the moves in a statement.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Armond White Expelled From Critics’ Group', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Film Critics Circle Expels Member', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Armond', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Film Critics Circle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T18:43:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6da461cd-1df6-5944-b1c9-03af1ba45e25', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6da461cd-1df6-5944-b1c9-03af1ba45e25'}, {'abstract': 'On “Post Tropical,” the Irish singer-songwriter throws out his acoustic sound in favor of hip-hop beats and ’90s soul. Here, he takes T on an audio tour of the making of his album.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/the-playlist-the-diverse-influential-sounds-behind-james-vincent-mcmorrows-sophomore-album/', 'snippet': 'On “Post Tropical,” the Irish singer-songwriter throws out his acoustic sound in favor of hip-hop beats and ’90s soul. Here, he takes T on an audio tour of the making of his album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Vincent McMorrow’s debut album, 2011’s “Early in the Morning,” was a promising, if sometimes frustrating, collection of indie folk songs — the kind of tuneful music one is likely to hear during the more earnest moments of a hit TV drama, or in a dimly lit pub. The Irish singer-songwriter’s full-length follow up, “Post Tropical,” out tomorrow on Vagrant Records, takes McMorrow’s intimate lyrics and hushed vocals and soaks them in ’90s R&B and early 2000s hip hop, often with stunning results. (For proof, listen to the epic “Red Dust,”\xa0in which McMorrow bares his soul over a thumping hip-hop beat before the song gives way to lush synths and a falsetto that calls to mind Jeff Buckley’s best work on “Grace.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/t-magazine/13oloizia-mcmorrow/13oloizia-mcmorrow-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/13/t-magazine/13oloizia-mcmorrow/13oloizia-mcmorrow-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/t-magazine/13oloizia-mcmorrow/13oloizia-mcmorrow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/t-magazine/13oloizia-mcmorrow/13oloizia-mcmorrow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/t-magazine/13oloizia-mcmorrow/13oloizia-mcmorrow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/13/t-magazine/13oloizia-mcmorrow/13oloizia-mcmorrow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/13/t-magazine/13oloizia-mcmorrow/13oloizia-mcmorrow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Playlist | The Diverse, Influential Sounds Behind James Vincent McMorrow’s Sophomore Album', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake (Rapper)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flying Lotus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Neil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T18:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc050239-320f-58c2-8425-567758f03a14', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc050239-320f-58c2-8425-567758f03a14'}, {'abstract': 'The travel site Expedia has added several feature for users, including one that recommends alternative itineraries.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/enhancements-for-expedia/', 'snippet': 'The travel site Expedia has added several feature for users, including one that recommends alternative itineraries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Expedia, the travel booking website, has stepped up its search game in recent weeks, adding three features to help travelers find — and organize — the best flights possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Enhancements for Expedia', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Expedia Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T18:51:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21313f7d-f527-51e1-ad96-905e44b73e9f', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21313f7d-f527-51e1-ad96-905e44b73e9f'}, {'abstract': 'The strategic imperative for the Japanese corporation is clear, as it is for just about any consumer goods company in the incredibly shrinking Japan, notes Rob Cox of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/a-bold-move-by-suntory/', 'snippet': 'The strategic imperative for the Japanese corporation is clear, as it is for just about any consumer goods company in the incredibly shrinking Japan, notes Rob Cox of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a Japanese corporation, Suntory Holdings has an especially aggressive corporate slogan: “Yatte Minahare,” which roughly translates as “Go for it.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bold Move by Suntory', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diageo PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pernod Ricard SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Suntory Holdings Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T19:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5336f796-a820-5b44-b0f7-41d963e6c409', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5336f796-a820-5b44-b0f7-41d963e6c409'}, {'abstract': 'The composer Ennio Morricone will conduct at concerts in Los Angeles and Brooklyn in March.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/a-sort-of-season-for-ennio-morricone/', 'snippet': 'The composer Ennio Morricone will conduct at concerts in Los Angeles and Brooklyn in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first part of 2014 is slowly shaping up as a low-key Ennio Morricone festival. The Italian composer, who turns 85 in November, is best known for his film scores — some 450 of them, including “The Good, the Bad and the Ugly,” with its unmistakable, undulating ocarina figure; and “The Untouchables” and “The Mission,” both packed with gripping, dramatic string writing. And though he conducts rarely in the United States (his last visit to New York was a Radio City concert in 2007), he will be leading a freelance orchestra and choir in two concerts in March — his Los Angeles conducting debut, at the Nokia Theater in on March 20, and a performance at Barclays Center in Brooklyn on March 23.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sort of Season for Ennio Morricone', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morricone, Ennio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T19:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c601e9eb-7b3f-5696-8c3c-768d2bba24c9', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c601e9eb-7b3f-5696-8c3c-768d2bba24c9'}, {'abstract': 'With American troops set to leave by the end of the year, worry is returning to the Panjshir Valley, a redoubt of Taliban opposition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/world/asia/afghan-panjshir-Valley.html', 'snippet': 'With American troops set to leave by the end of the year, worry is returning to the Panjshir Valley, a redoubt of Taliban opposition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAZARAK, Afghanistan — Even among Afghans, who are generally wary of outsiders, the members of the ethnic Tajik population of the Panjshir Valley are an unusually suspicious lot. So it is their good fortune to have been blessed with the closest thing to a naturally occurring “keep out” sign: a deep and narrow gorge at the valley’s mouth that seems tailor-made for obstruction and ambush.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/PANJSHIR/PANJSHIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/world/PANJSHIR/PANJSHIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/PANJSHIR/PANJSHIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/PANJSHIR/PANJSHIR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/PANJSHIR/PANJSHIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/world/PANJSHIR/PANJSHIR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/PANJSHIR/PANJSHIR-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recalling Past Threats, Afghans in Tranquil Valley Work to Keep It That Way', 'kicker': 'Bazarak Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recalling Past Threats, Afghans in Tranquil Valley Work to Keep It That Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panjshir Valley (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tajiks (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bazarak (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T19:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0a5c7d4-02ed-576f-87d1-5dd98f48e196', 'word_count': 1185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0a5c7d4-02ed-576f-87d1-5dd98f48e196'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Housing and Urban Development will investigate whether Gov. Chris Christie’s administration improperly spent federal money meant to encourage tourism after Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/nyregion/christie-faces-inquiry-into-use-of-hurricane-relief-money.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Housing and Urban Development will investigate whether Gov. Chris Christie’s administration improperly spent federal money meant to encourage tourism after Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal investigators have ordered an audit to determine whether Gov. Chris Christie’s administration improperly spent millions of dollars of relief meant to encourage tourists to visit New Jersey after the devastation of Hurricane Sandy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/14christie2_cnd/14christie2_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/14christie2_cnd/14christie2_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/14christie2_cnd/14christie2_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/14christie2_cnd/14christie2_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/14christie2_cnd/14christie2_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/14christie2_cnd/14christie2_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/14christie2_cnd/14christie2_cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Faces Audit Over Use of Hurricane Relief Money', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christie Faces Audit Over Use of Hurricane Relief Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T19:08:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41106ebc-b235-56b3-9193-4218dfeff0aa', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41106ebc-b235-56b3-9193-4218dfeff0aa'}, {'abstract': 'A $8.3 billion deal for the German pharmaceutical wholesaler failed to receive the minimum shareholder support, but McKesson did not say whether it would continue to try to acquire the company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/mckesson-comes-up-short-on-celesio-tender-offer/', 'snippet': 'A $8.3 billion deal for the German pharmaceutical wholesaler failed to receive the minimum shareholder support, but McKesson did not say whether it would continue to try to acquire the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The McKesson Corporation said on Monday that it had failed to receive the minimum shareholder support needed for its $8.3 billion acquisition of the German pharmaceutical wholesaler Celesio, despite a sweetened tender offer last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013