ssing boyfriend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/books/on-such-a-full-sea-chang-rae-lees-tale-of-dystopia.html', 'snippet': 'In Chang-rae Lee’s “On Such a Full Sea,” set in a future America divided into self-contained settlements, a 16-year-old goes in search of a missing boyfriend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chang-rae Lee’s new novel is part folk tale, part picaresque adventure, part dystopian satire. It signals a bold departure from both the carefully observed realism that distinguished Mr. Lee’s powerful earlier books “Aloft” (2004) and “A Gesture Life” (1999) — and the historical vistas of “The Surrendered” (2010). In eschewing one of his most potent gifts as a writer — his ability to map the inner lives of his characters with sympathy and precision — Mr. Lee has produced an ungainly and strangely inert novel. Instead of creating a palpably real flesh-and-blood heroine, he has chosen to center his book on an anime-like character named Fan; and instead of creating a fully imagined fictional realm (as Kazuo Ishiguro did in his bravura sci-fi-like novel, “Never Let Me Go,” from 2005), he’s dropped Fan into a futuristic world that seems at once overly familiar and unconvincing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/14BOOK/14BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/14BOOK/14BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 884}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/14BOOK/14BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 696, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/14BOOK/14BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/14BOOK/14BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/14BOOK/14BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/14BOOK/14BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sacrificing Gated Safety for a Lover and Herself', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sacrificing Gated Safety for a Lover and Herself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Chang-Rae', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'On Such a Full Sea (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T20:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ed28ac1-65b2-58d5-a052-0f1feb279cb6', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ed28ac1-65b2-58d5-a052-0f1feb279cb6'}, {'abstract': 'You may not associate the Loire Valley with game, but the hunt, especially for birds, is important in this region of France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/dining/quail-to-serve-with-loire-valley-reds.html', 'snippet': 'You may not associate the Loire Valley with game, but the hunt, especially for birds, is important in this region of France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may not associate the Loire Valley with game, but the hunt, especially for birds, is important in this region of France. I had that in mind when I decided on a seasonal preparation for quail to serve with the deliciously sturdy cabernet francs we tasted.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/dining/15PAIR/15PAIR-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/15/dining/15PAIR/15PAIR-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 634}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/dining/15PAIR/15PAIR-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 969, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/dining/15PAIR/15PAIR-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1876, 'width': 1774, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/dining/15PAIR/15PAIR-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/15/dining/15PAIR/15PAIR-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/dining/15PAIR/15PAIR-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quail to Serve With Loire Valley Reds'