h some relief from Western sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/world/middleeast/iran.html', 'snippet': 'Conservatives cautiously welcomed the completion of an interim agreement that would provide Tehran with some relief from Western sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iranian hard-liners on Monday cautiously welcomed the completion of an interim nuclear agreement that will provide Tehran with some relief from Western economic sanctions in return for a suspension of certain nuclear activities for six months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hard-Liners in Iran Offer Mild Praise for Interim Nuclear Agreement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hard-Liners in Iran Offer Mild Praise for Completed Interim Nuclear Agreement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasan, Mohammad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T21:06:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86c45b53-061b-593e-9c8a-60a8ab5dc622', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86c45b53-061b-593e-9c8a-60a8ab5dc622'}, {'abstract': 'A response to Noah Millman on atheism, religion and morality.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/of-new-atheists-and-noble-lies/', 'snippet': 'A response to Noah Millman on atheism, religion and morality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I began last week by responding to Jerry Coyne’s broadside against my Christmas column, so I suppose it’s fitting to begin this one by responding to Noah Millman’s lament that I need to “argue with better atheists,” instead of “weak combatants” like Coyne. My facile response to that line is that I’ll argue with better atheists when America’s flagship journal of liberal opinion publishes better atheists attacking things I’ve written; my more serious response is that my quarrel with atheism grows cooler and more modest the more serious (in my admittedly-biased view) the atheist in question. I’ll elaborate on that a bit below, but first, here’s Millman’s more serious complaint about my response to Coyne:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Of New Atheists and Noble Lies', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atheism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coyne, Jerry A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hart, David Bentley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConaughey, Matthew', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nagel, Thomas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alcoholics Anonymous', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T21:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bf68a70-a134-56a8-adc9-f47a1472ab0f', 'word_count': 1524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bf68a70-a134-56a8-adc9-f47a1472ab0f'}, {'abstract': 'Many saw the column as insensitive to a woman who has communicated about every aspect of the disease.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/readers-lash-out-about-bill-kellers-column-on-a-woman-with-cancer/', 'snippet': 'Many saw the column as insensitive to a woman who has communicated about every aspect of the disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Keller’s column in The Times on Monday about Lisa Bonchek Adams has generated a great deal of negative response. Xeni Jardin, the well-known writer who blogs on Boing Boing, sometimes about her own experience with cancer, was outraged, calling it bullying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Lash Out About Bill Keller’s Column on a Woman With Cancer', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-13T21:09:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfa55b7f-2dad-51c8-a6ce-d664bab80688', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfa55b7f-2dad-51c8-a6ce-d664bab80688'}, {'abstract': 'Julia Louis-Dreyfus and Leonardo DiCaprio played along; Jacqueline Bisset confounded.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/globes-highli