 significant setback to gay rights in Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tough ban on same-sex relationships that threatens violators with 14-year prison terms has been quietly signed into law by the president of Nigeria, Africa’s most populous nation, a step that rights advocates have long feared not only as a repression aimed at gays but as an affront to basic freedoms of speech and assembly. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/africa/14nigeria-img/14nigeria-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/world/africa/14nigeria-img/14nigeria-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 567}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/africa/14nigeria-img/14nigeria-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 968, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/africa/14nigeria-img/14nigeria-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1649, 'width': 1744, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/africa/14nigeria-img/14nigeria-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/world/africa/14nigeria-img/14nigeria-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/world/africa/14nigeria-img/14nigeria-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nigerian President Signs Ban on Same-Sex Relationships', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nigerian President Signs Ban on Same-Sex Relationships', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonathan, Goodluck', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T01:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ddb5517-6b01-5395-8212-cf82706e2b4a', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ddb5517-6b01-5395-8212-cf82706e2b4a'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Bradley transferred from Roma, of Italy’s Serie A, to Toronto F.C., of Major League Soccer — a move that subverted the conventional definition of success for an American soccer player.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/sports/soccer/bradley-invests-his-future-in-mls.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Bradley transferred from Roma, of Italy’s Serie A, to Toronto F.C., of Major League Soccer — a move that subverted the conventional definition of success for an American soccer player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last decade, Michael Bradley’s career path has seemed as pragmatic as one of his lateral passes, as persistently frontward as one of his box-to-box runs. It drove him along an ascendant path, to the top European leagues, to an indispensable role on the United States national team. But in recent days has come a dizzying improvisation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/sports/14bradleybw/14bradleybw-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/sports/14bradleybw/14bradleybw-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/sports/14bradleybw/14bradleybw-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/sports/14bradleybw/14bradleybw-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/sports/14bradleybw/14bradleybw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/sports/14bradleybw/14bradleybw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/sports/14bradleybw/14bradleybw-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Bigger Role, Bradley Invests His Future in M.L.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking Bigger Role, Bradley Invests His Future in M.L.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradley, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roma (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T01:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe08a569-df46-5d6a-b163-56368706e0d4', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe08a569-df46-5d6a-b163-56368706e0d4'}, {'abstract': 'With or without his approval, I was determined to write about my brother’s life as a mental patient.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/13/his-heart-my-sleeve-writing-about-my-brother/', 'snippet': 'With or without his approval, I was determined to write about my brother’s life as a mental patient.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On my 40th birthday, I began writing an essay about my brother, Robert, who, for the previous 16 years, had been in and out of mental hospitals. My intention was to write about his life as a patient, and also about the life he’d led before, when he was a bright, gifted young man who showed no signs, until his first breakdown at the age of 19, that any mental problems were likely or inevitable. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'His Heart, My Sleeve: Writing About My Brother', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T02:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Neugeboren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neugeboren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/942611f9-7879-5aab-90fb-7c0dc9eec915', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/942611f9-7879-5aab-90fb-7c0dc9eec915'}, {'abstract': 'What should today’s aspiring leaders do to pursue careers that lead to meaningful change?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/opinion/brooks-the-leadership-revival.html', 'snippet': 'What should today’s aspiring leaders do to pursue careers that lead to meaningful change?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are in politics or public life, you probably had some moment of spine-tingling transcendence. Maybe you read the Declaration of Independence or watched the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s mountaintop sermon, or read Nelson Mandela’s 1964 speech from the dock. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Brooks_New/Brooks_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Brooks_New/Brooks_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Brooks_New/Brooks_New-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Brooks_New/Brooks_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Brooks_New/Brooks_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Brooks_New/Brooks_New-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/09/16/opinion/Brooks_New/Brooks_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Leadership Revival', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Leadership Revival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T02:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/920fa956-70b3-5d16-b544-512325cd96bd', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/920fa956-70b3-5d16-b544-512325cd96bd'}, {'abstract': 'At least 29 people were killed as car bombs struck several Shiite neighborhoods in northern Baghdad on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/world/middleeast/iraq-deadly-bombings-erupt-in-baghdad.html', 'snippet': 'At least 29 people were killed as car bombs struck several Shiite neighborhoods in northern Baghdad on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least 29 people were killed as car bombs struck several Shiite neighborhoods in northern Baghdad on Monday. The deadliest bombing, in a market in the working-class Shaab neighborhood, killed at least 11 people, according to witnesses and officials. More than 8,000 Iraqis were killed last year as security deteriorated, and hundreds more have died this month. In recent days Sunni militants, including some linked to Al Qaeda, seized control of the western city of Falluja, challenging the authority of Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki. The violence on Monday coincided with a visit to Iraq by the United Nations secretary general, Ban Ki-moon, who appeared to scold Iraq’s political elites for not working together to “stop the senseless deaths of Iraqi women, children and men,” according to a text of his remarks on the United Nations website. “The challenges facing Iraq require all political leaders to fulfill their responsibilities to ensure social cohesion, dialogue and progress over political obstacles,” Mr. Ban said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Deadly Bombings Erupt in Baghdad', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Bombs Erupt in Baghdad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T02:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/146d808e-75fa-585c-b064-66266c1961a9', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/146d808e-75fa-585c-b064-66266c1961a9'}, {'abstract': 'It was called Ocean Village when Hurricane Sandy hit, leaving residents without heat or power. New owners made repairs, but some fear a new storm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/nyregion/despite-renovations-after-hurricane-unease-persists-in-the-rockaways.html', 'snippet': 'It was called Ocean Village when Hurricane Sandy hit, leaving residents without heat or power. New owners made repairs, but some fear a new storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The buildings are offset by the Atlantic, a pastiche of warm tones and cool grays, jutting balconies overlooking tranquil landscaped gardens and million-dollar views. The apartment complex is in the Arverne section of the Rockaway Peninsula; it looks as if it could be Boca Raton, Fla.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/oceanvillage1/oceanvillage1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/201