 there discovered a suspicious device in a backpack, officials said. Officials with the Katy Independent School District initially described it as a “potential explosive device,” but it was determined to be a homemade weapon known as a zip gun. An unidentified student was in custody, and a school spokesman said charges were pending. The fear of an explosive device prompted a large police response by the Harris County bomb squad, the F.B.I. and other agencies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: High School Is Evacuated', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: High School Is Evacuated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Manny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T04:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad84e9bf-699e-567d-8264-289eb52581e2', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad84e9bf-699e-567d-8264-289eb52581e2'}, {'abstract': 'New York is signing up enough young subscribers to make the insurance system viable, state senators were told at a hearing, but some enrollees have found problems in the program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/nyregion/mixed-reports-on-state-health-exchange.html', 'snippet': 'New York is signing up enough young subscribers to make the insurance system viable, state senators were told at a hearing, but some enrollees have found problems in the program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — New York is enrolling a significant number of young subscribers on its health insurance exchange, but many of those already enrolled have raised questions about rules that limit which doctors they can see, or are having problems finding out if their doctors are covered, according to testimony at a State Senate hearing on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/SUBEXCHANGE/SUBEXCHANGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/SUBEXCHANGE/SUBEXCHANGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/SUBEXCHANGE/SUBEXCHANGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/SUBEXCHANGE/SUBEXCHANGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/SUBEXCHANGE/SUBEXCHANGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/SUBEXCHANGE/SUBEXCHANGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/nyregion/SUBEXCHANGE/SUBEXCHANGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150