 the rules.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/injuries-to-domestic-helper-cast-light-on-abuses-in-hong-kong/', 'snippet': 'A human rights group says Indonesian domestic helpers are particularly subject to abuse in the territory because of lax enforcement of the rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An alleged beating of an Indonesian domestic helper by her Hong Kong employer has drawn new attention to the treatment of the hundreds of thousands of such workers in the territory, raising questions about whether the authorities are vigilant in preventing abuses in such cases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Injuries to Domestic Helper Cast Light on Abuses in Hong Kong', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Employment Agencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'South China Morning Post Limited', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T05:22:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d94785eb-92c3-56ed-9f53-9e7565eb7d80', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d94785eb-92c3-56ed-9f53-9e7565eb7d80'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Pastor, an aide under President Jimmy Carter, shepherded the 1977 Panama Canal treaties and was punished for it years later, when conservatives defeated his nomination to be an ambassador.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/us/politics/robert-pastor-66-dies-guided-panama-treaty.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Pastor, an aide under President Jimmy Carter, shepherded the 1977 Panama Canal treaties and was punished for it years later, when conservatives defeated his nomination to be an ambassador.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert A. Pastor, a White House aide under President Jimmy Carter who shepherded the 1977 Panama Canal treaties to ratification — and was punished for it 17 years later, when conservatives defeated his nomination to be ambassador to Panama — died on Wednesday at his home in Washington. He was 66.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/PASTOR-obit/PASTOR-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/us/PASTOR-obit/PASTOR-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 500}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/PASTOR-obit/PASTOR-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/PASTOR-obit/PASTOR-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 870, 'width': 1045, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/PASTOR-obit/PASTOR-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/us/PASTOR-obit/PASTOR-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/us/PASTOR-obit/PASTOR-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Pastor, 66, Dies; Guided Panama Treaty for Carter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robert Pastor, 66; Guided Panama Treaty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Douglas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pastor, Robert A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama Canal and Canal Zone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T05:37:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ef012ac-154f-5050-a641-251e7f53c932', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ef012ac-154f-5050-a641-251e7f53c932'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie’s State of the State address on Tuesday comes days after his last turn at the podium, when he accepted responsibility for his staff’s role in closing traffic lanes on the George Washington Bridge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/nyregion/governor-hopes-speech-will-obscure-a-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie’s State of the State address on Tuesday comes days after his last turn at the podium, when he accepted responsibility for his staff’s role in closing traffic lanes on the George Washington Bridge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a political high-wire act, Gov. Chris Christie will try on Tuesday to refocus attention from a controversy over a vindictive traffic jam to the day-to-day work of governing, by outlining plans to extend the school day, lower taxes for homeowners and reduce urban crime.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Governor Hopes Speech Will Obscure a Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Governor Hopes Speech Will Obscure a Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T05:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea42491c-ef48-5bed-97f0-621fe857117d', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea42491c-ef48-5bed-97f0-621fe857117d'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Esquire) FRIDAY NIGHT TYKES There’s no quitting in football. But there’s plenty of blood, sweat and tears when you’re a baby linebacker exhausted in 99-degree heat, and the coach orders you to bear-crawl across the field. “I don’t care how much pain you’re in!” Charles Chavarria, a former Marine, bellows at his team, the Junior Broncos. “You don’t quit!” This new reality show follows five San Antonio teams of 8- and 9-year-olds as they try to pass, run and tackle their way to the top of the Texas Youth Football Association, where ranting coaches, obsessive parents and helmet-to-helmet hits are de rigueur. “Sometimes, parents say I may be crossing a little bit of a line,” Mr. Chavarria says. “They need to toughen up. If you don’t push your kids, you’re accepting failure.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e618aa0d-05e8-5de5-a7d1-a1f8b9c1bb32', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e618aa0d-05e8-5de5-a7d1-a1f8b9c1bb32'}, {'abstract': 'The blaze in the Chinese province of Yunnan, in an area said to be the inspiration for the novel “Lost Horizon,” badly damaged or destroyed 343 structures and left about 2,600 people homeless, the local government said.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/electrical-problem-blamed-in-shangri-la-fire/', 'snippet': 'The blaze in the Chinese province of Yunnan, in an area said to be the