not look forward to understanding the inner workings of her character, the sadistic Mistress Epps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Accepting the award for best drama at the Golden Globes, the “12 Years a Slave” director Steve McQueen called Sarah Paulson “the Bette Davis of America.” Ms. Paulson is a theater, film and television veteran, most recently seen in the FX series “American Horror Story.” In “12 Years,” she plays the wife of Michael Fassbender’s sadistic plantation owner; her character, Mistress Epps, has some sadistic streaks of her own, which perhaps seem even crueler judged against her gender.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/paulson/paulson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/paulson/paulson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 964}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/paulson/paulson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 638, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/paulson/paulson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1275, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/paulson/paulson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/paulson/paulson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/arts/paulson/paulson-thumbLar