uri': 'nyt://article/5fdea22f-712d-54f8-9a8d-2ddc6c61894d'}, {'abstract': 'To avoid handing over their personal information, some readers said they feign deafness, act crazy, or hand over a fake email address belonging to their dog, or Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/feigning-deafness-giving-your-dogs-email-and-other-reader-tips-to-thwart-privacy-grubbers/', 'snippet': 'To avoid handing over their personal information, some readers said they feign deafness, act crazy, or hand over a fake email address belonging to their dog, or Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After venting my frustrations with an (admittedly very sweet) cashier lady and the entire data mining industry last Friday, I was thrilled to hear from hundreds of simpatico readers who had experienced similar, frustrating encounters\xa0and a few who weren’t afraid to administer some digital justice of their own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/business/14bits-dogemail/14bits-dogemail-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/business/14bits-dogemail/14bits-dogemail-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/business/14bits-dogemail/14bits-dogemail-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/business/14bits-dogemail/14bits-dogemail-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': No