was a lot of talk about the meaning of words at the Supreme Court — like “the,” “recess,” and “happen”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/recess-appointments-in-the-eye-of-the-beholder/', 'snippet': 'There was a lot of talk about the meaning of words at the Supreme Court — like “the,” “recess,” and “happen”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a lot of talk about the meaning of words at the Supreme Court on Monday — not exciting words like “life,” “liberty,” or “equality,” but more pedestrian words, like “the,” “recess,” and “happen” — as the justices considered for the first time what, exactly, the recess-appointments clause of the Constitution actually allows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s a ‘Recess’ Appointment?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T18:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe80de28-bd30-5922-a49e-ec5b0e73b5b8', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe80de28-bd30-5922-a49e-ec5b0e73b5b8'}, {'abstract': 'Egyptians lined up to vote on a new constitution under the watch of the security forces and military leadership of Gen. Abdel Fattah el-Sisi. A bomb exploded early in the day, but no one was injured.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000002649788/voting-under-heavy-security-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Egyptians lined up to vote on a new consti