ction_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b68af2-a1cf-5af0-a06b-04e122367ee8', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b68af2-a1cf-5af0-a06b-04e122367ee8'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/the-gun-report-january-14-2014/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Democratic Rep. Leslie Combs, a state representative from Kentucky, accidentally fired a gun in her Capitol Annex office. A House colleague, who was present at the time, said she was emptying a semi-automatic handgun and, thinking it was empty, pointed it away and down and pulled the trigger. No bullet fragments traveled outside the office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: January 14, 2014', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T19:05:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fea7075f-2dba-5a2e-9112-96dd6b8f9d74', 'word_count': 1818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fea7075f-2dba-5a2e-9112-96dd6b8f9d74'}, {'abstract': 'The use of temporary workers is a focus of labor activists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/automobiles/autoshow/protests-over-mississippi-plant-follow-nissan-to-detroit.html', 'snippet': 'The use of temporary workers is a focus of labor activists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Labor activists are using the larger stage of the North American International Auto Show to highlight complaints about conditions at Nissan’s plant in Canton, Miss. Before dawn on Monday, demonstrators from the United Automobile Workers stood in front of Cobo Center, where the show was being held, carrying yellow signs reading, “Tell Nissan: Labor rights are civil rights.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Over Mississippi Plant Follow Nissan to Detroit', 'kicker': 'Detroit Auto Show', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Automobile Workers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T19:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamara Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ca4f27-3206-51ef-9a1b-990400431ce0', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ca4f27-3206-51ef-9a1b-990400431ce0'}, {'abstract': 'The continuing debate over military spending originated as a debate over whether America should have a military at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/us/politics/despite-growing-military-budget-an-undercurrent-of-skepticism.html', 'snippet': 'The continuing debate over military spending originated as a debate over whether America should have a military at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The continuing debate over military spending originated as a debate, at the time of the nation’s founding, over whether America should have a military at all. At the time even conservatives like John Adams and Alexander Hamilton, both partial to strong central government, had their doubts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Despite Growing Military Budget, an Undercurrent of Skepticism', 'kicker': 'Think Back', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T19:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Tanenhaus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanenhaus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e1e7c9-49f4-5fdb-ad9f-1897b8c78fae', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e1e7c9-49f4-5fdb-ad9f-1897b8c78fae'}, {'abstract': 'In new report, Sotheby’s is defending the authenticity of an ancient calligraphy school that it sold to a Chinese collector in September.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/sothebys-report-defends-chinese-scroll-it-sold-as-authentic/', 'snippet': 'In new report, Sotheby’s is defending the authenticity of an ancient calligraphy school that it sold to a Chinese collector in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — Sotheby’s said Tuesday that an ancient calligraphy scroll the auction house sold in September for $