://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/world/africa/tunisian-constitution-praised-for-balance-nears-passage.html', 'snippet': 'Legislators across the political spectrum and human rights groups hailed the charter, considered one of the most liberal in an Arab nation, as a triumph of consensus politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS — Tunisia’s National Constituent Assembly is close to passing a new Constitution that legislators across the political spectrum, human rights organizations and constitutional experts are hailing as a triumph of consensus politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/world/15tunisia/15tunisia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/15/world/15tunisia/15tunisia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/world/15tunisia/15tunisia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/world/15tunisia/15tunisia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/world/15tunisia/15tunisia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/15/world/15tunisia/15tunisia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/world/15tunisia/15tunisia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisian Constitution, Praised for Balance, Nears Passage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ennahda Party (Tunisia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T20:02:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Gall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ff17dd1-3921-5bd9-af87-537d5dfe3536', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ff17dd1-3921-5bd9-af87-537d5dfe3536'}, {'abstract': 'Or at least one night: heroes are the theme of the Oscars telecast, the producers announced.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/heroes-just-for-one-day/', 'snippet': 'Or at least one night: heroes are the theme of the Oscars telecast, the producers announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Three of the top five grossing movies of 2013 involved superheroes — men in tights or high-tech suits or women who know their way around weaponry. (That’s “Man of Steel,” “Iron Man 3” and the No. 1 grossing film, “The Hunger Games: Catching Fire.”) On Tuesday, the Academy announced that the theme for this year’s Oscars is movie heroes. Coincidence? Do you also believe bridges close for no reason? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heroes, Just for One Day', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meron, Neil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zadan, Craig', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T20:07:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93603876-1858-5ec0-aa12-335dd9026fb6', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93603876-1858-5ec0-aa12-335dd9026fb6'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s New Orleans Jazz & Heritage Festival will run from April 25 through 27 and May 1 through 4.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/springsteen-and-clapton-to-headline-new-orleans-jazz-festival/', 'snippet': 'This year’s New Orleans Jazz & Heritage Festival will run from April 25 through 27 and May 1 through 4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Springsteen and the E Street Band, Eric Clapton, Phish and Christina Aguilera are among the artists who will headline this year’s New Orleans Jazz & Heritage Festival, its organizers said on Tuesday. The festival, which is celebrating its 45th anniversary and will be held at the Fair Grounds Race Course from April 25 through 27 and May 1 through 4, will also feature the Canadian indie-rock ensemble Arcade Fire (which will be fresh off its earlier headlining slot at the Coachella festival in California), as well as performers like Robin Thicke, Vampire Weekend, Robert Plant, Trey Songz, Public Enemy and Chaka Khan. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Springsteen and Clapton to Headline New Orleans Jazz Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jazz Festival Lands Springsteen and Clapton', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapton, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T20:14:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66f568ca-0078-5ef6-87cb-230c330af43e', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66f568ca-0078-5ef6-87cb-230c330af43e'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans are trying to direct attention away from Christie.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/bridgegate-benghazi-and-the-i-r-s-scandals-compared/', 'snippet': 'Republicans are trying to direct attention away from Christie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans with the unenviable task of defending Chris Christie seem to have been given talking points of the “yeah, but what about…” variety. Over the last few days, many have tried to downplay the politically motivated traffic jam by comparing it to Benghazi and the allegation that the Internal Revenue Service “targeted” conservative groups.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bridgegate, Benghazi and the I.R.S. ‘Scandals,’ Compared', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo