-f5ba-5081-8fc3-4dc6055128b8'}, {'abstract': 'Leslie Morgan Steiner’s book is a captivating exploration of the experience and ethics of surrogacy, and one of my favorite books about family from 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/motherlode-must-read-the-baby-chase-how-surrogacy-is-transforming-the-american-family/', 'snippet': 'Leslie Morgan Steiner’s book is a captivating exploration of the experience and ethics of surrogacy, and one of my favorite books about family from 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Baby Chase: How Surrogacy Is Transforming the American Family,” by Leslie Morgan Steiner, was among the best books on family from 2013. I’ve been meaning to share it with you for some time, and Amy Klein’s post about donor eggs (“Would a Pregnancy Through a Donor Egg Feel Like ‘Mine’?”) and the resulting discussion of the medicine and ethics of egg donation, and in particular overseas egg donation, provided a perfect opportunity. If you’re at all curious about egg donation and surrogacy (in fact, if you’re just a curious reader at all), “The Baby Chase” makes a fascinating read. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/style/motherlode-baby-chase/motherlode-baby-chase-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 186, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/style/motherlode-baby-chase/motherlode-baby-chase-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 186, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/style/motherlode-baby-chase/motherlode-baby-chase-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'im