erial': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2ffa4e0-e253-5411-b661-ac10d8dc47f0', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2ffa4e0-e253-5411-b661-ac10d8dc47f0'}, {'abstract': '“Generation War,” a film about early-1940s Germany, is notable for what it includes and for what it leaves out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/movies/generation-war-adds-a-glow-to-a-german-era.html', 'snippet': '“Generation War,” a film about early-1940s Germany, is notable for what it includes and for what it leaves out.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Generation War,” which was broadcast as a mini-series on German television last year, is perhaps more interesting as an artifact of the present than as a representation of the past. As the Second World War slips from living memory, as Germany asserts its dominant role in Europe with increasing confidence, and as long-suppressed information emerges from the archives of former Eastern bloc countries, the war’s cultural significance for Germans has shifted. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A History Lesson, Airbrushed', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A History Lesson, Airbrushed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kadelbach, Philipp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T22:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a061209-c2da-56a5-9731-e2a577e36996', 'word_count': 1206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a061209-c2da-56a5-9731-e2a577e36996'}, {'abstract': 'Shostakovich’s wartime Symphony No. 7 was performed Monday evening at a benefit concert for humanitarian aid to Syria at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/arts/music/shostakovich-for-the-children-of-syria-a-benefit-concert.html', 'snippet': 'Shostakovich’s wartime Symphony No. 7 was performed Monday evening at a benefit concert for humanitarian aid to Syria at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Context may not be everything in music but it can count for a lot. And the context for a performance of Shostakovich’s imposing wartime Symphony No. 7 (“Leningrad”) at Carnegie Hall on Monday evening was cryptically hailed in its title: “Shostakovich for the Children of Syria.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/shostakovich/shostakovich-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/shostakovich/shostakovich-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 290}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/shostakovich/shostakovich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/shostakovich/shostakovich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 990, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/shostakovich/shostakovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/shostakovich/shostakovich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumb