s the web for interesting and peculiar items.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Competing With North Korea on Credit Card Security', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T23:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fa5ff64-797f-5fa0-b161-07f01ff88a58', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fa5ff64-797f-5fa0-b161-07f01ff88a58'}, {'abstract': 'Co-founded by Ben Lovett of Mumford & Sons, the London-New York label has become a global tastemaker, as evidenced by its popular new club nights in various U.S. cities. Check out Lovett’s exclusive playlist of his favorite Communion offerings.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/14/listen-up-the-lofty-ambitions-of-communion-records/', 'snippet': 'Co-founded by Ben Lovett of Mumford & Sons, the London-New York label has become a global tastemaker, as evidenced by its popular new club nights in various U.S. cities. Check out Lovett’s exclusive playlist of his favorite Communion offerings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Tuesday, Ben Lovett, the London-born, New York-based co-founder of the record label and events company Communion, pondered the soon-to-be-packed floor of the Rockwood Music Hall on the Lower East Side. “It makes me feel quite old,” the 27-year-old said. “When you’re 19, you just sort of have limitless energy.” That’s how old he was in 2006, when he launched Communion in its earliest form as a club night in Notting Hill, London. A year later, he also co-founded the folk-rock band Mumford & Sons, which soon became a Grammy-winning touring juggernaut. Meanwhile, Communion has evolved into a promotions giant and global musical tastemaker with a presence in both London and New York. It’s enough to make anyone feel stretched.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | The Lofty Ambitions of Communion Records', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiwanuka, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rockwood Music Hall', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-14T23:26:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/828c1dc3-962f-5dfc-b1ec-add61