ne, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90205946-f9ce-5842-a558-459cf880082a', 'word_count': 1375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90205946-f9ce-5842-a558-459cf880082a'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats who endorsed Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey received big financial payouts for their towns; Democrats who did not suffered reprisals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/opinion/the-christie-way.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats who endorsed Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey received big financial payouts for their towns; Democrats who did not suffered reprisals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey tried to change the subject on Tuesday with his annual State of the State speech, talking about longer school days and reducing urban crime. But there is no diverting attention from the unanswered questions about how Mr. Christie and his close advisers have used his office to mete out rewards or punishment for political reasons. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Christie Way', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Christie Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '