omo and his aides keep repeating: It’s a New Jersey issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo of New York is not one to shy away from a political fight. But in the case of the scandal engulfing Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey over retaliatory lane closings at the George Washington Bridge, Mr. Cuomo and his aides have kept to a simple mantra from the beginning: This was and remains a New Jersey issue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Saying Little on Bridge Scandal ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Saying Little on Bridge Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T03:11:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan and Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bced603d-d522-5c01-93ae-a72e24e10d31', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bced603d-d522-5c01-93ae-a72e24e10d31'}, {'abstract': 'Sixty-two multifaith groups urged the Senate to delay a vote, while supporters of the bill pointed to what they called Iran’s insincerity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/world/middleeast/lobbying-picks-up-over-bill-to-toughen-antinuclear-sanctions-against-iran.html', 'snippet': 'Sixty-two multifaith groups urged the Senate to delay a vote, while supporters of the bill pointed to what they called Iran’s insincerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Partisans in the debate over a Senate bill that would threaten onerous new antinuclear sanctions on Iran escalated their lobbying on Tuesday, with critics submitting a letter to lawmakers signed by 62 multifaith organizations urging a delay and supporters pointing to what they called Iran’s insincerity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lobbying Picks Up Over Bill to Toughen Antinuclear Sanctions Against Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lobbying Picks Up Over Bill to Toughen Antinuclear Sanctions Against Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menendez, Robert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirk, Mark Steven', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T03:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, '