f891a-b98e-55f8-b4e7-8b441fcb095c'}, {'abstract': 'The eviction of migrant Roma squatters by French authorities doubled from the year prior in 2013, according to a report by rights groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/world/europe/france-roma-evictions-increase.html', 'snippet': 'The eviction of migrant Roma squatters by French authorities doubled from the year prior in 2013, according to a report by rights groups.', 'lead_paragraph': ' French authorities sharply accelerated the eviction of migrant Roma squatters in 2013, razing the unauthorized encampments of nearly 20,000 Roma, according to a report by rights groups on Tuesday. The evictions were double those of 2012, according to the French Human Rights League and the European Roma Rights Center. President François Hollande took office in 2012 pledging to break with the strict policies of his predecessor, Nicolas Sarkozy. But Mr. Hollande has reinforced those policies, demolishing at least 165 Roma camps last year, according to the report. French officials did not respond to requests for comment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Roma Evictions Increase', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Roma Evictions Increase', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Romani People', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evictions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T03:42:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e05bf1c0-ce6a-50e0-81a9-f867f6940374', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e05bf1c0-ce6a-50e0-81a9-f867f6940374'}, {'abstract': 'The head of the United Nations peacekeeping mission said that 8,000 fighters affiliated with a variety of armed factions had surrendered since the M23 rebel group was routed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/world/africa/congo-fighters-quit-un-says.html', 'snippet': 'The head of the United Nations peacekeeping mission said that 8,000 fighters affiliated with a variety of armed factions had surrendered since the M23 rebel group was routed.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The head of the United Nations peacekeeping mission in the Democratic Republic of Congo said Tuesday that 8,000 fighters affiliated with a variety of armed factions had surrendered since the M23 rebel group was routed in November. Among them are the Hutu militias that Rwanda holds responsible for the genocide 20 years ago. Martin Kobler, the United Nations’ special representative for Congo, said about 50 members of a Hutu group, Democratic Forces for the Liberation of Rwanda, had surrendered in each of the last two months alone, steadily diminishing what he said was a 1,800-strong force. He said his peacekeepers were focused on rooting out the rest, but warned that the group was not likely to be eliminated by military means alone. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congo: Fighters Quit, U.N. Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congo: Fighters Quit, U.N. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'March 23 Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T03:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/207a0040-8dbb-540e-a697-ff10b1e96c53', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/207a0040-8dbb-540e-a697-ff10b1e96c53'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Robles, an American weight lifter who became a crowd favorite at the 2012 Summer Games in London, received a two-year suspension after testing positive for a banned substance, Usada announced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/sports/american-weight-lifter-is-suspended.html', 'snippet': 'Sarah Robles, an American weight lifter who became a crowd favorite at the 2012 Summer Games in London, received a two-year suspension after testing positive for a banned substance, Usada announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Robles, an American weight lifter who became a crowd favorite at the 2012 Summer Games in London, received a two-year suspension after testing positive for a banned substance, Usada announced.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Weight Lifter Is Suspended', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Weight Lifting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Is Suspended', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pilon, Mary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'va