 feared drinking and cooking with it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/us/return-to-normal-in-parts-of-west-virginia-is-marred-by-distrust.html', 'snippet': 'Even as some 39,000 customers had received the all-clear signal by Tuesday, after a chemical spill last week contaminated tap water, many feared drinking and cooking with it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, W.Va. — The water was back on, but the anxiety had not shut off.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Return to Normal in Parts of West Virginia Is Marred by Distrust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Return to Normal in Parts of West Virginia Is Marred by Distrust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriel, Trip', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'West Virginia American Water Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eastman Chemical Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Elk River (W Va)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T04:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ec94bb6-6eff-50ee-917c-51059c3d31c5', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ec94bb6-6eff-50ee-917c-51059c3d31c5'}, {'abstract': 'In the end, cost-benefit analysis drives policy change more than economic research does, and the change from conscription to an army of enlistees is an example, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/ideas-costs-and-the-all-volunteer-army/', 'snippet': 'In the end, cost-benefit analysis drives policy change more than economic research does, and the change from conscription to an army of enlistees is an example, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago. He is the author of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ideas, Costs and the All-Volunteer Army', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Becker, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shleifer, Andrei', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T05:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5183e7eb-e78a-57b8-b790-922d58fc1c5a', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5183e7eb-e78a-57b8-b790-922d58fc1c5a'}, {'abstract': 'Those who race 50 to 100 miles at a time or longer tend to be older and have different health concerns than most of us might expect, new research shows.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/what-ultra-marathons-do-to-our-bodies/', 'snippet': 'Those who race 50 to 100 miles at a time or longer tend to be older and have different health concerns than most of us might expect, new research shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ultra-runners are different from you and me. They run more. But a new study of these racers, who compete in events longer than marathons, joins other recent science in finding that they also tend to be older and have some different health concerns than most of us might expect, suggesting that some beliefs about how much activity the human body can manage, especially in middle age, may be too narrow. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/health/15well_physed/15well_physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/15/health/15well_physed/15well_physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/health/15well_physed/15well_physed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/health/15well_physed/15well_physed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/health/15well_physed/15well_physed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb