nging report by the Senate Intelligence Committee released Wednesday concluded that the attack 16 months ago that killed four Americans in Benghazi, Libya, could have been prevented, singling out the State Department for criticism for its failure to bolster security in response to intelligence warnings about a growing security crisis around the city.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/world/16benghazi1/16benghazi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/world/16benghazi1/16benghazi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/world/16benghazi1/16benghazi1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/world/16benghazi1/16benghazi1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/world/16benghazi1/16benghazi1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/16/world/16benghazi1/16benghazi1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/world/16benghazi1/16benghazi1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Benghazi Attack Called Avoidable in Senate Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Benghazi Attack Called Avoidable in Senate Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzetti, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Intelligence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, J Christopher', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ham, Carter F', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Patrick F', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Innocence of Muslims (Movie)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T16:43:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti, Eric Schmitt and David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27b5556a-6a37-5f1a-92da-418105b35eaf', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27b5556a-6a37-5f1a-92da-418105b35eaf'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Tribute Artist,” Charles Busch plays a female impersonator whose landlady dies, leaving an opportunity to take on her identity — and her townhouse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/theater/location-location-impersonation.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Tribute Artist,” Charles Busch plays a female impersonator whose landlady dies, leaving an opportunity to take on her identity — and her townhouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alongside winning the lottery and buying a gorgeous full-floor penthouse perched alongside Central Park, acquiring a Greenwich Village townhouse at a steal must rank among a New Yorker’s real-estate fantasies. In “The Tribute Artist,” a new comedy by Charles Busch, known for his riotous, gender-bending farces, like “Vampire Lesbians of Sodom” and “The Divine Sister,” he plays a female impersonator whose landlady dies, leaving an opportunity to take on her identity — and her townhouse. The plan naturally hits some snags and leads to further nutty scheming.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19SUBGUIDE6/19SUBGUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19SUBGUIDE6/19SUBGUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 801}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19SUBGUIDE6/19SUBGUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19SUBGUIDE6/19SUBGUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg