This year’s Live Ideas Festival in Chelsea will present readings and multi-disciplinary performances inspired by the life and work of James Baldwin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Live Arts, the performance group based in Chelsea, describes its specialty as “movement-based artistry.” Given the group’s history — it was founded after a merger between the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Dance Company and Dance Theater Workshop, and Mr. Jones is its executive artistic director — “movement-based artistry” is usually taken to mean dance. But last year, Live Arts expanded into multidisciplinary performance with its first Live Ideas Festival, built around the work of Dr. Oliver Sacks, the neurologist and author.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Festival to Celebrate the Work of James Baldwin', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, James (1924-87)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T17:18:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/633c9ddd-9d7f-56c9-98ef-95ba76e5dadb', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/633c9ddd-9d7f-56c9-98ef-95ba76e5dadb'}, {'abstract': 'What is it really like to go the Academy Awards show? Melena Ryzik asked some annual Oscar attendees about their most mem