, a week of performances of “Giselle” at the Kennedy Center (May 20 through 25). First cast (May 20 and 22) are the Bolshoi’s prima, Svetlana Zakharova, and David Hallberg, the American star who joined the Bolshoi in 2011. Mr. Hallberg’s debut performance then, broadcast live internationally, was as Ms. Zakharova’s partner in “The Sleeping Beauty.” The April 20 performance will be his first performance on American soil as a member of the celebrated Russian company.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bolshoi Names Cast for First Part of American Tour', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bolshoi Announces American Tour Casting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hallberg, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zakharova, Svetlana (Dancer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T18:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e1a5949-8862-558e-9a72-485cce9ea94a', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e1a5949-8862-558e-9a72-485cce9ea94a'}, {'abstract': 'Davis, who was virtually assured an Olympic spot in 2010 before he crashed an A.T.V., hopes to reach the Games on his third try.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/sports/snowboarder-danny-davis-sochi-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'Davis, who was virtually assured an Olympic spot in 2010 before he crashed an A.T.V., hopes to reach the Games on his third try.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COPPER MOUNTAIN, Colo. — Danny Davis has been through it all before, and before that, too. As the top American snowboarders converge on the Mammoth Mountain ski area in California this week to decide who will compete next month in Sochi, Russia, the Winter Olympics are within Davis’s reach for the third time. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/sports/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/sports/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/sports/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/sports/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/sports/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/16/sports/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/sports/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Snowboarder Danny Davis’s Ambivalent Comeback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olympics? Sure, Why Not?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snowboarding', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Danny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T18:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb21ddd2-4552-5046-8ffe-978b7abff6c0', 'word_count': 1290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb21ddd2-4552-5046-8ffe-978b7abff6c0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Nesbo’s retelling will be part of the Hogarth Shakespeare series.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/jo-nesbo-to-write-updated-macbeth/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Nesbo’s retelling will be part of the Hogarth Shakespeare series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jo Nesbo’s best-selling series of thrillers has made the detective Harry Hole a famous name. Now Mr. Nesbo will turn his attention to a name with 400 years of history behind it: He will write a new version of “Macbeth” for Hogarth Shakespeare, a series that will feature contemporary authors retelling Shakespeare plays, beginning in 2016.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/books/15nesbo/15nesbo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 351, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/books/15nesbo/15nesbo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 351, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/books/15nesbo/15nesbo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/15/books/15nesbo/15nesbo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/books/15nesbo/15nesbo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jo Nesbo to Write Updated ‘Macbeth’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nesbo, Jo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T18:13:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0283be4c-b382-5d44-9b02-d42f4495b92c', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0283be4c-b382-5d44-9b02-d42f4495b92c'}, {'abstract': 'The Iranian-American artist Andisheh Avini layers references to his heritage with Pop Art influences and bold swaths of color.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/on-view-in-a-gagosian-gallerists-personal-work-cultures-collide/', 'snippet': 'The Iranian-American artist Andisheh Avini layers references to his heritage with Pop Art influences and bold swaths of color.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every so often, boxes bedecked with Iranian postage and customs stamps arrive at Andisheh Avini’s doorstep. He can instantly recognize the packages as containing handcrafted marquetry panels from a traditional woodworker in Iran, but, though he ordered them himself, couldn’t tell you what they look like. That’s because when he commissions the works a month before they arrive, his only instructions are their dimensions. The rest — the size and pattern of the decorative inlay on the lacquered wood boards, which are typically used for interior decor — is left to the maker, whom Avini has never met in person. This inscrutability is an essential part of the artist’s process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/t-magazine/14avini-bellman/14avini-bellman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/14/t-magazine/14avini-bellman/14avini-bellman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 311}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/t-magazine/14avini-bellman/14avini-bellman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 531, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/t-magazine/14avini-bellman/14avini-bellman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1309, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/14/t-magazine/14avini-bellman/14avini-bellman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/14/t-magazine/14avini-bellman/14avini-bellman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cr