-5957-841b-658760fe45db', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61620ad3-2b45-5957-841b-658760fe45db'}, {'abstract': 'As he awaits word of whether he will get an acting nomination for “All Is Lost,” he talks about challenges — with the role and with the festival he started 30 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/15/robert-redford-would-like-a-visitor-or-two-at-sundance/', 'snippet': 'As he awaits word of whether he will get an acting nomination for “All Is Lost,” he talks about challenges — with the role and with the festival he started 30 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Somehow, Robert Redford is a dark horse as a best actor candidate this season. Though his performance in “All Is Lost” drew some of the best reviews of his career, Mr. Redford was passed over for a nomination by his colleagues in the Screen Actors Guild (whose winners will be announced on Saturday), and lost the prize at the Golden Globes to Matthew McConaughey earlier this week. Whether he will get an Oscar nomination on Thursday is an open question among awards-watchers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/redford/redford-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/redford/redford-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 848}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/redford/redford-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/15/arts/redford/redford-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1450, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'su