tlebot: Dorsey on Disrupting Receipts, and Implications of the Net Neutrality Ruling', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T22:52:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/418bbc58-d42b-5883-abb5-fe4e3cec9e0f', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/418bbc58-d42b-5883-abb5-fe4e3cec9e0f'}, {'abstract': 'Touring again after a 15-year hiatus, Neutral Milk Hotel drew a crowd in Jersey City more than willing to be baffled all over again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/arts/music/reunited-neutral-milk-hotel-plays-in-jersey-city.html', 'snippet': 'Touring again after a 15-year hiatus, Neutral Milk Hotel drew a crowd in Jersey City more than willing to be baffled all over again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERSEY CITY — After a 15-year absence, the reunited Neutral Milk Hotel could have satisfied its fans at the Loew’s Jersey Theater here on Tuesday night with a rote run-through of the music it recorded in the 1990s. But the band did more than that: It revved up and magnified all the impulses that collide in Jeff Mangum’s songs, which have continued to collect and baffle fans since Neutral Milk Hotel released its last studio album, “In the Aeroplane Over the Sea,” in 1998. The band used to play clubs; now it is headlining sold-out theaters. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 482}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1644, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/NEUTRAL/NEUTRAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unkempt Yet Profound, a Cult Band Returns for More Interpretation', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unkempt yet Profound, a Cult Band Returns for More Interpretation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mangum, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neutral Milk Hotel (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-15T22:52:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materia