, 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/fashion/Pants-jeans-Longchamp-bag.html', 'snippet': 'Six essentials to help give your denim a rest; Longchamp celebrates the Year of the Horse; the jeweler Melissa Joy Manning opens a New York store; minimalist sneakers at Dover Street Market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, jeans are over? It was announced last week that Gwen Stefani was collaborating with Michael Glasser, the man behind 7 for All Mankind and other denim labels, on a line of nondenim pants, the aim being to replace the jeans in our closets with casual, sort-of-slouchy trousers. Unlikely as it is that we’ll be jettisoning our jeans anytime soon, it could be said that, in 2014, they do look a little ... safe. Should you want to give your precious denim a break, here are our six style essentials: 1. black trousers with a bit of souped-up detail, like this Acne pair with knee patches, to wear interchangeably with black jeans; 2. prints that could be crazy vacation pants but also cool with a big sweater and parka on the weekend; 3. leather in a new relaxed shape; 4. pants in an unexpected color, for work and beyond; 5. cropped pants to wear with heels (a little ankle is always sexy); and 6. a chic pair of white pants, for evening.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/fashion/16BROWSE1-copy1/16BROWSE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/fashion/16BROWSE1-copy1/16BROWSE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 845}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/fashion/16BROWSE1-copy1/16BROWSE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'supe