e': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41573d3f-3dc9-58b0-b265-9efb11864117', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41573d3f-3dc9-58b0-b265-9efb11864117'}, {'abstract': 'Maison Martin Margiela’s latest trompe l’oeil wallcovering looks very much like a staircase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/garden/look-before-you-climb.html', 'snippet': 'Maison Martin Margiela’s latest trompe l’oeil wallcovering looks very much like a staircase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maison Martin Margiela, the Paris-based fashion house founded by the reclusive Belgian designer, who parted ways with the business in 2009, has an idiosyncratic, avant-garde style that can go anywhere. Collaborating with L’Atelier d’Exercices, a French company, the design team is producing objects for the home that mix irony, mystery and humor, such as eggs filled with fortune-cookie-type messages and a melted wax candleholder. One of the group’s favored memes is trompe l’oeil, and it has created a series of black-and-white photographs of architectural details, which are printed on an easily repositioned adhesive fabric. The latest, an atmospheric staircase, would add wit and misdirection to any room and bring a new dimension to a cramped studio apartment. The mural measures 7.4 feet by 3.9 feet and is $320. Information: 888-266-1737 or sweetbellausa.com. or at Top Hat, 245 Broome Street, 212-677-4240.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/garden/16CURR5_WALLS/16CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/garden/16CURR5_WALLS/16CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600