-claims-that-it-fired-protesters.html', 'snippet': 'A complaint filed by the National Labor Relations Board says employees in several states were disciplined or fired after striking for better pay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Labor Relations Board, in a sweeping complaint filed on Wednesday, said that Walmart illegally disciplined and fired employees after strikes and protests for better pay. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walmart Is Facing Claims That It Fired Protesters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walmart Is Facing Claims That It Fired Protesters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T01:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df449429-e602-5da5-bf7e-22be2398959e', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df449429-e602-5da5-bf7e-22be2398959e'}, {'abstract': 'The New York river town has always been on the verge of something. It’s now rising again, betting on new arrivals and the “Marina” effect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/garden/cultivating-hudson-enter-the-tastemakers.html', 'snippet': 'The New York river town has always been on the verge of something. It’s now rising again, betting on new arrivals and the “Marina” effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HUDSON, N.Y. — Ann Marie Gardner has a buzzword for the “urban-rural confluence” she sees fueling this town’s most recent boomlet as a cultural hub. “Rurbanism,” as she describes it, is when urban expats bring their cultural touchstones and appetites with them when they move to a place like Hudson.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cultivating Hudson: Enter the Tastemakers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cultivating Hudson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Penelope', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T01:06:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Penelope Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Penelope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72b3736d-108b-50d0-9477-27ce17d80695', 'word_count': 2029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72b3736d-108b-50d0-9477-27ce17d80695'}, {'abstract': 'This year, the challenges of securing the Super Bowl will extend far beyond the game site in East Rutherford, N.J., across state lines and multiple jurisdictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/sports/football/security-for-super-bowl-is-a-far-reaching-task.html', 'snippet': 'This year, the challenges of securing the Super Bowl will extend far beyond the game site in East Rutherford, N.J., across state lines and multiple jurisdictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As is the case for other major sporting events, securing the Super Bowl is a complex and nerve-racking task that involves the coordination of many law enforcement agencies, the use of technologies like cameras and radiation detectors, and the identification of potential troublemakers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Puzzle of Super Bowl Security Has to Include New Pieces', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Security Puzzle Has to Include New Pieces ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Stadium (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Rutherford (NJ)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T01:07:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27bfe34e-225b-5274-bdbb-02761be79377', 'word_count': 1568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27bfe34e-225b-5274-bdbb-02761be79377'}, {'abstract': 'Why football fans should root for a frigid and snowy Super Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/opinion/the-coldest-yard.html', 'snippet': 'Why football fans should root for a frigid and snowy Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — IF I were to attack you and slam you to the ground as you stood in line for your morning coffee, you might not get up. But if I put a helmet on you and put you on a football field, then did the exact same thing, you’d pop up and ask for another. There is something powerful about football, something that grants men temporary invincibility, makes them immune to pain and anguish. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/opinion/0116OPEDzhu/0116OPEDzhu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 506, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/opinion/0116OPEDzhu/0116OPEDzhu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 506}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/opinion/0116OPEDzhu/0116OPEDzhu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 864, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/opinion/0116OPEDzhu/0116OPEDzhu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1729, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/opinion/0116OPEDzhu/0116OPEDzhu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2