ied on Dec. 28 in Honolulu. She was 88.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 756}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1625, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521/GUYSE-1-obit-1389830531521-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheila Guyse, Singer and Star in ‘Race Movies,’ Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sheila Guyse, 88, Singer and Actress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guyse, Sheila (1925-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T01:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/58799df1-8ac6-58e6-abd4-33a9c47822b0', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58799df1-8ac6-58e6-abd4-33a9c47822b0'}, {'abstract': 'Ad agencies add side projects to tap the entrepreneurial spirit of employees who have creative energy to spare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/business/media/have-your-job-and-moonlight-too.html', 'snippet': 'Ad agencies add side projects to tap the entrepreneurial spirit of employees who have creative energy to spare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALMOST a century ago, a hit song lamented the difficulty in persuading American soldiers who saw the world during the Great War to return to their rural homes. The title said it all: “How Ya Gonna Keep ’Em Down on the Farm? (After They’ve Seen Paree).” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 263, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 263}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/16/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/business/Adco/Adco-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Have Your Job and Moonlight, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Have Your Job and Moonlight, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Stuart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsch L A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T01:10:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2018d55e-cc4e-5033-802c-e29beac5b0cd', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2018d55e-cc4e-5033-802c-e29beac5b0cd'}, {'abstract': 'Ted Muehling’s polished quartz stones are part of a new collection of memorial objects from Three-Fourths of an Ounce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/garden/weighing-in-at-the-end.html', 'snippet': 'Ted Muehling’s polished quartz stones are part of a new collection of memorial objects from Three-Fourths of an Ounce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three-Fourths of an Ounce, a new line of condolence products including memorial candles and jewelry, is named after measurements taken by the early 1900s Massachusetts doctor Duncan MacDougall. After studying terminally ill people and euthanized dogs, he concluded that a body lost three-quarters of an ounce at the moment of death, so a soul must weigh that much. (Scientists, however, have since discredited his methods and data.) The designer Ted Muehling has contributed polished quartz ovals ($200 each) that weigh, yes, 0.75 ounces. His staff grinds the stones at a workshop behind his Manhattan boutique, on machines with wet sandpaper wheels that emit mournful sounds as they spin. Mr. Muehling, who was brought up Catholic, said the translucent stones remind him of his childhood image of the soul as an internal vapor that grows cloudier with every sin. The polished talismans are also ecumenically reminiscent of crystal orbs that Buddhist temple statues carry and pebbles that Jews place on gravestones. Information: 3-4oz.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/garden/16CURR4_GOODS/16CURR4_GOODS-articleLa