'', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0709ba15-9ee8-5cb0-8d9d-0a2e0b39d120', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0709ba15-9ee8-5cb0-8d9d-0a2e0b39d120'}, {'abstract': 'After a brief pause, the American home is continuing its historical march to massiveness.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/american-home-owners-living-larger-again/', 'snippet': 'After a brief pause, the American home is continuing its historical march to massiveness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That rattling noise you hear is the average American family moving about in the average American house, which — after a brief pause, due to the downturn — is continuing its historical march to massiveness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Home Owners, Living Larger Again', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Home Builders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T14:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3f45f4f-13be-54d8-9389-28caf0cdc9e9', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3f45f4f-13be-54d8-9389-28caf0cdc9e9'}, {'abstract': '“Brooklyn Abolitionists/In Pursuit of Freedom,” at the Brooklyn Historical Society, spotlights extraordinary figures in the history of slavery and abolition in New York, and James W. C. Pennington, a preacher and abolitionist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/arts/design/brooklyn-abolitionists-reveals-a-surprising-history.html', 'snippet': '“Brooklyn Abolitionists/In Pursuit of Freedom,” at the Brooklyn Historical Society, spotlights extraordinary figures in the history of slavery and abolition in New York, and James W. C. Pennington, a preacher and abolitionist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heroic terra-cotta busts of Columbus, Franklin, Shakespeare, Gutenberg, Beethoven and Michelangelo gaze down from the lovingly restored 1881 facade of the Brooklyn Historical Society, reminding the approaching visitor of what the place was once meant to represent. The founders of the society — which is now celebrating its 150th anniversary — conceived of its building in Brooklyn Heights as a repository of history that would aspire to the greatest achievements of European civilization. And why not? Brooklyn was the third-largest city in the United States, the architect was George B. Post (who later designed the New York Stock Exchange), and the society’s founders were among the elite.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Slavery and Its Foes Thrived in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Exhibition Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Slavery and Its Foes Thrived in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothstein, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Historical Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T15:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b679f867-d0c7-5fab-a124-fdb5dbf97eb5', 'word_count': 1589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b679f867-d0c7-5fab-a124-fdb5dbf97eb5'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “Andrew’s Brain” and “Ragtime” sometimes puts down a book because he can see where the story’s going. “As you practice your craft, you lose your innocence as a reader.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/books/review/e-l-doctorow-by-the-book.html', 'snippet': 'The author of “Andrew’s Brain” and “Ragtime” sometimes puts down a book because he can see where the story’s going. “As you practice your craft, you lose your innocence as a reader.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author of “Andrew’s Brain” and “Ragtime” sometimes puts down a book because he can see where the story’s going. “As you practice your craft, you lose your innocence as a reader.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/books/review/0119-bks-By-The-Book/0119-bks-By-The-Book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/books/review/0119-bks-By-The-Book/0119-bks-By-The-Book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 713}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/books/review/0119-bks-By-The-Book/0119-bks-By-The-Book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 862, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/books/review/0119-bks-By-The-Book/0119-bks-By-The-Book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1724, 'subType': 'superJum