ies to let in more light and better install 1,100 gems from its collection — including items designed for Marie Antoinette, Catherine the Great and Napoleon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victoria & Albert Museum to Overhaul Baroque and Rococo Galleries', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T15:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7005af7-10d7-59d6-92e5-1b6ac78cee19', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7005af7-10d7-59d6-92e5-1b6ac78cee19'}, {'abstract': 'The Academy has long been considered stodgy, but this year’s nominations suggest that reputation may be outdated.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/surprises-and-snubs-bold-choices-like-wolf-rewarded-veterans-like-hanks-ignored/', 'snippet': 'The Academy has long been considered stodgy, but this year’s nominations suggest that reputation may be outdated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Academy may not be as stodgy as people thought. In its nominations it overlooked films and performances that many considered classic Oscar bait, choosing instead to reward indie films and those with bold acting and filmmaking choices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/oscars-hanks/oscars-hanks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/oscars-hanks/oscars-hanks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth