'lead_paragraph': 'As I’m sure you’ve noticed, Motherlode (along with all of the other blogs at The Times) has joined the redesign, with a streamlined appearance and new navigation tools. For starters, and most importantly on a blog where reader interaction is a big part of the experience, you can pop up the comments as you read the post by clicking on the number of comments at the top of the post next to the headline. Comments still aren’t available for readers on mobile apps. (For this reason, I am considering a weekly post highlighting the best commentary.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Motherlode in The Times’s Redesign', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T17:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da3ae0ea-1d09-5618-b1a5-3d6a9731a1d9', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da3ae0ea-1d09-5618-b1a5-3d6a9731a1d9'}, {'abstract': 'Jessica Dickey, who grew up near Gettysburg, Pa., explores the Civil War in her new play, “Row After Row,” at City Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/theater/hometown-inspiration-for-jessica-dickeys-civil-war-play.html', 'snippet': 'Jessica Dickey, who grew up near Gettysburg, Pa., explores the Civil War in her new play, “Row After Row,” at City Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Growing up just outside Gettysburg, Pa., Jessica Dickey knew from an early age that she was surrounded by a complicated history. On the roads outside her home were signs marking where the Union and Confederate troops had marched. Downtown were buildings flecked with bullet holes. “I was always so intrigued by the idea of the presence of the past, the ghosts of the past,” Ms. Dickey said.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19DICKEY1/19DICKEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19DICKEY1/19DICKEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19DICKEY1/19DICKEY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19DICKEY1/19DICKEY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19DICKEY1/19DICKEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19DICKEY1/19DICKEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/arts/19DICKEY1/19DICKEY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Veteran Returns to Gettysburg', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Veteran Returns to Gettysburg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, Jessica', 