timedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Natalia V. Osipova and Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalia', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Osipova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/1e9b702f-aa40-5fc1-bf43-495e314924ef', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/1e9b702f-aa40-5fc1-bf43-495e314924ef'}, {'abstract': 'Hit golden beaches, soak up contemporary culture, explore atmospheric bars and, sure, catch a glimpse of that opera house during a weekend in Australia’s most populous city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/travel/36-hours-in-sydney.html', 'snippet': 'Hit golden beaches, soak up contemporary culture, explore atmospheric bars and, sure, catch a glimpse of that opera house during a weekend in Australia’s most populous city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In ever-sunny, easygoing Sydney, don’t let the famous attractions circling the handsome harbor consume all your attention. Focus instead on the evolving neighborhoods where art spaces are cropping up beside train tracks, and innovative, chef-driven restaurants are opening at a rapid clip. If you’re searching for flash, look to Darling Harbour, where celebrity chefs like David Chang and Luke Nguyen have opened outposts in the Star, a ritzy casino and entertainment complex that reopened in 2011 after a renovation costing around $800 million. For more discreet indulgences, seek out the diminutive drinking dens that now pepper the city, the result of a change in local liquor licensing laws that finally made business viable for small bars. Then when it’s time to dry out, the natural beauty of Australia’s most populous city will be waiting along the sandy beaches that lie just minutes from downtown. And don’t worry, you’re bound to pass a certain opera house along the way.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/travel/19-hours-span/19-hours-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/travel/19-hours-span/19-hours-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/travel/19-hours-span/19-hours-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/travel/19-hours-span/19-hours-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/travel/19-hours-span/19-hours-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/travel/19-hours-span/19-hours-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/travel/19-hours-span/19-hours-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Sydney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Sydney, Australia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Ingrid K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '