a82402ba03b'}, {'abstract': 'Among President François Hollande’s proposed changes – while dealing with revelations of his supposed infidelity with an actress – was a pledge to cut public spending and slash the payroll taxes for business.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/free-markets-infidelity-and-the-president-of-france/', 'snippet': 'Among President François Hollande’s proposed changes – while dealing with revelations of his supposed infidelity with an actress – was a pledge to cut public spending and slash the payroll taxes for business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS – Is it worse to be an ardent advocate of the free market than a suspected adulterer? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Markets, Infidelity and the President of France', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:04:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6865edc-1a86-59eb-9843-22a200d5d3a9', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6865edc-1a86-59eb-9843-22a200d5d3a9'}, {'abstract': 'I daydreamed that my book would end up in the White House library. But its real path was humbler, and more meaningful.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/a-reader-behind-bars/', 'snippet': 'I daydreamed that my book would end up in the White House library. But its real path was humbler, and more meaningful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am not proud of it, but I will admit to having felt a twinge of envy when I read, over the holidays, of President Obama’s latest book purchases. How amazing would it be to have the president buy, and read, your novel?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reader Behind Bars', 'kicker': 'Private Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:04:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ca20dd-0796-5bd1-87a9-18ad69cd5707', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ca20dd-0796-5bd1-87a9-18ad69cd5707'}, {'abstract': 'The Artist Book Foundation plans to document and distribute a visual record of work that would otherwise hardly be seen.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/new-foundation-to-focus-on-publishing-art-books/', 'snippet': 'The Artist Book Foundation plans to document and distribute a visual record of work that would otherwise hardly be seen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art books, monographs and catalogs are essential for historians, collectors and artists, but they rarely make money. Often oversized and lavishly illustrated on high-quality glossy paper, they are expensive to produce for the relatively tiny number of institutions and individuals who buy them.\xa0Enter the\xa0Artist Book Foundation, a new nonprofit organization dedicated to publishing fine-art references that otherwise would not be seen. Next month, it will release “Trucks: Recent Works by John Himmelfarb,” to accompany a new traveling exhibition of that Chicago artist’s work that opened last week at the\xa0Brauer Museum of Art at Valparaiso University\xa0in Valparaiso, Indiana.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Foundation to Focus on Publishing Art Books', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbcfdcdc-652c-5055-b434-ff977ac4dc80', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbcfdcdc-652c-5055-b434-ff977ac4dc80'}, {'abstract': 'The co-star, co-writer and producer of “Philomena” received several nominations but says whooping over good news is not a British thing to do. He did however celebrate in his own way.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/steve-coogan-shares-his-victory-march/', 'snippet': 'The co-star, co-writer and producer of “Philomena” received several nominations but says whooping over good news is not a British thing to do. He did however celebrate in his own way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Steve Coogan is playing catch-up. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/coogan/coogan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/coogan/coogan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth'