{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63f28f55-1314-5735-9521-b5450acb44e3', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63f28f55-1314-5735-9521-b5450acb44e3'}, {'abstract': 'The resourceful American Folk Art Museum continues to explore new ways of using its collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/arts/design/clothes-inspired-on-demand.html', 'snippet': 'The resourceful American Folk Art Museum continues to explore new ways of using its collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The resourceful American Folk Art Museum continues to explore new ways of using its collection, and in particular to involve living artists in its exhibitions. Its previous attempt, last fall’s “alt_quilts,” presented quilts from its collection and the quiltlike works of three contemporary artists, with weak results. Now, the museum has turned to the fashion world in “Folk Couture: Fashion and Folk Art,” which opens on Tuesday. To explore the idea of fashion designers finding inspiration in all sorts of unexpected places, 13 New York-based designers have been invited to create garments inspired by works they select from the museum’s collection.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clothes Inspired on Demand', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clothes Inspired On Demand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6084551-1d1c-5943-9f55-cc9a6b4e5ab8', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6084551-1d1c-5943-9f55-cc9a6b4e5ab8'}, {'abstract': 'It’s been almost two years since Sarah Michelson commandeered the fourth floor of the Whitney Museum of American Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/arts/dance/endurance-as-art-form.html', 'snippet': 'It’s been almost two years since Sarah Michelson commandeered the fourth floor of the Whitney Museum of American Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been almost two years since Sarah Michelson commandeered the fourth floor of the Whitney Museum of American Art, transforming several thousand square feet into the gleaming terrain for “Devotion Study #1 — The American Dancer.” Some audience members walked out. Others sat transfixed as Ms. Michelson’s dancers rose to the punishing task of walking backward, in circles, for a spectacularly long time, never doubting (or so it seemed) that their bodies would carry them through.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Endurance as Art Form', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Endurance As Art Form', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a458f58c-524f-5536-99fb-fb60b52ff8d5', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a458f58c-524f-5536-99fb-fb60b52ff8d5'}, {'abstract': 'Jeff Mangum returns with the rest of Neutral Milk Hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/arts/music/back-together-after-a-breakup.html', 'snippet': 'Jeff Mangum returns with the rest of Neutral Milk Hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Mangum, the songwriter who leads Neutral Milk Hotel, defused some suspense with his 2011-12 solo tours. Those were his first consistent reappearances since the group quietly disbanded after touring for its beloved 1998 album, “In the Aeroplane Over the Sea,” an oblique yet impassioned set of songs inspired by thoughts of Anne Frank, with Mr. Mangum’s ceaseless strumming punctuated by jaunty trombone tunes and outbursts of distortion. Mr. Mangum stayed largely out of sight as the album’s reputation spread and solidified, but his solo concerts showed him fully in command. Now, with the band, patient fans should hear the trombone, too. Elf Power shares the bill. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Together After a Breakup', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back Together After a Breakup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bd948b2-c489-51ff-b485-241dae3c0067', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bd948b2-c489-51ff-b485-241dae3c0067'}, {'abstract': 'Only 148 cases of Guinea worm disease, which is on the brink of extinction, were found in the world in 2013, the Carter Center announced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/health/guinea-worm-cases-drop-by-more-than-70.html', 'snippet': 'Only 148 cases of Guinea worm disease, which is on the brink of extinction, were found in the world in 2013, the Carter Center announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only 148 cases of Guinea worm disease were found in the world in 2013, a 73 percent drop from the 542 cases found one year earlier, the Carter Center announced Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guinea Worm Said to Infect Few in 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guinea Worm Said to Infect Few in 2013', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guinea Worm Disease', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parasites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carter Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:30:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be87d5f6-5734-5a4d-a140-01b88b5f082e', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be87d5f6-5734-5a4d-a140-01b88b5f082e'}, {'abstract': 'Christina Ricci showed early that she could play creepy: One of her first film credits is as Wednesday Addams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/arts/television/what-was-behind-all-those-whacks.html', 'snippet': 'Christina Ricci showed early that she could play creepy: One of her first film credits is as Wednesday Addams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christina Ricci showed early that she could play creepy: One of her first film credits is as Wednesday Addams in the 1991 movie “The Addams Family.” So the role of Lizzie Borden, the odd Massachusetts woman accused of killing her father and stepmother with an ax in 1892, seems a logical fit. “Lizzie Borden Took an Ax,” a telling of the real-life story being shown on Saturday at 8 p.m. on Lifetime, isn’t shy about speculating on what actually happened in the Borden household in Fall River that bloody August day, though that has remained in dispute for more than a century. The movie also presents the record of Lizzie’s arrest and trial, whose conclusion won’t be spoiled here for the sake of those not up on their murder history. The cast includes Billy Campbell as Lizzie’s lawyer and Clea DuVall as her sister, Emma. Also listed are credits for three “Jump Rope Girls.” You can probably guess why, though the film reminds us that the oft-chanted rhyme is inaccurate. The figures of 40 and 41 whacks are greatly inflated. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Was Behind All Those Whacks?', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Was Behind All Those Whacks?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T18:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17246b0d-c889-559f-80c1-9ed4bf5e5088', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17246b0d-c889-559f-80c1-9ed4bf5e5088'}, {'abstract': 'Bobby Parnell, the Mets’ closer, who had surgery to repair a herniated disk in his neck in September, said on Thursday that he had been throwing for several weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/sports/baseball/mets-parnell-says-hell-be-ready-for-opening-day.html', 'snippet': 'Bobby Parnell, the Mets’ closer, who had surgery to repair a herniated disk in his neck in September, said on Thursday that he had been throwing for several weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In September, as the Mets’ 2013 season was coming to a close, Bobby Parnell, the team’s closer, made a rare appearance in the clubhouse. He had been out since July with a herniated disk in his neck, and recently had surgery on it. As he visited with his teammates, he wore a big neck brace and looked thinner. Manager Terry Collins, for one, seemed worried about his appearance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/sports/baseball/17mets/17mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/sports/baseball/17mets/17mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/sports/baseball/17mets/17mets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/sports/baseball/17mets/17mets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 1916, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/sports/baseball/17mets/17mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/17/sports/baseball/17mets/17mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/1