e New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/16artsbeat-titanic/16artsbeat-titanic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/16artsbeat-titanic/16artsbeat-titanic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/16artsbeat-titanic/16artsbeat-titanic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/16artsbeat-titanic/16artsbeat-titanic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 1426, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/16artsbeat-titanic/16artsbeat-titanic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/16artsbeat-titanic/16artsbeat-titanic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/16artsbeat-titanic/16artsbeat-titanic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Musical ‘Titanic’ Headed Back to New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Musical u2018Titanicu2019 Headed Back to New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T19:40:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86fe5e37-e22c-5805-ac9a-e8fb27fe2a03', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86fe5e37-e22c-5805-ac9a-e8fb27fe2a03'}, {'abstract': 'The police said the explosives, found in the residence of the Palestinian ambassador after a safe there exploded, killing him, were undergoing ballistic tests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/world/europe/more-explosives-found-in-czech-residence-where-diplomat-was-killed.html', 'snippet': 'The police said the explosives, found in the residence of the Palestinian ambassador after a safe there exploded, killing him, were undergoing ballistic tests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRAGUE, Czech Republic — The police disclosed on Thursday that they had found additional explosives on Jan. 1 while investigating the explosion of a safe at a residence in Prague that  killed the Palestinian ambassador to the Czech Republic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Czech Police Reveal Discovery of More Explosives in Envoy’s Residence', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jamal, Jamal al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T19:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hana de Goeij', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Goeij', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/585883ff-198c-5562-aa22-148bdb8f0b03', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/585883ff-198c-5562-aa22-148bdb8f0b03'}, {'abstract': 'When asked how much sleep they “usually” get, Americans estimate just 6.8 hours. When asked to document their sleep the night before, slumber time jumps to 8.7 hours.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/you-sleep-more-than-you-claim-you-do/', 'snippet': 'When asked how much sleep they “usually” get, Americans estimate just 6.8 hours. When asked to document their sleep the night before, slumber time jumps to 8.7 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple years ago I wrote about how people don’t work nearly as many hours as they claim they do. That is, there’s a big gap between how many hours people estimate they “usually” work versus how many hours they log when asked to keep a time diary, especially for people who already keep long hours. (The typical person who reported having worked 40 hours, for example, actually worked about 37; people who claimed a usual week of 75 hours worked 50.) This discrepancy could be due to fuzzy memories, or a desire to sound more industrious, or both.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You Sleep More Than You Claim You Do', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gallup Poll', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T19:42:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/092cc0d1-6e1f-525e-92a2-f32b6a12b178', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/092cc0d1-6e1f-525e-92a2-f32b6a12b178'}, {'abstract': 'In the news: the obesity paradox, vaccines and probiotics. Test your knowledge of this week’s health news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/01/17/health/20140117_healthquiz.html', 'snippet': 'In the news: the obesity paradox, vaccines and probiotics. Test your knowledge of this week’s health news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the news: the obesity paradox, vaccines and probiotics. Test your knowledge of this week’s health news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/science/16wellobesity/16wellobesity-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/science/16wellobesity/16wellobesity-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/science/16wellobesity/16wellobesity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/science/16wellobesity/16wellobesity-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'