nnifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/960b60e7-cbf6-51a2-a590-480eef25b545', 'word_count': 1633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/960b60e7-cbf6-51a2-a590-480eef25b545'}, {'abstract': 'A suicide car bomb in a Lebanese town was a bloody backdrop on the opening day of the Special Tribunal for Lebanon.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/hariri-son-discusses-assassination-at-lebanon-tribunal/', 'snippet': 'A suicide car bomb in a Lebanese town was a bloody backdrop on the opening day of the Special Tribunal for Lebanon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Ben Hubbard reported, a suicide car bomber killed at least 3 people in a northeastern town in Lebanon, the latest in a string of attacks that many have interpreted as targeting groups backing opposite sides in the civil war in neighboring Syria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hariri Son Discusses Assassination at Lebanon Tribunal', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hariri, Rafik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Special Tribunal for Lebanon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beirut (Lebanon)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T19:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b800bbb6-b17b-59ac-8683-5be8ee4b51e4', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b800bbb6-b17b-59ac-8683-5be8ee4b51e4'}, {'abstract': 'In a decision that surprised many, a bankruptcy judge said it was “reasonably likely” that Detroit could free itself of costly swap contracts if it sued the two banks holding them.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/judge-rejects-detroits-deal-to-exit-swap-contracts/', 'snippet': 'In a decision that surprised many, a bankruptcy judge said it was “reasonably likely” that Detroit could free itself of costly swap contracts if it sued the two banks holding them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Thursday rejected a deal that Detroit had negotiated to help it move forward in bankruptcy, but he did offer some hope, saying the city could borrow $120 million it says it urgently needs to provide services to its residents.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/business/Swaps1/Swaps1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/business/Swaps1/Swaps1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/business/Swaps1/Swaps1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/business/Swaps1/Swaps1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJ