, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/411bde5e-4f75-54cd-ad8f-9cde6c4fda56', 'word_count': 1532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/411bde5e-4f75-54cd-ad8f-9cde6c4fda56'}, {'abstract': 'Ballet Next unveiled a program of three works by one choreographer on Tuesday at New York Live Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/arts/dance/brian-reeder-works-are-performed-by-ballet-next.html', 'snippet': 'Ballet Next unveiled a program of three works by one choreographer on Tuesday at New York Live Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ballet Next, the three-year-old company directed by the former American Ballet Theater principal Michele Wiles, is dedicated to presenting new choreography with live music. That’s a worthy goal, but whose choreography? The group’s New York performances have been undermined by poor choices. But on Tuesday at New York Live Arts, the company unveiled a program of three works by one choreographer: Brian Reeder. This choice was good.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17REEDER1_SPAN/17REEDER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17REEDER1_SPAN/17REEDER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17REEDER1_SPAN/17REEDER1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17REEDER1_SPAN/17REEDER1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJu