ne, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17GALLERIES4/17GALLERIES4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Josephine Meckseper', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Josephine Meckseper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meckseper, Josephine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T22:50:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/91fef568-84e3-5588-8f47-1f84ce5b6870', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91fef568-84e3-5588-8f47-1f84ce5b6870'}, {'abstract': 'Two-thirds of those polled said they were hopeful about the next four years with Bill de Blasio as mayor, and most endorsed a plan to tax wealthy New Yorkers to pay for prekindergarten.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/nyregion/most-new-york-voters-feel-hopeful-about-de-blasio-poll-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Two-thirds of those polled said they were hopeful about the next four years with Bill de Blasio as mayor, and most endorsed a plan to tax wealthy New Yorkers to pay for prekindergarten.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks into a new administration at City Hall, New York City voters are highly optimistic about Mayor Bill de Blasio and overwhelmingly endorse his plan to raise taxes on the wealthy to pay for prekindergarten, according to a new Quinnipiac University poll.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Most New York Voters Are Optimistic About the Mayor, a Poll Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Most New York Voters Are Optimistic About the Mayor, a Poll Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quinnipiac University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T22:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/891e3ad5-36fa-5460-93af-18e08de62473', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/891e3ad5-36fa-5460-93af-18e08de62473'}, {'abstract': 'Addressing matters of a pushy friend, a reluctant aunt, an absent skullcap and a boyfriend on autocorrect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/fashion/no-is-all-you-need-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'Addressing matters of a pushy friend, a reluctant aunt, an absent skullcap and a boyfriend on autocorrect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I made a reservation for my wife and me at our favorite restaurant. We were really looking forward to it. I casually mentioned our plans to an acquaintance, and the next day, he told me he had called the restaurant, changed our reservation from two people to four. He then asked, “Would it be O.K. if we joined you?” I didn’t know what to say. I was so astonished that I agreed. But we don’t know this couple very well and soon began dreading a long night of stilted conversation. Was there any way around his maneuver? Anonymous, Louisville, Ky.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Is All You Need', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Is All You Need', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T22:54:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebbf7b89-b0af-562c-9218-b2459d1b95b5', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebbf7b89-b0af-562c-9218-b2459d1b95b5'}, {'abstract': 'Having rejected God and a confining faith, I was alone and making up for lost time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/fashion/adrift-too-long-searching-for-a-navigator.html', 'snippet': 'Having rejected God and a confining faith, I was alone and making up for lost time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was hurtling toward Brooklyn on the Q train, wearing cherry-red pants that hugged my hips. He was tall, bald, in his early 30s, with pale skin, tired eyes and a thin nose over a goatee. His smile was bashful, but his legs, in baggy track pants, were spread confidently on the orange seat. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/fashion/19MODERNLOVE/19MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/fashion/19MODERNLOVE/19MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/fashion/19MODERNLOVE/19MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/fashion/19MODERNLOVE/19MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/fashion/19MODERNLOVE/19MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/fashion/19MODERNLOVE/19MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/fashion/19MODERNLOVE/19MODERNLOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adrift Too Long, Searching for a Navigator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adrift Too Long, Searching for a Navigator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T22:59:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Vincent', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vincent', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6ab38f8-69a2-5d08-ac1c-dae7e8344ab0', 'word_count': 1450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ab38f8-69a2-5d08-ac1c-dae7e8344ab0'}, {'abstract': '“An Opening of the Field” focuses on the San Francisco poet Robert Duncan and his life partner, the artist Jess, and the assorted band of offbeat artists and writers who found a common link in their friendship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/arts/design/robert-duncan-and-jess-and-their-wonderland-of-art.html', 'snippet': '“An Opening of the Field” focuses on the San Francisco poet Robert Duncan and his life partner, the artist Jess, and the assorted band of offbeat artists and writers who found a common link in their friendship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you were young, gifted and odd, San Francisco was a good place to be in the years after World War II, when big changes were brewing in American art and culture. And that city is the setting for “An Opening of the Field: Jess, Robert Duncan, and Their Circle,” an exhibition that feels like a chunk of Bay Area turf lifted from the past and set down, untrimmed and buzzing, in New York University’s Grey Art Gallery. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17GREY_SPAN/17GREY_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17GREY_SPAN/17GREY_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17GREY_SPAN/17GREY_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 6