], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/630498bf-6264-5c5a-b559-4083a05f8c1d', 'word_count': 1344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/630498bf-6264-5c5a-b559-4083a05f8c1d'}, {'abstract': 'John Ridley, nominated for his adaptation of Solomon Northup’s memoir, included details like how violin strings were made in the 19th century. That four-page description had to go.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/what-the-writer-had-to-edit-from-12-years-a-slave/', 'snippet': 'John Ridley, nominated for his adaptation of Solomon Northup’s memoir, included details like how violin strings were made in the 19th century. That four-page description had to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To celebrate his Oscar nod for “12 Years a Slave,” the screenwriter John Ridley was visiting the White House on Thursday afternoon — not in a special capacity as, say, an honored guest who had penned a major film but rather as a tourist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/ridley/ridley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/ridley/ridley-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 771}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/ridley/ridley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/ridley/ridley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1594, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/ridley/ridley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wi