test “Star Search,” belongs to a breed of hyperkinetic entertainer and vaudevillian who has been “on” since early childhood. He is still best known for his extravagantly flowery and emotional rendition of “Over the Rainbow,” the song that capped Wednesday’s opening-night performance of his show “Ham: Slices of a Life,” at 54 Below. The show’s title is also the name of Mr. Harris’s just-published book of essays and stories.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17HARRIS_SPAN/HARRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17HARRIS_SPAN/HARRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17HARRIS_SPAN/HARRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17HARRIS_SPAN/HARRIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17HARRIS_SPAN/17HARRIS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17HARRIS_SPAN/17HARRIS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/17HARRIS_SPAN/17HARRIS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Performer’s Life Story Leaps ‘Over the Rainbow’', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Performer’s Life Story Leaps ‘Over the Rainbow’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Samuel K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T23:02:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5c9aa7c-82ad-58d5-888b-1d45457ce6a7', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5c9aa7c-82ad-58d5-888b-1d45457ce6a7'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Lehman tried out some new material with his octet at the Stone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/arts/music/jazz-twists-from-steve-lehman-and-his-octet.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Lehman tried out some new material with his octet at the Stone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Lehman got a knowing laugh Wednesday night while introducing the last piece in his first set at the Stone, a stutter-stepping workout called “Beyond All Limits.” He began by pointing out that it shared a title with a tune by the post-bop trumpeter Woody Shaw. (Perhaps you know it from the classic 1965 album “Unity,” by Larry Young.) And so, Mr. Lehman suggested, this would be a tribute of sorts to Shaw, “even though it sounds completely different.” Ha-ha, replied the crowd, conspiratorially. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spectral Compound of Strange and Familiar', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Spectral Compound of Strange and Familiar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehman, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T23:02:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bc12243-7d62-5126-9219-875a3706e288', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bc12243-7d62-5126-9219-875a3706e288'}, {'abstract': 'In Milan, it became especially evident that the men wearing the clothes down the runway were as meticulously curated as the fabrics and embellishments that went into making the collections.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/16/in-fashion-model-casting-is-as-distinctive-to-a-house-as-its-designs/', 'snippet': 'In Milan, it became especially evident that the men wearing the clothes down the runway were as meticulously curated as the fabrics and embellishments that went into making the collections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It goes without saying that when putting together a fashion show, designers are as careful with casting as they are in designing their clothes. Nowhere is this more true than in Milan, where the models’ looks are as distinct as the Italian labels they’re representing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/t-magazine/16models-pask-slide-2909/16models-pask-slide-2909-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge'