ers and directors, Aharon Keshales and Navot Papushado, for whom murdered children are just an easy, conveniently blunt and effectively faceless (and headless) means to a self-satisfied, jokey and blood-slicked end.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Trail of a Vicious Killer, Eagerly Licking Their Chops', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Trail of a Vicious Killer, Eagerly Licking Their Chops', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keshales, Aharon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papushado, Navot', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Big Bad Wolves (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T23:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5560adce-a670-57b0-8958-0b476d5f6c6c', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5560adce-a670-57b0-8958-0b476d5f6c6c'}, {'abstract': 'The historic district proposed between 79th and 96th Streets has some people yawning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/realestate/an-exploratory-stroll-up-park-avenue.html', 'snippet': 'The historic district proposed between 79th and 96th Streets has some people yawning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The proposed Park Avenue Historic District, running from 79th to 96th Street, breaks new ground in landmarks preservation. Instead of sweeping up all the little brownstones and townhouses on the side streets, the district ignores them entirely; this district is all about the multiple-family dwelling. These are the comfortable residences of the rich, just as the brownstones and townhouses were a century ago, but is that alone enough for landmark designation?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/realestate/19STREETS_SPAN/19STREETS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/realestate/19STREETS_SPAN/19STREETS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/realestate/19STREETS_SPAN/19STREETS_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/realestate/19STREETS_SPAN/19STREETS_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/realestate/19STREETS_SPAN/19STREETS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/realestate/19STREETS_SPAN/19STREETS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/realestate/19STREETS_SPAN/19STREETS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Exploratory Stroll Up Park Avenue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Exploratory Stroll Up Park Avenue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-16T23:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7469f0b6-0d89-5804-8a7d-3f31c9aa7da8', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7469f0b6-0d89-5804-8a7d-3f31c9aa7da8'}, {'abstract': 'Opened about six months ago, Alain’s Wine & Tapas offers small plates of Spanish food, many of which have a French influence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/nyregion/a-review-of-alains-wine-and-tapas-in-nyack.html', 'snippet': 'Opened about six months ago, Alain’s Wine & Tapas offers small plates of Spanish food, many of which have a French influence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walk into Alain’s Wine & Tapas in Nyack and you are likely to hear Spanish guitar music playing in the background. Yet the prominent piece of art in the room is an old map not of Madrid, but of Paris (oddly, with the northern part of the city on the bottom).', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/