', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4f689fa-65f5-55e7-ba35-85102d2cb2c0', 'word_count': 3154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4f689fa-65f5-55e7-ba35-85102d2cb2c0'}, {'abstract': 'A sculpture exhibition, at the Heckscher Museum of Art in Huntington, displays traditional statues and busts in one room and abstract forms and assemblages in another.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/nyregion/both-ends-of-a-sculpture-spectrum.html', 'snippet': 'A sculpture exhibition, at the Heckscher Museum of Art in Huntington, displays traditional statues and busts in one room and abstract forms and assemblages in another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sculpture exhibition at the Heckscher Museum of Art in Huntington starts with two\xa019th-century marble figures, each about two feet high, flanking the entranceway like sentinels. One, titled “Industry,” shows a man wearing a miner’s helmet and balancing an ax on his shoulder. The other, called “Commerce,” depicts a sailor leaning casually on a post. Both were made by Emma Stebbins, an American artist who also created the angel that stands atop Bethesda Fountain in Central Park. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/nyregion/19ARTSLI1/19ARTSLI1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/nyregion/19ARTSLI1/19ARTSLI1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/nyregion/19ARTSLI1/19ARTSLI1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ra