ps://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/arts/spare-times-for-jan-17-23.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of walking tours, speaking engagements, cultural activities and Martin Luther King’s Birthday celebrations in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Second annual Black Comic Book Festival (Friday and Saturday) Commentary will be as abundant as illustrations when scholars, artists and collectors gather for this free symposium at the Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture, 515 Lenox Avenue, at 135th Street, Hamilton Heights. One of the earliest black superheroes to appear in mainstream comics is thought to be the Black Panther, who made his debut in Marvel’s Fantastic Four in 1966. At last year’s festival, a costumed Black Panther and Superman mingled with Khalil Gibran Muhammad, the center’s director.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Jan. 17-23', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Walking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T00:04:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/038791e2-4f26-586c-8486-643966651fc8', 'word_count': 3397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/038791e2-4f26-586c-8486-643966651fc8'}, {'abstract': 'The animated feature “The Nut Job” centers on a gang of humans trying to rob a bank, and a group of squirrels attempting a heist of a nut store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/movies/in-the-nut-job-a-surly-squirrel-plans-a-heist.