ge of legal settlements for their roles in mortgage practices leading up to the financial crisis, banks have been setting aside cash to fund impending payouts. But while understanding the size of these funds, called litigation reserves, is necessary for weighing the banks’ financial strength, many banks are continuing to keep this figure secret, Peter Eavis writes in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Keep Mouths Shut on Litigation Reserves', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T12:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5cd5fae-b6d7-5ce5-976f-f61f0b395802', 'word_count': 1909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5cd5fae-b6d7-5ce5-976f-f61f0b395802'}, {'abstract': 'There is a widening gulf between the way officials have attempted to portray the impact of the heat wave and what has actually happened with the players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/sports/tennis/players-are-not-cool-with-australian-open-heat-policy.html', 'snippet': 'There is a widening gulf between the way officials have attempted to portray the impact of the heat wave and what has actually happened with the players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — The Australian Sauna Championships, disguised as a Grand Slam tennis tournament, finally ended Saturday. Advancement had depended on survival, on remaining upright, on shade and hydration and on the coolest accessory in sports, something called an ice vest.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'