10-2fba9134627c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a lot worse than the usual number suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/the-case-for-a-better-u/', 'snippet': 'It’s a lot worse than the usual number suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unemployment has fallen a lot recently, but for a peculiar reason: not so much rising employment as a falling share of the population actively looking for work. This has sparked a debate over how much of the decline in labor force participation reflects a weak job market — why bother looking? — and how much demography, changing culture, and all that. And it looks like one of those debates that will go on, unresolved, for a long time — certainly past the point where a decisive win for one side or the other can inform policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case for a Better U', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T13:54:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d25e664-ebc0-5cb0-a212-7ce87bb2ee0a', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d25e664-ebc0-5cb0-a212-7ce87bb2ee0a'}, {'abstract': 'Paris', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/01/17/fashion/runway-mens/givenchy-fall-2014-menswear.html', 'snippet': 'Paris', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/fashion/runway-mens/givenchy-mens-fall-2014-slide-VRTJ/givenchy-mens-fall-2014-slide-VRTJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subTy