me and abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/live-coverage-of-obamas-n-s-a-speech/', 'snippet': 'President Obama delivered a much-anticipated speech Friday morning in which he announced that he is pulling back the government’s wide net of surveillance at home and abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama delivered a much-anticipated speech Friday morning in which he announced that he is pulling back the government’s wide net of surveillance at home and abroad. Times reporters provided live analysis of the speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis of Obama’s N.S.A. Speech', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T15:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c5b1c87-23e0-5c9b-a18c-b93c8877660d', 'word_count': 2863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c5b1c87-23e0-5c9b-a18c-b93c8877660d'}, {'abstract': 'Also, the secret to longevity and how to freak out truck drivers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/magazine/james-earl-jones-on-darth-vader-mufasa-and-natch-totes-mcgotes.html', 'snippet': 'Also, the secret to longevity and how to freak out truck drivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your new film, “Gimme Shelter,” is the latest of more than 65 features that you’ve acted in. What’s the secret to longevity? The secret is never forgetting that you’re a journeyman actor and that nothing is your final thing, nothing is your greatest thing, nothing is your worst thing. I still consider myself a novice.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1166}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 528, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1828, 'width': 941, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Earl Jones on Darth Vader, Mufasa and, natch, Totes McGotes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "‘I Don't Hear the Voice You Hear’", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, James Earl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gimme Shelter (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T15:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/311f3b06-520d-5298-b3a6-38bb8b1c8404', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/311f3b06-520d-5298-b3a6-38bb8b1c8404'}, {'abstract': 'A Turing test in reverse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/magazine/who-made-that-captcha.html', 'snippet': 'A Turing test in reverse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the presidential election in 1996, a computer company called Digital Equipment Corporation set up a website for opinion polls. There was one problem, though: Partisan hackers could use bots to fill the site with useless spam. So D.E.C. put a pixelated image of the U.S. flag at a random spot on the screen that users had to click before they registered their votes.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19wmt/19wmt-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 189, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19wmt/19wmt-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 189}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19wmt/19wmt-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19wmt/19wmt-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19wmt/19wmt-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19wmt/19wmt-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/magazine/19wmt/19wmt-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Captcha?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Captcha)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Engber, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Digital Equipment Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Mellon University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Ahn, Luis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broder, Andrei Z', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blum, Manuel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T15:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Engber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Engber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/879cd452-0397-517d-851a-69cefd9adefe', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/879cd452-0397-517d-851a-69cefd9adefe'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers take snowy rides on skateboards, lunch trays, sheet metal and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/magazine/tough-sledding.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers take snowy rides on skateboards, lunch trays, sheet metal and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was plenty of snow in New York City for the first weekend of the year after a huge storm hit the Northeast, but sleds appear to have been in shorter supply. The best alternatives, according to the photographer Nolan Conway, who visited several parks in Manhattan, Brooklyn and Queens to capture the resourceful at play, were made of glossy things and included corrugated plastic and skateboards with their wheels removed. Laundry baskets, broken sleds and mats were O.K.; brown cardboard boxes, lunch trays and trash-can lids didn’t work. And in the dangerous category: sheet metal. Some with real sleds, like Anyssa Mundle, 11, seemed to enjoy using found objects just as much. “This is a check off my Christmas list,” Anyssa said. “Sledding and going in a magazine.” Julie Bosman', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '41', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tough Sledding', 'kicker': ' Look', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tough Sledding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T15:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Photographs by Nolan Conway', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Photographs', 'middlename': 'Nolan', 'lastname': 'Conway', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89554233-dc10-5899-a006-58cb97345693', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89554233-dc10-5899-a006-58cb97345693'}, {'abstract': 'A guest list from beyond the grave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/magazine/the-mistress-at-the-funeral.html', 'snippet': 'A guest list from beyond the grave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My good friend just died. In the last weeks of his lucidity, he told me he absolutely wanted his mistress of many years to attend his memorial service. He relayed a few messages through me to her, as he lay dying. His wife did well in her role as caregiver, running an in-house hospice for him. But their marriage was — by his account and all available evidence — in shambles for years. His wife knew the mistress existed, and only in the waning months of his life did my friend sever the extramarital relationship (in order to die with less complexity at home). There will be a funeral, hosted by his family. The dilemma: Enact the expressed will of my friend and ensure the mistress is present or — given the wife’s emotional fragility and proneness to angry outbursts — enact my friend’s constant goal of peace and simplicity for his child. NAME WITHHELD, NEW YORK CITY', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {