oliday discuss the poet, playwright, critic and polemicist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most would agree that the essence of the poet, playwright, critic and polemicist Amiri Baraka, who died last week at the age of 79, is words on paper, and the ideas resounding from the words about black art, memory, racism, class struggle and political power relationships. There’s more to it, though.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/baraka-pop/baraka-pop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/baraka-pop/baraka-pop-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/baraka-pop/baraka-pop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/baraka-pop/baraka-pop-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/baraka-pop/baraka-pop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/baraka-pop/baraka-pop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/arts/baraka-pop/baraka-pop-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: Hearing Amiri Baraka', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baraka, Amiri', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T15:49:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/903916bd-a0ac-597d-b652-f2d34c455db0', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/903916bd-a0ac-597d-b652-f2d34c455db0'}, {'abstract': 'Raf Simons has good taste in art. That he proposed doing a complete line with Sterling Ruby is not surprising.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/hands-and-mind-raf-simons-and-sterling-ruby/', 'snippet': 'Raf Simons has good taste in art. That he proposed doing a complete line with Sterling Ruby is not surprising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raf Simons has good taste in art. Mike Kelley, Paul McCarthy, Cindy Sherman, Christopher Wool and Brian Calvin are among the artists whose work he admires and in some cases owns. About 15 years ago, Mr. Simons took a break from fashion to help a Belgian businessman expand his art collection. In more recent years, art has been a keystone of his fashion. He collaborated with Mr. Calvin on some T-shirts for his Antwerp-based Raf Simons men’s label, and in February 2013, he paid brilliant homage to Surrealism in a collection for Dior, where he is creative director.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hands and Mind: Raf Simons and Sterling Ruby', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'n