08'}, {'abstract': 'Maurice Peress will re-create the debut performance of George Gershwin’s jazz-tinged work at Town Hall on Feb. 12.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/concert-to-re-create-debut-of-gershwins-rhapsody-in-blue-on-90th-anniversary/', 'snippet': 'Maurice Peress will re-create the debut performance of George Gershwin’s jazz-tinged work at Town Hall on Feb. 12.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The stage setting was unconventional as the program,” the New York Times music critic Olin Downes wrote of a concert he attended at Aeolian Hall, on West 43rd Street, on Feb. 12, 1924. He went on to describe “a scene that would have curdled the blood of a Stokowski or a Mengelberg,” two of the most revered conductors of the day, not least because the musicians drew on an instrumental arsenal that included pianos in various states of disassembly, an array of wind, brass and percussion, and “frying pans, large tin utensils and a speaking trumpet, later stuck into the end of a trombone.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Concert to Re-Create Debut of Gershwin’s ‘Rhapsody in Blue’ on 90th Anniversary', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 90 Years, Revisiting ‘Rhapsody in Blue’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gershwin, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peress, Maurice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T17:08:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 