nt_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T19:23:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Men's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1d920b01-eaf0-5c90-9c0b-e317ce92831b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1d920b01-eaf0-5c90-9c0b-e317ce92831b'}, {'abstract': 'At Sundance, the exhibition “The Art of Black and White Stripes,” co-curated by the Fiat heir Lapo Elkann, offers a preview of a salacious forthcoming documentary about the Italian football club Juventus.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/on-view-sex-scandal-and-soccer-the-italian-way/', 'snippet': 'At Sundance, the exhibition “The Art of Black and White Stripes,” co-curated by the Fiat heir Lapo Elkann, offers a preview of a salacious forthcoming documentary about the Italian football club Juventus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmakers Marco and Mauro La Villa conceived of their forthcoming documentary, “Black and White Stripes: the Juventus Story,” shortly after their father, Giovanni, died in 2001. He had rooted for Juventus, Italy’s most storied soccer club, his entire life. In Pietramilar, the tiny village were Giovanni was born and raised, priests moonlighted as scouts for professional soccer clubs, and at a young age Giovanni was offered a scholarship to go to school in Turin to play for Juventus’s junior squad. His mother disapproved, though, and forced him into the family’s gravestone-painting business. “His life’s great regret was that he didn’t get to chase his dream,” Marco says. The brothers, however, chased theirs, and are currently at Sundance, not screening their movie but rather promoting it with “The Art of Black and White Stripes,” a traveling art exhibition they co-curated with Lapo Elkann, a scion of the Agnelli family, which has owned the team since 1923.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17juventus-french/17juventus-french-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17juventus-french/17juventus-french-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17juventus-french/17juventus-french-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17juventus-french/17juventus-french-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17juventus-french/17juventus-french-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17juventus-french/17juventus-french-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17juventus-french/17juventus-french-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sex, Scandal and Soccer, the Italian Way', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'ran