n the East Coast? We’d like to hear your questions and insights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be in the 40s in New York City, but it’s nonetheless prime season for solidifying summer plans if yours include renting a vacation home. Do you have questions about East Coast summer vacation rentals? What’s the best way to find a house? What should you expect to pay? What’s the etiquette in a share house? Whether you’re dreaming of sunbathing in the Hamptons or on Martha’s Vineyard, now’s the time to get real about what that might entail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Submit Your Summer Vacation Rental Questions', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Coast (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T22:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cb2ef45-3f0d-5fc0-a614-907dae7aa5ea', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cb2ef45-3f0d-5fc0-a614-907dae7aa5ea'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sarah Aubel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/the-scene-mens-paris-fashion-week-givenchy-fallwinter-2014/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sarah Aubel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Sarah Aubel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Men’s Paris Fashion Week: Givenchy Fall/Winter 2014', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T22:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Aubel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aubel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22c6d6a4-7677-5549-be78-de67b681b136', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22c6d6a4-7677-5549-be78-de67b681b136'}, {'abstract': 'Devin Bing and his band, the Secret Service, mix old tunes and new in a show at the Metropolitan Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/arts/music/devin-bing-is-performing-at-the-metropolitan-room.html', 'snippet': 'Devin Bing and his band, the Secret Service, mix old tunes and new in a show at the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’ve got more style than a Rolex watch/I’ve got more style than a Rolls-Royce car,” Devin Bing, a Long Island blue-eyed soul crooner declared in his original ballad “Smooth” in the opening of his show on Thursday evening at the Metropolitan Room. Accompanying Mr. Bing, who played piano, was his four-member band, the Secret Service (Michael Feinberg on bass, Blaise Lanzetta on drums, Gavi Grodsky on guitar and Mark Bader on percussion), who churned out the kind of sleek, generic pop-soul grooves with jazz flavoring that are associated with hits by the likes of Robin Thicke.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/arts/18BING/18BING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/18/arts/18BING/18BIN