ork City’s safety net, Mayor Bill de Blasio on Friday proposed a raft of changes to close some of the gaps and improve communication between the criminal justice system and the agency charged with preventing child abuse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/myls-2/myls-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/myls-2/myls-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/myls-2/myls-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/myls-2/myls-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/myls-2/myls-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/myls-2/myls-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/myls-2/myls-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio, Citing ‘Horrible’ Death of Abused Boy, Unveils Plans for Reforms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio, Citing ‘Horrible’ Death of Abused Boy, Unveils Plans for Reforms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dobson, Myls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Administration for Children's Services (NYC)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T23:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b9ca54f-502b-5791-b90f-da84cf72fb42', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b9ca54f-502b-5791-b90f-da84cf72fb42'}, {'abstract': 'The director — who shows his sixth film at the festival this month — traces his personal and professional history in Park City.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/17/defining-moments-filmmaker-ira-sachss-sundance-stories/', 'snippet': 'The director — who shows his sixth film at the festival this month — traces his personal and professional history in Park City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director Ira Sachs has shown five of his films at the Sundance Film Festival since 1994. This week, he returns with his sixth, the much-anticipated “Love Is Strange,” with a cast including John Lithgow, Alfred Molina and Marisa Tomei. Sachs, whose childhood was partly spent in Park City, Utah, has been attending the festival since its earliest days – even before it was called Sundance — and was present at many of its most famous premieres. Here, he recounts his pivotal festival memories and the lessons he’s learned about the industry along the way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17ira-sachs/17ira-sachs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17ira-sachs/17ira-sachs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17ira-sachs/17ira-sachs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17ira-sachs/17ira-sachs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17ira-sachs/17ira-sachs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17ira-sachs/17ira-sachs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/t-magazine/17ira-sachs/17ira-sachs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Filmmaker Ira Sachs’s Sundance Stories', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Ira', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-17T23:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk'