93-aeba-2aa290ae3c9a'}, {'abstract': 'Some live-in superintendents have taken to decorating the basements of their buildings with knickknacks, some of which were left behind by departing tenants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/nyregion/live-in-superintendents-create-basement-sanctuaries.html', 'snippet': 'Some live-in superintendents have taken to decorating the basements of their buildings with knickknacks, some of which were left behind by departing tenants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As many New York City apartment dwellers know, some live-in superintendents love to decorate the basements of their buildings. Whether this urge to adorn stems from a proprietary sensibility — what’s near the boiler room is mine! — or is simply the result of too many personal knickknacks spilling out of tiny living spaces, the “super cave,” with its birds, potted plants and blinking religious icons, is a phenomenon you have surely seen before.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live-In Superintendents Create Basement Sanctuaries', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lairs of Super Men', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feuer, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basements and Cellars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wurfel, Gesche', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T00:16:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf26b01-2962-5d48-ad1c-d363e3104ae7', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf26b01-2962-5d48-ad1c-d363e3104ae7'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers have until the end of the month to reach agreement on a new farm bill and halt 1949 policies that could cause the cost of milk double.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/us/politics/standstill-on-farm-bill-may-revive-1949-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers have until the end of the month to reach agreement on a new farm bill and halt 1949 policies that could cause the cost of milk double.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Pressure is mounting on lawmakers working on a farm bill to come up with a deal before the end of the month, when the Agriculture Department is to begin enforcing a series of decades-old laws that could cause the price of milk and other agricultural products to double.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Standstill on Farm Bill May Revive 1949 Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Standstill on Farm Bill May Revive 1949 Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milk', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Farm Bureau', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T00:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bca8975-8e17-5287-b68d-48bdcf3535ee', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bca8975-8e17-5287-b68d-48bdcf3535ee'}, {'abstract': 'Colleagues at Ogilvy & Mather tucked into lunch at a meat-and-beer place at the new Gotham West Market, happy to have new options near the office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/nyregion/eating-pigs-head-terrine-talking-nascar.html', 'snippet': 'Colleagues at Ogilvy & Mather tucked into lunch at a meat-and-beer place at the new Gotham West Market, happy to have new options near the office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are ever looking for the world’s best airport food court, you could do worse than to visit the Gotham West Market, the blocklong complex that opened on 11th Avenue by 44th Street in November. There you’ll find high-end branded ramen, upmarket coffee, a kiosk named for the borough of Brooklyn and another named for one of the borough’s streets, where workers and other slurpers from the Far West Side circulate in predatory patterns through the cavernous, music-filled mall or take their places at counters or communal tables. The market joins Eataly and the Todd English Food Hall at the Plaza Hotel in making culinary New York more amenable to people who — no names, please — can’t make up their minds about where to eat. Next up are food courts in Battery Park City and Hudson Yards, and a proposed food mall by Anthony Bourdain.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/nyreg