ave a speech that was in large part an admission that he had been wrong.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The President on Mass Surveillance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The President on Mass Surveillance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T02:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf67d7c5-14df-58ef-bfb5-549cfbe2dac1', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf67d7c5-14df-58ef-bfb5-549cfbe2dac1'}, {'abstract': 'Young adults are surging into the state and federal exchanges now that website glitches have been fixed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/opinion/a-good-start-for-health-care-sign-ups.html', 'snippet': 'Young adults are surging into the state and federal exchanges now that website glitches have been fixed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Enrollments in health insurance plans through state and federal exchanges are rising rapidly, especially among young adults, making it likely that the Affordable Care Act will achieve a large and stabilizing mix of enrollees by the end of the open enrollment period on March 31. Some 2.2 million people signed up in the first three months, from Oct. 1 through Dec. 28.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Good Start for Health Care Sign-Ups', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Good Start for Health Care Sign-Ups', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T02:14:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/50a3572d-22e7-5388-9001-813273236354', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50a3572d-22e7-5388-9001-813273236354'}, {'abstract': 'Over two days Fredrick Brennan, 19, who uses a wheelchair, had nearly $5,000 stolen from him, helped the police identify the thief, and was left to get home on his own during a winter storm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/nyregion/city-newcomer-is-let-down-by-a-stranger-then-the-police.html', 'snippet': 'Over two days Fredrick Brennan, 19, who uses a wheelchair, had nearly $5,000 stolen from him, helped the police identify the thief, and was left to get home on his own during a winter storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fredrick Brennan, 19, moved out of his mother’s home in New Jersey in August and into an apartment in Brooklyn that his boss helped him find. This leap 