lican lawmakers to take up an overhaul of immigration laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg of New York will be in Washington on Friday to pressure Republican lawmakers to take up an overhaul of immigration laws. The meeting, his first major public policy event since his term ended, is pegged to President Obama’s State of the Union address on Jan. 28. The meeting will include prominent Republicans and U.S. Chamber of Commerce representatives. Speaker John A. Boehner and his leadership team are preparing a policy blueprint that is likely to include at least some path to legal status for 11 million undocumented immigrants in the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg to Push G.O.P. for Immigration Action', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg to Push G.O.P. For Immigration Action', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T02:32:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5724ae3-5440-5a9d-949a-0ccf95a69a01', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5724ae3-5440-5a9d-949a-0ccf95a69a01'}, {'abstract': 'A clerical worker is back on her feet, thanks in