ion': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/133e8818-c0c3-5c7d-bc4d-036bff7aaa32', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/133e8818-c0c3-5c7d-bc4d-036bff7aaa32'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,291 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/us/us-military-deaths-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,291 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,291 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Military Deaths in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T03:29:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/91ece96d-8ab0-5460-93ba-08b4adb3e848', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91ece96d-8ab0-5460-93ba-08b4adb3e848'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt’s security forces killed at least two protesters and arrested more than a hundred on Friday during demonstrations around the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/world/middleeast/egypt-clashes-erupt-during-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s security forces killed at least two protesters and arrested more than a hundred on Friday during demonstrations around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Egypt’s security forces killed at least two protesters and arrested more than a hundred on Friday during demonstrations around the country against the military government, the state news media reported. In recent days millions voted to approve a new constitution validating the military takeover last summer. Friday’s clashes are the first evidence that the new charter is unlikely to resolve the complaints of the protest movement, the terrorist threat from a budding insurgency or Egypt’s deep divisions. At least one protester was killed in Fayoum, south of Cairo, and another on the outskirts of Cairo. Separately, a report from Democracy International, an election-monitoring group that sent 80 observers to track the constitutional referendum, said it had “serious concerns” about the political environment of the voting, with “arrests and detention of dissenting voices” and “no real opportunity for those opposed to the government’s road map of the proposed constitution to dissent.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Clashes Erupt During Protests', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Clashes Erupt During Protests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T03:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d7cbfc-ccc8-5295-8f2e-da7833616cbe', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d7cbfc-ccc8-5295-8f2e-da7833616cbe'}, {'abstract': 'When Beatriz Rivera was a child, her family moved from Mexico to Yonkers. But the possibility of deportation limited her job opportunities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/nyregion/fighting-to-keep-a-life-built-in-the-united-states.html', 'snippet': 'When Beatriz Rivera was a child, her family moved from Mexico to Yonkers. But the possibility of deportation limited her job opportunities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Things have not gone according to the plan hatched long ago by Beatriz Rivera’s family. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/neediest/neediest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/nyregion/neediest/neediest-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType':