nstallment of the Source, a series of conversations on the roots of creativity, the artist Doug Aitken interviews the late architect Paolo Soleri, who talks about the importance of the unknowable.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/the-source-paolo-soleri-in-conversation-with-doug-aitken/', 'snippet': 'In the latest installment of the Source, a series of conversations on the roots of creativity, the artist Doug Aitken interviews the late architect Paolo Soleri, who talks about the importance of the unknowable.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Reality is a process,” says the Italian-American architect Paolo Soleri, who passed away last year at the age of 93. “So we are a tiny, tiny, tiny, tiny, little processing plant.” Soleri, who is best known for Arcosanti, his experimental planned community in the Arizona desert, talks to the artist Doug Aitken about the importance of the unknowable. The interview is part of the Source, a series of candid video conversations with several dozen noteworthy figures about their creative process, currently on view in a custom pavilion at the Sundance Film Festival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Source | Paolo Soleri in Conversation With Doug Aitken', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aitken, Doug', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soleri, Paolo (1919-2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T17:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94de0178-fa81-54fe-b0d9-557cef19226b', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94de0178-fa81-54fe-b0d9-557cef19226b'}, {'abstract': 'Dani Raymon talks to us, cryptically.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/variety-cryptic-crossword-6/', 'snippet': 'Dani Raymon talks to us, cryptically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — I believe this is Daniel Raymon’s first cryptic crossword puzzle published in The New York Times, and if this one is any indication, he’s got a nice cryptic career ahead of him. This was a fun one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Cryptic Crossword', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T17:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/212b55cb-a82b-580e-bcea-84ac9ef42154', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/212b55cb-a82b-580e-bcea-84ac9ef42154'}, {'abstract': 'Why the sociologizers are wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/the-myth-of-the-deserving-rich/', 'snippet': 'Why the sociologizers are wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many influential people have a hard time thinking straight about inequality. Partly, of course, this is because of Upton Sinclair’s dictum: it’s hard for a man to understand something when his salary depends on his not understanding it. Part of it is because even acknowledging that inequality is a real problem implicitly opens the door to taking progressive policies seriously.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Myth of the Deserving Rich', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T17:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91cbfe9a-1c7d-5f1b-b910-9a27d065d557', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91cbfe9a-1c7d-5f1b-b910-9a27d065d557'}, {'abstract': 'American soldiers are struggling to find relevance in the face of an uncertain future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/01/19/us/20130119-GARRISON.html', 'snippet': 'American soldiers are struggling to find relevance in the face of an uncertain future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American soldiers are struggling to find relevance in the face of an uncertain future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20130119-GARRISON-slide-YURT/20130119-GARRISON-slide-YURT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20130119-GARRISON-slide-YURT/20130119-GARRISON-slide-YURT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20130119-GARRISON-slide-YURT/20130119-GARRISON-slide-YURT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20130119-GA