 'snippet': 'Patient costs have risen as doctors have become more entrepreneurial, protecting their turf through lobbying by medical societies and increasing revenues by offering new and more lucrative procedures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CONWAY, Ark. — Kim Little had not thought much about the tiny white spot on the side of her cheek until a physician’s assistant at her dermatologist’s office warned that it might be cancerous. He took a biopsy, returning 15 minutes later to confirm the diagnosis and schedule her for an outpatient procedure at the Arkansas Skin Cancer Center in Little Rock, 30 miles away.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20140119PROCEDURES-1/20140119PROCEDURES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20140119PROCEDURES-1/20140119PROCEDURES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20140119PROCEDURES-1/20140119PROCEDURES-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20140119PROCEDURES-1/20140119PROCEDURES-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20140119PROCEDURES-1/20140119PROCEDURES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20140119PROCEDURES-1/20140119PROCEDURES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/20140119PROCEDURES-1/20140119PROCEDURES-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Patients’ Costs Skyrocket; Specialists’ Incomes Soar', 'kicker': 'Paying Till It Hurts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patients’ Costs Skyrocket; Specialists’ Incomes Soar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Elisabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Little', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baptist Health Medical Center (Ark)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T18:44:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec5e8dc1-0b13-51ca-9a16-61af1d650d43', 'word_count': 3715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec5e8dc1-0b13-51ca-9a16-61af1d650d43'}, {'abstract': 'At men’s wear shows, the Victoria Beckham way of holding a large bag as though it were a tiny clutch infused runway style.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/threes-a-trend-clutching-mens-bags-big-or-small/', 'snippet': 'At men’s wear shows, the Victoria Beckham way of holding a large bag as though it were a tiny clutch infused runway style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a source of mild debate in the style-obsessed sphere whether Victoria Beckham truly originated, or at the very least popularized, the style of clutching — as opposed to toting or carrying — a leather handbag as one would a more diminutive evening style. This manner of wearing a large bag — with an arm slipped through both handles, the one hand supporting the bottom while the straps fall to the side — was surprisingly adopted by some major fashion houses for their men’s wear runway presentations. The slick dudes at Gucci looked no less manly carrying soft pastel leather bags in this fashion, nor did Tomas Maier’s athletic guys wearing the house‘s signature leather bags. At Valentino, an actual clutch replaced the large bag style, but the stylistic technique remained the same. And aside from the aesthetic affectation, this method also provides an added amount of security. It would certainly require a skilled purse snatcher to disentangle the bag from its owner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/t-magazine/18trend-clutch-pask/18trend-clutch-pask-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/18/t-magazine/18trend-clutch-pask/18trend-clutch-pask-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/t-magazine/18trend-clutch-pask/18trend-clutch-pask-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's