gic town of Bor from rebel forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Sudan Recaptures Town From Rebels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Sudan Recaptures Town From Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kulish, Nicholas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bor (South Sudan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T19:56:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24c2a634-17e9-5bff-88ce-07730e556b74', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24c2a634-17e9-5bff-88ce-07730e556b74'}, {'abstract': 'Life is performed on a million tiny stages. The one-man show never quite ends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/opinion/sunday/you-can-tell-everybody-this-is-your-song.html', 'snippet': 'Life is performed on a million tiny stages. The one-man show never quite ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR most of my 20s I played in the indie rock band Sleater-Kinney. We wrote songs, we recorded them, we toured. In my 30s, though, things changed. I started spending most of my time writing or working on the TV show “Portlandia.” I haven’t played many live shows in the past decade, but somehow I feel as if I’m still on tour — not just with my bandmates, but with everyone. So I thought I’d try writing a song again, so I’d have something to play. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/sunday-review/19SONG/19SONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 244, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/sunday-review/19SONG/19SONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 244}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/sunday-review/19SONG/19SONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/sunday-review/19SONG/19SONG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/sunday-review/19SONG/19SONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/19/sunday-review/19SONG/19SONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/sunday-review/19SONG/19SONG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Can Tell Everybody This Is Your Song', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Can Tell Everybody This Is Your Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}