r “neglected topics” for me to weigh in on this year. There were 1,300 comments that came pouring in, many with multiple ideas, and I’m still thinking them through. Today’s column takes off on one of the suggestions that came up regularly: climate change. It’s not 100 percent neglected of course, but I think it’s vastly undercovered considering the scale of the issues. So read the column and share your thoughts below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers and Climate Change', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T22:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae18f9a4-0841-5cac-8386-17863420eaa5', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae18f9a4-0841-5cac-8386-17863420eaa5'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Schoenholz takes us back.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/18/olden-goldies/', 'snippet': 'Dan Schoenholz takes us back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — Hands up if you like spoonerisms. For those of you just joining us, a spoonerism is a word or phrase in which letters or syllables are swapped. That can happen with tips of the slung, sorry, slips of the tongue, and today Dan Schoenholz has spoonerized a set of seven oldies songs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olden Goldies', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-18T23:00:00+0000', 'document_t