e': None, 'lastname': 'Droubi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cce30212-dcd9-5ee6-a0a0-b9e26d23320c', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cce30212-dcd9-5ee6-a0a0-b9e26d23320c'}, {'abstract': 'Excerpts from an interview with Jihad Makdissi, a former Foreign Ministry spokesman in Syria who fled in 2012 as the government cracked down on protesters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/world/middleeast/in-syria-former-official-says-nobody-is-winning.html', 'snippet': 'Excerpts from an interview with Jihad Makdissi, a former Foreign Ministry spokesman in Syria who fled in 2012 as the government cracked down on protesters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following are excerpts from an interview with Jihad Makdissi, a former Foreign Ministry spokesman in Syria who fled in 2012 as the government of President Bashar al-Assad cracked down on antigovernment protesters. Mr. Makdissi, however, has not supported the rebels. He casts himself as a voice for the Syrians who remain on the sidelines, skeptical of the armed uprising but still wanting change. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Syria, Former Official Says, ‘Nobody Is Winning’', 'kicker': 'Q. and A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Syria, Former Official Says, ‘Nobody Is Winning’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Makdissi, Jihad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T03:44:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f65d19-1f93-59eb-bd89-8fe7eb994b7d', 'word_count': 1661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f65d19-1f93-59eb-bd89-8fe7eb994b7d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Pinkney, a strategist who ran the campaigns in landmark races for black politicians, also advised Hubert H. Humphrey in his second bid for the Democratic presidential nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/us/arnold-r-pinkney-dies-at-83-steered-1984-jackson-run.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Pinkney, a strategist who ran the campaigns in landmark races for black politicians, also advised Hubert H. Humphrey in his second bid for the Democratic presidential nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There are always more slaves than slave masters,” the Rev. Jesse Jackson roared in a speech in Selma, Ala., early in his 1984 presidential campaign. “We can win! We got master’s degrees in disappointment and Ph.D.s in how to overcome!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/dog-pickney-obit/dog-pickney-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/us/dog-pickney-obit/dog-pickney-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 523}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/dog-pickney-obit/dog-pickney-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/us/dog-pickney-obit/dog-pickney-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1784, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption':