at killed at least 20 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PESHAWAR, Pakistan — A bomb exploded inside a vehicle at a Pakistani military compound in the country’s northwest on Sunday, killing at least 20 members of a paramilitary unit and wounding 30 more, a security official said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deadly Bomb Blast Rocks Pakistan Military Compound', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deadly Bomb Blast Rocks Pakistan Military Compound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Ismail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bannu (Pakistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehrik-e-Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frontier Corps', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T08:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ismail Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22eaa160-9fa7-53c8-8a83-77093933c8ad', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22eaa160-9fa7-53c8-8a83-77093933c8ad'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/arts/whats-on-today.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights', 'lead_paragraph': '1:30 P.M. (Showtime2) AMÉLIE (2001) Audrey Tautou, above, in her breakthrough role, plays a French sprite working as a waitress who lays out elaborate practical jokes as payback for those who offend her friends. When she falls in love with Nino (Mathieu Kassovitz), Amélie finds herself incapable of revealing her feelings and instead turns Paris, recreated through sets and computer-generated imagery, into a kind of treasure hunt as she leaves clues about her identity, and he trails after her. Writing in The New York Times, Elvis Mitchell called this comedy from Jean-Pierre Jeunet, whose original title was “Le Fabuleux Destin d’Amélie Poulain,” “a sugar-rush of a movie.” It has, he said, “a hypnotic sense of romance; it’s a fable filled with longing, with a heroine who constantly flirts with failure.” The film’s “fastidious complex of flesh and fantasy is a dazzling achievement,” he added. There is no denying, he said “that ‘Amélie’ is, to paraphrase its title, fabulous.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Today?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T09:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1061766-88e1-515c-8aba-ed5676f4ca8b', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1061766-88e1-515c-8aba-ed5676f4ca8b'}, {'abstract': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/in-our-pages-january-20/', 'snippet': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', '