 end the “epidemic” of traffic violence in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/nyregion/pedestrian-and-bicyclist-are-killed-in-separate-traffic-accidents.html', 'snippet': 'Four people were struck and killed in crashes over the weekend, coinciding with Mayor Bill de Blasio’s call on Friday to end the “epidemic” of traffic violence in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A large highway sign flashed orange warnings to pedestrians. Patrol officers in neon vests directed traffic; others gave tickets to drivers and nearly a dozen jaywalkers. And at each corner of West 96th Street and Broadway on the Upper West Side of Manhattan on Sunday, residents warned one another to use caution: The traffic here can be deadly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Traffic Fatalities in Two Days As Mayor Vows to Make Streets Safer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Four Traffic Fatalities in Two Days as Mayor Vows to Make Streets Safer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Samantha', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santiago, Pedro', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurtado, Angela', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tinoco, Abel', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T17:48:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b17a43-4d14-516c-875d-5757b4b988c5', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b17a43-4d14-516c-875d-5757b4b988c5'}, {'abstract': '“Ride Along,” featuring Ice Cube and Kevin Hart, continues a winning streak at the box office for movies with predominantly black casts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/19/a-fast-start-for-ride-along-at-the-box-office/', 'snippet': '“Ride Along,” featuring Ice Cube and Kevin Hart, continues a winning streak at the box office for movies with predominantly black casts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The action comedy “Ride Along” burned rubber at North American theaters, taking in a projected $47.8 million for the four-day Martin Luther King Jr. holiday and leaving another new film, “Jack Ryan: Shadow Recruit,” choking on its fumes. “Ride Along” (Universal Pictures), featuring Ice Cube and the increasingly popular Kevin Hart, cost about $25 million to make and continues a winning streak at the box office for movies with predominantly black casts. About 50 percent of opening-weekend ticket buyers were black, with Hispanic moviegoers making up 30 percent, according to Universal. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fast Start for ‘Ride Along’ at the Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fast Start For u2018Ride Alongu2019', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam