umbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/klondike/klondike-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/klondike/klondike-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/klondike/klondike-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/klondike/klondike-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gold and Survival, Yes, but Scripts and Stars, Too', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gold and Survival, Yes, but Scripts and Stars, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T22:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9feecda-207c-5d3b-8d90-4042d369cf45', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9feecda-207c-5d3b-8d90-4042d369cf45'}, {'abstract': 'Ringo Starr is part of “Dance Pantsed,” a new animated special featuring the Powerpuff Girls on the Cartoon Network.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/arts/television/ringo-starr-joins-the-powerpuff-girls-for-dance-pantsed.html', 'snippet': 'Ringo Starr is part of “Dance Pantsed,” a new animated special featuring the Powerpuff Girls on the Cartoon Network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Very soon now, the airwaves will be jammed with remembrances of the Beatles’ first appearance on “The Ed Sullivan Show,” because there’s nothing the baby-boom generation likes better than commemorating 50th anniversaries. If you stare hard enough at the clips of those screaming young female fans from February 1964, you can see an unspoken question in their eyes: “Will one of these guys, in 2014, be singing a song aimed at my grandchildren or even my great-grandchildren about dressing up as a superpower-endowed little girl?”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Little Help From a Friend of Buttercup', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Little Help From a Friend of Buttercup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cartoon Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Starr, Ringo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T22:03:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fa7e386-53c0-5307-8ff7-4fd530921962', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fa7e386-53c0-5307-8ff7-4fd530921962'}, {'abstract': 'The soprano Anna Netrebko, absent from the first two performances of “L’Elisir d’Amore” at the Met, arrived to inhabit the leading role fully on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/arts/music/anna-netrebko-in-bel-canto-mode-for-lelisir-damore.html', 'snippet': 'The soprano Anna Netrebko, absent from the first two performances of “L’Elisir d’Amore” at the Met, arrived to inhabit the leading role fully on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 7, two days before the Metropolitan Opera’s revival of Bartlett Sher’s 2012 production of Donizetti’s “L’Elisir d’Amore” was scheduled to open, the company announced that the soprano Anna Netrebko had the flu and would not perform the role of Adina. Curiously, the announcement specified that Ms. Netrebko, probably the most celebrated soprano in opera right now, would miss the first two performances but planned to return for the third. Singers grappling with an illness usually cannot anticipate how long their incapacity will last. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunefully Purveyed Snake Oil, Anyone?', 'kicker': 'Opera Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunefully Purveyed Snake Oil, Anyone?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netrebko, Anna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "L'Elisir D'Amore (Movie)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T22:04:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a21a20ac-909c-5746-958e-cc94da036bb8', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a21a20ac-909c-5746-958e-cc94da036bb8'}, {'abstract': 'The guitarist Bill Frisell was joined by Buddy Miller and Carrie Rodriguez in playing songs from a historic 1927 recording session in Tennessee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/arts/music/bill-frisell-and-friends-play-venerable-country-tunes.html', 'snippet': 'The guitarist Bill Frisell was joined by Buddy Miller and Carrie Rodriguez in playing songs from a historic 1927 recording session in Tennessee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there were an appropriate emoji ideogram for the Bristol Sessions, the 1927 recordings that helped start the framing of what we now know as country music, it wouldn’t be a cartoon face conveying anger, sadness or gratitude — nothing that simple. It might be one of the lesser-known ones: the image of Japanese-carp wind socks on a flagpole, the flags flown on Children’s Day in Japan representing high hopes to navigate the currents of an uncertain life and grow up with health and courage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/bristol/bristol-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/bristol/bristol-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/bristol/bristol-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/bristol/bristol-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1478, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/bristol/bristol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/bristol/bristol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/bristol/bristol-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tipping a Hat to Country Music Pioneers', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tipping a Hat to Country Music Pioneers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frisell, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Buddy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Carrie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T22:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1873bad3-702a-5292-9347-e253d1e1d548', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1873bad3-702a-5292-9347-e253d1e1d548'}, {'abstract': 'The mandolinist Avi Avital was joined by the Enso String Quartet and others in Weill Recital Hall at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/arts/music/avi-avital-helps-revive-and-grow-an-instrument.html', 'snippet': 'The mandolinist Avi Avital was joined by the Enso String Quartet and others in Weill Recital Hall at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pianists can spend a lifetime learning a vast established repertory, but a greater degree of creativity is essential for double bassists, trumpeters or mandolinists hoping for careers in the spotlight. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Repertory of Mandolin Is in Motion', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Repertory of Mandolin is in Motion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Avital, Avi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Enso String Quartet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-19T22:08:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9d0513a-dc44-5445-a4d8-4fe0cc21ab55', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9d0513a-dc44-5445-a4d8-4fe0cc21ab55'}, {'abstract': 'Fred Frith and Nels Cline, virtuosos with conventional guitar techniques, performed their first public duet at the Alternative Guitar Summit at Subculture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/arts/music/fred-frith-and-nels-cline-create-new-soundscapes.html', 'snippet': 'Fred Frith and Nels Cline, virtuosos with conventional guitar techniques, performed their first public duet at the Alternative Guitar Summit at Subculture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the guitarists Fred Frith and Nels Cline played their first public duet on Saturday night at Subculture, it didn’t always sound like guitar music. It sounded, at times, like a sanitation truck’s trash compactor, like an orchestra tuning up, like a brawl between flocks of geese, like a creaky water pump, like a collapsing carillon and like a slowed-down train wreck. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/guitar/guitar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/guitar/guitar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/guitar/guitar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/guitar/guitar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/guitar/guitar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/guitar/guitar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/guitar/guitar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wh