e, 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e11441-04f2-5057-93e8-f11db1ac6e34', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e11441-04f2-5057-93e8-f11db1ac6e34'}, {'abstract': 'Although there is a feeling that the Yankees will make the highest bid among the many teams pursuing the Japanese pitcher Masahiro Tanaka, he does not have to take the most lucrative offer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/sports/baseball/many-choices-for-tanaka-as-deadline-nears.html', 'snippet': 'Although there is a feeling that the Yankees will make the highest bid among the many teams pursuing the Japanese pitcher Masahiro Tanaka, he does not have to take the most lucrative offer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Masahiro Tanaka’s baseball fate will be decided by Friday afternoon, and it appears that more than a half-dozen teams have made bids for him or are prepared to. The Yankees, the Los Angeles Dodgers, the Arizona Diamondbacks, the Chicago White Sox and the Chicago Cubs are said to be among the teams in hot pursuit of Tanaka, a Japanese right-handed pitcher.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/baseball/20tanaka-1/20tanaka-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/baseball/20tanaka-1/20tanaka-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 799}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/baseball/20tanaka-1/20tanaka-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ