5ba-5843-ac04-9a9edfb68ee2'}, {'abstract': 'In my courtroom, it is far too easy for claimants to cheat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/opinion/fixing-disability-courts.html', 'snippet': 'In my courtroom, it is far too easy for claimants to cheat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — IT’S hard to imagine a more cynical fraud. According to an indictment unsealed last week by the Manhattan district attorney’s office, post-9/11 phobias of airplanes and skyscrapers were among the fictitious ailments described by retired New York City police officers and firefighters who, in a scheme involving as many as 1,000 people, are accused of ripping off the Social Security disability system by filing false claims.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fixing Disability Courts', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fixing Disability Courts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disability Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Social Security Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T01:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By D. Randall Frye', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://a