b81-495eac33d7e8'}, {'abstract': 'One of Egypt’s most prominent liberal intellectuals was charged with insulting the judiciary because he criticized a court ruling against three American nonprofits that promote democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/world/middleeast/egypt-says-twitter-post-by-liberal-was-crime.html', 'snippet': 'One of Egypt’s most prominent liberal intellectuals was charged with insulting the judiciary because he criticized a court ruling against three American nonprofits that promote democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A prosecutor on Sunday charged one of Egypt’s most prominent liberal intellectuals with insulting the judiciary because he posted a message on Twitter criticizing a court ruling against three American nonprofits that promote democracy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Says Twitter Post by Liberal Was Crime', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Says Twitter Post by Liberal Was Crime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamzawy, Amr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T01:48:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16ab40ce-e006-5816-9ab6-c4c2b9f1dc3b', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16ab40ce-e006-5816-9ab6-c4c2b9f1dc3b'}, {'abstract': 'John Tortorella had a history of blowups during his career, including one when he led the Rangers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/sports/hockey/tortorellas-temper-lands-him-in-trouble-again.html', 'snippet': 'John Tortorella had a history of blowups during his career, including one when he led the Rangers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Tortorella had kept his temper in check remarkably well this season, but in an explosion of fury Saturday night, his inability to ignore provocation got the better of him. Now Tortorella, the Vancouver coach, almost certainly faces a substantial fine and may be suspended.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/KLEIN/KLEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/KLEIN/KLEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/KLEIN/KLEIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/KLEIN/KLEIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/KLEIN/KLEIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/KLEIN/KLEIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/sports/KLEIN/KLEIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tortorella’s Temper Lands Him in Trouble Again', 'kicker': 'On Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tortorella’s Temper Lands Him in Trouble Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calgary Flames', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hartley, Bob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T01:49:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23b2b606-9194-56b7-b73e-76412db59518', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23b2b606-9194-56b7-b73e-76412db59518'}, {'abstract': 'Sixteen-year-olds in New York belong in the juvenile system, not in adult courts or prisons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/opinion/when-children-become-criminals.html', 'snippet': 'Sixteen-year-olds in New York belong in the juvenile system, not in adult courts or prisons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is one of two states, the other being North Carolina, in which 16-year-olds are automatically tried as adults. This is the case despite overwhelming evidence that sending children into adult courts, rather than the juvenile justice system, needlessly destroys lives and further endangers the public by turning nonviolent youngsters into hardened criminals. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Children Become Criminals', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Children Become Criminals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T02:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c51f6c0-4c19-5a3e-bdfb-8154a9c86151', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c51f6c0-4c19-5a3e-bdfb-8154a9c86151'}, {'abstract': 'When the F.E.C. staff did its job and sought an investigation of Crossroads GPS, it was blocked by the usual deadlock vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/opinion/dangerous-inaction-by-the-election-commission.html', 'snippet': 'When the F.E.C. staff did its job and sought an investigation of Crossroads GPS, it was blocked by the usual deadlock vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all its signature dysfunction, the Federal Election Commission has a staff of professionals working to track big money and shady behavior in the nation’s congressional and presidential campaigns. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dangerous Inaction by the Election Commission', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dangerous Inaction by the Election Commission', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T02:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/964730b9-8cbe-5943-b6b3-8142f200dcdd', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964730b9-8cbe-5943-b6b3-8142f200dcdd'}, {'abstract': 'The top-ranked Huskies overwhelmed the Scarlet Knights for their 25th straight victory and their 19th this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/sports/ncaabasketball/undefeated-connecticut-leaves-no-doubts-at-rutgers.html', 'snippet': 'The top-ranked Huskies overwhelmed the Scarlet Knights for their 25th straight victory and their 19th this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PISCATAWAY, N.J. — C. Vivian Stringer, the women’s basketball coach at Rutgers, appeared on the video scoreboard before Sunday’s game against Connecticut in a film clip intended to stoke her players and the announced 6,480 fans at Rutgers Athletic Center.', 'print_section': 'D', 