: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-jan-19-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 19, 2014', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Lottery Numbers for Jan. 19, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T05:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/0752daa1-6e1b-55df-88ac-1bbf813b7d38', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0752daa1-6e1b-55df-88ac-1bbf813b7d38'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers estimated that N.H.L. teams and their insurers paid about $653 million in salary to players sidelined by concussions and other injuries over three recent seasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/sports/hockey/citing-costs-nhl-injury-study-urges-more-safety.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers estimated that N.H.L. teams and their insurers paid about $653 million in salary to players sidelined by concussions and other injuries over three recent seasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An author of a new medical study said the high cost of paying injured N.H.L. players should push the league to stiffen what he described as inadequate measures to prevent brain trauma, including rules that still allow fighting. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citing Costs, N.H.L. Injury Study Urges More Safety', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citing Costs, Study Urges More Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Injury Prevention (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T05:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84630486-4269-500b-9311-17dd5b372499', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84630486-4269-500b-9311-17dd5b372499'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:10 A.M. (Starz) CHARLIE BARTLETT (2008) After being kicked out of private school for making fake IDs, Charlie (Anton Yelchin, above) goes the public route, arriving at a high school in a chauffeured limousine, wearing a navy blazer with a Latin insignia and toting a briefcase. An instant pariah, he discovers a road to popularity paved with prescription drugs. Soon, he has become a sort of therapist, dispensing advice and medication to classmates. Hope Davis plays his flaky, depressed mother; Robert Downey Jr. is the high school’s alcoholic principal, whose relationship with Charlie turns into warfare, once he learns that Charlie is dating his rebellious daughter (Kat Dennings). “In the movie’s funniest scene, Charlie and his business partner, Murphy, the school bully who beat him up and dunked his head in the toilet when he first arrived, dispense Ritalin to the students and turn a dance into a frenzied free-for-all with bare-breasted girls running down the halls,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times. “The movie, directed by Jon Poll from a screenplay by Gustin Nash, is never more amusingly subversive than in this scene, which suggests the hypocrisy of American attitudes toward drugs without putting it in words.” Still, he said, “as the movie dashes from one base to the next, it never coalesces into the character-driven, serious comedy with heart that you want it be.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T05:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f157e663-a2da-57a4-bcac-dd1f939fc2cc', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f157e663-a2da-57a4-bcac-dd1f939fc2cc'}, {'abstract': 'Because of Martin Luther King’s Birthday, alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/nyregion/parking-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Because of Martin Luther King’s Birthday, alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because of Martin Luther King’s Birthday, alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Monday. Other regulations remain in effect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parking Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parking Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T05:44:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bc89c89-e276-5b34-a874-a71500be92e3', 'word_count': 23, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bc89c89-e276-5b34-a874-a71500be92e3'}, {'abstract': 'Social commentary, some of it born of personal tragedy, was just one hallmark of Mr. Gelman’s work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/arts/international/juan-gelman-leftist-argentine-poet-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Social commentary, some of it born of personal tragedy, was just one hallmark of Mr. Gelman’s work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Juan Gelman, an Argentine poet who challenged the petty and profound tyrannies of his country’s military junta — including those directed against his family — in works that established him as a formidable presence in the Spanish-language literary canon, died on Tuesday at his home in Mexico City, where he had lived for many years. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/obit-gelman/obit-gelman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/obit-gelman/obit-gelman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/20/arts/o