settes, digital albums and LPs, fell 8 percent from 2012 to 2013, to 289 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/01/20/business/media/20most.html', 'snippet': 'Album sales declined again this year. Total sales, a figure that includes CDs, cassettes, digital albums and LPs, fell 8 percent from 2012 to 2013, to 289 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Album sales declined again this year. Total sales, a figure that includes CDs, cassettes, digital albums and LPs, fell 8 percent from 2012 to 2013, to 289 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/business/20Most/20Most-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/18/business/20Most/20Most-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/business/20Most/20Most-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/business/20Most/20Most-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 1851, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/business/20Most/20Most-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/18/business/20Most/20Most-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/18/business/20Most/20Most-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Popular Demand', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T06:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e28c8f88-500a-5204-a838-5af7eee06466', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e28c8f88-500a-5204-a838-5af7eee06466'}, {'abstract': 'The tie is a first for the guild. Until now, the honor has been considered a good indicator of which film would win the best-picture Oscar.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/gravity-and-12-years-in-unprecedented-tie-for-producers-guild-award/', 'snippet': 'The tie is a first for the guild. Until now, the honor has been considered a good indicator of which film would win the best-picture Oscar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — In an indication of how highly competitive this year is for film, the Producers Guild of America announced a tie for its best feature award on Sunday. “Gravity” and “12 Years a Slave” both took the top honors, the first time there has been a tie for the award. The producers prize is considered a good forecaster for the eventual Oscar best picture winner; the two prizes have matched up for the last six years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Gravity’ and ‘12 Years’ in Unprecedented Tie for Producers Guild Award', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Producers Guild of America', 'rank': 2, 'major':