://article/b6be5088-f383-5fba-a5e9-01ea7db78813'}, {'abstract': 'The sharp swing in the stock on Monday came after an announcement that sales of the company’s Wii U console were smaller than expected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/business/international/nintendo-shares.html', 'snippet': 'The sharp swing in the stock on Monday came after an announcement that sales of the company’s Wii U console were smaller than expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Nintendo shares plunged on Monday, then recovered much of their losses as investors focused on indications that the company was softening its resistance to mobile video gaming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nintendo Shares Recover Slightly After Plunge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nintendo Co Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wii (Video Game System)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T09:07:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/309c5a3a-fbc2-5d7d-a192-4a35a902712a', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/309c5a3a-fbc2-5d7d-a192-4a35a902712a'}, {'abstract': 'Han Seok-woo of the Korea Trade-Investment Promotion Agency was kidnapped on Sunday by four gunmen, officials at the South Korean Foreign Ministry said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/world/asia/south-korean-trade-official-abducted-in-libyan-capital.html', 'snippet': 'Han Seok-woo of the Korea Trade-Investment Promotion Agency was kidnapped on Sunday by four gunmen, officials at the South Korean Foreign Ministry said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Gunmen have kidnapped a South Korean trade official in the Libyan capital of Tripoli, according to the South Korean government, which advised its citizens Monday to leave the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korean Trade Official Abducted in Libyan Capital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya: South Korean Official Abducted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tripoli (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Han Seok-woo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T09:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51a62019-8c08-5e86-b11a-8bd58d2d49f6', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51a62019-8c08-5e86-b11a-8bd58d2d49f6'}, {'abstract': 'A letter exchange between President Xi Jinping of China and overseas Chinese students in Germany highlights what one Western intelligence analyst called a well-honed system to bring technology from the West to China by appealing to patriotism.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/from-chinese-students-in-germany-a-technology-promise-to-motherland/', 'snippet': 'A letter exchange between President Xi Jinping of China and overseas Chinese students in Germany highlights what one Western intelligence analyst called a well-honed system to bring technology from the West to China by appealing to patriotism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Illustrating the grip the Communist Party and government try to maintain on overseas Chinese students, researchers and businesspeople, an exchange of letters between President Xi Jinping and Chinese students in Germany has produced passionate promises from the students to serve the motherland — and deliver “advanced technology” back to China, the state news media reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Chinese Students in Germany, a Technology Promise to the Motherland', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Industrial Espionage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunar New Year', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T09:16:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc7adafb-3bff-5bca-9f58-e46a37afb3e9', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc7adafb-3bff-5bca-9f58-e46a37afb3e9'}, {'abstract': 'While Leonard Freed made historic images of the civil rights era, they would not have been seen if not for his loyal master printer — his wife, Brigitte Freed.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/the-photographer-and-his-printer-partners-in-art-and-love/', 'snippet': 'While Leonard Freed made historic images of the civil rights era, they would not have been seen if not for his loyal master printer — his wife, Brigitte Freed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leonard Freed’s photos from Harlem, Brooklyn and the historic 1963 March on Washington lay on a workroom table in the home he shared with his wife, Brigitte. She stood over the images — as she has over his reputation — with a slight smile of pride.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/blogs/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/17/blogs/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/blogs/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/17/blogs/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY/20140117-lens-freed-slide-0CPY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1516, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capt