/article/91e8490a-daf7-522e-9891-c5c143ca227f'}, {'abstract': 'With his re-election campaign looming, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo has enviable voter approval ratings and general support for many of his newest proposals, according to a new poll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/nyregion/majority-of-new-york-voters-say-they-would-re-elect-cuomo-poll-finds.html', 'snippet': 'With his re-election campaign looming, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo has enviable voter approval ratings and general support for many of his newest proposals, according to a new poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With his re-election campaign looming, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo has enviable approval ratings from New York voters and general support for many of his newest proposals, including legalizing medical marijuana, according to a new poll released on Monday. But his specific plan for the drug — to use an obscure law, and not new action by the State Legislature, to provide it to patients — is much less popular.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Majority of New York Voters Say They Would Re-elect Cuomo, Poll Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voters Back Another Term for Cuomo, a Poll Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, Jesse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Siena College', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T10:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'bylin