ased on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Financial Services Sector Optimistic, Survey Finds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Confederation of British Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PricewaterhouseCoopers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T11:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddcea369-dfa9-5e86-830d-3bd89b68ffb6', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddcea369-dfa9-5e86-830d-3bd89b68ffb6'}, {'abstract': 'Calm down, protesters. Namibia’s conservation policy is working.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/opinion/a-trophy-hunt-thats-good-for-rhinos.html', 'snippet': 'Calm down, protesters. Namibia’s conservation policy is working.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s stipulate up front that there is no great sport in hunting a black rhinoceros, especially not in Namibia’s open countryside. The first morning we went out tracking in the northern desert there, we nosed around in vehicles for several hours until our guides spotted a rhino a half mile off. Then we hiked quietly up into a high valley. There, a rhino mom with two huge horns stood calmly in front of us next to her calf, as if triceratops had come back to life, at a distance of 200 yards. We shot them, relentlessly, with our cameras.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 583, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 583}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 667, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 667, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trophy Hunt That’s Good for Rhinos', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rhino Trophy Hunt That’s Good for Rhinos', 'name': None