blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/sundance-a-food-documentary-that-hopes-to-start-a-movement/', 'snippet': '“Fed Up,” whose backers include Katie Couric and Laurie David, hopes to organize town hall meetings as part of its argument that food companies have misled consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — Stephanie Soechtig’s “Fed Up,” as one might guess from the title, is not a cheery little documentary. While not quite delivering a Michael Moore-style vituperation, Ms. Soechtig and her executive producers — among them Katie Couric and Laurie David — make their exasperation extremely clear. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance: A Food Documentary That Hopes to Start a Movement', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couric, Katie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'David, Laurie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T18:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d043997-6646-5109-865f-fb522d314012', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d043997-6646-5109-865f-fb522d314012'}, {'abstract': 'Lt. Gov. Kim Guadagno denies that she linked a redevelopment project to federal assistance for projects in the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/video-of-new-jersey-lt-governor-denying-hoboken-mayors-allegation/', 'snippet': 'Lt. Gov. Kim Guadagno denies that she linked a redevelopment project to federal assistance for projects in the aftermath of Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lt. Gov. Kim Guadagno of New Jersey flatly denied allegations made over the weekend that she linked federal aid to support of the Christie administration, as my colleague Alan Feuer reports. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of New Jersey Lt. Governor Denying Hoboken Mayor’s Allegation', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guadagno, Kimberly M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kornacki, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmer, Dawn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hoboken (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T18:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ae1b1cd-1e91-58de-81a4-8972058d9c4e', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ae1b1cd-1e91-58de-81a4-8972058d9c4e'}, {'abstract': 'I do not think that word means what Bret Stephens thinks it means.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/department-of-corrections-and-not/', 'snippet': 'I do not think that word means what Bret Stephens thinks it means.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So Bret Stephens of the WSJ has contacted the Times to protest my remark, in today’s column, that his error in using nominal incomes has not been c