ied as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,292 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the death of the following American recently:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Military Deaths in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T23:08:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/2846dc32-a2cf-5e89-a7fe-72c52d4bc9b5', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2846dc32-a2cf-5e89-a7fe-72c52d4bc9b5'}, {'abstract': 'A sale would be the latest step in IBM’s evolution from a dominant producer of hardware like computers and servers into a company focused on providing services to governments and businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/ibm-restarts-talks-on-low-end-server-business/', 'snippet': 'A sale would be the latest step in IBM’s evolution from a dominant producer of hardware like computers and servers into a company focused on providing services to governments and businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IBM has restarted efforts to sell its low-end server business and is in talks with companies including Dell and Lenovo, two people briefed on the process said Monday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi