s, offer “direct evidence” of torture and execution.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/20/war-crimes-experts-call-syrian-defectors-photographs-direct-evidence-of-assads-killing-machine/', 'snippet': 'A team of legal and forensic experts concluded that post-mortem photographs, provided to the Syrian opposition by a man who describes himself as a defector from President Bashar al-Assad’s security forces, offer “direct evidence” of torture and ex...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, Wednesday, Jan. 22 | Thousands of post-mortem photographs of scarred, emaciated corpses, provided to the Syrian opposition by a man who describes himself as a defector from the security forces of President Bashar al-Assad, appear to offer “direct evidence” of torture and execution on a mass scale, a team of legal and forensic experts concluded in a report made public on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'War Crimes Experts Call Syrian Defector’s Photographs ‘Direct Evidence’ of Assad’s ‘Killing Machine’', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-20T23:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ccd5bdf-d0a1-5a18-863a-dd9027f442ca', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ccd5bdf-d0a1-5a18-863a-dd9027f442ca'}, {'abstract': 'Ten people were taken to local hospitals, four of them in critical condition, according to Bernard J. Kanger Jr., Omaha’s interim fire chief. Seven others were injured but did not go to the hospital, he said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/us/omaha-plant-explosion.html', 'snippet': 'Ten people were taken to local hospitals, four of them in critical condition, according to Bernard J. Kanger Jr., Omaha’s interim fire chief. Seven others were injured but did not go to the hospital, he said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — At least two people were killed and more than a dozen injured here on Monday after part of a plant that manufactures food supplements for animals collapsed, burst into flames and set off a struggle for survival for those trying to escape the crushing debris.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/us/OMAHA/OMAHA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/21/us/OMAHA/OMAHA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/us/OMAHA/OMAHA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/us/OMAHA/OMAHA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/us/OMAHA/OMAHA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'