rs, ending a dispute over whether they were spending too much time seated at tables drinking coffee.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elderly Patrons End Dispute With a McDonald’s in Queens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elderly Patrons End McDonald’s Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzsimmons, Emma G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ham, Jiha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Loitering', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T03:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons and Jiha Ham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jiha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abdc12d7-fccd-54fd-b272-e13c4a6b72d5', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abdc12d7-fccd-54fd-b272-e13c4a6b72d5'}, {'abstract': 'On campuses filled with foreign-born students, Janet Napolitano, who was named president of the University of California last summer, faces anger over her role in the Obama administration’s deportation of 1.9 million unauthorized immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.n