': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mansi Choksi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mansi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Choksi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6caeac3e-c501-5552-a1c9-cf503397d5b8', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6caeac3e-c501-5552-a1c9-cf503397d5b8'}, {'abstract': 'Irving and his grandson Micah share a special bond that Irving’s age and dementia cannot break.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/booming/for-micahs-birthday-his-grandfathers-blessing.html', 'snippet': 'Irving and his grandson Micah share a special bond that Irving’s age and dementia cannot break.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 91, my father, Irving Effron, can barely remember his children’s names, though he has acute recollections of long-forgotten battles that he fought as a Marine in the Philippines during World War II. My mother, Ruth, grieves for the loss of the guy who swept her off her feet on a Rockaway beach the summer after he came home from the war. That guy was here up until a few years ago, when dementia set in and Irving’s rare good days became something to cherish, even as his bad days became more numerous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/booming/21mystory-booming-irving2/21mystory-booming-irving2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/21/booming/21mystory-booming-irving2/21mystory-booming-irving2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/booming/21mystory-booming-irving2/21mystory-booming-irving2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumb