 him if he told anyone. Another, the Rev. Robert C. Becker, would take boys to a trailer where, they said, he slept beside them and molested them. And the Rev. Joseph R. Bennett was accused of raping a girl with the handle of a paten, a plate used to hold eucharistic bread.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/us/CHICAGO/CHICAGO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/22/us/CHICAGO/CHICAGO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/us/CHICAGO/CHICAGO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/us/CHICAGO/CHICAGO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1313, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/us/CHICAGO/CHICAGO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/22/us/CHICAGO/CHICAGO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/us/CHICAGO/CHICAGO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Files, a History of Sexual Abuse by Priests in Chicago Archdiocese', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Files, a History of Sexual Abuse by Priests in Chicago Archdiocese', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yaccino, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George, Francis E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T11:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino and Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e3939ed-cc71-5117-a5af-b39c3afb65fb', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e3939ed-cc71-5117-a5af-b39c3afb65fb'}, {'abstract': 'Civil war is hard to end. Before Dayton, there were four failed peace plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/opinion/bosnias-lessons-for-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Civil war is hard to end. Before Dayton, there were four failed peace plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — DESPITE the last-minute diplomatic row over the cancellation of the United Nations’ invitation to Iran, the “Geneva II” peace talks between the government of Bashar al-Assad and the Syrian opposition are scheduled to start today, with support from NATO members and Russia. But the process faces daunting challenges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bosnia’s Lessons for Syria', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bosnia’s Lessons for Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leroux-Martin, Philippe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T11:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philippe Leroux-Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philippe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leroux-Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c7f0386-c8be-5cdd-a837-7e61426cdfcb', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c7f0386-c8be-5cdd-a837-7e61426cdfcb'}, {'abstract': 'Weixin, a fast-growing app from the Chinese Internet company Tencent, is no mere copy of any existing service, and its success may thwart Facebook’s ambitions in China.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/daily-report-homegrown-social-app-dominates-chinese-market/', 'snippet': 'Weixin, a fast-growing app from the Chinese Internet company Tencent, is no mere copy of any existing service, and its success may thwart Facebook’s ambitions in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Weixin (pronounced way-shin) is this country’s killer app, a highly addictive social networking tool that allows smartphone users to send messages and share news, photos, videos and web links, much like America’s WhatsApp, or Line, a Japanese communications and messaging app. In the United States, a similar version is known as WeChat, Da