 buys back s South Korean brewer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/morning-agenda-whos-in-and-whos-out-at-davos/', 'snippet': 'The World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, is as notable for its absentees as for its attendees. | Deutsche Bank’s $1 billion fourth-quarter loss has European markets on edge. | IBM is renewing efforts to sell its server business. | Anheuser-...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Economic Forum in Davos, which begins this Wednesday, is as notable for its attendees as for its absentees, Andrew Ross Sorkin writes in the DealBook column. While this year’s guest list includes prime ministers, chief executives of some of the largest financial institutions and at least one movie star, others in the financial world’s inner circle are, perhaps surprisingly, electing not to go to Switzerland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who’s In and Who’s Out at Davos', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T13:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00546575-b8c7-5e64-83e4-b17ad76a7979', 'word_count': 2040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00546575-b8c7-5e64-83e4-b17ad76a7979'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A teenage friend explained why after-school soccer teams in Bensonhurst were divided by ethnicity (it’s not about hatred).', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/arab-vs-russian-soccer-teams/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A teenage friend explained why after-school soccer teams in Bensonhurst were divided by ethnicity (it’s not about hatred).', 'le