 Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mead, Rebecca', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T15:53:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0acc18f1-ce28-5cb0-bce5-889228c14d4d', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0acc18f1-ce28-5cb0-bce5-889228c14d4d'}, {'abstract': 'Made with luxurious cashmere on the inside and out, these coats with soft silhouettes are the ultimate in luxury.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/threes-a-trend-two-faced-coats/', 'snippet': 'Made with luxurious cashmere on the inside and out, these coats with soft silhouettes are the ultimate in luxury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Double-faced cashmere is one of the softest, most luxurious fabrics around — specially woven with two “right” sides, or faces, so that the wearer feels the ultrasoft fiber both on the inside and out. It’s a hallmark of many high-end fashion collections, as there’s no difference in quality between the front and the back of the fabric. And the drape of a coat made with this material, unencumbered by the usual structure, is loose and fluid, like a bathrobe. At Valentino, a new capsule, haute couture collection for men included a classic, double-faced cashmere coat in camel that looks as luxurious as it feels. Varied versions of the high-class standby included Tomas Maier’s olive offering at Bottega Veneta, which he layered over equally cozy, athletic-style pants and zip top. And at Louis Vuitton, the designer Kim Jones draped a gray, peaked lapel coat over the shoulders of a suit and tank top, for the height of elegance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/t-magazine/21trend-coats-pask/21trend-coats-pask-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/21/t-magazine/21trend-coats-pask/21trend-coats-pask-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/t-magazine/21trend-coats-pask/21trend-coats-pask-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/t-magazine/21trend-coats-pask/21trend-coats-pask-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/t-magazine/21trend-coats-pask/21trend-coats-pask-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/21/t-magazine/21trend-coats-pask/21trend-coats-pask-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/t-magazine/21trend-coats-pask/21trend-coats-pask-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three’s a Trend | Two-Faced Coats', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T15:59:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': Non