ents and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Small Business: ‘Letmein’', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T17:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62f33283-f786-5825-8e4e-d3a4119ae01d', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62f33283-f786-5825-8e4e-d3a4119ae01d'}, {'abstract': 'The co-star of “American Hustle” explains what effect his hair choices had on his performance.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/video-bradley-cooper-and-that-perm/', 'snippet': 'The co-star of “American Hustle” explains what effect his hair choices had on his performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Quick, viewers of “American Hustle”: can you separate Christian Bale’s swindler Irving Rosenfeld from his elaborate comb-over or Bradley Cooper’s tightly wound F.B.I. agent from his coiled perm? (To say nothing of high-maintenance wife Jennifer Lawrence’s towering updo.) The David O. Russell film was nominated for an Academy Award for its costume design but, in a highly noted snub, not for its hair or makeup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Bradley Cooper and That Perm', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {