d try to find the owners of others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — France’s culture minister, Aurélie Filippetti, on Tuesday pledged to return three artworks looted in World War II “without delay,” including a 17th-century landscape by the Flemish painter Joos de Momper. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France to Return 3 Artworks Looted in World War II', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filippetti, Aurelie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T18:54:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d964c84-2fcd-5fe3-a2f9-95919e88e822', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d964c84-2fcd-5fe3-a2f9-95919e88e822'}, {'abstract': 'UniCredit, the large Italian bank, is the first to take advantage of the funds from the Mariner Investment Group, which will help European banks and other financial institutions free up capital.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/funds-created-to-offload-credit-risk-from-big-projects/', 'snippet': 'UniCredit, the large Italian bank, is the first to take advantage of the funds from the Mariner Investment Group, which will help European banks and other financial institutions free up capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mariner Investment Group, a $10 billion global alternative investment firm, has created two funds that will buy up credit risk from deals used to finance large projects in areas like infrastructure, transportation and energy, allowing financial institutions, including European banks, to free up capital they would otherwise need to hold under regulatory requirements.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/business/dbpix-unicredit2/dbpix-unicredit2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/22/business/dbpix-unicredit2/dbpix-unicredit2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/business/dbpix-unicredit2/dbpix-unicredit2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/business/dbpix-unicredit2/dbpix-unicredit2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/business/dbpix-unicredit2/dbpix-unicredit2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/22/business/dbpix-unicredit2/dbpix-unicredit2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/business/dbpix-unicredit2/dbpix-unicredit2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Funds Created to Offload Credit Risk From Big Projects', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buying Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mariner Investment Group LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unicredito Italiano SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T18:56:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ca3291-25f6-525e-a2d7-0a369c488ff8', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ca3291-25f6-525e-a2d7-0a369c488ff8'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for Mathew Martoma, a former portfolio manager at SAC Capital Advisors who is accused of with insider trading, want to portray the trades in question as routine. But they do not want the jury to hear about the firm’s own guilty plea to insider trading, Peter Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/martoma-defense-walks-a-tightrope/', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for Mathew Martoma, a former portfolio manager at SAC Capital Advisors who is accused of with insider trading, want to portray the trades in question as routine. But they do not want the jury to hear about the firm’s own guilty plea to ins...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trial of Mathew Martoma presents a challenge often seen in recent insider trading prosecutions: how to mount a defense denying any wrongdoing when the defendant is unlikely to testify. One way to persuade a jury to return a not-guilty verdict is by focusing on the ordinary nature of the trading to raise questions about whether any confidential information was even used.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-martoma/dbpix-martoma-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-martoma/dbpix-martoma-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-martoma/dbpix-martoma-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-martoma/dbpix-martoma-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-martoma/dbpix-martoma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-martoma/dbpix-martoma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-martoma/dbpix-martoma-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Martoma Defense Walks a Tightrope', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Co