eneration as hapless, with no ambition, talent or self-respect. But these slackers happen to be women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For so long, women tried to succeed as much as men.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/22BROADCITY/22BROADCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/22BROADCITY/22BROADCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/22BROADCITY/22BROADCITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/22BROADCITY/22BROADCITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/22BROADCITY/22BROADCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/22BROADCITY/22BROADCITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/22BROADCITY/22BROADCITY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They’re Young, Female and, Darn It, Need to Work', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They’re Young, Female and, Darn It, Need to Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Alessandra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poehler, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glazer, Ilana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobson, Abbi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Broad City (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T21:57:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4672a11d-67f1-53fb-baf2-5be8b0b11c93', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4672a11d-67f1-53fb-baf2-5be8b0b11c93'}, {'abstract': 'Jacob Riis’s copy of “How the Other Half Lives,” with his signature and annotations, has been donated to the New-York Historical Society by Ted Gup, a journalism professor.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/21/a-new-york-home-for-riiss-other-half/', 'snippet': 'Jacob Riis’s copy of “How the Other Half Lives,” with his signature and annotations, has been donated to the New-York Historical Society by Ted Gup, a journalism professor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ted Gup, a professor of journalism at Emerson College, has donated a first edition copy of Jacob Riis’s “How the Other Half Lives” — a searing exposé of life in New York tenements, published in 1890 — to the New-York Historical Society, the society announced on Tuesday. The copy was owned by Riis, who not only wrote for “How the Other Half Lives,” but also illustrated it with his own photographs. It includes his signature and a date (Nov. 15, 1890), as well as marginal annotations that expand on some of the ideas in the text. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New York Home for Riis’s ‘Other Half’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gup, Ted', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riis, Jacob A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New-York Historical Society', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T21:58:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ae6838b-b29e-54e4-88a9-9a64958067c3', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ae6838b-b29e-54e4-88a9-9a64958067c3'}, {'abstract': 'How long you wait for a table doesn’t always say much about the winningness of the food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/dining/restaurant-review-han-dynasty-in-the-east-village-and-hirohisa-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'How long you wait for a table doesn’t always say much about the winningness of the food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Independent thinkers find this hard to admit, but when you see crowds of New Yorkers standing outside a bakery or putting their names on the list at the door of a restaurant, more often than not the food they’re hanging around for is worth eating. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Factoring in the Mystique of Long Lines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he