organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eb2816f-8072-5f18-82c7-555d408f9a2b', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eb2816f-8072-5f18-82c7-555d408f9a2b'}, {'abstract': 'Musicians from Brazil, Uruguay and Peru were among the players in Guitar Marathon: Las Americas, part of the New York Guitar Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/arts/music/badi-assad-is-a-headliner-at-new-york-guitar-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Musicians from Brazil, Uruguay and Peru were among the players in Guitar Marathon: Las Americas, part of the New York Guitar Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Folk, pop and classical music meet in unlikely places in South America. That was one recurring motif, along with nimble fingers, attention to detail and a sense of humor, in Monday night’s concert at Merkin Concert Hall. It was the evening half of the New York Guitar Festival’s free pair of concerts, “Guitar Marathon: Las Americas,” which was recorded for WNYC’s Soundcheck. The afternoon show had featured North American music, down through Mexico. The evening concert was a quintuple bill largely chosen by its headliner, the Brazilian guitarist Badi Assad, with musicians from Brazil, Uruguay and Peru and a repertoire that also embraced Argentina and Venezuela. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/badi4/badi4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/badi4/badi4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/arts/badi4/badi4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,