ating first — and only then determines how to produce the food to meet those goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The relatively new notion that around a third or more of the world’s population is badly (“mal”) nourished conflates hunger and diet-spawned illnesses like diabetes, both of which are preventable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/contibutors-bittman/contibutors-bittman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/contibutors-bittman/contibutors-bittman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 677}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/contibutors-bittman/contibutors-bittman-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/contibutors-bittman/contibutors-bittman-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/contibutors-bittman/contibutors-bittman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/contibutors-bittman/contibutors-bittman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/contibutors-bittman/contibutors-bittman-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Abundance Doesn’t Mean Health', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oxfam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T23:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5b385a9-1f7f-592b-9ffa-253d114d09d8', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5b385a9-1f7f-592b-9ffa-253d114d09d8'}, {'abstract': 'Forensic experts said a theory that Michelle O’Connell shot herself with her boyfriend’s gun lacked credibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/01/21/us/two-gunshots-standalone.html', 'snippet': 'Forensic experts said a theory that Michelle O’Connell shot herself with her boyfriend’s gun lacked credibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forensic experts said a theory that Michelle O’Connell shot herself with her boyfriend’s gun lacked credibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Holes in a Theory of Suicide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-21T23:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'n