': 'nyt://article/5528f508-092f-5f7d-bfce-aeb69c7958f7'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in North Carolina blocked the state’s ultrasound law from going into effect.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/the-first-amendment-protects-abortion-providers-too/', 'snippet': 'A judge in North Carolina blocked the state’s ultrasound law from going into effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday a district court judge in North Carolina issued a ruling that blocked the state’s ultrasound law from going into effect — a move worth celebrating on the 41st anniversary of Roe v. Wade, and at a time when Republican-led states are rushing to enact aggressive new abortion restrictions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The First Amendment Protects Abortion Providers, Too', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eagles, Catherine C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perdue, Beverly E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T15:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a28870d-2f5e-5c23-87e7-42dac3878e51', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a28870d-2f5e-5c23-87e7-42dac3878e51'}, {'abstract': 'At a panel looking at Africa in 2015, several speakers argued that opening and supporting more foreign investment would naturally trickle down to the populace.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/financial-sector-can-help-african-economy-boom-panelists-say/', 'snippet': 'At a panel looking at Africa in 2015, several speakers argued that opening and supporting more foreign investment would naturally trickle down to the populace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland – One of the stated aims of this year’s World Economic Forum is inclusion. A panel discussion on Africa’s future, one that included two sitting presidents from that continent, did its best to emphasize that theme.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-wef-africa1/dbpix-wef-africa1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-wef-africa1/dbpix-wef-africa1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-wef-africa1/dbpix-wef-africa1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-wef-africa1/dbpix-wef-africa1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1576, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-wef-africa1/dbpix-wef-africa1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-wef-africa1/dbpix-wef-africa1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-wef-africa1/dbpix-wef-africa1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Sector Can Help Bolster Africa’s Economy, Panelists Say', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonathan, Goodluck', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahama, John Dramani', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T15:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/242429af-7a17-534f-917f-95746735fff9', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/242429af-7a17-534f-917f-95746735fff9'}, {'abstract': 'There are programs out there, in the city and around the country, with an encouraging success rate.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/how-to-help-homeless-families/', 'snippet': 'There are programs out there, in the city and around the country, with an encouraging success rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seeing Dasani Coates standing alongside the dignitaries at Mayor Bill de Blasio’s inauguration earlier this month was a heartening sign. In December, the 12-year-old girl’s struggles living with her family in a decrepit city shelter had been vividly captured in this newspaper in Andrea Elliott’s series “Invisible Child.”  Dasani’s story struck a chord. More than 2,200 readers commented online, expressing sentiments that ranged from admiration for her grit to outrage at the Dickensian circumstances in which she lived. De Blasio had laid out an aggressive agenda to help the city’s most vulnerable residents, promising to expand affordable housing and revive rental-assistance programs for homeless families. Here was a gesture to suggest he was serious. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Help Homeless Families', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coates, Dasani', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T16:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bec6a56b-0be0-56b7-a60d-38849052da4e', 'word_count': 2254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bec6a56b-0be0-56b7-a60d-38849052da4e'}, {'abstract': 'Graham Holdings, the education and media company left after The Washington Post Company sold its namesake newspaper, is venturing back into news with a new app, Trove, that makes it easy for users to find and curate articles on their favorite topics.', 'web_url': 'https://bi