: '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/718f1111-794b-58ee-9966-a06b341b2507', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/718f1111-794b-58ee-9966-a06b341b2507'}, {'abstract': 'On a family trip to a remote Colombian territory, the author finds spots for swimming and serenity — just not excitement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/travel/quiet-in-the-caribbean.html', 'snippet': 'On a family trip to a remote Colombian territory, the author finds spots for swimming and serenity — just not excitement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrapped my arms around Leonardo, our “moto” driver, as he pushed our overloaded Yamaha across the hot, potholed concrete.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26EXPLORER1/26EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26EXPLORER1/26EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26EXPLORER1/26EXPLORER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26EXPLORER1/26EXPLORER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26EXPLORER1/26EXPLORER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26EXPLORER1/26EXPLORER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26EXPLORER1/26EXPLORER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quiet in the Caribbean', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Middle of Somewhere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Islands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moon, Freda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Providencia (Colombia)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T17:41:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Freda Moon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Freda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72f1e714-5d89-51cd-b588-ac9f6a0d0fae', 'word_count': 1856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72f1e714-5d89-51cd-b588-ac9f6a0d0fae'}, {'abstract': 'This spot, which opened in April, serves serious seafood with a side of humor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/travel/restaurant-report-fishing-with-dynamite-in-manhattan-beach-calif.html', 'snippet': 'This spot, which opened in April, serves serious seafood with a side of humor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When putting together Fishing With Dynamite, David LeFevre had a specific sort of nostalgia in mind. The floor tiles are stripes of red, orange and blue; the chef and owner said they reminded him of the classic Ocean Pacific T-shirt with a sunset emblazoned across the chest. Beneath the bar, skateboard trucks have been repurposed as hooks for purses, and Japanese lobster buoys hang from the ceiling. “It took probably 50 visits to flea markets over two years,” said Mr. LeFevre about compiling items to decorate his East Coast-meets-West Coast seafood restaurant, which opened in April. “It was tough to describe, but I knew when people saw it, they would be like, ‘Oh, God, the space is so comfortable and right.’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26BITES_SPAN/26BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26BITES_SPAN/26BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26BITES_SPAN/26BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26BITES_SPAN/26BITES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26BITES_SPAN/26BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26BITES_SPAN/26BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/travel/26BITES_SPAN/26BITES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Report: Fishing With Dynamite in Manhattan Beach, Calif.', 'kicker': 'Bites ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Served With a Dash of Humor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moon, Freda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeFevre, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T17:43:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Freda Moon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Freda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/419fb5d3-c788-5226-be0c-d71b9f9369ea', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/419fb5d3-c788-5226-be0c-d71b9f9369ea'}, {'abstract': '“Stop Hitting Yourself” views “late-stage capitalism” through the prism of the Busby Berkeley musicals of the 1930s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/theater/singing-dancing-and-economics.html', 'snippet': '“Stop Hitting Yourself” views “late-stage capitalism” through the prism of the Busby Berkeley musicals of the 1930s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'January is a heady, if exhausting, month in New York for lovers of experimental theater. If you didn’t get your fill at the Under the Radar or the Coil festivals, fear not. Just around the corner is more venturesome theater, this time from the acclaimed collective Rude Mechanicals from Austin, Tex. The company has previously presented its productions “The Method Gun” and “Dionysus in 69” in the city. Those shows illustrated the company’s interest in exploring the history of theater making; the latest production tilts toward Hollywood.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26GUIDE1_SPAN/26GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26GUIDE1_SPAN/26GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26GUIDE1_SPAN/26GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26GUIDE1_SPAN/26GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26GUIDE1_SPAN/26GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26GUIDE1_SPAN/26GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26GUIDE1_SPAN/26GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Singing, Dancing and Economics', 'kicker': 'Theater | The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Singing, Dancing and Economics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rude Mechs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Stop Hitting Yourself (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T17:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9197ab2e-5dc9-5b3f-b6fb-b51cc2220a35', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9197ab2e-5dc9-5b3f-b6fb-b51cc2220a35'}, {'abstract': 'Why focus on inequality?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/a-note-on-the-political-economy-of-populism/', 'snippet': 'Why focus on inequality?', 'lead_paragraph': 'All indications are that President Obama will make inequality the central theme of his State of the Union address. Assuming he does, he will face two different kinds of sniping. One will come from the usual suspects on the right, shrieking “class warfare”. The other will come from a variety of people, some of them well-intentioned, arguing that while sure, inequality is an issue, the crucial thing now is to get the economy growing and create more jobs; these people will argue that populism is a diversion from the main issue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Note on the Political Economy of Populism', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T17:50:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93ddef3f-f71c-536e-8980-94dcc10606b3', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93ddef3f-f71c-536e-8980-94dcc10606b3'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Gelsinger, the chief executive of VMWare, believes some older companies are moving into cloud computing and others are retrenching as customers demand new sorts of technologies.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/vmware-looks-to-improve-its-cloud-with-airwatch/', 'snippet': 'Patrick Gelsinger, the chief executive of VMWare, believes some older companies are moving into cloud computing and others are retrenching as customers demand new sorts of technologies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the technology world, 2014 has become momentous quickly, with billions of dollars moving around and thousands of people losing their jobs. It is all happening as the industry builds for the dominant feature of the next few decades: supercomputing everywhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/technology/22bits-airwatch/22bits-airwatch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/22/technology/22bits-airwatch/22bits-airwatch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/technology/22bits-airwatch/22bits-airwatch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/technology/22bits-airwatch/22bits-airwatch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo'