'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b2d8016-4abd-5ab2-85fd-e92182489054', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b2d8016-4abd-5ab2-85fd-e92182489054'}, {'abstract': 'At the Paris Couture shows, designers featured elegantly simple shapes and ethereal fabrics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/fashion/couture-paris-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'At the Paris Couture shows, designers featured elegantly simple shapes and ethereal fabrics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Magical handwork separates haute couture from the rest of fashion, but it depends on modern ideas to be relevant. Looking at the Paris spring shows online, what stands out are lightness and agility, soothing colors and a reductive view of luxury that feels unusually sensitive to the times.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Airy Enough to Take Flight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airy Enough to Take Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Raf', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiaparelli, Elsa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMANI, GIORGIO', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagerfeld, Karl', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valli, Giambattista', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Versace, Donatella', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T21:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0446d5e4-f3ed-5ce7-9894-5c0e23f945dd', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0446d5e4-f3ed-5ce7-9894-5c0e23f945dd'}, {'abstract': 'In the Russian city of Sochi, the grandiose and economically dubious megaproject has returned — another Soviet legacy pursued by the singular will of President Vladimir V. Putin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/magazine/putins-olympic-fever-dream.html', 'snippet': 'In the Russian city of Sochi, the grandiose and economically dubious megaproject has returned — another Soviet legacy pursued by the singular will of President Vladimir V. Putin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anatoly Pakhomov was elected mayor of Sochi after the type of ersatz campaign that passes for democracy in Russia. It was 2009, and he had been appointed acting mayor — effectively the local manager of the massive construction project already underway — and in Russia incumbency means victory. His many prospective challengers included a K.G.B. veteran accused of poisoning the fugitive secret-service officer Aleksandr Litvinenko with polonium; a prima ballerina who had become even more famous after the Bolshoi dismissed her for being overweight; and a pornographic actress, Yelena Berkova, who ran a campaign ad that showed her gamboling topless along one of the Black Sea beaches that first made Sochi popular in the early 20th century.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url