int. What’s more, they’re in trouble with the law. A federal regulation passed in 2007 calls for the production of energy-wasting incandescents to effectively cease as of Jan. 1 of this year — though existing bulbs will remain on store shelves, and ambience-minded interior designers aware of the regulation have for several years been furtively stockpiling them. Last week, Congressional Republicans — apparently not fans themselves of the ghoulish glow of energy-efficient compact fluorescent (C.F.L.) bulbs — attached a provision to the new spending bill that eliminates funding for the law’s enforcement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/t-magazine/22plumen-hartman/22plumen-hartman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/22/t-magazine/22plumen-hartman/22plumen-hartman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/t-magazine/22plumen-hartman/22plumen-hartman-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 627, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/t-magazine/22plumen-hartman/22plumen-hartman-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1255, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/t-magazine/22plumen-hartman/22plumen-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/22/t-magazine/22plumen-hartman/22plumen-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/22/t-magazine/22plumen-hartman/22plumen-hartman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | An Eco-Lightbulb that Looks Better Naked', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compact Fluorescent Light Bulbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T22:36:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7c67ba8-49db-578c-a804-a5c19929b041', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7c67ba8-49db-578c-a804-a5c19929b041'}, {'abstract': 'Things I didn’t say.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/the-bubble-canard/', 'snippet': 'Things I didn’t say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ah, this one never goes away. I’ll leave the cleanup in the excellent hands of Dean Baker. He’s right to say that anyone trying to make this particular claim is revealing what’s wrong with them, not with me. But I’d quarrel with his “either a fool or a liar” line; why not both?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bubble Canard', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T22:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37de4df5-4b02-5d15-847e-73072289d9dd', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37de4df5-4b02-5d15-847e-73072289d9dd'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet begins its six-week winter season at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/arts/dance/balanchine-evening-ignites-city-ballet-winter-season.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet begins its six-week winter season at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The experience of Balanchine choreography in performance is as intensely multilayered as anything in the arts. A little ballet, less than 20 minutes long, can plunge us into consuming revelations of style, expression, drama, history, morality, entertainment; into a demonstration of dancing to music as the most exciting interconnection of time and space possible; into complex overlaps among classicism, Romanticism and modernism; into the tension between pure form and poetic communication. And into the capacity of human beings to demonstrate the ideal. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Founder’s Footsteps', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Founder’s Footsteps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-22T22:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/19d83577-2791-504a-8ca6-287901cf5bf8', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19d83577-2791-504a-8ca6-287901cf5bf8'}, {'abstract': 'Wells Fargo said on Wednesday that it sold the rights to service 184,000 mortgages to Ocwen Financial Corporation, a rapidly expanding company known for its expertise in dealing with subprime borrowers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/wells-fargo-sells-servicing-rights-on-39-billion-in-mortgages/', 'snippet': 'Wells Fargo said on Wednesday that it sold the rights to service 184,000 mortgages to Ocwen Financial Corporation, a rapidly expanding company known for its expertise in dealing with subprime borrowers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another sign of the banking industry’s retreat from the mortgage market, Wells Fargo is selling servicing rights on $39 billion of home loans to a nonbanking firm.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-ocwen/dbpix-ocwen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-ocwen/dbpix-ocwen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-ocwen/dbpix-ocwen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/business/dbpix-ocwen/dbpix-ocwen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_