a.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PLEASANTON, Calif. — LAST year the private sector spent $67.2 billion on cybersecurity services. Nevertheless, according to a recent investigation by Verizon, 60 percent of successful hacks were not detected until months after the attacks began. In the wake of recent high-profile hacker attacks against Target, Neiman Marcus and other retailers, the obvious question is: Why hasn’t all that money done any good?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding a Needle in a Digital Haystack', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding a Needle in a Digital Haystack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Target Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neiman Marcus Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T01:02:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim White', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'White', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b252b7f9-fcea-5244-9ee2-a99d1db4a98a', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b252b7f9-fcea-5244-9ee2-a99d1db4a98a'}, {'abstract': 'Freedom Industries revealed this week that the chemical spill in West Virginia on Jan. 9 contained an additional chemical, one that had not been disclosed before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/us/a-second-chemical-was-part-of-west-virginia-chemical-spill-company-reveals.html', 'snippet': 'Freedom Industries revealed this week that the chemical spill in West Virginia on Jan. 9 contained an additional chemical, one that had not been disclosed before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chemical spill that left 300,000 West Virginia residents without usable water involved more chemicals than the company responsible had previously reported, officials revealed this week, leading the state’s Department of Environmental Protection to order that company to give a full accounting of the chemicals that had leaked into the Elk River. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Second Chemical Was Part of West Virginia Chemical Spill, Company Reveals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Second Chemical Was Part of West Virginia Chemical Spill, Company Reveals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Elk River (W Va)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freedom Industries Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemicals', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T01:06:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/262fe347-7ca9-5368-9297-adf2549789a5', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/262fe347-7ca9-5368-9297-adf2549789a5'}, {'abstract': 'Abortion opponents, trying out a humbler, more inclusive strategy, toned down the rhetoric as they marched on the 41st anniversary of the Supreme Court’s decision in Roe v. Wade.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/abortion-opponents-march-in-washington-on-anniversary-of-roe-v-wade-decision/', 'snippet': 'Abortion opponents, trying out a humbler, more inclusive strategy, toned down the rhetoric as they marched on the 41st anniversary of the Supreme Court’s decision in Roe v. Wade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thousands of abortion opponents descended on Washington for the annual March for Life rally on Wednesday on the 41st anniversary of the decision in Roe v. Wade, the landmark Supreme Court case that legalized abortion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abortion Opponents March in Washington on Anniversary of Roe v. Wade Decision', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roe v Wade (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T01:09:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17889c2f-64fa-52e2-bff6-10cd6e371b5a', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17889c2f-64fa-52e2-bff6-10cd6e371b5a'}, {'abstract': 'My corporation values diversity, but somehow being a home-schooling parent felt so far outside the norm that I couldn’t talk about it.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/owning-up-to-being-a-home-schooling-parent/', 'snippet': 'My corporation values diversity, but somehow being a home-schooling parent felt so far outside the norm that I couldn’t talk about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sitting across from the principal, I tried to argue — in a logical, lawyerly way — that my third grader’s standardized test scores were compelling evidence that she needed more than “Clifford, the Big Red Dog.” Although my daughter was bored to distraction by the simple books the teacher assigned, maybe I should have thought twice before requesting special treatment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Owning Up to Being a Home-Schooling Parent', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Schooling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T01:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Kulynych', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulynych', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d2fb41-17c7-5738-87c0-1a0431045ea7', 'word_count': 983, 'uri':