{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blackmun, Harry A', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALITO, SAMUEL A JR', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pauley, William H III', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burger, Warren E', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T01:17:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/66cced7f-0112-57f6-aefa-697e32ded930', 'word_count': 1579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66cced7f-0112-57f6-aefa-697e32ded930'}, {'abstract': 'In our latest installment of this exclusive series of interviews by Doug Aitken, the artist interviews the artist and urban planner Theaster Gates.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/22/the-source-theaster-gates-in-conversation-with-doug-aitken/', 'snippet': 'In our latest installment of this exclusive series of interviews by Doug Aitken, the artist interviews the artist and urban planner Theaster Gates.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I have this great problem of space,” Theaster Gates says. “When planners use words like blight and underdeveloped, it’s like actually what you are talking about is available land.” The artist and urban planner talks to Doug Aitken in an abandoned property on Chicago’s South Side that he calls the Archive House. By adding a reading room and a space for records, Gates has reimagined the property as a hub for artists. Gates (who chatted with Perry Chen of Kickstarter in a conversation published by T last year) has made it his mission 