ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/6816f345-85d7-595f-a5f9-787fe7e3c1ca', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6816f345-85d7-595f-a5f9-787fe7e3c1ca'}, {'abstract': 'Coach Mike Woodson has dismissed concerns about his defensive schemes, but the problems were glaring in the loss to Philadelphia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/sports/basketball/knicks-defensive-disarray-in-loss-to-76ers-puts-woodson-on-the-spot.html', 'snippet': 'Coach Mike Woodson has dismissed concerns about his defensive schemes, but the problems were glaring in the loss to Philadelphia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The list of items that have haunted Knicks Coach Mike Woodson started early this season — practically from opening night. There were personality conflicts with Iman Shumpert, then J. R. Smith, then Chris Smith, then Beno Udrih. Critics nitpicked Woodson’s lineup choices before games and then admonished him over his time management at the end of games. Woodson was not being tough enough on players. He was being too tough on players.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image