/these-can-go-anywhere.html', 'snippet': 'Seventy-three dealers will participate in the 60th Winter Antiques Show, including R & Company, which is offering an unusual work by Wendell Castle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the eclectic goods at the 60th Winter Antiques Show, which opens Friday, will be a set of library steps. “It’s an unusual piece of furniture,” said Wendell Castle, 81, who designed the piece in 1977 as a departure from staircases, which were more his usual thing. Speaking from his studio in Scottsville, N.Y., he added: “You don’t have to have a specific site. I always like to make things that can go anywhere.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR5_EVENTS/23CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR5_EVENTS/23CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR5_EVENTS/23CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR5_EVENTS/23CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 1430, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR5_EVENTS/23CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR5_EVENTS/23CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR5_EVENTS/23CURR5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'These Can Go Anywhere', 'kicker': 'Currents | Shows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'These Can Go Anywhere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Wendell', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter Antiques Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T04:06:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b74e4c-5048-552c-bf9b-2d4d09006b45', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b74e4c-5048-552c-bf9b-2d4d09006b45'}, {'abstract': 'PIQ, a gift shop with something for everyone (no, really), opens in Grand Central Terminal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/garden/a-niche-for-oomph.html', 'snippet': 'PIQ, a gift shop with something for everyone (no, really), opens in Grand Central Terminal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PIQ, a gift shop that opened last week at Grand Central Terminal, in a space formerly occupied by Pylones, is, like its predecessor, wildly colorful. But the similarities end there. “The Pylones look was about cuteness, and I was tired of cuteness,” said Frédéric A. Rambaud, a founder of the Sarut Group, which manages Pylones stores in New York (two remain) and an owner of the new PIQ. “There’s a new aspect in retail that’s a mix of day-to-day with designer toys. So the grandmother can come in and find something for the grandchildren, and at the same time find something for herself.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR1_OPEN_SPAN/23CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR1_OPEN_SPAN/23CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR1_OPEN_SPAN/23CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR1_OPEN_SPAN/23CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR1_OPEN_SPAN/23CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR1_OPEN_SPAN/23CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/garden/23CURR1_OPEN_SPAN/23CURR1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Niche for Oomph', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Niche for Oomph', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'su