8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T11:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5a4ed9-af96-5578-99b4-7c15e68e486e', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5a4ed9-af96-5578-99b4-7c15e68e486e'}, {'abstract': 'A poll of purchasing managers showed factory output rising at the fastest rate in nearly three years, but many experts remain wary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/business/international/european-economic-activity-accelerates-survey-finds.html', 'snippet': 'A poll of purchasing managers showed factory output rising at the fastest rate in nearly three years, but many experts remain wary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — An index of industrial activity in the euro zone has reached its highest level since mid-2011, according to a report released on Thursday. But policy makers, business leaders and economists gathered at the World Economic Forum here seem deeply skeptical about whether growth will be strong enough to cut high levels of youth unemployment in the bloc.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caution in Davos Over Report of Growth in Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Growth Report Brings Caution in Davos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolly, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Production', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Markit Group Ltd', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T11:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing and David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b3c1ca2-68e8-5ec3-a54d-b67e9b144087', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b3c1ca2-68e8-5ec3-a54d-b67e9b144087'}, {'abstract': 'While profit-sharing is almost always a popular topic, I don’t remember ever hearing anyone talk about loss-sharing.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/deciding-how-much-employees-and-owners-should-make/', 'snippet': 'While profit-sharing is almost always a popular topic, I don’t remember ever hearing anyone talk about loss-sharing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my last post, I wrote about my decision not to pay year-end bonuses. As usual, I received some insightful comments in response, including several suggesting that I start sharing more information with my employees so that they have a better sense of how the company is doing. This is something I have thought about quite a bit and I intend to do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deciding How Much Employees and Owners Should Make', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Employment Law Project', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T12:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c7ef5aa-c9a9-5d6e-b706-43747c79a4d6', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c7ef5aa-c9a9-5d6e-b706-43747c79a4d6'}, {'abstract': 'The first big stories of the year have come from the International Consortium of Investigative Journalists, which had received a trove of financial documents on activity mostly in the British Virgin Islands.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/investigative-stories-delve-into-the-use-of-offshore-companies-by-chinese/', 'snippet': 'The first big stories of the year have come from the International Consortium of Investigative Journalists, which had received a trove of financial documents on activity mostly in the British Virgin Islands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first big China investigative story of the year has come from the International Consortium of Investigative Journalists, which on Tuesday published, in tandem with several Western news organizations, a detailed look at the widespread use of offshore companies and tax havens by Chinese businesspeople and relatives of Communist Party leaders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investigative Stories Delve Into the Use of Offshore Companies by Chinese', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sun Tiangang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhou Yongkang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Caixin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China National Offshore Oil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China National Petroleum Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Petroleum and Chemical Corporation (Sinopec)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hong Kong Stock Exchange', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Consortium of Investigative Journalists', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PetroChina Company Ltd', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinopec Corp', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T12:15:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cef85d84-770a-59d6-aa56-f0b8d96d6ad6', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cef85d84-770a-59d6-aa56-f0b8d96d6ad6'}, {'abstract': 'Tugan Sokhiev of the Orchestre National du Capitole in Toulouse, France, will take over from Vassily Sinaisky, who resigned abruptly last month.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/bolshoi-theater-names-new-music-director/', 'snippet': 'Tugan Sokhiev of the Orchestre National du Capitole in Toulouse, France, will take over from Vassily Sinaisky, who resigned abruptly last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bolshoi Theater has named Tugan Sokhiev of the Orchestre National du Capitole in Toulouse, France, as its new music director and chief conductor, the theater announced earlier this week. He fills the vacancy left by Vassily Sinaisky, who resigned abruptly last month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bolshoi Theater Names New Music Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gergiev, Valery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T12:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Kishkovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kishkovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b37c7549-2e0c-5eb6-a5bf-53b68c4aafe5', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b37c7549-2e0c-5eb6-a5bf-53b68c4aafe5'}, {'abstract': 'The findings are laid out in a report that represent the first major public statement by the Privacy and Civil Liberties Oversight Board, which Congress made an independent agency in 2007 and which only recently became fully operational.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/daily-report-n-s-a-surveillance-program-is-illegal-watchdog-says/', 'snippet': 'The findings are laid out in a report that represent the first major public statement by the Privacy and Civil Liberties Oversight Board, which Congress made an independent agency in 2007 and which only recently became fully operational.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An independent federal privacy watchdog has concluded that the National Security Agency’s program to collect bulk phone call records has provided only “minimal” benefits in counterterrorism efforts, is illegal and should be shut down, Charlie Savage reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bi