he saw comparisons between Britain and a rising Germany in 1914 and the current tensions between Japan and China.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Historians and columnists have made comparisons between Britain and a rising Germany in 1914 and the current tensions between Japan and China; a hot topic at the start of the centenary year of World War I.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abe’s Version of History Doesn’t Sit Well With Chinese', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cui Tiankai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rachman, Gideon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East China Sea', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T12:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80ad2eac-14ac-5323-9cb3-6284779bf093', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80ad2eac-14ac-5323-9cb3-6284779bf093'}, {'abstract': 'James Guay, a marriage counselor, believes the shift in sexual mores helps break apart relationships couples were once willing to maintain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/booming/when-one-person-lives-a-lie.html', 'snippet': 'James Guay, a marriage counselor, believes the shift in sexual mores helps break apart relationships couples were once willing to maintain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Jan. 16 Unhitched column (“In a Confrontation, a Secret Is Revealed”), Deborah Wells-Clinton and Phil Clinton discussed their 28-year marriage and the enormous secret he had kept from her: Mr. Clinton is gay. Their split, after such a long union, was difficult, but they were able to retain a friendship.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/booming/19unhitched-sfront/19unhitched-sfront-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 301, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/19/booming/19unhitched-sfront/19unhitched-sfront-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 301}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/booming/19unhitched-sfront/19unhitched-sfront-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/booming/19unhitched-sfront/19unhitched-sfront-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1027, 'width': 2046, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/19/booming/19unhitched-sfront/19unhitched-sfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7