o', '_id': 'nyt://video/a5f711d1-0c4c-5bd0-bc54-cadd88203179', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a5f711d1-0c4c-5bd0-bc54-cadd88203179'}, {'abstract': 'Waterfall Press will publish fiction and nonfiction titles to “provide spiritual refreshment and inspiration,” Amazon announced on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/amazon-publishing-starts-a-christian-imprint/', 'snippet': 'Waterfall Press will publish fiction and nonfiction titles to “provide spiritual refreshment and inspiration,” Amazon announced on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amazon Publishing on Thursday announced that its book empire was expanding to include Waterfall Press, a Christian imprint to “provide spiritual refreshment and inspiration,” according to a statement announcing the new imprint. The Waterfall titles, fiction and nonfiction in several genres, will be put out by Brilliance Publishing, part of the Amazon.com group of companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Publishing Starts a Christian Imprint', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waterfalls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hein, Jay F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T19:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felica R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felica', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ac089be-8e94-5edd-8b20-9d6c4aed3f74', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ac089be-8e94-5edd-8b20-9d6c4aed3f74'}, {'abstract': 'Cheap servers were a drag on Big Blue. Now the company plans to focus on computer hardware with better profit margins.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/ibm-happy-to-be-rid-of-low-end-server-business/', 'snippet': 'Cheap servers were a drag on Big Blue. Now the company plans to focus on computer hardware with better profit margins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lenovo of China, already the world’s largest maker of personal computers, has purchased from IBM one of the world’s largest computer server businesses, for what seems like a rock-bottom price. Lenovo gets market share in an area where it is a small player. IBM is shedding a business that was killing its profitability in higher-margin software and services.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/technology/23bits-ibmserver/23bits-ibmserver-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/technology/23bits-ibmserver/23bits-ibmserver-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/technology/23bits-ibmserver/23bits-ibmserver-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/technology/23bits-ibmserver/23bits-ibmserver-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/technology/23bits-ibmserver/23bits-ibmserver-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, '