desire to “stop talking and start doing something” about homelessness: these were the dominant reactions to the series “Invisible Child: Dasani’s Homeless Life” among the 190 students who participated in our most recent installment of The Learning Network’s Reading Club.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/nyregion/10poverty-img-LN/10poverty-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/nyregion/10poverty-img-LN/10poverty-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/nyregion/10poverty-img-LN/10poverty-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/nyregion/10poverty-img-LN/10poverty-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1461, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/nyregion/10poverty-img-LN/10poverty-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/nyregion/10poverty-img-LN/10poverty-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/nyregion/10poverty-img-LN/10poverty-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading Club | Our Favorite Comments on ‘Invisible Child: Dasani’s Homeless Life’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T19:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne and Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb9e736-29bb-5479-9988-954178fdda97', 'word_count': 1401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb9e736-29bb-5479-9988-954178fdda97'}, {'abstract': 'A violin made by the Italian luthier Carlo Ferdinando Landolfi was recovered on Thursday in the Hague.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/stolen-landolfi-violin-is-recovered/', 'snippet': 'A violin made by the Italian luthier Carlo Ferdinando Landolfi was recovered on Thursday in the Hague.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rare violin by the Italian luthier Carlo Ferdinando Landolfi, one of three instruments stolen last week from a house in Abcoude, a small town in the Netherlands, was recovered on Thursday, when two men tried to sell it to a violin maker in The Hague, a Dutch news site reported. The violin dates from 1731, although there are few extant Landolfi instruments from before around 1750. It is said to be worth about $205,000. The owner of the violin shop, who had heard about the burglary, notified the police when he was offered the violin. The police arrested the two men, but the other two stolen violins have not yet been found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stolen Landolfi Violin Is Recovered', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': No