 a mini-survey of this photographer’s challenging Ukraine work made before, during and after the collapse of the Soviet Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/arts/design/a-boris-mikhailov-survey-looks-at-ukraines-soviet-era.html', 'snippet': '“Boris Mikhailov: Four Decades,” at the Dominique Lévy gallery, is a mini-survey of this photographer’s challenging Ukraine work made before, during and after the collapse of the Soviet Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Boris Mikhailov, born in Ukraine in 1938, has become widely known in late career for his wry and wrenching pictures of post-Soviet life. His series “Case History” (seen at MoMA in 2011) unnerved viewers with large-scale color portraits of homeless people in Ukraine, pictures that seemed to violate the codes of serious documentary photography. The subjects flashed naked flesh to the camera and had been paid and fed by the photographer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24BORIS1_SPAN/BORIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 253, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24BORIS1_SPAN/BORIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 253}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24BORIS1_SPAN/BORIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24BORIS1_SPAN/BORIS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24BORIS1_SPAN/BORIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24BORIS1_SPAN/BORIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24BORIS1_SPAN/BORIS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Ukraine, the Chilling Winds of Change', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Ukraine, the Chilling Winds of Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mikhailov, Boris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T22:50:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c30f5ad-ac94-53fe-8c3a-7a86da33716f', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c30f5ad-ac94-53fe-8c3a-7a86da33716f'}, {'abstract': '“Antonio Canova: The Seven Last Works,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, exhibits plaster reliefs that represent scenes from the Old and New Testaments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/arts/design/antonio-canova-the-seven-last-works-debuts-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': '“Antonio Canova: The Seven Last Works,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, exhibits plaster reliefs that represent scenes from the Old and New Testaments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Antonio Canova (1757-1822) produced some of the sexiest sculptures in the history of European art. A good example is in the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s European sculpture court: “Reclining Naiad,” a life-size marble representation of a fit young woman lying naked on a sheet over a bearskin, her most impressive feature being her exquisitely supple backside. But if that’s how you think of this artist, you may be shocked by the museum’s exhibition “Antonio Canova: The Seven Last Works.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24CANOVA1/CANOVA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24CANOVA1/CANOVA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 536}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24CANOVA1/CANOVA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 915, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24CANOVA1/CANOVA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1829, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24CANOVA1/CANOVA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24CANOVA1/CANOVA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24CANOVA1/CANOVA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 