 the World Trade Center will remain free, and families of victims will not be charged admission, the museum foundation said.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/911-museum-to-charge-24-admission/', 'snippet': 'Admission to the memorial at the World Trade Center will remain free, and families of victims will not be charged admission, the museum foundation said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The foundation that oversees the National September 11 Memorial Museum at the World Trade Center voted on Thursday to charge visitors $24 for admission to the underground museum that is scheduled to open this spring. The above-ground memorial that occupies the footprints of the twin towers — and has hosted 11.5 million visitors since it opened two years ago — will continue to be free. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '9/11 Museum to Charge $24 Admission', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T22:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed3e245c-6dec-51b2-afa3-85913afe101a', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed3e245c-6dec-51b2-afa3-85913afe101a'}, {'abstract': '“Art Interrupted,” opening at the Georgia Museum of Art, includes work that was prevented from making a national tour during the Cold War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/arts/design/art-interrupted-exhibition-ends-tour-in-georgia.html', 'snippet': '“Art Interrupted,” opening at the Georgia Museum of Art, includes work that was prevented from making a national tour during the Cold War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A short-lived traveling art show that caused an outcry in 1946 but that now looks tame has been meticulously reinstalled with documentation about how government maneuverings shut it down. “Art Interrupted: Advancing American Art and the Politics of Cultural Diplomacy,” an exhibition of paintings that the United States government briefly owned at the outset of the Cold War, opens on Saturday at the Georgia Museum of Art in Athens in the final stop of a tour.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 821}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 749, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1498, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLa