ticle/74cb53b8-d857-55ec-a130-7261f1726000', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74cb53b8-d857-55ec-a130-7261f1726000'}, {'abstract': 'Many buyers of high-end condos in Manhattan have started shopping for beachfront retreats in the Bahamas, some developed by New Yorkers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/realestate/the-bahamas-on-the-radar.html', 'snippet': 'Many buyers of high-end condos in Manhattan have started shopping for beachfront retreats in the Bahamas, some developed by New Yorkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For several years, wealthy New Yorkers, even those relatively unscathed by the financial crisis, seemed to put their second-home dreams on hold. But as the real estate market in the city has strengthened, many of these high-end buyers have started shopping for beachfront retreats again. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26DEAL1_SPAN/26deal-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26DEAL1_SPAN/26deal-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26DEAL1_SPAN/26deal-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26DEAL1_SPAN/26deal-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26DEAL1_SPAN/26deal-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26DEAL1_SPAN/26deal-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26DEAL1_SPAN/26deal-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bahamas on the Radar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bahamas on the Radar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nassau (Bahamas)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahama Islands', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T23:13:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Satow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Satow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aac6b6d8-dc24-5437-afef-307c56aa803f', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aac6b6d8-dc24-5437-afef-307c56aa803f'}, {'abstract': 'A stretch of beach and its adjoining woods, which serve as a gay cruising spot, become a crime scene in “Stranger by the Lake,” by the French filmmaker Alain Guiraudie.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/movies/death-and-desire-in-stranger-by-the-lake.html', 'snippet': 'A stretch of beach and its adjoining woods, which serve as a gay cruising spot, become a crime scene in “Stranger by the Lake,” by the French filmmaker Alain Guiraudie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not every mystery is a whodunit. In Alain Guiraudie’s “Stranger by the Lake,” a murder takes place early on, in full view of the audience and a crucial witness, a young man named Franck (Pierre Deladonchamps). Franck has spent the afternoon — as he apparently spends many afternoons — on a stretch of beach that serves as a gay cruising spot. Earlier, he had a brief flirtation with a muscular, mustachioed swimmer, only to be shooed away by someone who seemed to be a jealous boyfriend. Now, from behind a scrim of trees, just before darkness falls, Franck sees the two men together in the water and watches as horseplay turns to homicide.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dangerous Undertow in a Cruisers’ Haven', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dangerous Undertow in a Cruisers’ Haven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guiraudie, Alain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T23:17:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f31319cd-8064-51bd-bf0e-c5cb988eb77e', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f31319cd-8064-51bd-bf0e-c5cb988eb77e'}, {'abstract': 'Greg Whiteley’s “Mitt” is a behind-the-scenes look at a likable but failed presidential candidate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/arts/television/mitt-goes-behind-the-scenes-of-romneys-presidential-bids.html', 'snippet': 'Greg Whiteley’s “Mitt” is a behind-the-scenes look at a likable but failed presidential candidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voters will learn a lot about Mitt Romney from “Mitt,” a new documentary having its premiere on Netflix on Friday. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24MITT_SPAN/24MITT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24MITT_SPAN/24MITT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24MITT_SPAN/24MITT_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24MITT_SPAN/24MITT_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1072, 'width': 1608, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24MITT_SPAN/24MITT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24MITT_SPAN/24MITT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24MITT_SPAN/24MITT_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Times, Nice Guys Finish Second', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Times, Nice Guys Finish Second', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Alessandra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mitt (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T23:18:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/224540e0-b662-5183-8929-57da733c489d', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/224540e0-b662-5183-8929-57da733c489d'}, {'abstract': 'Solve Crosswords with a friend', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/crosswords/set.html', 'snippet': 'Solve Crosswords with a friend', 'lead_paragraph': 'Solve Crosswords with a friend', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Play with a Friend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T23:23:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Crosswords & Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/635ba3b8-70d3-529d-b73a-26d24bfc8da9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/635ba3b8-70d3-529d-b73a-26d24bfc8da9'}, {'abstract': '“Jewels,” George Balanchine’s three-part ballet from 1967, returns to the New York City Ballet repertory, with nine company principals among the first leads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/arts/dance/jewels-returns-to-new-york-city-ballets-repertory.html', 'snippet': '“Jewels,” George Balanchine’s three-part ballet from 1967, returns to the New York City Ballet repertory, with nine company principals among the first leads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Balanchine’s full-length “Jewels,” new in 1967, remains a perfect education in the art of ballet — in particular\xa0the diversity of ballet as he refashioned it in the mid-20th century. I go on learning from it myself. Part of its fascination is that its three parts — “Emeralds” (to pieces by Fauré), “Rubies” (to Stravinsky’s Capriccio for Piano and Orchestra) and “Diamonds” (to the last four movements of Tchaikovsky’s Third Symphony) — are so unalike. “Emeralds” is Romantic-medievalist, French, seeming to occur in a large garden, deep glade or forest. “Rubies” is 20th-century American, indeed New York: merry, hard, dense, high-rise. “Diamonds” is imperial Russian, courtly. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24JEWELS3_SPAN/JEWELS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24JEWELS3_SPAN/JEWELS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24JEWELS3_SPAN/JEWELS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24JEWELS3_SPAN/JEWELS3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1265, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24JEWELS3_SPAN/JEWELS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24JEWELS3_SPAN/JEWELS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24JEWELS3_SPAN/JEWELS3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Revealing New Facets, After Sparkling for Half a Century', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Revealing New Facets, After Sparkling for Half a Century', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-23T23:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/004508a2-ec7d-5f3a-ae5f-8f663cbcbf98', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/004508a2-ec7d-5f3a-ae5f-8f663cbcbf98'}, {'abstract': 'The humor site Uproxx offers alternative ideas for “Gravity” and other awards season contenders.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/23/what-would-truly-honest-movie-posters-look-like/', 'snippet': 'The humor site Uproxx offers alternative ideas for “Gravity” and other awards season contenders.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Don’t Torrent It. Don’t Watch It On Your Phone”', 'source': 'The New