p and more in the New York City area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prices may not reflect ticketing service charges. For full reviews of recent concerts: nytimes.com/music. A searchable guide to these and other shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rock & Pop Listings for Jan. 24-30', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Pop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T00:17:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/67233053-5e7a-5215-84a5-d7e614ec7a32', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67233053-5e7a-5215-84a5-d7e614ec7a32'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/arts/music/jazz-listings-for-jan-24-30.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Full reviews of recent jazz performances: nytimes.com/jazz. A searchable guide to these and other shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz Listings for Jan. 24-30', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Jazz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T00:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6f5473-0b72-5214-a04d-cd0bdb41b191', 'word_count': 2117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6f5473-0b72-5214-a04d-cd0bdb41b191'}, {'abstract': 'New books by Doug Most, Ellen NicKenzie Lawson and Steven Hart examine the New York subway’s birth, Prohibition in the city and the mayors of two New Jersey cities 80 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/nyregion/books-about-builders-bootleggers-and-bosses.html', 'snippet': 'New books by Doug Most, Ellen NicKenzie Lawson and Steven Hart examine the New York subway’s birth, Prohibition in the city and the mayors of two New Jersey cities 80 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aside from some overlooked plaques in the City Hall subway station and elsewhere, names like Barclay, Hewitt, McDonald, Parsons, Pearson, Sprague, Steinway, even Belmont — much less the Whitney brothers — have been all but forgotten. Doug Most, an editor at The Boston Globe, remedies that oversight in “The Race Underground: Boston, New York and the Incredible Rivalry That Built America’s First Subway” (St. Martin’s Press).', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26BOOK/26BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26BOOK/26BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26BOOK/26BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26BOOK/26BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}},