 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85b11674-a90e-5243-9f32-1bfd980822c2', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85b11674-a90e-5243-9f32-1bfd980822c2'}, {'abstract': 'When an Irish husband, father and craftsman suffers a stroke, his family, and an outsider, reflect the changed balance of the household.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/movies/run-jump-brings-home-the-joy-and-pain-of-family-life.html', 'snippet': 'When an Irish husband, father and craftsman suffers a stroke, his family, and an outsider, reflect the changed balance of the household.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vanetia Casey (Maxine Peake), the plucky, flame-haired central character of “Run & Jump,” infuses this Irish family drama with a snapping, whooshing electricity. The wife of Conor (Edward MacLiam), a 38-year-old carpenter who was seriously disabled by a stroke, she is a sexy, spirited dynamo who has all she can handle raising their two children while Conor lumbers around the house in a partial fog. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24RUN_SPAN/RUN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24RUN_SPAN/RUN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24RUN_SPAN/RUN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/arts/24RUN_SPAN/RUN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption':