s not to engage in any deals still pending after the accord’s July 20 expiration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Warns Against Business With Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Warns Against Business With Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T02:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/785c8fd1-dd7c-5962-b94d-71fd3888c2e8', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/785c8fd1-dd7c-5962-b94d-71fd3888c2e8'}, {'abstract': 'Filings in a Brooklyn bankruptcy case show that the money had “recently been improperly taken” from accounts of the victim, Menachem Stark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/nyregion/dead-developers-accounts-missing-2-million.html', 'snippet': 'Filings in a Brooklyn bankruptcy case show that the money had “recently been improperly taken” from accounts of the victim, Menachem Stark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As detectives pressed their search for culprits in the kidnapping and killing of a Brooklyn real estate developer this month, filings this week in a bankruptcy case in Brooklyn revealed that nearly $2 million had been improperly removed from accounts in the developer’s name.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dead Developer’s Accounts Missing $2 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dead Developer’s Accounts Missing $2 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stark, Menachem', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlmutter, Israel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T02:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42b2924a-3cd0-5227-90ad-357efbbfc7f7', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42b2924a-3cd0-5227-90ad-357efbbfc7f7'}, {'abstract': 'The trains were stopped around 7:45 p.m. on the Hudson, Harlem and New Haven lines, stranding thousands of commuters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/nyregion/metro-north-grinds-to-a-halt-with-computer-trouble.html', 'snippet': 'The trains were stopped around 7:45 p.m. on the Hudson, Harlem and New Haven lines, stranding thousands of commuters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A power failure at Metro-North Railroad’s control center at Grand Central Terminal cut service to its three main lines on Thursday night, stranding thousands of passengers across the metropolitan region for nearly two hours and setting off a chaotic scene as the hub swelled with bemused commuters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/METRONORTHweb/METRONORTHweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/METRONORTHweb/METRONORTHweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/METRONORTHweb/METRONORTHweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/METRONORTHweb/METRONORTHweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/METRONORTHweb/METRONORTHweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/METRONORTHweb/METRONORTHweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/METRONORTHweb/METRONORTHweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Metro-North Grinds to Halt for 2 Hours', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea