ternational aid and development group Oxfam has distanced itself from one of its own global ambassadors, the actress Scarlett Johansson, since she agreed to become the face of SodaStream, an Israeli company that makes products in a settlement built on West Bank territory Israel has occupied since 1967.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scarlett Johansson’s SodaStream Endorsement Deal Conflicts With Charity Work, Aid Group Says', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johansson, Scarlett', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boycott, Divestment and Sanctions (BDS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oxfam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SodaStream International Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T02:47:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a6e203c-1519-5aee-87d2-a088dc69aeaa', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a6e203c-1519-5aee-87d2-a088dc69aeaa'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-jan-23-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 23, 2014', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Lottery Numbers for Jan. 23, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T02:50:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/7748b7e8-5612-5d7d-a59d-da99c0a61595', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7748b7e8-5612-5d7d-a59d-da99c0a61595'}, {'abstract': 'Professional critics weigh in on the United States team’s outfits for the Olympic opening and closing ceremonies, with some seeing a bold, patriotic statement and others seeing garish Christmas sweaters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/sports/olympics/us-olympic-outfits-worthy-of-stares-if-not-medals.html', 'snippet': 'Professional critics weigh in on the United States team’s outfits for the Olympic opening and closing ceremonies, with some seeing a bold, patriotic statement and others seeing garish Christmas sweaters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most passive-aggressive reviews of the United States Olympic team’s new gear from Ralph Lauren were probably those directed at Zach Parise by his Minnesota Wild teammates. They stashed dozens of 8-by-10-inch photos of Parise wearing the Olympic team’s garish new sweater around the Wild’s locker room before he arrived for work Thursday. “I got a lot of requests,” Parise said with a sheepish smile, “from guys who want to get that sweater.” The best part of his public — at least on Twitter — humiliation? He may never get another chance to wear the outfit. The United States hockey team will arrive at the Sochi Olympics after the opening ceremony, at which the sweater will make its runway debut, and will depart before the Games end. But since Parise’s teammates are only amateur critics, The New York Times asked some professionals to weigh in.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/sports/OLYFASHIONsilo1/OLYFASHIONsilo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/sports/OLYFASHIONsilo1/OLYFASHIONsilo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/sports/OLYFASHIONsilo1/OLYFASHIONsilo1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 447, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/sports/OLYFASHIONsilo1/OLYFASHIONsilo1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 893, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/sports/OLYFASHIONsilo1/OLYFASHIONsilo1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/sports/OLYFASHIONsilo1/OLYFASHIONsilo1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/sports/OLYFASHIONsilo1/OLYFASHIONsilo1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S.