ial': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8e61cb9-19d6-50d6-b007-36dc6b3a2b43', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8e61cb9-19d6-50d6-b007-36dc6b3a2b43'}, {'abstract': 'The United States did not specify the guilty pleas it would expect from Edward J. Snowden before opening talks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/us/politics/us-willing-to-hold-talks-if-snowden-pleads-guilty.html', 'snippet': 'The United States did not specify the guilty pleas it would expect from Edward J. Snowden before opening talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. said Thursday that the United States was willing to discuss how the criminal case against Edward J. Snowden would be handled, but only if Mr. Snowden pleaded guilty first.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Willing to Hold Talks if Snowden Pleads Guilty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Willing to Hold Talks if Snowden Pleads Guilty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenny, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T04:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/822b08c3-ad15-537d-9cc4-99b8c0d60ca1', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/822b08c3-ad15-537d-9cc4-99b8c0d60ca1'}, {'abstract': 'The blunt remarks, which concurred with others made recently by prominent historians, provoked an angry response from Beijing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/world/asia/japans-leader-compares-strain-with-china-to-germany-and-britain-in-1914.html', 'snippet': 'The blunt remarks, which concurred with others made recently by prominent historians, provoked an angry response from Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Relations between Asia’s two biggest powers, Japan and China, have been strained for months, with near-constant sniping over a territorial dispute and the two countries’ fraught history.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Leader Compares Strain With China to Germany and Britain in 1914', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan’s Leader Compares Strain With China to Germany and Britain in 1914', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlez, Jane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T04:17:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f1e3970-eeb8-58a2-a621-a895f0104ea3', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f1e3970-eeb8-58a2-a621-a895f0104ea3'}, {'abstract': 'In an audio recording released Thursday, the leader of Al Qaeda called on Islamist brigades in northern Syria to stop fighting one another.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/world/middleeast/al-qaeda-calls-for-rebel-unity-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'In an audio recording released Thursday, the leader of Al Qaeda called on Islamist brigades in northern Syria to stop fighting one another.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In an audio recording released Thursday, the leader of Al Qaeda, Ayman al-Zawahri, called on Islamist brigades in northern Syria to stop fighting one another, to focus on toppling President Bashar al-Assad and to form an Islamic court to arbitrate disputes. Fifteen days of infighting between rebel brigades and fighters from the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria, which is inspired by Al Qaeda, had killed nearly 1,400 people as of Wednesday, according to a count kept by the opposition Syrian Observatory for Human Rights. Mr. Zawahri has little sway over most of the groups fighting in Syria. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Qaeda Calls for Rebel Unity in Syria', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Al Qaeda Calls for Rebel Unity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zawahri, Ayman Al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T04:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b922e67b-b0a6-543e-b6db-b683aaf64ca9', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b922e67b-b0a6-543e-b6db-b683aaf64ca9'}, {'abstract': 'The fire in Quebec killed at least five people and left 30 missing, all of them believed to be 80 or older and many with limited mobility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/world/americas/deadly-fire-at-a-nursing-home-in-canada.html', 'snippet': 'The fire in Quebec killed at least five people and left 30 missing, all of them believed to be 80 or older and many with limited mobility.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Five people were confirmed dead and 30 were missing after a fire destroyed much of a nursing home in L’Isle-Verte, Quebec, early Thursday morning. The missing and dead are all believed to be 80 or older, many with limited mobility, and were residents of the home, which is in a village of about 1,400 northeast of the city of Quebec. “We can keep a bit of hope, but in reality there seems to have been a considerable loss of life,” Prime Minister Stephen Harper said. The fire destroyed the three-story, wooden portion of the home, La Résidence du Havre, which opened in 1997. A newer wing of the building that was equipped with sprinklers remained standing. Unusually cold weather hampered firefighters and restricted fire investigators. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deadly Fire at a Nursing Home in Canada', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Deadly Fire at a Nursing Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T04:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f019fda7-5ecb-5ea0-9a0e-d52d94d81a13', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f019fda7-5ecb-5ea0-9a0e-d52d94d81a13'}, {'abstract': 'Jasper Johns took the stand in the case of Brian Ramnarine, a former owner of a Queens foundry who is accused of creating at least 13 fake sculptures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/nyregion/an-artist-testifies-that-a-reproduction-of-a-famous-work-wasnt-authorized.html', 'snippet': 'Jasper Johns took the stand in the case of Brian Ramnarine, a former owner of a Queens foundry who is accused of creating at least 13 fake sculptures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was not quite a lecture on contemporary art or postmodern sensibility, but in Federal District Court in Manhattan on Thursday, the painter and sculptor Jasper Johns discussed his methodology, corrected a lawyer on the pronunciation of the artist Robert Rauschenberg’s name and said, quite firmly, that he had never authorized a foundry owner to reproduce one of his famous works depicting the American flag.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/