ly once does ‘Finding Neverland’ grasp both the writer and his play’s dark undertow, when the wonderful Scottish actress Kelly Macdonald, in the role of Peter, realizes that Tinker Bell may die. Rousing all the heartbreak and deep feeling in Barrie’s world, she entreats us to believe and, for one glorious moment, you do.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T06:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aee5cb0-c8dd-541d-9400-82fddbb5b740', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aee5cb0-c8dd-541d-9400-82fddbb5b740'}, {'abstract': 'Osmo Vanska, who resigned as music director during the Minnesota Orchestra’s 15-month lockout, will conduct several concerts this spring.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/vanska-to-conduct-minnesota-orchestra-concerts/', 'snippet': 'Osmo Vanska, who resigned as music director during the Minnesota Orchestra’s 15-month lockout, will conduct several concerts this spring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no word as to whether Osmo Vanska will be returning as music director to help nurse the Minnesota Orchestra back to artistic health now that its 15-month lockout is over, but the orchestra announced on Friday that Mr. Vanska would conduct several concerts this spring.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vanska to Conduct Minnesota Orchestra Concerts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vanska to Lead Some Minnesota Concerts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vanska, Osmo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Orchestra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T06:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/922a8a56-fb49-5cca-9d48-44ce6efe4f06', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/922a8a56-fb49-5cca-9d48-44ce6efe4f06'}, {'abstract': 'The director Ashim Ahluwalia said he never thought his movie about the sex-horror film industry of 1980s Mumbai would get past the Indian review board, much less draw an enthusiastic response from local audiences.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/the-journey-of-miss-lovely-from-cannes-to-the-censors/', 'snippet': 'The director Ashim Ahluwalia said he never thought his movie about the sex-horror film industry of 1980s Mumbai would get past the Indian review board, much less draw an enthusiastic response from local audiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGALORE — For the director Ashim Ahluwalia, “Miss Lovely,” his movie about the soft-core pornography business in Mumbai, has led to a series of delightful surprises: Last year, it won the award for the best film at the 14th Mumbai International Film Festival, the award for best feature film at the 11th Indian Film Festival of Los Angeles and was included in the Un Certain Regard section at the Cannes Film Festival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 