a-new-comedy-team/', 'snippet': '“Land Ho!” stars an An ocular plastic surgeon from Kentucky and a veteran actor from Australia, and the two had a lot to say about their casting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — “Did you like our movie?” Earl Lynn Nelson boomed point-blank from the stage, after a screening of the comedy “Land Ho!” in which he stars. The audience in the Egyptian Theater here on Wednesday evening cheered and applauded, then lined up to pose for photos with him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance: The Plastic Surgeon and the Actor, a new Comedy Team', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, David Gordon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Aaron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Earl Lynn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephens, Martha', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T14:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6717cb43-cbab-5ea5-b63d-a5787f44fb55', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6717cb43-cbab-5ea5-b63d-a5787f44fb55'}, {'abstract': 'The beloved Dior fine jewelry designer exhibits a new series of small-scale works.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/on-view-victoire-de-castellanes-blinged-out-sculptures-at-gagosian/', 'snippet': 'The beloved Dior fine jewelry designer exhibits a new series of small-scale works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the head of Dior’s haute joaillerie division since 1998, Victoire de Castellane has infused the luxury brand’s precious offerings with a signature pop whimsy. In 2007, she began toying with sculpture in the form of small-scale works festooned with jewels and anchored by sand-cast silver bases. Beginning January 28, they will be on display at Gagosian’s London gallery in her latest fine-art exhibition, “animalvegetablemineral,” which takes its name from a parlor game. The works incorporate flora and fauna motifs, as well as rough, unpolished geodes — the raw material for the precious stones de Castellane knows and loves. Each is presented beneath a glass globe (“as they would in a natural history museum,” she explains) and christened with a girlish name (Cana Glitter Night Baby, Lunae Lumen Holly Clorum). And although the pieces are art, de Castellane couldn’t help but incorporate a sparkling bauble, to be detached and worn, into each one. “Creating jewelry is my way of expressing myself,” she says. “It’s like a language.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/t-magazine/23castellane-hartman/23castellane-hartman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/t-magazine/23castellane-hartman/23castellane-hartman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 633}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/t-magazine/23castellane-hartman/23castellane-hartman-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/t-magazine/23castellane-hartman/23castellane-hartman-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/t-magazine/23castellane-hartman/23castellane-hartman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/23/t-magazine/23castellane-hartman/23castellane-hartman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/t-magazine/23castellane-hartman/23castellane-hartman-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Victoire de Castellane’s Blinged-Out Sculptures at Gagosian', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Objects: All That Sparkles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T14:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1d3f6e0-6c99-5810-9081-560d49368458', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1d3f6e0-6c99-5810-9081-560d49368458'}, {'abstract': 'The first question everyone asked after my nephew was killed after being struck by a car was whether the driver was drunk. Yet merely looking for alcohol or drug involvement by the driver misses the point.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/treat-reckless-driving-like-drunk-driving/', 'snippet': 'The first question everyone asked after my nephew was killed after being struck by a car was whether the driver was drunk. Yet merely looking for alcohol or drug involvement by the driver misses the point.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a rainy, foggy night earlier this month, a New York City taxi driver making a left turn at a light apparently did not see my 9-year-old nephew and his 6-foot-3 father crossing the street at a crosswalk, beckoned by a lighted “walk” sign. Whether because of haste, inattention, cellphone use or perhaps the poor weather conditions, the cab driver drove directly into them.\xa0My beloved nephew, Cooper Stock, died instantly.\xa0His father suffered minor injuries. The Manhattan District Attorney’s office is investigating the circumstances of Cooper’s death.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/health/23well-reckless/23well-reckless-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/health/23well-reckless/23well-reckless-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/health/23well-reckless/23well-reckless-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/health/23well-reckless/23well-reckless-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1362, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/health/23well-reckless/23well-reckless-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/23/health/23well-reckless/23well-reckless-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/health/23well-reckless/23well-reckless-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Treat Reckless Driving Like Drunk Driving', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T14:05:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barron H. Lerner, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barron', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Lerner', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2620349e-49c4-59bd-aac5-3c1f4ccf3302', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2620349e-49c4-59bd-aac5-3c1f4ccf3302'}, {'abstract': 'The number of people fleeing their homes in Anbar Province is bigger than at the height of sectarian violence years ago, the United Nations said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/world/middleeast/iraq.html', 'snippet': 'The number of people fleeing their homes in Anbar Province is bigger than at the height of sectarian violence years ago, the United Nations said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The United Nations sounde