tion': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/nyregion/de-blasio/de-blasio-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1286, 'width': 1961, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/nyregion/de-blasio/de-blasio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/25/nyregion/de-blasio/de-blasio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/nyregion/de-blasio/de-blasio-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Private Speech on Israel, de Blasio Is Pressed on Openness Pledge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Private Speech on Israel, de Blasio Is Pressed on Openness Pledge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ISRAEL PUBLIC AFFAIRS COMMITTEE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T15:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b1bd247-76e4-55c9-bdb1-e24e082064e3', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b1bd247-76e4-55c9-bdb1-e24e082064e3'}, {'abstract': 'What New York’s Penn Station looked like before it was torn down in 1963.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/magazine/photographs-of-the-old-penn-station.html', 'snippet': 'What New York’s Penn Station looked like before it was torn down in 1963.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The razing of New York’s Penn Station in 1963 still ranks as one of the city’s great architectural disasters. At the time, The New York Times wrote, “We will probably be judged not by the monuments we build but by those we have destroyed.” Walter Chandoha, a photographer who is now 93, remembers the old train station fondly. He was living in New York in the late 1940s and studying at N.Y.U. on the G.I. Bill when he would duck out between classes, Rolleiflex in hand, and wander around the city. Penn Station was a cherished spot, even before it was slated for demolition. “When I look at the pictures now and I see the magnificence of it, I think, How could anybody knock this thing down?” Chandoha says. “It’s like knocking down the Colosseum or the Brandenburg Gate. It’s impossible to imagine.” Julie Bosman', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '39', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographs of the Old Penn Station', 'kicker': 'Look', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Last Station', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pennsylvania Station (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stations and Terminals (Passenger)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T16:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Photographs by Walter Chandoha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Photographs', 'middlename': 'Walter', 'lastname': 'Chandoha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09f117a6-8a83-573f-913a-1c5567936d48', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09f117a6-8a83-573f-913a-1c5567936d48'}, {'abstract': 'We gave up our guns — and a bit of our past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/magazine/the-buyback.html', 'snippet': 'We gave up our guns — and a bit of our past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a rainy Saturday afternoon, my husband and I finally gave up our guns. How we came to possess a small arsenal speaks to a past, though, not a predilection. We’re neither hunters nor collectors; we sign petitions demanding stricter controls and call our congressmen to do likewise. But throughout the years of my husband’s career as a diplomat, spent mostly in chaotic corners of Africa and Latin America, we acquired guns: mementos of the often-turbulent history that we witnessed. Strange as it was to have the weapons among our possessions, we could no more part with them than, say, burn an old photo album.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/magazine/26lives/mag-26Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/magazine/26lives/mag-26Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/magazine/26lives/mag-26Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/magazine/26lives/mag-26Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'c