-glove Manhattan co-op” has invariably conjured the image of a fortresslike residence whose precincts could be stormed only via a gantlet distinguished by mountains of paperwork and a daunting personal interview. The New York condominium, the relatively new kid on the block, has seemed the opposite: laissez-faire in everything, from rules governing pets and smoking to regulations determining who could rent an apartment.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26COVER/26COVER-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26COVER/26COVER-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 755}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26COVER/26COVER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 814, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26COVER/26COVER-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2004, 'width': 1593, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26COVER/26COVER-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26COVER/26COVER-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/realestate/26COVER/26COVER-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Co-ops Chill, Condos Don’t', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Co-ops Chill, Condos Don’t', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenblum, Constance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooperatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T17:36:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Constance Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Constance', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82a4ed8b-0dcc-5a6f-b2ce-e2c1c9eb2a50', 'word_count': 2359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82a4ed8b-0dcc-5a6f-b2ce-e2c1c9eb2a50'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Denis Matsuev has postponed a Carnegie Hall concert scheduled for next Thursday because he is being treated for pneumonia.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/matsuev-postpones-carnegie-hall-concert/', 'snippet': 'The pianist Denis Matsuev has postponed a Carnegie Hall concert scheduled for next Thursday because he is being treated for pneumonia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 1:17 p.m. | The pianist Denis Matsuev has postponed a Carnegie Hall concert scheduled for Thursday, Jan. 30, because he is being treated for pneumonia, the hall announced. It said in a statement that Mr. Matsuev is “currently in Moscow under doctor’s care and not permitted to travel,’’ and that he had been forced to cancel or reschedule a number of concerts in the United States, Israel and Russia. Mr. Matsuev, who has been active in cultural preparations for the Winter Olympics in Sochi, is scheduled to play a concert there on Feb. 6 at the\xa0 Zimniy Theater. One of his representatives, Silke Zimmermann, said that “we firmly count on his participation” at the Sochi games. Mr. Matsuev’s Carnegie Hall appearance — which was to feature the music of Schumann, Rachmaninoff and Tchaikovsky — has been rescheduled for June 15.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matsuev Postpones Carnegie Hall Concert', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matsuev, Denis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T17:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe1190d7-5b64-56d3-8c2c-98068250111c', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe1190d7-5b64-56d3-8c2c-98068250111c'}, {'abstract': 'The Times critic Stephen Holden reviews "Visitors."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002669164/movie-review-visitors.html', 'snippet': 'The Times critic Stephen Holden reviews "Visitors."', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times critic Stephen Holden reviews "Visitors."', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/multimedia/movies-visitors-012414/movies-visitors-012414-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/multimedia/movies-visitors-012414/movies-vi