n Saturday will help awards watchers figure out whether there’s a three-way race, a situation the Weinstein Company could exploit to “Philomena’s” advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES – The Directors Guild Awards, to be held here on Saturday, are usually a reliable barometer of which way the wind is blowing, best picture-wise. Even last year, when the guild saw fit to give its top prize to Ben Affleck, who had been famously snubbed in the directing category by the Academy, it was an indication of how much love there was for his movie “Argo,” which went on to win best picture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alfonso Cuarón May Be a DGA Favorite, but ‘Philomena’ Is Rising Fast', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuaron, Alfonso', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frears, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Steve', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, David O', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Directors Guild of America', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T18:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a22bd1a2-b1fc-5f37-9171-4510f11e5182', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a22bd1a2-b1fc-5f37-9171-4510f11e5182'}, {'abstract': 'The opossum is North America’s only native marsupial, with a short and difficult life.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/opossums-are-unloved-yet-hard-to-resist/', 'snippet': 'The opossum is North America’s only native marsupial, with a short and difficult life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Virginia opossum is more closely related to kangaroos and koalas than to the rats and rodents with which it is frequently compared. North America’s only native marsupial, the opossum is probably more frequently observed in New York City trash cans than in New York City parks.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opossums Are Unloved, Yet Hard to Resist', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unloved, Yet Hard to Resist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opossums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T18:48:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Taft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4006eb2-5ed8-533f-9e81-f8a1c7a56d85', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4006eb2-5ed8-533f-9e81-f8a1c7a56d85'}, {'abstract': 'The decline in Argentina’s currency is the steepest since the country’s economic collapse in 2002, and it is raising fears of a global slump in developing countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/world/americas/argentina-eases-currency-controls-but-citizens-are-not-reassured.html', 'snippet': 'The decline in Argentina’s currency is the steepest since the country’s economic collapse in 2002, and it is raising fears of a global slump in developing countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Cities across Argentina are still unnerved by all the looting that broke out last month after police officers went on strike, protesting salaries eroded by rampant inflation. Residents fumed over blackouts that left them sweltering during a recent heat wave. Then the currency plunged this week, the steepest decline since the nation’s economic collapse in 2002, stirring fears that another major financial crisis could be around the corner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/world/latin/latin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/25/world/latin/latin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/world/latin/latin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/world/latin/latin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/world/latin/latin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/25/world/latin/latin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/world/latin/latin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thum