ct': 'Advice from Walter Chandoha, who has been photographing cats for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/how-to-take-a-perfect-cat-photo-or-at-least-make-a-living-as-an-artist/', 'snippet': 'Advice from Walter Chandoha, who has been photographing cats for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look pages in this weekend’s magazine feature Walter Chandoha’s pictures of the old Penn Station, which he took in the late 1940s in between classes at N.Y.U.’s School of Commerce, Accounts and Finance (now the Stern School of Business). After one of these photographic excursions, Chandoha found a stray kitten in the Village and took it back to his home in Astoria, Queens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Take a Perfect Cat Photo (or at Least Make a Living as an Artist)', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David La Spina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Spina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63a4c408-4d2a-5f5f-8222-6681cb331888', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63a4c408-4d2a-5f5f-8222-6681cb331888'}, {'abstract': 'Range Rovers have a well-deserved reputation for on- and off-road driving manners, and few can do fancy as well as Land Rover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/automobiles/autoreviews/video-range-rover-offers-off-road-capability-in-an-opulent-package.html', 'snippet': 'Range Rovers have a well-deserved reputation for on- and off-road driving manners, and few can do fancy as well as Land Rover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The luxury off-road mission of Jaguar Land Rover’s Range Rover is a curious thing. Last time I checked, polar fleece formal wear never made it big, not even in Seattle. And yet, everywhere I go, people fawn over this opulent S.U.V.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Range Rover Offers Off-Road Capability in an Opulent Package', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jaguar Land Rover', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Land Rover', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/31c2a26c-0b1c-57a8-b94a-3ea7cba8d873', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31c2a26c-0b1c-57a8-b94a-3ea7cba8d873'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Del Zotto helped the Nashville Predators beat the Canucks in Vancouver on Thursday, one day after being traded by the Rangers for Kevin Klein.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/sports/hockey/after-a-long-trip-a-good-predators-debut-for-del-zotto.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Del Zotto helped the Nashville Predators beat the Canucks in Vancouver on Thursday, one day after being traded by the Rangers for Kevin Klein.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VANCOUVER, British Columbia — Michael Del Zotto made his debut with the Nashville Predators on a good note with a 2-1 road win over the Vancouver Canucks on Thursday night. A former Rangers defenseman, Del Zotto is hoping to tune up his N.H.L. career in Music City after being traded on Wednesday for Kevin Klein.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/sports/25delzotto1/25delzotto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/25/sports/25delzotto1/25delzotto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/sports/25delzotto1/25delzotto1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/sports/25delzotto1/25delzotto1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/sports/25delzotto1/25delzotto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/25/sports/25delzotto1/25delzotto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/sports/25delzotto1/25delzotto1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Long Trip, a Good Predators Debut for Del Zotto', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Zotto, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nashville Predators', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:05:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucas Aykroyd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aykroyd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25ba8ed4-e51f-5353-bd49-e85c08f57cbc', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25ba8ed4-e51f-5353-bd49-e85c08f57cbc'}, {'abstract': '“12 O’Clock Boys” is a documentary examining Baltimore dirt-bike aficionados who gather once a week to ride en masse and perform stunts like wheelies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/movies/12-oclock-boys-documents-dirt-bike-riders-in-baltimore.html', 'snippet': '“12 O’Clock Boys” is a documentary examining Baltimore dirt-bike aficionados who gather once a week to ride en masse and perform stunts like wheelies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They gather usually once a week on dirt bikes of all varieties, cruising down the road, engines revved, wheelies popped as they turn the streets of Baltimore into an urban playground. They are called the 12 o’clock boys, and they are the subject of a new documentary of the same name opening Friday. They are also seen as a menace by some in the city’s Police Department and as a danger by some residents. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Running Wild, Wheelies to the Wind', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Running Wild, Wheelies to the Wind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Mekado', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "12 O'Clock Boys (Movie)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nathan, Lotfy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:08:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0684510-a6db-5b90-b311-199aeeb15e1c', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0684510-a6db-5b90-b311-199aeeb15e1c'}, {'abstract': 'Next to James Bond, Ian Fleming’s greatest creation may have been himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/arts/television/a-template-007-named-fleming.html', 'snippet': 'Next to James Bond, Ian Fleming’s greatest creation may have been himself.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Everything I write has a precedent in truth,” Ian Fleming once said, and next to James Bond, his greatest creation may have been himself. A failed stockbroker, the rakish Fleming imbibed drink, women and the family fortune as he tried to escape the shadow of his adventurous older brother Peter and the disappointment of his formidable mother. Then the Naval Intelligence Division cornered him, using his talent for spinning a tale in the World War II effort.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Template 007 Named Fleming', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Template 007 Named Fleming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ee9bda4-91c9-5b7b-ba78-d1740880c06d', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ee9bda4-91c9-5b7b-ba78-d1740880c06d'}, {'abstract': 'John DeLuca runs a hardware store on Staten Island that doubles as a quirkly gallery for his collection of handmade planes, ships and other figures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/nyregion/hardware-shop-owner-sculpts-art-from-odds-and-ends.html', 'snippet': 'John DeLuca runs a hardware store on Staten Island that doubles as a quirkly gallery for his collection of handmade planes, ships and other figures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DeLuca General Store, an old-style hardware shop on Bay Street in the Rosebank section of Staten Island, has a Norman Rockwell-looking storefront with windows displaying garden tools and plumbing supplies.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26CHARACTER_SPAN/26character-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26CHARACTER_SPAN/26character-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26CHARACTER_SPAN/26character-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26CHARACTER_SPAN/26character-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26CHARACTER_SPAN/26character-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26CHARACTER_SPAN/26character-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26CHARACTER_SPAN/26character-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hardware Shop Owner Sculpts Art From Odds and Ends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sculpting From the Trash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hobbies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeLuca, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DeLuca General Store (Staten Island, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:11:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/842a7e87-5b83-5477-b366-3c111c89f844', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/842a7e87-5b83-5477-b366-3c111c89f844'}, {'abstract': 'Martin Garrix became dance music’s boy wonder last year, but, in fact, the kid is a veteran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/arts/music/bragging-rights-of-an-up-and-comer.html', 'snippet': 'Martin Garrix became dance music’s boy wonder last year, but, in fact, the kid is a veteran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Garrix became dance music’s boy wonder last year, thanks to “Animals,” a springy and chipper slice of progressive house with just a touch of attitude. It made him, at 17, the youngest D.J. with a No. 1 chart hit at Beatport, the online electronic music store. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bragging Rights of an Up-and-Comer', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bragging Rights of an Up-and-Comer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:11:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e989c37c-519a-5749-b3bf-6037e08301d5', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e989c37c-519a-5749-b3bf-6037e08301d5'}, {'abstract': 'A film follows a crew herding reindeer in Finnish Lapland, inside the Arctic Circle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/movies/like-john-wayne-but-in-anoraks.html', 'snippet': 'A film follows a crew herding reindeer in Finnish Lapland, inside the Arctic Circle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The doldrums of winter in the city can really get to you. What could be worse? The filmmaker Jessica Oreck, with her Kickstarter-financed documentary “Aatsinki: The Story of Arctic Cowboys” (at IFC Center through Thursday), has an idea. Her film follows the brothers Aarne and Lasse Aatsinki and their crew over one year as they herd reindeer in Finnish Lapland, inside the Arctic Circle. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like John Wayne, but in Anoraks', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like John Wayne, but in Anoraks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edefc3be-1288-5f51-8e0d-e6fb5c5d06de', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edefc3be-1288-5f51-8e0d-e6fb5c5d06de'}, {'abstract': 'Beginning on Tuesday, Rennie Harris Puremovement is back at the Joyce Theater with a selection of repertory favorites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/arts/dance/star-crossed-meets-hip-hop.html', 'snippet': 'Beginning on Tuesday, Rennie Harris Puremovement is back at the Joyce Theater with a selection of repertory favorites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decade has passed since Rennie Harris Puremovement graced the stage of the Joyce Theater. In dance, that’s practically forever. Beginning on Tuesday, the company, led by the astute and poetic hip-hop choreographer Mr. Harris, is back with a selection of repertory favorites, including a newly excerpted and remounted version of “Rome and Jewels.” That Bessie Award-winning work from 2000 — created in collaboration with the dramaturge Ozzie Jonesand the composer Darin Ross — transfers Shakespeare’s “Romeo and Juliet” and “West Side Story” to a captivating b-boy world pitting the Monster Q’s (the Montagues) against the Caps (the Capulets). Mr. Jones reprises his role as narrator, while the astonishing Rodney Mason returns to star as Rome. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Star-Crossed Meets Hip-Hop', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Star-Crossed Meets Hip-Hop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41408ab6-847a-5b7b-af2b-3cafb2b6ca08', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41408ab6-847a-5b7b-af2b-3cafb2b6ca08'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Schick, a star in the world of solo percussion music and the author of “The Percussionist’s Art,” celebrates his 60th birthday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/arts/music/art-of-collision-sticks-to-cymbals.html', 'snippet': 'Steven Schick, a star in the world of solo percussion music and the author of “The Percussionist’s Art,” celebrates his 60th birthday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Schick, a star in the world of solo percussion music and the author of “The Percussionist’s Art,” celebrates his 60th birthday with two concerts at Miller Theater that trace the trajectory of this repertory. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art of Collision, Sticks to Cymbals', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art of Collision, Sticks to Cymbals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:14:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c97b54-5035-5819-ae9e-623e419d9c12', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c97b54-5035-5819-ae9e-623e419d9c12'}, {'abstract': 'Two exhibitions opening this week sample opposite ends of the history of photography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/arts/design/before-and-after-paris-in-the-1800s.html', 'snippet': 'Two exhibitions opening this week sample opposite ends of the history of photography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two exhibitions opening this week sample opposite ends of the history of photography. First is Charles Marville, appointed official photographer of Paris in 1862. Over the next eight years, he documented old parts of the city destined for a drastic makeover, then photographed the new boulevards, gas lamps, pissoirs and other amenities that transformed Paris into a modern metropolis. “Charles Marville: Photographer of Paris,” opening Wednesday at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, presents about 100 of his lucid and evocative photographs. (Through May 4, 212-535-7710, metmuseum.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before and After, Paris in the 1800s', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before and After, Paris in the 1800s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:14:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4824b4e5-d2fa-5498-9438-c57940271b1e', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4824b4e5-d2fa-5498-9438-c57940271b1e'}, {'abstract': 'In our latest installment of this exclusive series of interviews by Doug Aitken, the artist interviews the digital media and visualization artist Aaron Koblin.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/the-source-aaron-koblin-in-conversation-with-doug-aitken/', 'snippet': 'In our latest installment of this exclusive series of interviews by Doug Aitken, the artist interviews the digital media and visualization artist Aaron Koblin.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There’s all this invisible infrastructure that’s surrounding us,” says the digital media artist Aaron Koblin, who serves as the Creative Director of the Data Arts Team at Google. With visualization projects such as “Flight Patterns,” he has sought to bring that hidden world to light. Koblin speaks with the artist Doug Aitken about the intersection of art and technology as part of the Source, a series of candid video conversations with several dozen noteworthy figures about their creative processes, currently on view in a custom pavilion at the Sundance Film Festival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Source | Aaron Koblin in Conversation With Doug Aitken', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aitken, Doug', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/183bdbb9-255f-52e6-a131-12f58387d21d', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/183bdbb9-255f-52e6-a131-12f58387d21d'}, {'abstract': 'The frontwomen of Warpaint agree: In the event of an apocalypse, they would outfit themselves more sensibly than Beyoncé.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/arts/music/making-waves-at-sea-and-in-the-studio.html', 'snippet': 'The frontwomen of Warpaint agree: In the event of an apocalypse, they would outfit themselves more sensibly than Beyoncé.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The frontwomen of Warpaint agree: In the event of an apocalypse, they would outfit themselves more sensibly than Beyoncé. “You’re not going to be wearing a shirt” that is “just barely covering your nipples,” Theresa Wayman said of the futuristic video for the recent Beyoncé song “Superpower.” Emily Kokal added, “You’re going to be covering yourself from the elements.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1235, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1235}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 498, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 995, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJ