orward, almost toppling over his head. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SCARLETT_SPAN/26SCARLETT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SCARLETT_SPAN/26SCARLETT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SCARLETT_SPAN/26SCARLETT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SCARLETT_SPAN/26SCARLETT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SCARLETT_SPAN/26SCARLETT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SCARLETT_SPAN/26SCARLETT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26SCARLETT_SPAN/26SCARLETT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gestures of a Hot Hand', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gestures of a Hot Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulcas, Roslyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scarlett, Liam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fb39552-5a1d-5109-8317-8112bf98ab25', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fb39552-5a1d-5109-8317-8112bf98ab25'}, {'abstract': 'With a body similar to the original 1998 Navigator, the refreshed 2015 model gets a more potent, more efficient EcoBoost engine and an updated grille.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/automobiles/autoreviews/the-2015-lincoln-navigator-a-familiar-shape-with-a-new-face.html', 'snippet': 'With a body similar to the original 1998 Navigator, the refreshed 2015 model gets a more potent, more efficient EcoBoost engine and an updated grille.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lincoln Navigator first appeared in 1998 as an upscale Ford Expedition, which in turn was a larger version of that era’s Ford Explorer. If you saw the 2015 model coming from far away, or in low light, you might not be able to tell that anything had changed over the last decade and a half. But the Lincoln Motor Company assures us that the Navigator, familiar in profile as it is, is better than ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/automobiles/25LINCOLN/25LINCOLN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/25/automobiles/25LINCOLN/25LINCOLN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, 