le after last year’s performance. Shareholders should have a loud say against this pay – and the lead director, Lee Raymond.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/business/dealbook/dbpix-chase/dbpix-chase-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/business/dealbook/dbpix-chase/dbpix-chase-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/business/dealbook/dbpix-chase/dbpix-chase-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/business/dealbook/dbpix-chase/dbpix-chase-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/business/dealbook/dbpix-chase/dbpix-chase-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/business/dealbook/dbpix-chase/dbpix-chase-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/business/dealbook/dbpix-chase/dbpix-chase-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dismay for Pay at JPMorgan Chase', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T19:48:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd1f0ee5-c41a-5083-800c-9b70918c51f9', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd1f0ee5-c41a-5083-800c-9b70918c51f9'}, {'abstract': 'Claude Lanzmann’s documentary “The Last of the Unjust” centers on a rabbi who served as the head of the Jewish council at the Theresienstadt concentration camp.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/movies/the-last-of-the-unjust-about-a-jewish-camp-official.html', 'snippet': 'Claude Lanzmann’s documentary “The Last of the Unjust” centers on a rabbi who served as the head of the Jewish council at the Theresienstadt concentration camp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theresienstadt was called Hitler’s “gift to the Jews.” In an 18th-century military town some 40 miles north of Prague, this “model ghetto” was established to show the world that life in a concentration camp was practically halcyon. Grown-ups lingered over delicious meals between fulfilling workdays and evening concerts or lectures. Children devoured sweets. Soccer matches were played in the town square.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26LANZMAN1_SPAN/26LANZMAN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26LANZMAN1_SPAN/26LANZMAN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/arts/26LANZMAN1_SPAN/26LANZMAN1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, '