nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fda4b97-968f-54a5-9a42-53e7c0388e25', 'word_count': 1466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fda4b97-968f-54a5-9a42-53e7c0388e25'}, {'abstract': 'The move is intended to produce a nominee earlier in the process, preventing bruising and costly primary battles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/us/politics/republicans-approve-changes-to-nominating-process.html', 'snippet': 'The move is intended to produce a nominee earlier in the process, preventing bruising and costly primary battles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Republican National Committee moved Friday to consolidate its presidential nominating process in 2016, a pre-emptive effort to avoid a drawn-out campaign that many in the party say could imperil their effort to reclaim the White House.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/us/rnc/rnc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/25/us/rnc/rnc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/us/rnc/rnc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/us/rnc/rnc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/us/rnc/rnc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/25/us/rnc/rnc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/us/rnc/rnc-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Vote to Streamline Nominating Process', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Vote to Streamline Nominating Process', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T20:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0983c8ee-2eb4-56ac-b34e-5ac7af43acba', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0983c8ee-2eb4-56ac-b34e-5ac7af43acba'}, {'abstract': 'On Sundays, Michael Dorf, founder of the Knitting Factory music club and the City Winery restaurant, hangs out with his family, without the music he can’t get his children to love.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/nyregion/all-together-now-eyes-on-the-screen.html', 'snippet': 'On Sundays, Michael Dorf, founder of the Knitting Factory music club and the City Winery restaurant, hangs out with his family, without the music he can’t get his children to love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You start off a brash outsider, testing the limits of acceptability, and if you’re good enough and lucky enough, you eventually become the Establishment, explaining to your children why the things you’re passionate about aren’t too boring for words. Such is the trajectory of Michael Dorf, who founded the edgy music club Knitting Factory in 1986 and, 22 years later, City Winery, where middle-aged singer-songwriter types pluck and warble for patrons having braised rabbit and merlot-cabernet blends. Mr. Dorf, 51, plans to open City Winery outposts this year in Nashville and Napa Valley, Calif. On March 31 he will present his 10th annual benefit concert at Carnegie Hall to raise money for music education, this one dedicated to the songs of Paul Simon. He lives in TriBeCa with his wife, Sarah Connors, 49, a film producer, and their children, Sophia, 10, and 15-year-old twins, Eli and Zachary (who was away on a recent Sunday). The family has a rescue mutt and a rabbit.\xa0', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE2/26ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE2/26ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE2/26ROUTINE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE2/26ROUTINE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur