s-davis-performances-to-be-released/', 'snippet': '“Miles at the Fillmore – Miles Davis 1970: The Bootleg Series, Vol. 3,” a four-CD set, includes unreleased performances by Davis with Chick Corea, Keith Jarrett, Dave Holland, Airto Moreira and Steve Grossman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two hours of previously unreleased performances by Miles Davis, leading a band that included Chick Corea, Keith Jarrett, Dave Holland, Airto Moreira and Steve Grossman, will be included in “Miles at the Fillmore – Miles Davis 1970: The Bootleg Series, Vol. 3,” a four-CD set to be released by Columbia/Legacy on March 25.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unreleased Miles Davis Performances to Be Released', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Miles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T22:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eba3663-3c40-5521-965d-93f1ef6759da', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eba3663-3c40-5521-965d-93f1ef6759da'}, {'abstract': 'The Belgians make a lot of beers that defy categorization. The tasting panel gathered 23 that have one thing in common: they are excellent summer quenchers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2007/08/22/dining/20070822_TASTING_FEATURE.html', 'snippet': 'The Belgians make a lot of beers that defy categorization. The tasting panel gathered 23 that have one thing in common: they are excellent summer quenchers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Belgians make a lot of beers that defy categorization. The tasting panel gathered 23 that have one thing in common: they are excellent summer quenchers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ales of The Times: Belgian Pale Ales', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T22:33:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/abb307f5-5186-5ee9-899f-2f958dc5026e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/abb307f5-5186-5ee9-899f-2f958dc5026e'}, {'abstract': 'Sheep. They’re not as harmless as they seem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/opinion/sunday/pastoral-icon-or-woolly-menace.html', 'snippet': 'Sheep. They’re not as harmless as they seem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU don’t have to look far to see the woolly influence of sheep on our cultural lives. They turn up as symbols of peace and a vaguely remembered pastoral way of life in our poetry, our art and our Christmas pageants. Wolves also rank high among our cultural icons, usually in connection with the words “big” and “bad.” And yet there is now a debate underway about substituting the wolf for the sheep on the (also iconic) green hills of Britain.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/02/opinion/richard-conniff/richard-conniff-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 583, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLa