oth the Smithsonian Institution and the National WWII Museum in New Orleans announced new ventures to coincide with the Feb. 7 release of “The Monuments Men.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/museums-follow-the-call-of-a-clooney-movie/', 'snippet': 'Both the Smithsonian Institution and the National WWII Museum in New Orleans announced new ventures to coincide with the Feb. 7 release of “The Monuments Men.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s nothing like the advent of a George Clooney movie to put historical institutions on a war footing. Timed to coincide with the Feb. 7 release of “The Monuments Men,” about the heroics of the soldiers and scholars who chased after European cultural treasures plundered by the Nazis, both the Smithsonian Institution and the National WWII Museum in New Orleans announced new ventures. The New Orleans museum said it would open a permanent gallery about the unit in 2016. It will show, among other things, how the soldiers descended into an Austrian salt mine to recover masterpieces hoarded there by Germans. The exhibition will highlight the recovery of works by Rembrandt, Vermeer, Picasso and Leonardo da Vinci and the continuing search for works like Raphael’s “Portrait of a Young Man” and Michelangelo’s marble “Mask of a Faun.” Meanwhile in Washington on Feb. 7, the Smithsonian Institution’s Archives of American Art will open an exhibition called “Monuments Men: On the Frontline to Save Europe’s Art, 1942-1946.” It will showcase the work of the scholars in the original unit, one of whom is played by Mr. Clooney.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museums Follow the Call of a Clooney Movie', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Museums Follow the Call of a Clooney Movie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monuments Men', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T23:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Mashberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af9b7f9e-a38b-5047-a9fc-66b71b0fb691', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af9b7f9e-a38b-5047-a9fc-66b71b0fb691'}, {'abstract': 'The District 3 Winter Regional took place at the Hilton hotel in Rye Brook, N.Y., from Jan. 14 through last Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/crosswords/bridge/the-district-3-winter-regional-in-rye-brook-ny.html', 'snippet': 'The District 3 Winter Regional took place at the Hilton hotel in Rye Brook, N.Y., from Jan. 14 through last Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The District 3 Winter Regional took place at the Hilton hotel in Rye Brook, N.Y., from Jan. 14 through last Monday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 342, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 342, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/25cards-1/25cards-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail