weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Film On Feb. 6, the 64th Berlin International Film Festival, or Berlinale, will begin . The film festival will award lifetime honors to the British director Ken Loach and feature over 400 films, including the world premiere of “The Monuments Men,” about an Allied group who recovered stolen artworks from the Nazis, with George Clooney and Matt Damon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Horizon: Berlin International Film Festival; ‘This Is Not a Silent Movie’', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clooney, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loach, Ken', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Contemporary Craft (Portland, Ore)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-24T23:14:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e912d26a-8ec1-5111-993a-e6537a82dcef', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e912d26a-8ec1-5111-993a-e6537a82dcef'}, {'abstract': 'Loving ‘Downton Abbey’ in the new Gilded Age.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/sympathy-for-the-toffs/', 'snippet': 'Loving ‘Downton Abbey’ in the new Gilded Age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, we turned on the plutocrats. Everyone from Pope Francis to Bill de Blasio denounced them. Even Bill and