me': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c202b134-bb59-56a3-b52e-80b0ad1eba4b', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c202b134-bb59-56a3-b52e-80b0ad1eba4b'}, {'abstract': 'The federal Department of Housing and Urban Development ended a two-year legal dispute on Friday with the state and a private developer of subsidized housing, which it had accused of discrimination for favoring the deaf and the hard-of-hearing over others seeking to live in a 75-unit complex for the elderly built to fit the needs of the deaf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/us/arizona-challenge-to-housing-for-the-deaf-is-dropped.html', 'snippet': 'The federal Department of Housing and Urban Development ended a two-year legal dispute on Friday with the state and a private developer of subsidized housing, which it had accused of discrimination for favoring the deaf and the hard-of-hearing ove...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal Department of Housing and Urban Development ended a two-year legal dispute on Friday with the state and a private developer of subsidized housing, which it had accused of discrimination for favoring the deaf and the hard-of-hearing over others seeking to live in a 75-unit complex for the elderly built to fit the needs of the deaf. In a letter, HUD officials said that the type of federal funding used to build the complex, Apache ASL Trails, in Tempe, did not prevent it from giving preference to a specific group of disabled individuals. The agency closed its investigation and removed its legal challenges against the development, which was designed by a deaf architect and offers video phones and lights that flash when the phone or doorbell rings at each unit, among other features. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: Challenge to Housing for the Deaf Is Dropped', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: Challenge to Housing for the Deaf Is Dropped', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T02:43:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce1c2773-778d-59b5-96dd-f44c07e5f8ab', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce1c2773-778d-59b5-96dd-f44c07e5f8ab'}, {'abstract': 'David Herszenhorn reports from Kiev, Ukraine, where fighting has resumed between antigovernment protestors and the riot police, not far from the Dynamo soccer stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000002670573/kiev-cease-fire-ends.html', 'snippet': 'David Herszenhorn reports from Kiev, Ukraine, where fighting has resumed between antigovernment protestors and the riot police, not far from the Dynamo soccer stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Herszenhorn reports from Kiev, Ukraine, where fighting has resumed between antigovernment protestors and the riot police, not far from the Dynamo soccer stadium.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'c