ocument_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/905150c6-176d-50cd-9133-ebe1b2ab3643', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/905150c6-176d-50cd-9133-ebe1b2ab3643'}, {'abstract': 'In this new Sun Kil Moon song, you’ll hear the melancholy I’ve carried around with me since I was young.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/24/the-song-remains-the-same-and-kind-of-blue/', 'snippet': 'In this new Sun Kil Moon song, you’ll hear the melancholy I’ve carried around with me since I was young.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you grew up in the 1970s and you loved ’70s rock as much as I did, then there is a good chance you saw the Led Zeppelin concert film, “The Song Remains the Same.” The film documents a 1973 Zeppelin concert at Madison Square Garden and played in theaters throughout the late ’70s and after. It became an almost instant cult classic, bringing my favorite rock band ever to life, with only a trip to the local theater. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Song Remains the Same (and Kind of Blue)', 'kicker': 'Measure for Measure', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Led Zeppelin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sun Kil Moon (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T02:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Kozelek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozelek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eb23e87-d495-5aad-b2bf-fdc877555669', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eb23e87-d495-5aad-b2bf-fdc877555669'}, {'abstract': 'After reaching a nuclear deal, President Hassan Rouhani now needs to help stop the catastrophic civil war in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/opinion/irans-charm-offensive.html', 'snippet': 'After reaching a nuclear deal, President Hassan Rouhani now needs to help stop the catastrophic civil war in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Hassan Rouhani of Iran made his debut this week at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, where he expanded on his government’s charm offensive by wooing investors and reassuring political leaders of his determination to complete a comprehensive nuclear deal with the major powers. But his benign image and deft political skills could not erase or excuse the ugly fact that Iran remains the main ally of Syria’s president, Bashar al-Assad, in the destruction of Syria and its people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Charm Offensive', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran&#8217;s Charm Offensive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T02:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/63bd425d-a82b-52c5-ab93-0a362b886b34', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63bd425d-a82b-52c5-ab93-0a362b886b34'}, {'abstract': 'In New York, all the money from mortgage deals should go to help homeowners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/opinion/dividing-the-bank-settlement.html', 'snippet': 'In New York, all the money from mortgage deals should go to help homeowners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo has deservedly lost Round 1 of the unnecessary fight he picked recently with the New York State attorney general, Eric Schneiderman, over the distribution of proceeds from a bank settlement. To persist in his pique could hurt all New Yorkers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dividing the Bank Settlement', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dividing the Bank Settlement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T02:49:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/62ef71b8-1f65-588f-90e6-802fa0664c96', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62ef71b8-1f65-588f-90e6-802fa0664c96'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Steve King’s broadly written amendment would jeopardize states’ powers to enact their own agricultural standards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/opinion/a-hidden-threat-in-the-farm-bill.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Steve King’s broadly written amendment would jeopardize states’ powers to enact their own agricultural standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mammoth farm bill is reportedly near a conference compromise in Congress, bristling with more tragic cuts in the food stamp program for the needy and a revision of lucrative commodity subsidies for mostly big farmers. Running below the radar is a dangerous, broadly written amendment that would threaten states’ current powers to enact their own agricultural standards — standards that can extend far beyond farmyards to consumer, worker and environmental safety. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hidden Threat in the Farm Bill', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hidden Threat in the Farm Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Steven A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Conference of State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of 