 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d40e6b7-6668-5f08-ad33-27c0198db8fa', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d40e6b7-6668-5f08-ad33-27c0198db8fa'}, {'abstract': 'Taking stock 30 years after the powerful story of a severe schizophrenic was told.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/opinion/nocera-for-the-mentally-ill-its-worse.html', 'snippet': 'Taking stock 30 years after the powerful story of a severe schizophrenic was told.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, one of the landmark nonfiction books of the last 50 years was reissued by Vintage Books. “Is There No Place on Earth for Me?” by Susan Sheehan began in 1981 as a four-part series in The New Yorker; in 1982, it came out as a book, winning the Pulitzer Prize. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 975, 'width': 850, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Mentally Ill, It’s Worse', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For the Mentally Ill, It&#8217;s Worse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Schizophrenia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheehan, Susan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Torrey, E Fuller', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Is There No Place on Earth for Me? (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T03:18:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e8a647-a72d-503a-9f6e-bce6e8f40d4b', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e8a647-a72d-503a-9f6e-bce6e8f40d4b'}, {'abstract': 'A spokesman for the archdiocese of Philadelphia said he expects Pope Francis to attend an event there in September 2015, although the Vatican has not given official word.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/world/europe/us-catholics-hope-for-2015-papal-visit.html', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for the archdiocese of Philadelphia said he expects Pope Francis to attend an event there in September 2015, although the Vatican has not given official word.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Pope Francis may make his first trip as pope to the United States in September 2015 to attend the Roman Catholic Church’s World Meeting of Families in Philadelphia. Popes traditionally attend these events, which have been held every three years since 1994. “We are planning as if Pope Francis will be with us and have no indication that he will not attend,” said Kenneth A. Gavin, a spokesman for the archdiocese of Philadelphia. But he added that any reports that Francis would make the trip “are not official.” There is speculation that Francis would stop in New York on that same trip to speak to the United Nations General Assembly, but Joseph Zwilling, a spokesman for the archdiocese of New York, said the archdiocese had not heard anything from the Vatican. The last papal visit to the United States was in April 2008, when Pope Benedict XVI traveled to Washington and New York. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Catholics Hope for 2015 Papal Visit', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Vatican: U.S. Catholics Hope for 2015 Papal Visit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T03:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee062d6a-e936-5d9e-9b8f-714e803c9769', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee062d6a-e936-5d9e-9b8f-714e803c9769'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 25, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/pageoneplus/corrections-january-25-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 25, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':