ganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/937ca54b-6195-50af-a9d2-a29fee8a72fc', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/937ca54b-6195-50af-a9d2-a29fee8a72fc'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Marshall also appeared in films like “The Long, Hot Summer” and was nominated for a Tony for “Goodbye, Charlie.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/arts/television/sarah-marshall-actress-in-twilight-zone-and-star-trek-dies-at-80.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Marshall also appeared in films like “The Long, Hot Summer” and was nominated for a Tony for “Goodbye, Charlie.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Marshall, an actress who was born into show business and worked on Broadway, in film and on television, perhaps most memorably in episodes of “The Twilight Zone” and “Star Trek,” died on Jan. 18 at her home in Los Angeles. She was 80.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/marshall-obit/marshall-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/marshall-obit/marshall-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/marshall-obit/marshall-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/marshall-obit/marshall-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1030, 'width': 1405, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/marshall-obit/marshall-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/marshall-obit/marshall-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/arts/marshall-obit/marshall-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sarah Marshall, Actress in ‘Twilight Zone’ and ‘Star Trek’, Dies at 80', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sarah Marshall, 80, Television Actress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Sarah (1933-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Twilight Zone (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Star Trek (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T05:47:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b52f72d-39ed-5fda-997f-d17107498d09', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b52f72d-39ed-5fda-997f-d17107498d09'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (Starz) THIS IS THE END (2013) A group of funny guys — among them, from left above, James Franco, Jonah Hill, Craig Robinson, Seth Rogen, Jay Baruchel and Danny McBride, each playing himself —\xa0gather at a party at Mr. Franco’s house in Los Angeles, during which events foretold in the Book of Revelation occur. The righteous are raptured up to heaven; the rest, including many of the most famous people in Hollywood, are swallowed into fiery pits or pursued by horned demons. The movie, written and directed by Mr. Rogen and Evan Goldberg, “at its phoned-in worst and also at its riotous best, has a terminal feeling,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “It suggests that a comic subgenre based on the immaturity, sexual panic and self-mocking tendencies of men who should be old enough to know better has reached its expiration date.” But, “as crude as the movie’s humor often is, its spirit is sweet, sensitive and innocuous. In their script for ‘Superbad,’ Mr. Rogen and Mr. Goldberg zeroed in on the tenderness and vulnerability that lie at the heart of male friendship, and here they go even further, using the prospect of global annihilation as an occasion for some touchy-feely relationship workshopping.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T06:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/69f71f7d-c066-5a2c-b3e6-5cc87a390cdd', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69f71f7d-c066-5a2c-b3e6-5cc87a390cdd'}, {'abs