ervice as useful as possible for the crowd, and are instead trying to distinguish themselves from one another.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At some point, Twitter and the rest of social media became less about wanting to share the news and more about wanting to be the news. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/technology/24bits-bieber1/24bits-bieber1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/technology/24bits-bieber1/24bits-bieber1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/technology/24bits-bieber1/24bits-bieber1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/technology/24bits-bieber1/24bits-bieber1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1396, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/technology/24bits-bieber1/24bits-bieber1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/technology/24bits-bieber1/24bits-bieber1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/technology/24bits-bieber1/24bits-bieber1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Valley of the Blahs: How Justin Bieber’s Troubles Exposed Twitter’s Achilles’ Heel', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T13:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77602fba-95c2-5fbf-9a5c-3d571a775bf8', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77602fba-95c2-5fbf-9a5c-3d571a775bf8'}, {'abstract': 'A video by George King, who has been filming Lonnie Holley for 18 years.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/lonnie-holley-in-his-alabama-yard-art-element/', 'snippet': 'A video by George King, who has been filming Lonnie Holley for 18 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 18 years, the Atlanta-based documentary filmmaker George King has been shooting Lonnie Holley, an artist and musician that I write about in this weekend’s magazine. King has mined the footage to make a video for “Looking for All (All Rendered Truth),” a song from Holley’s 2012 debut album, “Just Before Music.” If, like me, you’ve met Holley only recently, the footage is fascinating to watch, offering glimpses of the artist as a young man: showing off his intricate sandstone sculptures or wandering amid the scavenged materials — a baby doll, a “Dead End” sign, a lawn jockey, a wrecked car, a child’s dress — in his Alabama yard-art environment. (There are also shots of a bulldozer tearing the place down, after it was condemned by the airport authority.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lonnie Holley, in His Alabama Yard-Art Element', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T13:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Binelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Binelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abd5c2eb-49c8-5fd7-a531-34c78a024e92', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abd5c2eb-49c8-5fd7-a531-34c78a024e92'}, {'abstract': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/sports/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Sports Editor:', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Inbox', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sherman’s Behavior Is Nothing to Emulate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman, Richard (1988- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T16:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/0daae0ec-6f11-5236-b992-50f9f0d42c99', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0daae0ec-6f11-5236-b992-50f9f0d42c99'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe talks Bitcoin.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/25/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-january-24-2014/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe talks Bitcoin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Digital currency is inching its way onto Wall Street, with a new “Bitcoin center” next door to the New York Stock Exchange. As the currency gains prominence and popularity, regulators—like New York’s Department of Financial Services, which is holding hearings next week—are trying to work out where they figure in. Joe talks about the future of Bitcoin, while Rana Foroohar of Time magazine reports from the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/opinion/bitcoin/bitcoin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/24/opinion/bitcoin/bitcoin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 322}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/opinion/bitcoin/bitcoin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/opinion/bitcoin/bitcoin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/opinion/bitcoin/bitcoin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/24/opinion/bitcoin/bitcoin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/24/opinion/bitcoin/bitcoin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on 