. They’re pouring back into the market, and adding options galore to their new homes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/business/in-housing-big-is-back-not-counting-the-extras.html', 'snippet': 'The bursting of the housing bubble didn’t deter affluent buyers for long. They’re pouring back into the market, and adding options galore to their new homes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katie Sleep and her husband, Jonathan, lived in the same four-bedroom home in a Washington suburb for 23 years. After Ms. Sleep decided to retire, they began looking for a new house, and, after viewing a model home in a new development, decided to move to Leesburg, Va., about 40 miles from the city. In having their new home built, they saw an opportunity — not to downsize, but to create a far larger home catering to their every need. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/business/26-TOLL1SUB/26-TOLL1SUB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/business/26-TOLL1SUB/26-TOLL1SUB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/business/26-TOLL1SUB/26-TOLL1SUB-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/business/26-TOLL1SUB/26-TOLL1SUB-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1110, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/business/26-TOLL1SUB/26-TOLL1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, '