rea have battled not only their opponents but wind, ice or mud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/26/sports/football/new-york-area-weather-has-a-history-with-the-super-bowl.html', 'snippet': 'Teams playing in title games in the New York area have battled not only their opponents but wind, ice or mud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the countdowns to each of the previous 47 Super Bowls, the primary question was, quite simply, Which team will win? But as Denver and Seattle await XLVIII next Sunday at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, N.J., questions about the weather for the first outdoor cold-climate Super Bowl have upstaged even the point spread.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Area Weather Has a History with the Super Bowl', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Playing Here? Bring Sneakers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-25T21:39:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20905188-730b-5043-b918-cdf3bf96caa6', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20905188-730b-5043-b918-cdf3bf96caa6'}, {'abstract': 'The adulteration of Italian olive oil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/01/24/opinion/food-chains-extra-virgin-suicide.html', 'snippet': 'The adulteration of Italian olive oil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The adulteration of Italian oli