 'Offering a preview of the State of the Union address, two aides to President Obama said on Sunday morning talk shows that Mr. Obama was willing to bypass a gridlocked Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Aides to President Obama on Sunday offered a preview of the strategy of the president’s State of the Union address, emphasizing Mr. Obama’s willingness to bypass a gridlocked Congress to achieve his goals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aides Say Obama Is Willing to Work With or Without Congress to Meet Goals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pfeiffer, Daniel H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Jay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-26T20:26:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/436c65c5-cd5d-5600-b006-4d8a796490b9', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/436c65c5-cd5d-5600-b006-4d8a796490b9'}, {'abstract': 'George Rothman conducted the Riverside Symphony at Alice Tully Hall in “Shadow and Light,” a program that included works by the composers Toru Takemitsu and Arthur Honegger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/arts/music/riverside-symphony-performs-works-by-takemitsu-and-honegger.html', 'snippet': 'George Rothman conducted the Riverside Symphony at Alice Tully Hall in “Shadow and Light,” a program that included works by the composers Toru Takemitsu and Arthur Honegger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The international career of the Japanese composer Toru Takemitsu began after Stravinsky heard one of his works in the late ’50s and began championing his music. Although Takemitsu initially resisted traditional music because of its association with Japanese militarism, which he loathed, he later included indigenous instruments and folk music in his understated, eloquent and coloristic works scores, influenced by European modernism and French composers like Debussy. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/SUBriverside/SUBriverside-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/SUBriverside/SUBriverside-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/SUBriverside/SUBriverside-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/SUBriverside/SUBriverside-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im