/26/grammy-parties-aplenty-before-the-big-party/', 'snippet': 'There were some extraordinary musical events in the days leading up to the Grammy Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Music, as you might expect, is everywhere in the parties, showcases and music-industry hobnobs leading up to the Grammy Awards. And while the sight of a person singing into a microphone is sometimes the cue for executives to reach for their smartphones, there were some extraordinary musical events over the last few days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/theater/26keys/26keys-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/26/theater/26keys/26keys-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/theater/26keys/26keys-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/theater/26keys/26keys-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1129, 'width': 1520, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/theater/26keys/26keys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/26/theater/26keys/26keys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/26/theater/26keys/26keys-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grammy Parties Aplenty Before the Big Party', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grammy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Clive', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Carole', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beats Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MusiCares', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-26T21:17:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fa51cbb-6bc6-5171-be59-74abc2af3854', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fa51cbb-6bc6-5171-be59-74abc2af3854'}, {'abstract': 'In “All Joy and No Fun,” Jennifer Senior looks at overscheduling and other tendencies in contemporary middle-class child rearing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/books/jennifer-senior-studies-parenthood-in-all-joy-and-no-fun.html', 'snippet': 'In “All Joy and No Fun,” Jennifer Senior looks at overscheduling and other tendencies in contemporary middle-class child rearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer Senior’s astute book about parents and children, “All Joy and No Fun,” is especially eye opening about how many prejudices are usually built into such studies. Take “parenting,” a word that invariably makes its way into books about parent-child dynamics: Ms. Senior would like to remind us that this was not always a verb, and that the emphasis on parents’ need to devote themselves 24/7 to their offspring is a relative novelty. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27book-jp/27book-jp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27book-jp/27book-jp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27book-jp/27book-jp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27book-jp/27book-jp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1691, 'width': 1691, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27book-jp/27book-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27book-jp/27book-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27book-jp/27book-jp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Kid’s Idle for a Second? Oh, Horrors!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Kid’s Idle for a Second? Oh, Horrors!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Senior, Jennifer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-26T22:07:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b9cac6-eed2-56f6-9cc4-d231b76b49c0', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b9cac6-eed2-56f6-9cc4-d231b76b49c0'}, {'abstract': 'With her work “4,” the choreographer Sarah Michelson used many elements to continue her Devotion series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/arts/dance/sarah-michelsons-4-at-the-whitney-continues-a-series.html', 'snippet': 'With her work “4,” the choreographer Sarah Michelson used many elements to continue her Devotion series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A central problem with the choreographer Sarah Michelson is that the admirer who surrounds her with the greatest claims for Sarah Michelson’s greatness is Sarah Michelson herself. In the four works of hers I’ve seen since 2009, her dances strike me as obviously limited, largely unoriginal, though not devoid of interest. But as theater works, especially in their use of recorded speech and music, they’re vexing. And in “4,” her new piece now showing at the Whitney Museum of American Art, she emerges as the most pretentious artist of my entire experience, and among the most self-infatuated.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27michelson/27michelson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/27michelson/27michelson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 290}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'captio