 on women’s rights is plainly not helping it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Formula for Repelling Women Voters', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Formula for Repelling Women Voters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Christopher H', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T02:17:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/89f5c278-edbc-5ef6-b06e-37a35cd83cac', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89f5c278-edbc-5ef6-b06e-37a35cd83cac'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court’s momentous ruling on same-sex marriage is used to protect gay jurors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/opinion/the-expanding-power-of-us-v-windsor.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court’s momentous ruling on same-sex marriage is used to protect gay jurors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The heartening effects of the Supreme Court’s landmark ruling last June striking down the core of the Defense of Marriage Act, or DOMA, continue to ripple outward. On Jan. 21, the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit held that gays and lesbians may not be excluded from juries on the basis of their sexual orientation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Expanding Power of U.S. v. Windsor', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Expanding Power of U.S. v. Windsor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reinhardt, Stephen R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T02:20:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0984194c-6268-5a16-a298-6ff1a48ca181', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0984194c-6268-5a16-a298-6ff1a48ca181'}, {'abstract': 'American intelligence agencies are concerned that they could lose their air bases used for drone strikes if a final security deal cannot be struck with the Afghan president, Hamid Karzai.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/world/asia/afghanistan-exit-is-seen-as-peril-to-drone-mission.html', 'snippet': 'American intelligence agencies are concerned that they could lose their air bases used for drone strikes if a final security deal cannot be struck with the Afghan president, Hamid Karzai.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The risk that President Obama may be forced to pull all American troops out of Afghanistan by the end of the year has set off concerns inside the American intelligence agencies that they could lose their air bases used for drone strikes against Al Qaeda in Pakistan and for responding to a nuclear crisis in the region. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/27INTEL/27INTEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/world/27INTEL/27INTEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/27INTEL/27INTEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/27INTEL/27INTEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/27INTEL/27INTEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/28/world/27INTEL/27INTEL-thumbSta