 The data show that only one in four New York City students who started high school in 2009 and graduated in 2013 performed well enough on the Regents exams to meet the state definition of college readiness. Racial and ethnic breakdowns are not yet available. But they are likely to mirror last year’s statistics, which showed striking racial disparities: Only about 11 percent of black and about 12 percent of Hispanic graduates were deemed college-ready. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting an Accurate Fix on Schools', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting an Accurate Fix on Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T02:23:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/732b675d-29fc-50d8-8fba-9b9fab849d00', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/732b675d-29fc-50d8-8fba-9b9fab849d00'}, {'abstract': 'A review of competitive congressional contests suggests that Republicans will hold on to the House, while Senate Democrats will almost certainly see their majority narrowed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/us/politics/2014-elections-likely-to-keep-capitals-split.html', 'snippet': 'A review of competitive congressional contests suggests that Repub