estioned whether NHK, Japan’s influential public broadcaster, was under political pressure to adhere to the views of the right-leaning government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/world/asia/japan-official-under-fire-for-saying-public-broadcaster-wont-criticize-government.html', 'snippet': 'Some members of the news media questioned whether NHK, Japan’s influential public broadcaster, was under political pressure to adhere to the views of the right-leaning government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The head of Japan’s influential public broadcaster drew sharp criticism on Sunday for saying that the broadcaster would refrain from criticizing the right-leaning government on such delicate issues as visits to a controversial shrine honoring war dead. He also said his nation should not be singled out for forcing women into sexual servitude during World War II.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Official Under Fire for Saying Public Broadcaster Won’t Criticize Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Official Draws Fire for Saying Public Broadcaster Won’t Criticize Japan on War Issues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Momii, Katsuto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NHK (Japan Broadcasting Corp)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T05:27:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': 