es to defeat an injured Rafael Nadal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/sports/tennis/wawrinka-nadal-and-two-unforeseen-opponents-fear-and-pain.html', 'snippet': 'The Australian Open men’s final included psychological and physical struggles, with Stanislas Wawrinka playing a superb opening set and ultimately winning his battle with nerves to defeat an injured Rafael Nadal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pain and fear are two subplots that can lurk in the background for athletes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wawrinka, Nadal and Two Unforeseen Opponents: Fear and Pain', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wawrinka, Nadal and Two Unforeseen Opponents: Fear and Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wawrinka, Stanislas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T05:37:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/445ec5a1-5612-5d0f-bcdd-d53448bc8bb9', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/445ec5a1-5612-5d0f-bcdd-d53448bc8bb9'}, {'abstract': 'Many of New York City’s iconic water towers have not been cleaned or inspected in years, and regulations governing the tanks are rarely enforced, an examination shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/nyregion/inside-citys-water-tanks-layers-of-neglect.html', 'snippet': 'Many of New York City’s iconic water towers have not been cleaned or inspected in years, and regulations governing the tanks are rarely enforced, an examination shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With their quaint barrel-like contours and weathered cedar-plank sides, rooftop water towers are a constant on the New York City skyline. And though they may look like relics of a past age, millions of residents get their drinking water from the tanks every day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside City’s Water Tanks, Layers of Neglect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside City’s Water Tanks, Layers of Neglect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Ray', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Mental Hygiene Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T05:41:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Rivera, Frank G. Runyeon and Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rivera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Runyeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News'