 so-called sharing economy: Who is responsible when things go wrong?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/uber-and-a-childs-death/', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit set to be filed on Monday seeks to unravel the biggest question of the so-called sharing economy: Who is responsible when things go wrong?', 'lead_paragraph': ' Travis Kalanick, chief executive of the on-demand transportation service Uber, originally used “The Fountainhead” as his Twitter icon. It was viewed by many as a proclamation: Ayn Rand’s novel is beloved by Silicon Valley’s regulation-is-useless crowd, and Uber is in too much of a hurry to want anyone slowing it down with questions about safety and responsibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/technology/27bits-ubersuit/27bits-ubersuit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/27/technology/27bits-ubersuit/27bits-ubersuit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/technology/27bits-ubersuit/27bits-ubersuit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/technology/27bits-ubersuit/27bits-ubersuit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/technology/27bits-ubersuit/27bits-ubersuit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/27/technology/27bits-ubersuit/27bits-ubersuit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/technology/27bits-ubersuit/27bits-ubersuit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Uber and a Child’s Death', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driver Distraction and Fatigue', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kalanick, Travis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, Sofia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muzaffar, Syed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T12:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e995eda5-269c-51a8-91be-8c7655c02366', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e995eda5-269c-51a8-91be-8c7655c02366'}, {'abstract': 'For 27 years, my main worry has been whether we will find new customers. At the beginning of 2013 I realized that selling was no longer my biggest problem — that I needed to turn my attention to making sure the shop floor could keep up with the sales team.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/how-we-increased-productivity-on-the-shop-floor/', 'snippet': 'For 27 years, my main worry has been whether we will find new customers. At the beginning of 2013 I realized that selling was no longer my biggest problem — that I needed to turn my attention to making sure the shop floor could keep up with the sa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the beginning of last year, I started using a new technique to analyze my numbers: the trailing sum or average. In a nutshell, you track a set of numbers looking back from the present, at regular intervals, and see how the results change over time. Doing so shows patterns that can be hard to see if you are used to looking at calendar years — it’s as if every month represents the end of the year. It also smooths out variations in shorter time periods. Over all, I find it a useful way to track progress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How We Increased Productivity on the Shop Floor', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downs, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T12:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be7015f2-bf82-5dde-9374-76469e39ff93', 'word_count': 1515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be7015f2-bf82-5dde-9374-76469e39ff93'}, {'abstract': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 3 p.m. Eastern time.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/whats-going-on-in-this-picture-jan-27-2014/', 'snippet': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 3 p.m. Eastern time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: Jan. 28, 2014', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/learning/VTS01-27-14LN/VTS01-27-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/learning/VTS01-27-14LN/VTS01-27-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/learning/VTS01-27-14LN/VTS01-27-14LN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/learning/VTS01-27-14LN/VTS01-27-14LN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/learning/VTS01-27-14LN/VTS01-27-14LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_n