 season long, awards show hosts, tasked with being flip about this year’s cinematic hopefuls, have faced the major comedic stumbling block of “12 Years a Slave.” How to make light of one of the most grotesque periods of humanity? Amy Poehler, at the Golden Globes, quipped that after seeing the movie, she “would never look at slavery the same way again.” (Tina Fey: “Wait, how were you looking at it?”) At the Directors Guild awards on Saturday, the M.C., Jane Lynch, handled it this way: “12 Years a Slave,” she said, is “the story of an educated black man trying to prove his real identity to those that wanted to bring him down — or as Barack Obama calls it, ‘Tuesday.’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/janelynch/janelynch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/janelynch/janelynch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/janelynch/janelynch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/janelynch/janelynch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/janelynch/janelynch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/27/arts/janelynch/janelynch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cred