tealth ‘Saturday Night Live’ Oscar Campaign', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cera, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Jonah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T17:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb0da176-2c85-5393-8ee0-7da37ba69e43', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb0da176-2c85-5393-8ee0-7da37ba69e43'}, {'abstract': 'Marc Minkowski is to lead the annual celebration of Mozart’s music, presented by the Salzburg Mozarteum Foundation, through 2017.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/artistic-director-extends-contract-for-mozart-week-in-salzburg/', 'snippet': 'Marc Minkowski is to lead the annual celebration of Mozart’s music, presented by the Salzburg Mozarteum Foundation, through 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French conductor Marc Minkowski has renewed his term as artistic director of Mozart Week, the annual celebration of Mozart’s music presented by the Salzburg Mozarteum Foundation, the foundation announced on Monday. The festival typically runs during the week that includes Mozart’s birthday (Jan. 27) in Salzburg, the Austrian city where he was born. Mr. Minkowski’s term will run through the 2017 festival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artistic Director Extends Contract for Mozart Week in Salzburg', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salzburg (Austria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T17:28:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ae5f936-854c-58ef-a621-2910c0c2c319', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ae5f936-854c-58ef-a621-2910c0c2c319'}, {'abstract': 'As personal data pour onto mobile networks, American and British eavesdroppers are prying into so-called leaky apps to extract geographical data, address books and phone logs, secret documents show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/world/spy-agencies-scour-phone-apps-for-personal-data.html', 'snippet': 'As personal data pour onto mobile networks, American and British eavesdroppers are prying into so-called leaky apps to extract geographical data, address books and phone logs, secret documents show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a smartphone user opens Angry Birds, the popular game application, and starts slinging birds at chortling green pigs, spies could be lurking in the background to snatch data revealing the player’s location, age, sex and other personal information, according to secret British intelligence documents.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spy Agencies Tap Data Streaming From Phone Apps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spy Agencies Tap Data Streaming From Phone Apps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glanz, James', 'rank': 1, '