chnology/25bits-snapchat/25bits-snapchat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/25/technology/25bits-snapchat/25bits-snapchat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Use Snapchat: It’s Fast, Ugly and Ephemeral', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snapchat Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T18:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c31fede0-1fb0-53e9-a5ab-b3a2ba658b04', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c31fede0-1fb0-53e9-a5ab-b3a2ba658b04'}, {'abstract': 'The writer of this week’s cover story explains how she navigates the innerworkings of Hillary Clinton’s political circle.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/behind-the-cover-story-amy-chozick-on-her-adventures-in-hillaryland/', 'snippet': 'The writer of this week’s cover story explains how she navigates the innerworkings of Hillary Clinton’s political circle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amy Chozick, a political reporter for The Times, wrote this week’s cover story about the people who are readying themselves for\xa0Hillary Clinton‘s possible run for the presidency in 2016.Since July, your full-time beat at The Times has been the Clintons. How did you choose this aspect of Hillary Clinton’s political future for lengthier treatment?When I moved onto this beat, friends and colleagues said, “You’re going to cover one person for the next four years?!” But with Hillary Clinton, it’s never just one person (or even three people, with President Clinton and Chelsea). I found out that there is a huge cast of characters the Clintons have collected over the years. Their perspective and place in this world is an essential part of who Hillary is and what her future might look like. A person who went to Georgetown with Bill Clinton told me lots of his classmates were thinking about running for president, but only Clinton was building his cabinet. They’re unique in American politics in that they’ve collected so many people over the years — from Arkansas to the White House and to whatever she does in the future. I wanted to explore that dynamic, and the benefits of having such an enormous brain trust, but also the downside to having so many voices who all have a stake in 2016.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/27/magazine/27-amy-chozick/27-amy-chozick-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/06/27/magazine/27-amy-chozick/27-amy-chozick-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/27/magazine/27-amy-chozick/27-amy-chozick-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/27/magazine/27-amy-chozick/27-amy-chozick-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/27/magazine/27-amy-chozick/27-amy-chozick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/06/27/magazine/27-amy-chozick/27-amy-chozick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/06/27/magazine/27-amy-chozick/27-amy-chozick-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Amy Chozick on Her Adventures in Hillaryland', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chozick, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T18:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26a8e996-51d0-5ea9-8351-a11259114546', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26a8e996-51d0-5ea9-8351-a11259114546'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Henny Garfunkel worked with actors and directors at t