ri': 'nyt://article/229ea272-d776-5ef5-b5fe-b4d1d5bec546'}, {'abstract': 'A variety of reports indicate that the job interview process is lengthier than it was four years ago, even as jobs remain vacant longer.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/the-endless-interview-process/', 'snippet': 'A variety of reports indicate that the job interview process is lengthier than it was four years ago, even as jobs remain vacant longer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my “It’s the Economy”\xa0on Sunday, I mentioned that the job application process has dragged on and on for many Americans. This is a subject I wrote about\xa0last year. I’ve heard anecdotes about very long hoop-jumping processes, and so I asked Glassdoor, a site that collects user-submitted information on hiring at different companies, to check for any discernible trends in the duration of the job application gantlet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Endless Interview Process', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T19:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffe81c9c-a0e9-5cd7-8503-eff392418338', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffe81c9c-a0e9-5cd7-8503-eff392418338'}, {'abstract': 'Randolph L. Braham, a Holocaust survivor and professor, said the government’s effort to whitewash the country’s role in the death of Jews had shocked him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/world/europe/holocaust-scholar-returns-top-award-to-hungary-in-protest.html', 'snippet': 'Randolph L. Braham, a Holocaust survivor and professor, said the government’s effort to whitewash the country’s role in the death of Jews had shocked him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — A prominent Hungarian-American Holocaust scholar, Randolph L. Braham, said on Sunday he is returning a high state award to Hungary to protest what he called the government’s efforts to whitewash the country’s collusion in the murder of hundreds of thousands of Jews during the Second World War.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holocaust Scholar Returns Top Award to Hungary in Protest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braham, Randolph L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horthy, Miklos (1868-1957)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T19:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a97c2af7-0941-54ba-a285-7078310bcc31', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a97c2af7-0941-54ba-a285-7078310bcc31'}, {'abstract': 'Google has acquir