rdles/', 'snippet': 'A document released by the Syrian government made no mention of the words “transition” or “reform” and appeared to suggest that the country was already a rule-of-law democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — As we reported, a tenuous peace conference in Geneva between the Syrian opposition and the government has yet to produce concrete results, and on Monday, the third day of face-to-face talks, a communiqué released by President Bashar al-Assad’s government showed just how far apart they are from any agreement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Assad Government Communiqué, a Clue to Syria Peace Talks’ Hurdles', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brahimi, Lakhdar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaaban, Bouthaina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Geneva (Switzerland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T19:28:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard and Hala Droubi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hala', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Droubi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bab2a5a-04c4-5531-ad35-a850e8b16213', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bab2a5a-04c4-5531-ad35-a850e8b16213'}, {'abstract': 'One of the most prominent players in the Bitcoin universe, Charles Shrem, was arrested on Sunday, accused of conspiring to facili