m/2014/01/27/on-view-at-an-exhibition-from-the-master-of-el-bulli-food-becomes-art/', 'snippet': '“Ferran Adrià: Notes on Creativity” at the Drawing Center uses drawings, paintings, documents and films to delve into the renowned Catalan chef’s intensely visual worldview.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ferran Adrià made food into art at El Bulli, his renowned, now-shuttered restaurant near the town of Roses on the Catalan coast of Spain. Now, “Ferran Adrià: Notes on Creativity” at the Drawing Center in New York offers a peek behind the curtain of the world’s most celebrated culinary laboratory, and a glimpse at what Adrià is cooking up next.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At an Exhibition From the Master of El Bulli, Food Becomes Art', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADRIA, FERRAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Bulli (Catalonia, Spain, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T21:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9cde6a9-cf78-505d-a3ea-3fd031c48972', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9cde6a9-cf78-505d-a3ea-3fd031c48972'}, {'abstract': 'The huge numbers killed in what some call a “Holocaust by bullets” have garnered greater attention as historians sift through records that became available after the fall of the Soviet Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/world/europe/a-light-on-a-vast-toll-of-jews-killed-away-from-the-death-camps.html', 'snippet': 'The huge numbers killed in what some call a “Holocaust by bullets” have garnered greater attention as historians sift through records that became available after the fall of the Soviet Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSWIECIM, Poland — As one gazes out from the main watchtower at the grim desert that is the crumbling chimneys and crematories, vanished prisoners’ huts, barbed wire and ditches of Auschwitz-Birkenau, it is hard to fathom that there were corners of the Nazi realm where, collectively, more killing occurred than at Auschwitz.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/AUSCHWITZ/AUSCHWITZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/world/AUSCHWITZ/AUSCHWITZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/AUSCHWITZ/AUSCHWITZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/AUSCHWITZ/AUSCHWITZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/AUSCHWITZ/AUSCHWITZ-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/28/world/AUSCHWITZ/AUSCHWITZ-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0