ing musical will play down Asian stereotypes that caused concern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leaders of the Dalton School, one of Manhattan’s top private schools, this month canceled a student production of the musical “Thoroughly Modern Millie” over concerns about the show’s use of Asian stereotypes and a subplot involving a white slavery ring in China, planning to replace it with a revue of the show’s songs instead. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Complaints, ‘Millie’ Gets Thoroughly Modern Makeover for Dalton School', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Millie’ Gets Thoroughly Modern Makeover for Dalton', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scanlan, Dick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tesori, Jeanine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dalton School', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T21:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab1dde09-26da-527b-9bb2-8a2b915e4ffb', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab1dde09-26da-527b-9bb2-8a2b915e4ffb'}, {'abstract': 'A grand jury indicted Randall Kerrick, a white officer, on voluntary manslaughter charges for firing 10 shots into a young black man who had driven off the road and was apparently looking for help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/us/charlotte-police-officer-indicted-in-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'A grand jury indicted Randall Kerrick, a white officer, on voluntary manslaughter charges for firing 10 shots into a young black man who had driven off the road and was apparently looking for help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — Three times since a police officer fired 10 bullets into her son Jonathan last September, Georgia Ferrell has made the long journey from the family home in Tallahassee, Fla. Each time, she sought to understand why her son, a former Florida A&M football star and a homebody who wanted to take his mother with him to the junior prom, was gunned down when he was just asking for help.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/us/28CHARLOTTE/28CHARLOTTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/us/28CHARLOTTE/28CHARLOTTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/us/28CHARLOTTE/28CHARLOTTE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/us/28CHARLOTTE/28CHARLOTTE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Grand Jury Indicts Officer in Shooting Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Second Grand Jury Indicts Officer in Shooting Death', 'name': No