omeone whose economic status is about the same as theirs, and that has contributed to growing income inequality in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can tax the rich, you can educate the poor, but there is another way to reduce the nation’s growing income inequality: Marry your scullery maid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Income Inequality in the U.S. Means Princes Don’t Go After Cinderellas', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T22:25:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72de6765-9416-5dac-b795-3a53ed98dc64', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72de6765-9416-5dac-b795-3a53ed98dc64'}, {'abstract': 'The David H. Koch Theater was transformed by an installation by the artist JR in its foyer, and the troupe introduced a new program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballet-erring-on-side-of-variety.html', 'snippet': 'The David H. Koch Theater was transformed by an installation by the artist JR in its foyer, and the troupe introduced a new program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The installation by the artist JR at the David H. Koch Theater has transformed that building’s greatest glory, its tall, spacious first-floor foyer. Unlike the 2013 cartoon tower by the Brooklyn art collective Faile, it doesn’t spoil or invade the space; it both deepens and teases it. Go up to the fourth ring, and, from above, it looks like a Baroque ceiling. Virtually life-size images of New York City Ballet dancers are arrayed in rings, whorls and patterns around the floor in various trompe l’oeil effects.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flitting Through Fleeting Encounters', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flitting Through Fleeting Encounters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T22:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0007e2f0-0c50-5f5d-bc08-b07963d6768d', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0007e2f0-0c50-5f5d-bc08-b07963d6768d'}, {'abstract': 'The Minnesota Orchestra, which just ended a bitter 15-month lockout and plans to get back to business next month, won the Grammy Award for best orchestral performance.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/minnesota-orchestra-rebuilding-after-lockout-celebrates-a-grammy-win/', 'snippet': 'The Minnesota Orchestra, which just ended a bitter 15-month lockout and plans to get back to business next month, won the Grammy Award for best orchestral performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Minnesota Orchestra, which just ended a bitter 16-month lockout and plans to get back to business next month, won the Grammy Award for “best orchestral performance” on 