': 'Beyond Early Childhood Education', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond Early Childhood Education', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T22:52:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e7f0a77-5dc6-5d72-902f-275c1e70c75d', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e7f0a77-5dc6-5d72-902f-275c1e70c75d'}, {'abstract': 'At Alice Tully Hall, the Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center presented a program of early-19th-century pieces that experiment with instrumentation and style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/arts/music/chamber-music-society-presents-classical-flowering.html', 'snippet': 'At Alice Tully Hall, the Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center presented a program of early-19th-century pieces that experiment with instrumentation and style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the program notes for the Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center’s concert on Sunday afternoon at Alice Tully Hall, the Adagio of Spohr’s Grand Nonetto in F is described as “beautiful and attractive without stirring any deep emotions.” That observation could easily have been applied to all the genial works in this lineup of cocktail party pleasantries. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/28CHAMBER/28CHAMBER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/28CHAMBER/28CHAM