zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/87a06006-9e53-56ad-8482-093445d33d90', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87a06006-9e53-56ad-8482-093445d33d90'}, {'abstract': 'As polar bears spend more time on land in a warming climate, they are adapting their diets, eating more snow-goose eggs and caribou instead of ringed seal pups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/science/polar-bears-turn-to-snow-goose-egg-diet.html', 'snippet': 'As polar bears spend more time on land in a warming climate, they are adapting their diets, eating more snow-goose eggs and caribou instead of ringed seal pups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a warming climate causes sea ice in the Arctic to melt earlier each year, polar bears are spending more time on land — and changing their diets accordingly. A new study shows that the bears, whose traditional prey is ringed seal pups, are now eating more snow-goose eggs and caribou.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28OBOX2/28OBOX2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28OBOX2/28OBOX2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28OBOX2/28OBOX2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28OBOX2/28OBOX2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 