isorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T22:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/9679d4d0-cf4b-5654-bd99-03e8210f8f9e', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9679d4d0-cf4b-5654-bd99-03e8210f8f9e'}, {'abstract': 'Wayne Pacelle, president of the Humane Society of the United States, condemns the sale of hunting rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/opinion/a-high-priced-rhino-hunt.html', 'snippet': 'Wayne Pacelle, president of the Humane Society of the United States, condemns the sale of hunting rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A High-Priced Rhino Hunt', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A High-Priced Rhino Hunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rhinoceroses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Namibia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conniff, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T22:55:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8587deb9-8bf0-55a0-845d-9bfd0feb01bb', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8587deb9-8bf0-55a0-845d-9bfd0feb01bb'}, {'abstract': 'Those flying on JetBlue during the Super Bowl on Sunday will be able to watch the game with a Buffalo-wings-flavored snack and an inexpensive drink.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/up-in-the-air-on-sunday-jetblue-has-a-super-bowl-plan/', 'snippet': 'Those flying on JetBlue during the Super Bowl on Sunday will be able to watch the game with a Buffalo-wings-flavored snack and an inexpensive drink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any true football fan wouldn’t be caught anywhere near an airport on Super Bowl Sunday, but just in case, JetBlue Airways is at the ready, with in-flight viewing options to watch the game, cheap beer and a snack that tastes like wings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Up in the Air on Sunday? JetBlue Has a Super Bowl Plan', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JetBlue Airways Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T23:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e039d68-37e9-552c-b68d-6693f0acaae2', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e039d68-37e9-552c-b68d-6693f0acaae2'}, {'abstract': 'A team of bee investigators say the dying species may be passing around a virus, while two government agencies say 2013 was among the hottest ever recorded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/science/new-lead-in-honeybee-deaths-and-another-hot-year-on-earth.html', 'snippet': 'A team of bee investigators say the dying species may be passing around a virus, while two government agencies say 2013 was among the hottest ever recorded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a satisfying twist, meteorologists called out the public last week for being inaccurate. Weeks after introducing us to “polar vortex” — the term for a weather pattern that typically swirls above northern Canada or Siberia and sometimes sends cold air south — the nation’s forecasters grew tired of hearing it. The Weather Channel meteorologists Chris Dolce and Nick Wiltgen complained on their Weather Underground blog that the word had become a catchphrase, mistakenly used to refer to the cold air itself, and not the vortex, which “never really moves through the atmosphere above the United States.” So please, everybody. Chill.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28WEEK_SPAN/Week-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28WEEK_SPAN/Week-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28WEEK_SPAN/Week-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28WEEK_SPAN/Week-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28WEEK_SPAN/Week-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014