9cf-568a-b730-28274aeda1b4', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/172a5072-d9cf-568a-b730-28274aeda1b4'}, {'abstract': 'Marathon Asset Management has gained a reputation for finding opportunities by picking over what is left in the aftermath of financial disaster. It’s starting a new fund dedicated to distressed debt in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/distressed-debt-hedge-fund-commits-530-million-to-europe/', 'snippet': 'Marathon Asset Management has gained a reputation for finding opportunities by picking over what is left in the aftermath of financial disaster. It’s starting a new fund dedicated to distressed debt in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marathon Asset Management has gained a reputation for being a rag-and-bone picker, finding opportunities in the aftermath of financial disaster. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Distressed Debt Hedge Fund Commits $530 Million to Europe', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marathon Asset Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-27T23:28:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5e8a03c-c07f-58ed-acc5-aba1659ef98c', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5e8a03c-c07f-58ed-acc5-aba1659ef98c'}, {'abstract': 'History tells us that the Plague of Justinian and the Black Death each took a large fraction of the earth’s population. Science tells us that the plague is still out there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/science/no-longer-leading-killer-plague-still-raises-fears.html', 'snippet': 'History tells us that the Plague of Justinian and the Black Death each took a large fraction of the earth’s population. Science tells us that the plague is still out there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bubonic plague, caused by the rodent-borne bacterium Yersinia pestis, has killed a large fraction of the earth’s population at least twice — most famously in the medieval Black Death, but before that in the Plague of Justinian, which began in A.D. 541. That pandemic, named for the Byzantine emperor, may have killed half of Europe and Asia; it hastened the collapse of the Roman Empire’s remnants and ushered in the Dark Ages.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28GLOB/28GLOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28GLOB/28GLOB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28GLOB/28GLOB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28GLOB/28GLOB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/science/28GLOB/28GLOB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'i