-fall-on-the-resale-market-brokers-say.html', 'snippet': 'The asking price of Super Bowl tickets being resold has fallen nearly 25 percent since the game’s participants became known, according to a market tracker, though a surge is expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is filled with firsts and superlatives, and this year’s Super Bowl is providing more. The first outdoor Super Bowl in a cold climate. The first mass transit Super Bowl. A fanfest staged in the heart of Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ticket Prices Fall on the Resale Market, Brokers Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ticket Prices Fall on the Resale Market, Brokers Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ticket Scalping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T01:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c49376-8a05-5990-b9e7-1471c243a4bc', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c49376-8a05-5990-b9e7-1471c243a4bc'}, {'abstract': 'Membership has its perks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/opinion/nocera-from-your-friends-at-the-nra.html', 'snippet': 'Membership has its perks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following are verbatim excerpts from emails sent by the National Rifle Association. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 975, 'width': 850, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/opinion/Nocera_New/Nocera_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Your Friends at the N.R.A.', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Your Friends at the N.R.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Second Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T01:59:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a94e1c9-274c-5084-97e3-f5dd906812d4', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a94e1c9-274c-5084-97e3-f5dd906812d4'}, {'abstract': 'Any word can be translated. But there is no way of dealing with the larger problem: untranslatable worlds.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/27/william-weaver-and-translation-as-a-performing-art/', 'snippet': 'Any word can be translated. But there is no way of dealing with the larger problem: untranslatable worlds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty years ago I moved to Milan to work for an Italian art magazine called FMR. It was an odd and ambitious enterprise: FMR started publishing in the United States a year later with the slogan “the most beautiful magazine in the world.” The offices hardly seemed like offices at all: they were located in Palazzo Visconti di Modrone, an exceptionally fine piece of Milanese rococo architecture. The building was Luchino Visconti’s childhood home, and it was a gorgeous and dramatic workplace. When it was time for coffee, we ordered in rounds of espressos, which were brought by a white-coated young man carrying a silver trayful of demitasse thermoses. Every few months, one of the magazine’s production managers would take orders for prosciutto from his hometown, Parma — the whole ham, what they thin-slice in an Italian gastronomia. Price: about $20. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Translation as a Performing Art', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation and Interpreters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weaver, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '20