, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7d7d06f-0fec-5be8-82a9-bb8c55c6824d'}, {'abstract': 'Experts are skeptical that any federal initiative can combat the upheaval of lost coal jobs or the economic woes caused by remoteness, poor infrastructure and undereducated workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/business/job-aid-zones-face-a-new-test-in-coal-country.html', 'snippet': 'Experts are skeptical that any federal initiative can combat the upheaval of lost coal jobs or the economic woes caused by remoteness, poor infrastructure and undereducated workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HAZARD, Ky. — Joseph Nantz still looks back fondly at his job as a heavy machinery operator at the mountaintop coal mine here, helping to blast and cart away layers of rock to reveal seams of coal and then restore the rubble for a handsome $24 an hour.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/business/Zones1/Zones1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/business/Zones1/Zones1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/business/Zones1/Zones1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/business/Zones1/Zones1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/business/Zones1/Zones1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard',