 World Economic Forum, there was a remarkable economic and political risk that appeared to have been largely overlooked: The long-simmering battle between China and Japan may be close to boiling over. One top executive went so far as to describe the nations’ relationship as a “stealth war.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anxiety Rising Over Relations Between Japan and China', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anxiety Rises Over Japan and China’s Relations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T02:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6515c3f5-a37a-5b1a-9a28-a69dd97c5dc7', 'word_count': 1101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6515c3f5-a37a-5b1a-9a28-a69dd97c5dc7'}, {'abstract': 'Against long odds, Mayor Bill de Blasio made a strong case in Albany for his prekindergarten plan and his tax on wealthy residents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/opinion/the-mayor-pushes-back-for-pre-k.html', 'snippet': 'Against long odds, Mayor Bill de Blasio made a strong case in Albany for his prekindergarten plan and his tax on wealthy residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio went to Albany on Monday to answer the naysayers and skeptics — chief among them, Gov. Andrew Cuomo — who want him to abandon his prekindergarten plan and his tax on wealthy residents. Mr. de Blasio was there to make an ambitious case: to extend free, full-day, “high-quality” pre-K across the city in two years, eventually to reach more than 73,000 4-year-olds. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mayor Pushes Back, for Pre-K', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mayor Pushes Back, for Pre-K', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T02:18:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/90c3d069-9506-5292-b767-302adba7820f', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90c3d069-9506-5292-b767-302adba7820f'}, {'abstract': 'The concern is that the schedule of deadlines to destroy the weapons stockpile is falling dangerously behind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/world/middleeast/second-cargo-of-chemical-agents-leaves-syria-as-pace-is-criticized.html', 'snippet': 'The concern is that the schedule of deadlines to destroy the weapons stockpile is falling dangerously behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second cargo of Syria’s most toxic chemical weapons was exported by ship on Monday for eventual destruction at sea, officials overseeing the effort reported. But the slow pace of removal, which is way behind schedule and has missed one deadline already, is causing increased concern and threatening to violate another deadline in less than two weeks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/CHEMICALS/CHEMICALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/world/CHEMICALS/CHEMICALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/CHEMICALS/CHEMICALS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/CHEMICALS/CHEMICALS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1996, 'width': 1437, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/CHEMICALS/CHEMICALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/28/world/CHEMICALS/CHEMICALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/world/CHEMICALS/CHEMICALS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Cargo of Chemical Agents Leaves Syria as Pace Is Criticized', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Second Cargo of Chemical Agents Leaves Syria as Pace Is Criticized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freight (Cargo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T02:19:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone and Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bf613e1-ca75-5497-9a56-b790010726b1', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bf613e1-ca75-5497-9a56-b790010726b1'}, {'abstract': 'The chairman of Japan’s public broadcaster apologized Monday after drawing criticism for saying that his nation should not be singled out for forcing women into sexual servitude during World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/world/asia/japan-broadcast-chief-apologizes-for-comment-on-comfort-women.html', 'snippet': 'The chairman of Japan’s public broadcaster apologized Monday after drawing criticism for saying that his nation should not be singled out for forcing women into sexual servitude during World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The new chairman of Japan’s public broadcaster apologized Monday after drawing sharp criticism for saying that his nation should not be singled out for forcing women into sexual servitude during World War II. Katsuto Momii, the newly appointed chairman of the public broadcaster, NHK, also was criticized for saying that the broadcaster would refrain from criticizing the government on such delicate issues as visits to a controversial shrine honoring war dead. On Monday, Mr. Momii said his comments on Sunday about the so-called comfort women forced to work in wartime military brothels were “personal opinions that were not appropriate to say.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan: Broadcast Chief Apologizes for Comment on ‘Comfort Women’', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: Broadcast Chief Apologizes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NHK (Japan Broadcasting Corp)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Momii, Katsuto', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T02:27:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/da6da631-819c-565b-99cb-491fc6ac508e', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da6da631-819c-565b-99cb-491fc6ac508e'}, {'abstract': 'Congress has approved the delivery of six Apache attack helicopters to the Iraqi military, Pentagon and congressional officials said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/world/middleeast/iraq-united-states-to-deliver-helicopters.html', 'snippet': 'Congress has approved the delivery of six Apache attack helicopters to the Iraqi military, Pentagon and congressional officials said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Congress has approved the delivery of six Apache attack helicopters to the Iraqi military, Pentagon and congressional officials said Monday. The leased Apaches will not arrive in Iraq until this summer after they have been equipped and Iraqi pilots have been trained. The transfer had been held up for months until members of Congress were assured that the helicopters would be used for national security purposes, and not for Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki to employ against his political enemies. Iraqi troops have been locked in a standoff with militants in the western province of Anbar in recent weeks, and insurgents in other parts of the country have been carrying out a campaign of attacks for months. The United States has also agreed to sell Iraq 24 new Apaches, but that delivery is still three years away. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: United States to Deliver Helicopters', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: U.S. to Deliver Helicopters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ira