 Knights Templar, the organized crime gang that has spread such terror in the western state of Michoacán that citizens have formed vigilante groups to fight it. Dionisio Loya Plancarte, who is believed to handle the gang’s public relations, was found hiding in a closet in Michoacán and arrested. He faces charges related to organized crime and drug trafficking, the Interior Ministry said. President Enrique Peña Nieto sent troops and more police officers into Michoacán two weeks ago, but the self-defense groups refused to lay down their arms. On Monday, they agreed to work under military command, but they will not disband. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Gang Leader Is Arrested', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Gang Leader Is Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knights Templar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michoacan (Mexico)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plancarte, Dionisio Loya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T02:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1df88f71-e393-5d65-a0df-60da19e8c32d', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1df88f71-e393-5d65-a0df-60da19e8c32d'}, {'abstract': 'Broncos receiver Wes Welke