ue': 'Auction Systems Auctioneers and Appraisers Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T12:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Weidenhamer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weidenhamer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebff8773-d55d-5168-88a7-18ca323fbc34', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebff8773-d55d-5168-88a7-18ca323fbc34'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration will allow Internet companies to talk more specifically about when they are forced to turn over customer data to government agents, the Justice Department said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/daily-report-u-s-eases-some-rules-on-data-disclosure/', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration will allow Internet companies to talk more specifically about when they are forced to turn over customer data to government agents, the Justice Department said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration says it will allow Internet companies to give customers a better idea of how often the government demands their information, but will not allow companies to disclose what is being collected or how much, Matt Apuzzo and Nicole Perlroth report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype