on': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da0232dc-cd5a-5a10-9a62-861f3492624f', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da0232dc-cd5a-5a10-9a62-861f3492624f'}, {'abstract': 'Always double-check the spelling of names, our most common source of errors. And let’s triple-check names with multiple popular versions — like “Katherine,” “Katharine,” Catherine,” “Cathryn” and “Kathryn.”', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/can-you-spell-that-please/', 'snippet': 'Always double-check the spelling of names, our most common source of errors. And let’s triple-check names with multiple popular versions — like “Katherine,” “Katharine,” Catherine,” “Cathryn” and “Kathryn.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Publishing tens of thousands of words a day, on tight deadlines, we know we can’t avoid all errors. But it’s frustrating to run correction after correction for certain mistakes that are predictable and therefore eminently avoidable. In my last post, I talked about millions and billions. This week, consider Katherine and Katharine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can You Spell That, Please?', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T13:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By PHILIP B. CORBETT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2504fb49-2510-573f-ab5a-0c2a73609722', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2504fb49-2510-573f-ab5a-0c2a73609722'}, {'abstract': 'The actress performs a scene from her solo show based on notes passed between two 11-year-old girls.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/in-performance-okwui-okpokwasili-of-bronx-gothic/', 'snippet': 'The actress performs a scene from her solo show based on notes passed between two 11-year-old girls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s video features Okwui Okpokwasili in a scene from “Bronx Gothic,” her solo show which grew out of a series of notes passed between two 11-year-old girls. Directed by Peter Born, the piece, which Ms. Okpokwasili wrote and stars in, continues through Feb. 1 at Danspace Project at St. Mark’s Church.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Okwui Okpokwasili of ‘Bronx Gothic’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okpokwasili, Okwui', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T13:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8d29d38-7033-5010-820d-4e261df2e495', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8d29d38-7033-5010-820d-4e261df2e495'}, {'abstract': 'Teatro Real’s production of Wagner’s “Tristan und Isolde” by Peter Sellars features video by Bill Viola.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/arts/music/operas-filled-with-forbidden-love-in-madrid.html', 'snippet': 'Teatro Real’s production of Wagner’s “Tristan und Isolde” by Peter Sellars features video by Bill Viola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Wagner’s “Tristan und Isolde,” a tale of forbidden, ill-fated love, was presented at the Teatro Real this week when one of the major events of the international opera season was also taking place at the theater: the Tuesday premiere of the composer Charles Wuorinen’s “Brokeback Mountain,” an adaptation of the acclaimed short story by Annie Proulx, who wrote the libretto. The “Tristan,” in a production by Peter Sellars, with video by Bill Viola, is a powerful staging that is new to Madrid. On Monday, the house was packed for the fifth performance of the run, attended by Queen Sofía of Spain, who waved to onlookers from the royal box, though among the applause there were scattered boos that could have been motivated by any number of political and economic issues.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/tristan_Cap/tristan_Cap-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/tristan_Cap/tristan_Cap-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/tristan_Cap/tristan_Cap-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 828, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/tristan_Cap/tristan_Cap-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1655, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/tristan_Cap/tristan_Cap-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/28/arts/tristan_Cap/tristan_Cap-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't