s of a film’s front-runner status is its ability to be parodied. So it’s got to be good news for Spike Jonze and the team behind “Her” that the film has attracted plenty of knock-offs, from “Saturday Night Live’s” version with Jonah Hill, “Me,” to the countless takes on YouTube, like “Troubleshooting her,” which imagines a software upgrade that helps fix the problems that develop when you fall for your computer. (“Would you like Element Software to send you a new OS1 that is not looking for anything serious right now? Reassure you that your ex-OS1 didn’t deserve you, and that you’ll meet someone new, besides he or she was, like, crazy anyway”?)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/jonze/jonze-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/jonze/jonze-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 808}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/jonze/jonze-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/jonze/jonze-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1521, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/jonze/jonze-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/jonze/jonze-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/16/arts/jonze/jonze