le/13f0a5f6-5aa8-5c84-a370-4f96516a3b25', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13f0a5f6-5aa8-5c84-a370-4f96516a3b25'}, {'abstract': 'Though an affiliate of Al Qaeda has taken control of much of Falluja, Iraq, in recent weeks, a Marine officer refuses to believe that her service in the country was for nothing.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/reflections-on-falluja-and-the-impermanence-of-victory/', 'snippet': 'Though an affiliate of Al Qaeda has taken control of much of Falluja, Iraq, in recent weeks, a Marine officer refuses to believe that her service in the country was for nothing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before there was a battle for Falluja, we threw darts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reflections on Falluja and the Impermanence of Victory', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Darts (Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Falluja (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T18:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Fazio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fazio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6785fc6-bf03-5c38-bdac-f8faa9af6605', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6785fc6-bf03-5c38-bdac-f8faa9af6605'}, {'abstract': 'No more Kool-Aid.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/kocherlakota-and-the-cultists/', 'snippet': 'No more Kool-Aid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Narayana Kocherlakota, president of the Minneapolis Fed, is the prodigal son of monetary stimulus. He was the Fed’s leading hawk a few years ago, reflecting in part the ultra-freshwater macro doctrines of the Minnesota econ department and his bank’s closely associated research department. But he did something amazing: he looked at evidence, listened to his critics, and changed his views — becoming the Fed’s leading dove.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kocherlakota and the Cultists', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T18:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd522e7-f73b-53e4-91f1-db588c9dec35', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd522e7-f73b-53e4-91f1-db588c9dec35'}, {'abstract': 'Ratko Mladic, a Bosnian Serb former general, was reunited with his old political boss, Radovan Karadzic, in court in The Hague. Both are accused of war crimes, including helping to engineer the 1995 massacre at Srebrenica.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/serbian-ex-fugitives-mladic-and-karadzic-reunite-in-court/', 'snippet': 'Ratko Mladic, a Bosnian Serb former general, was reunited with his old political boss, Radovan Karadzic, in court in The Hague. Both are accused of war crimes, including helping to engineer the 1995 massacre at Srebrenica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — One is a former warrior known as the Butcher of Bosnia who spent more than 15 years on the run in his native Serbia, where he was finally captured.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Serbian Ex-Fugitives Mladic and Karadzic Reunite in Court', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karadzic, Radovan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mladic, Ratko', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Srebrenica (Bosnia and Herzegovina)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T18:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8db97724-2f42-5396-8eff-b20d6f7d5529', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8db97724-2f42-5396-8eff-b20d6f7d5529'}, {'abstract': 'The Marijuana Policy Project, a group that is asking the N.F.L. to change its rules on marijuana, has spent $5,000 to rent billboards near MetLife Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/nyregion/marijuana-advocates-are-bringing-their-message-to-the-super-bowl.html', 'snippet': 'The Marijuana Policy Project, a group that is asking the N.F.L. to change its rules on marijuana, has spent $5,000 to rent billboards near MetLife Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Jersey probably looks a lot like home to the Denver Broncos. The bill