ing Malala Yousafzai, the Pakistani education advocate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/world/asia/pakistani-university-malala-yousafzai.html', 'snippet': 'Officials at Peshawar University said the provincial government of Khyber-Pakhtunkhwa had forced them to cancel a ceremony honoring Malala Yousafzai, the Pakistani education advocate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PESHAWAR, Pakistan — Malala Yousafzai may be a global celebrity, but in her home province, she remains a focus of controversy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani University Cancels Event Promoting Teenager’s Memoir', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: ‘Malala’ Event Canceled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yousafzai, Malala', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peshawar (Pakistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Imran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T19:26:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ismail Khan and Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c5fee3-ec28-5e23-9617-9052496c48ea', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c5fee3-ec28-5e23-9617-9052496c48ea'}, {'abstract': 'Malinee Chakrabandhu is a champion of elections at a time when many in Thailand’s upper classes are calling for the overthrow of the government and a suspen