 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4ae60871-e83a-53e2-996b-45af6070df17', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4ae60871-e83a-53e2-996b-45af6070df17'}, {'abstract': 'A closer examination of these energy-boosting snacks shows that their blessings are mixed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/dining/protein-bars.html', 'snippet': 'A closer examination of these energy-boosting snacks shows that their blessings are mixed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protein is the hot ingredient of the moment in processed foods, joining the terms organic and low-fat as a major selling point to pitch to health-conscious shoppers. While carbohydrates and many fats are still widely regarded as suspect, protein is being proudly added to products throughout the grocery store, especially the snack aisle, which has made way for a new star: the protein bar. But a closer look shows that its blessings are mixed.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look Inside the Protein Bar', 'kicker': "What's in It? ", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protein Bar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Proteins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T21:51:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22147e4e-984b-52a8-b357-1d92f1b91b35', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22147e4e-984b-52a8-b357-1d92f1b91b35'}, {'abstract': 'The State of the Union address on Tuesday spawned a bipartisan embrace of photo- and video-sharing platforms, and a rush to create tweetable graphics and hashtags to amplify party messages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/us/politics/a-night-no-longer-just-the-presidents-pulpit.html', 'snippet': 'The State of the Union address on Tuesday spawned a bipartisan embrace of photo- and video-sharing platforms, and a rush to create tweetable graphics and hashtags to amplify party messages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Twitter has fast become the conventional-wisdom clearinghouse and real-time echo chamber for major political events, so it was not surprising Tuesday evening when Twitter also became the forum where opinion on President Obama’s State of the Union address seemed to crystallize before he had even finished speaking.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/us/SUB-SOCIAL/SUB-SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/29/us/SUB-SOCIAL/SUB-SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/us/SUB-SOCIAL/SUB-SOCIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/us/SUB-SOCIAL/SUB-SOCIAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1581, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/us/SUB-SOCIAL/SUB-SOCIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'w