he top of President Obama’s agenda in his State of the Union address on Tuesday night. But that doesn’t mean the financial community won’t be listening for certain cues. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street Listens for Litigation and Tax Clues in Obama’s Speech', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T22:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d908408e-b3c4-590a-a831-7c58204a5540', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d908408e-b3c4-590a-a831-7c58204a5540'}, {'abstract': 'Frigid temperatures have led to greater outreach efforts and some people who live on the streets and in parks to accept beds, even if temporarily.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/nyregion/severe-cold-moves-new-yorks-homeless-to-seek-help.html', 'snippet': 'Frigid temperatures have led to greater outreach efforts and some people who live on the streets and in parks to accept beds, even if temporarily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Scott managed to survive in the nooks and crannies of Manhattan for two winters, burrowing under piles of blankets and cardboard on West 31st Street if he could not find a spot at Pennsylvania Station, the Port Authority Bus Term