: 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc21e71f-7d07-597c-aad3-270793cb6c14', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc21e71f-7d07-597c-aad3-270793cb6c14'}, {'abstract': 'The actress explains how physicality, not historical research, was essential to her turn in “12 Years a Slave.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/video-alfre-woodards-sole-scene/', 'snippet': 'The actress explains how physicality, not historical research, was essential to her turn in “12 Years a Slave.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Alfre Woodard has just one scene in “12 Years a Slave,” but it is a pivotal one for the film and for the screenwriter, John Ridley. The moment, which was not in the Solomon Northup memoir on which the film is based, involves the slaves Patsey (Lupita Nyong’o) and Solomon (Chiwetel Ejiofor) visiting another plantation for a tea party of sorts held by a slave turned favored lady, Mistress Shaw (played by Ms. Woodard). Mr. Ridley invented the scene, and it was the most difficult thing he wrote, he said, containing one of the few touches of humor in the film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Alfre Woodard’s Sole Scene', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ridley, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodard, Alfre', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Screen Actors Guild', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T22:27:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ba45127-051e-5c8e-9fb2-207006c4e9fa', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ba45127-051e-5c8e-9fb2-207006c4e9fa'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Sturridge scored twice and Luis Suárez got his 23rd goal of the Premier League season as Liverpool ran over Everton, 4-0, in the Merseyside Derby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/sports/soccer/liverpool-thrashes-everton-at-anfield.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Sturridge scored twice and Luis Suárez got his 23rd goal of the Premier League season as Liverpool ran over Everton, 4-0, in the Merseyside Derby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIVERPOOL, England — Everton Manager Roberto Martínez is a genuinely upbeat man, a coach who can seemingly find positives in anything. When his former team, Wigan, was relegated from the Premier League last year, he admitted to disappointment, but noted that the club was on “fantastic financial footing” and had a promising “football philosophy.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/soccer/29liverpool/29liverpool-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/soccer/29liverpool/29liverpool-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/soccer/29liverpool/29liverpool-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0