uare feet at 280 Broadway in Lower Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/agnes-varis-trust-to-give-3-million-to-gibney-dance/', 'snippet': 'The gift is earmarked to fund the restoration of 36,000 square feet at 280 Broadway in Lower Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Agnes Varis Trust will give $3 million to Gibney Dance, the formerly all-women dance troupe that is known for its social activism and is about to expand its operations to 280 Broadway in Lower Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agnes Varis Trust to Give $3 Million to Gibney Dance', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dance New Amsterdam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T22:47:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff6a5067-6a67-5a06-8e92-11dcb2425db5', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff6a5067-6a67-5a06-8e92-11dcb2425db5'}, {'abstract': 'Alibaba’s acquisition of a sleepy technology company set of a flurry of speculation. After Alibaba’s public debut, scrutiny of its deals will only intensify, the Deal Professor writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/answers-to-a-puzzling-deal-at-alibaba-remain-in-the-shadows/', 'snippet': 'Alibaba’s acquisition of a sleepy technology company set of a flurry of speculation. After Alibaba’s public debut, scrutiny of its deals will only intensify, the Deal Professor writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chinese Internet giant Alibaba is looking to join the ranks of Google and Microsoft with an initial public offering that could give it a value of more than $100 billion. But the company’s recent acquisition of the Hong Kong-listed company Citic 21CN shows just how much we still don’t know about Alibaba and its business.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/business/DEALPROF/DEALPROF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/29/business/DEALPROF/DEALPROF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/business/DEALPROF/DEALPROF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/business/DEALPROF/DEALPROF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1162, 'width': 1162, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/business/DEALPROF/DEALPROF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/29/business/DEALPROF/DEALPROF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/business/DEALPROF/DEALPROF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers to a Puzzling Deal at Alibaba Remain in the Shadows', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Answers to a Puzzling Deal at Alibaba Remain in the Shadows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALIBABA.COM', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citic 21CN Co Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hong Kong Stock Exchange', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T22:51:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/268c9115-baf4-575b-920d-5466bfcfd3fc', 'word_count': 1188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/268c9115-baf4-575b-920d-5466bfcfd3fc'}, {'abstract': 'A lawyer for Abdel Malik Ahmed Abdel Wahab al-Rahabi, a Guantánamo inmate for 12 years, sought his return to Yemen, but a military profile said there were risks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/us/military-is-asked-to-return-guantanamo-inmate-to-yemen.html', 'snippet': 'A lawyer for Abdel Malik Ahmed Abdel Wahab al-Rahabi, a Guantánamo inmate for 12 years, sought his return to Yemen, but a military profile said there were risks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A lawyer for a Yemeni man who has been held for 12 years without trial at the prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, asked a parole-style military board on Tuesday to recommend that he be sent home, where he planned to teach and possibly start a “milk and honey farm” or work for his father’s tailoring business, according to a prepared statement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Military Is Asked to Return Guantánamo Inmate to Yemen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rahabi, Malik Ahmed Abdel Wahab al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T22:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26a7adad-1da9-5d26-90fe-ac698086a815', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26a7adad-1da9-5d26-90fe-ac698086a815'}, {'abstract': 'The company sold just 79 percent of its seats in the 2012-13 season, a fall it attributes to higher prices and Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/arts/music/met-opera-reports-falling-attendance.html', 'snippet': 'The company sold just 79 percent of its seats in the 2012-13 season, a fall it attributes to higher prices and Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although the Metropolitan Opera is raising more money from donors and earning more from its “Live in HD” movie theater presentations, it is making less at the box office, selling just 79 percent of its seats in the 2012-13 season, it announced in a financial filing. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/altopera2/altopera2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 296, 'width': 251, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/altopera2/altopera2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 296, 'width': 251, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/altopera2/altopera2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/altopera2/altopera2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/altopera2/altopera2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Opera Reports Falling Attendance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met Opera Reports Falling Attendance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-28T22:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86eb6616-8566-535c-a318-e6f26382657d', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86eb6616-8566-535c-a318-e6f26382657d'}, {'abstract': 'While the National Football League season is about to end, EA Sports is preparing the next version of its Madden NFL video game, adding new movements recorded using stunt players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/arts/video-games/capturing-footballs-snaps-crackles-and-pops-in-madden-nfl.html', 'snippet': 'While the National Football League season is about to end, EA Sports is preparing the next version of its Madden NFL video game, adding new movements recorded using stunt players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BURNABY, British Columbia — The football players strutted down a 40-yard strip of synthetic turf, yelling, jumping and flailing their arms to whip the fans into a frenzy. But there was no stadium and no crowd here on this recent day, only a barnlike studio with an animator directing the mock celebration and a few computer technicians recording the movements with dozens of high-speed motion-capture cameras that zero in on 65 reflective markers Velcroed to the players’ uniforms.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Capturing Football’s Snaps, Crackles and Pops in Madden NFL', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Capturing N.F.L. Snaps, Crackles, Pops', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Electronic Arts Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Madden NFL (Video Game)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_