tract': 'The brain-dead pregnant woman who was taken off life support after her family’s battle to gain custody of her body from a Fort Worth hospital will be cremated, her mother said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/us/texas-woman-at-center-of-struggle-will-be-cremated.html', 'snippet': 'The brain-dead pregnant woman who was taken off life support after her family’s battle to gain custody of her body from a Fort Worth hospital will be cremated, her mother said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The brain-dead pregnant woman who was taken off life support after her family’s battle to gain custody of her body from a Fort Worth hospital will be cremated, her mother said Tuesday. Marlise Muñoz, 33, had been on life support since November against her family’s wishes. The hospital had refused to disconnect her, citing a Texas law that prohibits doctors from withdrawing life support to pregnant patients. The hospital removed her from the machines on Sunday after a judge’s order. She was 22 weeks pregnant. Her fetus, which the hospital said was not viable, was a girl. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Woman at Center of Struggle Will Be Cremated', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Woman at Center of Struggle Will Be Cremated ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Life-Sustaining Support Systems, Withdrawal Of', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cremation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munoz, Marlise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T01:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'last