ine': {'main': 'For $28.50, All the Super Bowl Hype a Fan Could Stand', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For $28.50, All the Hype a Fan Could Stand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T01:53:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f225e9-2568-5b18-9aae-d18b3df6b0a0', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f225e9-2568-5b18-9aae-d18b3df6b0a0'}, {'abstract': 'A judge rightfully blocked onerous restrictions imposed by Missouri on counselors who help people enroll in health insurance plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/opinion/roadblocks-on-health-reform.html', 'snippet': 'A judge rightfully blocked onerous restrictions imposed by Missouri on counselors who help people enroll in health insurance plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Onerous restrictions imposed by Missouri on federally approved counselors who help people understand and enroll in health insurance plans under the Affordable Care Act have rightly been blocked by a federal district judge in Kansas City. Although the ruling by Judge Ortrie Smith applies only to Missouri, its reasoning applies to similar laws or regulations adopted by more than a dozen Republican-led states that are doing their best to sabotage health care reform.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roadblocks on Health Reform', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roadblocks on Health Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Ortrie D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T01:53:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e52ef76-787d-5fc2-a5cf-dab9df5becdd', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e52ef76-787d-5fc2-a5cf-dab9df5becdd'}, {'abstract': 'The visit by United Nations inspectors is part of a temporary international agreement aimed at resolving the longstanding dispute over the Iranian nuclear program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/world/middleeast/iran-un-to-visit-uranium-mine.html', 'snippet': 'The visit by United Nations inspectors is part of a temporary international agreement aimed at resolving the longstanding dispute over the Iranian nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': ' United Nations nuclear inspectors arrived in Iran on Tuesday to examine a uranium mine in the southern part of the country, Iranian news agencies reported. Their visit is part of a temporary international agreement aimed at resolving the longstanding dispute over the Iranian nuclear program, which Iran says is for energy and medical use but which Western nations and Israel suspect is a cloak for developing the ability to make bombs. Under the accord, which took effect on Jan. 20, Iran agreed to freeze most uranium-enrichment activities for six months and allow inspectors more intrusive access, in return for a relaxation of some Western economic sanctions. An exact date and a location have not been set for talks aimed at achieving a permanent agreement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: U.N. to Visit Uranium Mine', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East: Iran: U.N. to Visit Uranium Mine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T01:55:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/74f6197c-99c9-5004-91e7-974de3040eb6', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74f6197c-99c9-5004-91e7-974de3040eb6'}, {'abstract': 'Snow days: celebrated and rued by kids and parents everywhere, in that order.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/28/more-winter-less-school/', 'snippet': 'Snow days: celebrated and rued by kids and parents everywhere, in that order.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Schools open. I’m cheering, kids aren’t. I just went over to the dark side.”'