ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d69604e-daa9-56b2-b95c-d8534279d7ef', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d69604e-daa9-56b2-b95c-d8534279d7ef'}, {'abstract': 'Broncos tight end Julius Thomas, who switched from basketball to football at Portland State, will be a key player for Denver as it takes on Seattle’s No. 1-ranked defense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/sports/football/big-and-fast-tight-end-poses-a-threat-to-an-intimidating-secondary.html', 'snippet': 'Broncos tight end Julius Thomas, who switched from basketball to football at Portland State, will be a key player for Denver as it takes on Seattle’s No. 1-ranked defense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — To find the end zone against a hard-hitting Seattle secondary known as the Legion of Boom, the Denver Broncos may have to rely on a player some call Mr. Red Zone. The name sounds like a comic book character, but Sunday in Super Bowl XLVIII, the performance of Julius Thomas, the Broncos’ tight end, will go a long way in determining how well Denver’s offense fares against the N.F.L.’s No. 1 defense.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/sports/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2/CITY-NFL-THOMAS-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big and Fast Tight End Poses a Threat to an Intimidating Secondary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big and Fast Tight End Poses a Threat to an Intimidating Secondary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Julius (1988- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T04:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ee3c1f-b343-5db5-a6d5-3f9e955b3730', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ee3c1f-b343-5db5-a6d5-3f9e955b3730'}, {'abstract': 'An emerging group of young Los Angeles sculptors are branching out into functional pieces for the home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/t-magazine/los-angeles-blurring-the-line-between-art-and-housewares.html', 'snippet': 'An emerging group of young Los Angeles sculptors are branching out into functional pieces for the home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no surprise that many sculptors have a yen for making furniture. After all, the tools are right within reach, and the process isn’t that different. In Los Angeles, which has a long history of furniture manufacturing and an abundance of interior spaces to fill, a growing number of young artists are making forays into the realm of domestic utility. “There’s a lot of sculpture out there that doesn’t want to admit to being furniture,” says the local artist Michael Rey, who has of late branched into objects that retain his affinity for the visual language of cartoons and ’90s pop culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In L.A., Blurring the Line Between Art and Housewares', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Su Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Su', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b4a5eed-f9c2-5fda-a0d8-d1a62974bba8', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b4a5eed-f9c2-5fda-a0d8-d1a62974bba8'}, {'abstract': 'Becoming physically active in middle age, even if someone has been sedentary for years, substantially reduces the likelihood that he or she will become seriously ill or physically disabled in retirement, new research shows.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/exercise-to-age-well-regardless-of-age/', 'snippet': 'Becoming physically active in middle age, even if someone has been sedentary for years, substantially reduces the likelihood that he or she will become seriously ill or physically disabled in retirement, new research shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Offering hope and encouragement to the many adults who have somehow neglected to exercise for the past few decades, a new study suggests that becoming physically active in middle age, even if someone has been sedentary for years, substantially reduces the likelihood that he or she will become seriously ill or physically disabled in retirement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/health/29well-physed/29well-physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/29/health/29well-physed/29well-physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/health/29well-physed/29well-physed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/health/29well-physed/29well-physed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 