r of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s a 29er', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T05:01:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa10c0f6-975c-59de-9ad3-050391ba29ed', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa10c0f6-975c-59de-9ad3-050391ba29ed'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in four New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/word-of-the-day-imprecation/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in four New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'imprecation •\\ˌim-pri-ˈka-shən\\• noun ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | imprecation', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T05:02:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf425f1d-82d7-5e44-8e6a-b49b88c1f58a', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf425f1d-82d7-5e44-8e6a-b49b88c1f58a'}, {'abstract': 'A reporter offers his best translation of what President Obama really meant as he addressed Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/us/politics/state-of-the-union-as-it-was-spoken-and-as-decoded.html', 'snippet': 'A reporter offers his best translation of what President Obama really meant as he addressed Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In an excellent scene from “Mitt,” the new documentary about the former Massachusetts governor Mitt Romney’s two presidential campaigns, the filmmaker asks one of Mr. Romney’s sons, Josh, whether all the hassle and indignity of campaigning is worth it. Josh Romney hesitates, saying that he had been so “trained” to deliver scripted happy talk in media interviews, that this might be hard. “To actually speak my mind is very different,” he finally says. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State of the Union, as It Was Spoken and as Decoded', 'kicker': 'Reporter’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State of the Union, as It Was Spoken and as Decoded', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovich, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T05:10:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'origi