s as the country’s first elected government after the Arab Spring of 2011. The government departed under pressure, criticized for failing to halt rising terrorism and steady a faltering economy, but Ennahda was nevertheless assured of its place in Tunisian politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamist Party in Tunisia Hands Power to Caretaker Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Islamist Party in Tunisia Hands Power to Caretaker Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ennahda Party (Tunisia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laarayedh, Ali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ben Ali, Zine El-Abidine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, State Legislature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T06:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Gall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ba95c55-dcba-5311-b0ed-95c030b7a91a', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ba95c55-dcba-5311-b0ed-95c030b7a91a'}, {'abstract': 'The largest retail book fair, which begins Wednesday in West Bengal’s capital, also features the three-day Kolkata Language and Literary Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/a-pocket-guide-to-the-2014-kolkata-book-fair/', 'snippet': 'The largest retail book fair, which begins Wednesday in West Bengal’s capital, also features the three-day Kolkata Language and Literary Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KOLKATA — The 38th Kolkata Book Fair may have lost the Kolkata Literary Meet, which has spun off into a standalone event, but it has filled the void by adding the three-day Kolkata Language and Literary Festival, which is set to be inaugurated by Shashi Tharoor, the minister of state for human resource development.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pocket Guide to the 2014 Kolkata Book Fair', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Fairs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandra, Subhash', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Llosa, Mario Vargas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tharoor, Shashi', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kolkata (India)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Machu Picchu (Peru)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T06:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anurad