mic Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T11:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a641d61-4a5a-5859-a9e4-f388a8b0e80f', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a641d61-4a5a-5859-a9e4-f388a8b0e80f'}, {'abstract': 'At the start, no one wants to haggle over shares because, at this stage, the company isn’t worth anything. Right?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/the-co-founder-dilemma/', 'snippet': 'At the start, no one wants to haggle over shares because, at this stage, the company isn’t worth anything. Right?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The idea for Posse struck me while relaxing in my apartment one Sunday afternoon. I didn’t know how to run a technology company, wasn’t at all confident the idea would work, and feared I might end up with egg on my face. In the interests of spreading the personal and financial risk, I asked a few friends to help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Co-Founder Dilemma', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T12:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebekah Campbell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebekah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Campbell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52b7478c-d29d-5236-8629-eb19ff0b0a71', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52b7478c-d29d-5236-8629-eb19ff0b0a71'}, {'abstract': 'Those exotic doggy treats may come back to haunt you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/booming/fido-prefers-organic.html', 'snippet': 'Those exotic doggy treats may come back to haunt you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was invited for dinner at some old friends’ place the other day and I thought it would be nice to go to my local Greenwich Village pet store and pick up a treat for their dog, Manny. It is not that I am so crazy about Manny, who is a mix of a poodle and something even more annoying; I have had mixed feelings about him ever since he ate one of my sneakers. I just thought I would get him something he might enjoy chewing on as a diversionary tactic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/booming/28wadler-booming-pets2/28wadler-booming-pets2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/28/booming/28wadler-booming-pets2/28wadler-booming-pets2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 694}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/booming/28wadler-booming-pets2/28wadler-booming-pets2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/28/booming/28wadler-boomi