conomist once considered too negative by some has offered an upbeat interpretation of the most recent jobs report.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/the-sunny-side-of-the-unemployment-report/', 'snippet': 'An economist once considered too negative by some has offered an upbeat interpretation of the most recent jobs report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David A. Rosenberg, the chief economist at Gluskin Sheff, a Canadian research firm, is not known for his rose-colored glasses. Indeed, when he was at Merrill Lynch in New York, there were complaints that he was too negative. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sunny Side of the Unemployment Report', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, David A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gluskin Sheff and Associates Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T15:32:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b318902-eb99-51e3-9125-e11e2e2eaf3e', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b318902-eb99-51e3-9125-e11e2e2eaf3e'}, {'abstract': 'The office of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu issued a warning to a right-wing political partner, Naftali Bennett, over his harsh criticism of Mr. Netanyahu’s positions in recent days.', 'web_url': 'htt