yt://article/ae3d8cc9-9168-523b-908e-200e1f742249'}, {'abstract': 'The architects whose design for an expanded Museum of Modern Art calls for the demolition of the former home of the American Folk Art Museum defended their decision at a public forum in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/in-rare-public-forum-architect-defends-decision-to-take-down-former-folk-art-museum/', 'snippet': 'The architects whose design for an expanded Museum of Modern Art calls for the demolition of the former home of the American Folk Art Museum defended their decision at a public forum in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An architect typically doesn’t go before the public to defend a private project. But on Tuesday night Liz Diller of Diller Scofidio & Renfro stood before a crowd of 650 people, many of them her peers, to explain in detail the six-month process by which her firm tried to save the former home of the American Folk Art Museum before deciding it was impossible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/29artsbeat-moma3/29artsbeat-moma3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/29artsbeat-moma3/29artsbeat-moma3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 901}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/29artsbeat-moma3/29artsbeat-moma3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/arts/29artsbeat-moma3/29artsbeat-moma3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1461, 'width': 973, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,