,000 years after their extinction, finding Neanderthal genes in skin and hair that may have helped humans evolve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since the discovery in 2010 that Neanderthals interbred with the ancestors of living humans, scientists have been trying to determine how their DNA affects people today. Now two new studies have traced the history of Neanderthal DNA, and have pinpointed a number of genes that may have medical importance today.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/science/30dna/30dna-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/30/science/30dna/30dna-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/science/30dna/30dna-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/science/30dna/30dna-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1491, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/science/30dna/30dna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/30/science/30dna/30dna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/science/30dna/30dna-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Neanderthals Leave Their Mark on Us', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Studies Show a Little Bit of Neanderthal in Us All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Neanderthal Man', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution (Biology)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reich, David E (1974- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akey, Joshua M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vernot, Benjamin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T19:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8689d5e6-bed3-591b-8691-00a3e3fff619', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8689d5e6-bed3-591b-8691-00a3e3fff619'}, {'abstract': 'Egyptian prosecutors said that the journalists, all employees of the Al Jazeera television network, worked to help and spread propaganda for the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/world/middleeast/egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Egyptian prosecutors said that the journalists, all employees of the Al Jazeera television network, worked to help and spread propaganda for the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egyptian prosecutors said on Wednesday that they were charging 20 journalists working for the Al Jazeera television network with conspiring with a terrorist group and broadcasting false images of “a civil war that raises alarms about the state’s collapse.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '20 Al Jazeera Journalists Face Charges in Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '20 Al Jazeera Journalists Face Charges in Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T19:18:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd2c0c48-a6c8-5ca2-b6b4-81ace5c628c8', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd2c0c48-a6c8-5ca2-b6b4-81ace5c628c8'}, {'abstract': 'There were three organized responses—one official, one Tea Party, one libertarian—to the State of the Union.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/all-right-there-are-two-republican-parties/', 'snippet': 'There were three organized responses—one official, one Tea Party, one libertarian—to the State of the Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican pundits have been arguing recently that immigration reform could splinter the party ahead of the 2014 elections. They shouldn’t be worrying about immigration. The Republicans’ response to President Obama’s State of the Union showed that the G.O.P. is actually two parties, or perhaps even more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Right, There Are Two Republican Parties', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimm, Michael G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Michael S (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMorris Rodgers, Cathy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T19:32:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe54fb7-a442-5086-9513-aebf320887c1', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe54fb7-a442-5086-9513-aebf320887c1'}, {'abstract': 'Daft Punk and Paul McCartney saw gains in music streaming after the awards show; Katy Perry’s song “Dark Horse” topped the singles chart.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/grammys-spur-streaming-katy-perry-single-hits-no-1/', 'snippet': 'Daft Punk and Paul McCartney saw gains in music streaming after the awards show; Katy Perry’s song “Dark Horse” topped the singles chart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lorde may have been the Grammy Awards’ most talked-about artist on Sunday night — more of the 15.2 million Grammy tweets were about her than any other act, Twitter reported — but when it came to streaming music, Daft Punk appears to have gotten the biggest early lift.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grammys Spur Streaming; Katy Perry Single Hits No. 1', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grammy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamar, Kendrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lorde', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daft Punk (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Macklemore & Ryan Lewis (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Recording Arts and Sciences', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T19:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a454da7-9418-5463-9cdd-c22515da6daa', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a454da7-9418-5463-9cdd-c22515da6daa'}, {'abstract': 'During Tuesday night’s State of the Union address, representatives and senators – or members of their staffs sent just under 1,500 tweets while President Obama was speaking.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/applaud-tweet-and-repeat-at-the-state-of-the-union/', 'snippet': 'During Tuesday night’s State of the Union address, representatives and senators – or members of their staffs sent just under 1,500 tweets while President Obama was speaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Immediately after a president’s State of the Union address is delivered, news organizations frequently seek to answer a question: How many times did members of Congress stand and applaud? In this era when social media has become an important arena for politics, and in some ways eclipses the statements and interviews representatives and senators issue after an address like the State of the Union, another question may be more important: How many tweets did members of Congress send during the speech?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Applaud, Tweet and Repeat at the State of the Union', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-29T19:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Roston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f2d0e5-b090-5c14-8907-bd2e818602ce', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f2d0e5-b090-5c14-8907-bd2e818602ce'}, {'abstract': 'Dow Chemical may have expanded its stock buyback program and dividend, but it showed little inclination to make further concessions to activist investors li