b854b3240', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d36e2e3-8a62-5758-982c-295b854b3240'}, {'abstract': 'The controversial young star discusses his new play, “Intimacy,” which opens tonight, adapting “Uncle Tom’s Cabin” and how ethnic slurs are different in New Jersey and Chicago.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/q-and-a-playwright-thomas-bradshaw-on-race-porn-and-suburbia/', 'snippet': 'The controversial young star discusses his new play, “Intimacy,” which opens tonight, adapting “Uncle Tom’s Cabin” and how ethnic slurs are different in New Jersey and Chicago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Bradshaw’s plays have elicited belly laughs from some viewers and disgust from others. Naysayers have called the 33-year-old playwright’s shows, which include “Purity,” “Burning” and “Job,” “ugly fantasies” and “horror shows.” One Chicago theater critic went so far as to warn Bradshaw to get out of town. The reactions are due to the fact that Bradshaw, who is black, stages outrageous behavior — including child rape, racially charged sex and modern-day slavery — in casual, conversational ways.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/t-magazine/29bradshaw-murphy/29bradshaw-murphy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/29/t-magazine/29bradshaw-murphy/29bradshaw-murphy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/t-magazine/29bradshaw-murphy/29bradshaw-murphy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/29/t-magazine/29bradshaw-murphy/29bradshaw-murphy-superJumbo.