 were designed for a Bond villain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — New arrivals to this city are often told by locals to hop in the car and take Sunset Boulevard to the Pacific Ocean. It is a beautiful drive, world famous. It is also an initiation into the California myth without the downsides: you glide past the traffic-clogged 405 freeway, wind through rustic canyons where movie stars live and breathe in the ocean breezes west of Brentwood, as if nature had provided Angelenos with free air-conditioning.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mystery at the Bend', 'kicker': 'Who Lives There', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mystery at the Bend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bridges, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f7bad28-8c02-52ee-b190-f1adf7f6e74e', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f7bad28-8c02-52ee-b190-f1adf7f6e74e'}, {'abstract': 'Helen Yoest wrote a book about natural aphrodisiacs called “Plants With Benefits.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/garden/sometimes-asparagus-is-more-than-asparagus.html', 'snippet': 'Helen Yoest wrote a book about natural aphrodisiacs called “Plants With Benefits.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Helen Yoest didn’t set out, as she said recently, to write a horticultural Kama Sutra. It was sort of an accident. Ms. Yoest, a garden writer, was researching an article on avocados when she learned that the fruit was considered an aphrodisiac. What makes it so, she wondered: The nutrients? The shape? Bingo. Turns out their reputation dates to the Aztecs, who marveled at how avocados grew in pairs, and named the plant “the testicle tree.”\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/garden/30QNA1/30QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/30/garden/30QNA1/30QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 894}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/garden/30QNA1/30QNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/garden/30QNA1/30QNA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1374, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/garden/30QNA1/30QNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/30/garden/30QNA1/30QNA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/garden/30QNA1/30QNA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sometimes Asparagus Is More Than Asparagus', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seduced by Plants and Veggies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Penelope', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoest, Helen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Plants With Benefits: An Uninhibited Guide to the Aphrodisiac Herbs, Fruits, Flowers and Veggies in Your Garden (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:24:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Penelope Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Penelope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/d55a7ab5-cdf2-56e9-b2c4-07ba6732410d', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d55a7ab5-cdf2-56e9-b2c4-07ba6732410d'}, {'abstract': 'The chief executive of Blue Bottle, a gourmet coffee purveyor, confirmed that his company had raised $25.75 million in a new round of financing, including from co-founders of Instagram and Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/blue-bottle-raises-25-75-million-including-from-high-powered-friends/', 'snippet': 'The chief executive of Blue Bottle, a gourmet coffee purveyor, confirmed that his company had raised $25.75 million in a new round of financing, including from co-founders of Instagram and Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few brands are as beloved in the tech community as the Blue Bottle Coffee Company, a nearly 12-year-old purveyor of gourm