e': 'persons', 'value': 'Systrom, Kevin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Evan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Bottle Coffee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:25:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86447efa-53ae-5d5f-a308-88ffb5ea2fdb', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86447efa-53ae-5d5f-a308-88ffb5ea2fdb'}, {'abstract': 'The budget at the newspaper owned by Jeffrey Bezos, the founder of Amazon.com, will be increased and dozens of new employees will be hired for the newsroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/business/media/major-expansion-ahead-at-the-washington-post.html', 'snippet': 'The budget at the newspaper owned by Jeffrey Bezos, the founder of Amazon.com, will be increased and dozens of new employees will be hired for the newsroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Washington Post has significantly increased its budget and plans to make dozens of newsroom hires under its new owner, the Amazon founder Jeffrey P. Bezos, the paper’s executive editor, Marty Baron, said in an interview on Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Major Expansion Ahead at The Washington Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Major Expansion Ahead at The Washington Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:28:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/518a8b67-bdc8-56d1-93c7-a7ebacf85127', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/518a8b67-bdc8-56d1-93c7-a7ebacf85127'}, {'abstract': 'When choosing containers, the garden designer Jon Carloftis said, remember that the plants are the “real stars,” and the planter is just the “vessel.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/garden/planters-best-supporting-actors.html', 'snippet': 'When choosing containers, the garden designer Jon Carloftis said, remember that the plants are the “real stars,” and the planter is just the “vessel.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may seem like an odd time to be thinking about planters, with signs of the polar vortex still in evidence. But as Jon Carloftis, a garden designer with clients like Google and Maker’s Mark, said, “Now is the time everyone needs something green in their life.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Planters: Best Supporting Actors', 'kicker': 'Shopping With Jon Carloftis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Best Supporting Actors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carloftis, Jon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebb5b64d-0064-501f-8af0-a27ac08807e4', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebb5b64d-0064-501f-8af0-a27ac08807e4'}, {'abstract': 'The plane maker’s stock dropped 5.3 percent on Wednesday following projections that its revenue would increase less than expected in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/business/boeing-shares-fall-as-it-cautions-on-its-profits-in-2014.html', 'snippet': 'The plane maker’s stock dropped 5.3 percent on Wednesday following projections that its revenue would increase less than expected in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After doubling over the last year, Boeing’s stock dropped 5.3 percent on Wednesday when the plane maker projected flattening profits in 2014.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boeing Shares Fall as It Cautions on Its Profits in 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boeing Shares Fall as It Cautions on Its Profits in 2014', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b3b130-f8f6-55c1-952e-9c0e10582e8c', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b3b130-f8f6-55c1-952e-9c0e10582e8c'}, {'abstract': 'Gracenote will work with the data company Next Big Sound as it develops a system that would let almost any anyone create an Internet radio service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/business/media/music-data-firms-to-collaborate-on-internet-radio-platform.html', 'snippet': 'Gracenote will work with the data company Next Big Sound as it develops a system that would let almost any anyone create an Internet radio service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gracenote, a digital music data service that the Tribune Company bought last month for $170 million, is quickly moving forward with its plans for a customizable Internet radio program that would let consumer brands, car companies and anyone else have their own music app.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Music Data Firms to Collaborate on Internet Radio Platform', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gracenote Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a43dc7da-e06f-54b8-bcb7-86f31c4e1686', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a43dc7da-e06f-54b8-bcb7-86f31c4e1686'}, {'abstract': 'Do Grill Daddy’s King Tong fire tong