n said Iman Shumpert, who was injured in Tuesday’s win over Boston, will have his sprained right shoulder re-evaluated Thursday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Knicks Coach Mike Woodson said the sprained right shoulder Iman Shumpert sustained in Tuesday’s victory over the Boston Celtics would be re-evaluated Thursday morning. Appearing Wednesday on ESPN Radio, Woodson said Shumpert was “day to day” but cast doubt over his availability for Thursday’s game against the Cleveland Cavaliers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks’ Shumpert Is ‘Day to Day’ After Shoulder Injury', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shumpert Is ‘Day to Day’ After Injury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shumpert, Iman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodson, Mike', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:58:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8d7117f-66be-588a-8cef-801e3aed61ad', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8d7117f-66be-588a-8cef-801e3aed61ad'}, {'abstract': 'The president cannot both open markets and close the wage gap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/opinion/obamas-free-trade-conundrum.html', 'snippet': 'The president cannot both open markets and close the wage gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — IN his State of the Union address on Tuesday, President Obama focused on reversing the growth of economic inequality in the United States and restoring the American dream. At the same time, he also announced his support for fast track authority that would limit Congress’s role in determining the content of trade agreements.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Free-Trade Conundrum', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama’s Free-Trade Conundrum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American Free Trade Agreement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T00:59:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Bonior', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Bonior', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3f32f66-7844-5d73-9830-cda2c37637da', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3f32f66-7844-5d73-9830-cda2c37637da'}, {'abstract': 'A turnabout has the exile coalition and its Western backers declaring an early, if modest, victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/world/middleeast/syrian-oppositions-calm-at-talks-surprises-as-officials-falter.html', 'snippet': 'A turnabout has the exile coalition and its Western backers declaring an early