al', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/288a409e-dadd-5bfa-a279-11728286c615', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/288a409e-dadd-5bfa-a279-11728286c615'}, {'abstract': 'Because the N.F.L.’s recent settlement promises payments to an unknown number of players, the $765 million called for in the deal could run out faster than expected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/sports/football/under-nfl-settlement-making-pie-without-knowing-total-slices.html', 'snippet': 'Because the N.F.L.’s recent settlement promises payments to an unknown number of players, the $765 million called for in the deal could run out faster than expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As intriguing football matchups go, Sunday’s Super Bowl has nothing on one looming down the turnpike in federal court in Philadelphia — with Judge Anita B. Brody the ultimate referee.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncertainty Over Whether N.F.L. Settlement’s Money Will Last', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Pie Without Knowing Total Slices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwarz, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brody, Anita B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T02:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Schwarz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f340d0f2-9561-5d37-bff5-2d7279cfc1a7', 'word_count': 1313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f340d0f2-9561-5d37-bff5-2d7279cfc1a7'}, {'abstract': 'A terrible ruling involving a case in Missouri allows states to hide the untested drugs they use to put inmates to death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/opinion/secrecy-behind-executions.html', 'snippet': 'A terrible ruling involving a case in Missouri allows states to hide the untested drugs they use to put inmates to death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is bad enough that the death penalty is barbaric, racist and arbitrary in its application, but it is also becoming less transparent as the dwindling number of death-penalty states work to hide the means by which they kill people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secrecy Behind Executions', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Secrecy Behind Executions ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smulls, Herbert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T02:11:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdfba973-966d-5fd7-bbd2-d56c70f2d262', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdfba973-966d-5fd7-bbd2-d56c70f2d262'}, {'abstract': 'President Milos Zeman of the Czech Republic appointed a new center-left government on Wednesday, ending a protracted period of political paralysis that has destabilized the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/world/europe/new-government-for-czech-republic.html', 'snippet': 'President Milos Zeman of the Czech Republic appointed a new center-left government on Wednesday, ending a protracted period of political paralysis that has destabilized the country.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Milos Zeman of the Czech Republic appointed a new center-left government on Wednesday, ending a protracted period of political paralysis that has destabilized the country. The freshly installed prime minister, Bohuslav Sobotka, 42, has pledged to shepherd the country toward stability following a corruption scandal last summer that forced Prime Minister Petr Necas to resign. A subsequent interim government failed to win parliament’s confidence. Mr. Sobotka, a Social Democrat, has pledged to combat some austerity measures of previous conservative governments. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Government for Czech Republic', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Government for Czech Republic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeman, Milos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sobotka, Bohuslav', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Necas, Petr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T02:12:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/06269788-48c8-598a-ba6f-f105b96da8c6', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06269788-48c8-598a-ba6f-f105b96da8c6'}, {'abstract': 'The song’s composer, who serves on the executive committee of the Academy’s music branch, emailed branch members, which was considered a violation of rules on promotions.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/29/academy-rescinds-song-nomination-for-alone-yet-not-alone/', 'snippet': 'The song’s composer, who serves on the executive committee of the Academy’s music branch, emailed branch members, which was considered a violation of rules on promotions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES —The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences said its governors had voted to rescind an Oscar nomination for the song “Alone Yet Not Alone,” from the movie of the same title, because one of its creators, Bruce Broughton, had improperly advised fellow members of the Academy’s music branch that he was in the running for a nomination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Academy Rescinds Song Nomination for ‘Alone Yet Not Alone’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacs, Cheryl Boone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T02:12:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstn