9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yusufzai, Rahimullah', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T02:42:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90ae9ba4-1835-5ff6-a090-da43d67ade78', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90ae9ba4-1835-5ff6-a090-da43d67ade78'}, {'abstract': 'Darion Aguilar, the suspect in a deadly shooting at a mall, wrote about killing people in his journal and said that he was ready to die.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/us/maryland-shooting-suspect-wrote-of-death.html', 'snippet': 'Darion Aguilar, the suspect in a deadly shooting at a mall, wrote about killing people in his journal and said that he was ready to die.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The suspect in a deadly shooting at a mall wrote about killing people in his journal and said that he was ready to die, the police said Wednesday. The man, Darion Aguilar, 19, “expressed a general hatred of others” in entries over the past year, the Howard County police department said. Mr. Aguilar wrote that his plan was set, but did not say what that meant, and apologized to his family for what he was about to do, the police said. The police said Mr. Aguilar wrote that he might need help for a mental health problem, but never told his family. The police believe Mr. Aguilar killed two employees of the skate shop Zumiez on Saturday at the Mall in Columbia before killing himself. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maryland: Shooting Suspect Wrote of Death', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Mid-Atlantic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he