/riddled-with-spelling-problems/', 'snippet': 'Dan Schoenholz digs up an old one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — Before we discuss today’s puzzle, I’d like to take a moment to talk about the format changes in our commenting system, as well as the issues that have occurred as a result. The Times is well aware of the general reaction that readers across the website, not just on Wordplay, have had to the changes, as well as the specific bugs you have reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riddled With Spelling Problems', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T03:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ad6e18f-b5bf-5789-a5ce-fb99f058194c', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ad6e18f-b5bf-5789-a5ce-fb99f058194c'}, {'abstract': 'State labor officials have dropped charges that a Chinese high-tech bus company was paying a handful of workers below minimum wage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/us/california-charges-against-bus-company-dropped.html', 'snippet': 'State labor officials have dropped charges that a Chinese high-tech bus company was paying a handful of workers below minimum wage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'State labor officials have dropped charges that a Chinese high-tech bus company was paying a handful of workers below minimum wage. Last fall, investigators said that the company, Build Your Dreams, was paying workers here temporarily from China in Chinese currency equivalent to less than $8 an hour, the state’s minimum wage. But the company, known as BYD, has provided bank documents that showed the workers were paid the equivalent of $12 to $17 an hour in California. On Tuesday, lawyers for the state labor agency removed citations that ordered nearly $12,000 in back wages. The company agreed to pay $1,900 in penalties for paying the workers in Chinese currency rather than dollars. The company has won several contracts to create electric buses across the country, including in Los Angeles. It operates its American headquarters in downtown Los Angeles and a manufacturing plant in northeast Los Angeles County. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Charges Against Bus Company Dropped', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Charges Against Bus Company Dropped', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Build Your Dreams', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T03:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4033c144-c3c7-5788-b337-01