tors’ admonishments about the risks of theft and waste have raised new questions about the wisdom of giving huge amounts of aid directly to a government known for corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/world/asia/report-says-afghanistan-cant-be-trusted-to-prevent-misuse-of-us-aid.html', 'snippet': 'Auditors’ admonishments about the risks of theft and waste have raised new questions about the wisdom of giving huge amounts of aid directly to a government known for corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — With billions of dollars in American aid increasingly flowing straight into Afghan government coffers, the United States hired two global auditing firms three years ago to determine whether Afghanistan could be trusted to safeguard the money.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Aid to Afghans Flows On Despite Warnings of Misuse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Says Afghanistan Can’t Be Trusted to Prevent Misuse of U.S. Aid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Special Inspector General for Afghanistan Reconstruction', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sopko, John F', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T05:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rose