er opera about the jazz saxophonist Charlie Parker, the company is expected to announce Thursday. The work will have a libretto by Bridgette A. Wimberly, and is being produced in a partnership with Gotham Chamber Opera, in New York. It is expected to have its world premiere in Philadelphia in June 2015 in a production directed by Ron Daniels, with later performances by Gotham Chamber Opera.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Be-Bopera: ‘Charlie Parker’s Yardbird’ Coming From Opera Philadelphia', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s a Be-Bopera: ‘Charlie Parker’s Yardbird’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Charlie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schnyder, Daniel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opera Philadelphia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T05:01:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc20d565-59be-5340-8fc6-63c1ea28d202', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc20d565-59be-5340-8fc6-63c1ea28d202'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury’s Office of Financial Research seems to have little gusto for taking on the biggest banks and the dangers they pose, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/the-disappointing-office-of-financial-research/', 'snippet': 'The Treasury’s Office of Financial Research seems to have little gusto for taking on the biggest banks and the dangers they pose, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, former chief economist of the International Monetary Fund, is the Ronald A. Kurtz professor of entrepreneurship at the M.I.T. Sloan School of Management and co-author of “White House Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Disappointing Office of Financial Research', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warner, Mark R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Financial Research (United States Treasury)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T05:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdecb350-8b1a-5cb3-8bda-29ab69aeef34', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdecb350-8b1a-5cb3-8bda-29ab69aeef34'}, {'abstract': 'William J. Baer, assistant attorney general for the Justice Department’s antitrust division, also said any proposed merger among cable television companies would face similar scrutiny.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/wireless-mergers-will-draw-scrutiny-antitrust-chief-says/', 'snippet': 'William J. Baer, assistant attorney general for the Justice Department’s antitrust division, also said any proposed merger among cable television companies would face similar scrutiny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The nation’s leading antitrust enforcer said this week that it would be difficult for the Justice Department to approve a merger among any of the top four wireless phone companies, casting doubt on recent speculation that T-Mobile and Sprint might consummate a deal in coming months.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/business/Antitrust1/Antitrust1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/30/business/Antitrust1/Antitrust1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/business/Antitrust1/Antitrust1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/business/Antitrust1/Antitrust1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/business/Antitrust1/Antitrust1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTy