terfeit merchandise and a reprieve from the extreme cold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 10:45 a.m. Good Thursday morning. It’s in the low 20s, and the temperature is struggling back up to normal.Meanwhile, Manhattan has been converted into a Super Bowl fan zone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: For Non-Fans, an Open Field', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T10:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a4ab4ae-0cc7-5159-a606-ed998abb9724', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a4ab4ae-0cc7-5159-a606-ed998abb9724'}, {'abstract': 'Viktor F. Yanukovych, saddled by respiratory issues, went on leave even as talks remained unsettled and the repeal of new curbs on speech and assembly was yet to be signed into law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/world/europe/ukraine-unrest.html', 'snippet': 'Viktor F. Yanukovych, saddled by respiratory issues, went on leave even as talks remained unsettled and the repeal of new curbs on speech and assembly was yet to be signed into law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — Critical negotiations between the embattled Ukrainian government and opposition leaders were thrown into disarray on Thursday when President Viktor F. Yanukovych went on sick leave, complaining of a respiratory infection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/world/europe/Ukraine/Ukraine-articleLarge.jpg'