with Sri Lanka have become increasingly frosty, largely because of the government’s reluctance to investigate reports of abuses from a civil war that ended five years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/world/asia/sri-lanka.html', 'snippet': 'Relations with Sri Lanka have become increasingly frosty, largely because of the government’s reluctance to investigate reports of abuses from a civil war that ended five years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — A top State Department official is expected to arrive in Sri Lanka on Friday, just three days after the United States announced that it would again seek a resolution at the United Nations Human Rights Council pressing for an investigation into allegations of war crimes in Sri Lanka.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Envoy to Visit Sri Lanka as Pressure Builds for War Crimes Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia; Sri Lanka: Pressure Builds for a War Crimes Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tamils (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T13:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2635c