pled stretches of the Deep South, life eased back toward normal, students slept in their homes again and drivers sought abandoned cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Parts of the Deep South sputtered slowly toward normalcy on Thursday, two days after a winter storm crippled vast stretches of the region and created unprecedented gridlock in its most populated areas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials Remain in the Hot Seat as the South Thaws', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Kasim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T14:46:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f94ad9-83a9-51c8-a501-8b6af710a269', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f94ad9-83a9-51c8-a501-8b6af710a269'}, {'abstract': 'Oh noes, another crisis!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/istanbearish/', 'snippet': 'Oh noes, another crisis!', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, did we need this? Turkey? Who was paying attention to Turkey?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Istanbearish', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T14:55:40+0000', 'documen