beat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/bieber-faces-assault-charge-in-toronto/', 'snippet': 'Justin Bieber was charged with assaulting a limousine driver in December, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s episode of the Justin Bieber Show, the 19-year-old\xa0Canadian singer has returned to his homeland, only to find himself once more chatting with the police. This time, he went to the Toronto police voluntarily, a stark\xa0contrast with last week’s installment, in which Mr. Bieber was arrested in Miami Beach and charged with driving under the influence, resisting arrest and driving without a valid license.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bieber Faces Assault Charge in Toronto', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T16:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b218aa72-14da-5504-817a-5db91e04d732', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b218aa72-14da-5504-817a-5db91e04d732'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio announced on Thursday that the city would ends its battle over the Police Department’s aggressive practice by agreeing to reforms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/nyregion/de-blasio-stop-and-frisk.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio announced on Thursday that the city would ends its battle over the Police Department’s aggressive practice by agreeing to reforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City will settle its long-running legal battle over the Police Department’s practice of stopping, questioning and often frisking people on the street — a divisive issue at the heart of the mayoral race last year — by agreeing to reforms that a judge ordered in August, Mayor Bill de Blasio announced on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Says New York City Will Settle Suits on Stop-and-Frisk Tactics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor Says City Will Settle Suits on Frisk Tactics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Torres, Analisa J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bratton, William J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T16:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser and Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5079cbb1-7a10-567d-8d2d-188c75bc8627', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5079cbb1-7a10-567d-8d2d-188c75bc8627'}, {'abstract': 'The President of World Jewish Congress on Thursday called for the creation of a new panel that resolve the issue of how to resolve the issue of art that was looted by the Nazis from Jewish families and dealers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/lauder-calls-for-new-panel-to-resolve-nazi-art-looting-restitution-issues/', 'snippet': 'The President of World Jewish Congress on Thursday called for the creation of a new panel that resolve the issue of how to resolve the issue of art that was looted by the Nazis from Jewish families and dealers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronald S. Lauder, an art collector and philanthropist who is president of the World Jewish Congress, called on Thursday for the establishment of a new commission, made up of German and foreign experts, that would resolve once and for all the issue of art looted from Jews by the Nazis. Some of these works, Mr. Lauder said, still hang in German museums and even government offices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lauder Calls for New Panel to Resolve Nazi Art-Looting Restitution Issues', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurlitt, Cornelius', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauder, Ronald S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'v