ut his hearing loss.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/sports/21macur-1/21macur-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/31/sports/21macur-1/21macur-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/sports/21macur-1/21macur-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/sports/21macur-1/21macur-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/sports/21macur-1/21macur-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/31/sports/21macur-1/21macur-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/sports/21macur-1/21macur-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Showing Deaf Players They Fit In, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showing Deaf Players They Fit In, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macur, Juliet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gallaudet University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleman, Derrick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Talaat, Adham', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T18:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af1a6dad-0547-5b2c-a94e-44363a448920', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af1a6dad-0547-5b2c-a94e-44363a448920'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans say they support equal pay for equal work, but won’t pass legislation to help close the gender pay gap.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/equality-as-handout/', 'snippet': 'Republicans say they support equal pay for equal work, but won’t pass legislation to help close the gender pay gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his State of the Union address, President Obama endorsed a basic feminist concept that no national politician would dare contradict: “A woman deserves equal pay for equal work.”\xa0Representative Cathy McMorris Rodgers, who delivered the official Republican response to the president’s speech, didn’t hesitate to endorse the principle in a Wednesday CNN interview: “Republicans and I support equal pay for equal work,” she said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Equality as Handout', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blitzer, Wolf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMorris Rodgers, Cathy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T18:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84566958-0c3e-5791-bebf-79603d4af5c4', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84566958-0c3e-5791-bebf-79603d4af5c4'}, {'abstract': 'This year, a new kind of advertising — personalized and based on physical location down to a matter of feet — will greet fans in Times Square and MetLife Stadium, where the Super Bowl will be played this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/technology/For-Super-Bowl-Personalized-Phone-Alerts.html', 'snippet': 'This year, a new kind of advertising — personalized and based on physical location down to a matter of feet — will greet fans in Times Square and MetLife Stadium, where the Super Bowl will be played this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Want to see the Vince Lombardi Trophy that goes to the Super Bowl winner? Take a left in 15 feet. Looking to buy some Super Bowl merchandise? Try the fourth floor of Macy’s, straight ahead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/technolo