ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1d47c78-ae3e-59eb-9f61-1f686b669b8b', 'word_count': 24, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1d47c78-ae3e-59eb-9f61-1f686b669b8b'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Polan spent so much time drawing in Taco Bell that he decided to invite other people to join him.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/the-combination-drawing-club-and-taco-bell/', 'snippet': 'Jason Polan spent so much time drawing in Taco Bell that he decided to invite other people to join him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the cold New York weather has you looking for indoor activities, a little-known (and free) drawing club is held most Wednesdays from 4:30 p.m. to 6 p.m. at the Taco Bell on 14th Street just west of Union Square. The artist Jason Polan started the Taco Bell Drawing Club nine years ago and still attends many of the weekly meetings. Polan is a prolific artist; he has drawn every piece of art in the Museum of Modern Art (not once but twice) and is currently on a mission to draw every person in New York. The club meetings are open to anyone who wants to show up and draw. Having visited recently, I decided to ask Polan some questions about the group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/magazine/27-taco-bell-drawing-club-main/27-taco-bell-drawing-club-main-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/27/magazine/27-taco-bell-drawing-club-main/27-taco-bell-drawing-club-main-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/27/magazine/27-taco-bell-drawing-club-main/27-taco-bell-drawing-club-main-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cred