, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fcf81d0-b648-53d1-8fd8-f361964d40be'}, {'abstract': 'With a new appreciation for Bill Clinton’s leadership style, and more of Mr. Clinton’s former advisers on his team, President Obama is embracing a modest approach to getting things done.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/us/politics/obama-orders-review-of-us-job-training-programs.html', 'snippet': 'With a new appreciation for Bill Clinton’s leadership style, and more of Mr. Clinton’s former advisers on his team, President Obama is embracing a modest approach to getting things done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — In the summer of his first year in power, President Obama made clear that he envisioned a lofty mission. “I wasn’t sent here to do school uniforms,” he told aides one day in the Oval Office. The implication was clear: He did not want to govern like Bill Clinton.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/31-OBAMA-1/31-OBAMA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/31/us/31-OBAMA-1/31-OBAMA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/31-OBAMA-1/31-OBAMA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/31-OBAMA-1/31-OBAMA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/31-OBAMA-1/31-OBAMA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/31/us/31-OBAMA-1/31-OBAMA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/31-OBAMA-1/31-OBAMA-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Once Disdained Clinton’s Small Steps and Now Takes His Own', 'kicker': 'White House Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Once Disdained Clinton’s Small Steps and Now Takes His Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vocational Training', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T19:18:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc7864f1-33c7-55f9-825d-184eb5bd785e', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc7864f1-33c7-55f9-825d-184eb5bd785e'}, {'abstract': 'The decision against Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, accused of killing and maiming people with homemade bombs at the Boston Marathon last year, is not necessarily final, because such cases often end in plea deals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/us/boston-marathon-bombing-case.html', 'snippet': 'The decision against Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, accused of killing and maiming people with homemade bombs at the Boston Marathon last year, is not necessarily final, because such cases often end in plea deals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department said Thursday that it would seek the death penalty against Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, the man accused of killing and maiming people with homemade bombs at the Boston Marathon finish line last year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/us/30marathon/30marathon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/30/us/30marathon/30marathon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 663}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/us/30marathon/30marathon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 928, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/us/30marathon/30marathon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1811, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/us/30marathon/30marathon-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/30/us/30marathon/30marathon-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0