", 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — LVMH Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton, the world’s largest luxury goods group, said Thursday that its profit was almost flat last year amid flagging demand for some of its core fashion brands in key markets like China and the impact of weaker currencies in its main overseas markets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Annual Profit Nearly Flat for Luxury Group LVMH', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Luxury Goods Group Posts Flat Earnings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci Group NV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prada SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods and Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T20:28:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0183c4bc-8bd5-5310-a951-0ae195a7f325', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0183c4bc-8bd5-5310-a951-0ae195a7f325'}, {'abstract': 'Football shoulder pads have become lighter by as much as 50 percent over the past 10 to 15 years, manufacturers said, thanks to advances in technology and players’ preferences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/sports/football/shoulder-pads-slim-down-in-faster-sleeker-nfl.html', 'snippet': 'Football shoulder pads have become lighter by as much as 50 percent over the past 10 to 15 years, manufacturers said, thanks to advances in techn