ceit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the State-of-the-Union cameras are off, House Republicans are eager to discard their frozen smiles and return to their jobs of undermining virtually every goal President Obama set out in his speech on Tuesday night. They made that clear in a letter that the top four House officials sent to the president today, which purports to seek agreement on four points in the speech. It actually does quite the opposite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Republicans Say Versus What Republicans Mean', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMorris Rodgers, Cathy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T21:27:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee89b92a-055f-50f0-a675-441d42054d10', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee89b92a-055f-50f0-a675-441d42054d10'}, {'abstract': 'Chevrolet, Audi, Kia and Toyota are among repeat Super Bowl advertisers, but Jaguar will be a first timer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/automobiles/super-bowl-will-again-be-a-showcase-for-automakers.html', 'snippet': 'Chevrolet, Audi, Kia and Toyota are among repeat Super Bowl advertisers, but Jaguar will be a first timer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Denver Broncos and Seattle Seahawks get ready for the Super Bowl, automakers have also prepared for their own game-day competition: television ads.', 'source': 