ype': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/05/dining/05PAIR_SPAN/05PAIR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/05/dining/05PAIR_SPAN/05PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/05/dining/05PAIR_SPAN/05PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/05/dining/05PAIR_SPAN/05PAIR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With California Syrahs, an Asian-Accented Chili', 'kicker': 'Pairings', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With California Syrahs, an Asian-Accented Chili', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chili (Food)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T21:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/360bf958-7f70-53d8-b7a4-32ed3fc0b889', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/360bf958-7f70-53d8-b7a4-32ed3fc0b889'}, {'abstract': 'Why limited-government ideology isn’t necessarily the biggest hurdle facing Republican reformers.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/the-real-challenge-for-reform-conservatism/', 'snippet': 'Why limited-government ideology isn’t necessarily the biggest hurdle facing Republican reformers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote a post last week about whether a conservative reform project would necessitate a return to Bush-era deficit spending, or whether there’s any space available between “deficits don’t matter” Republicanism and Tea Party-era austerity. Since then, a number of writers have looked at the emerging conservative policy blueprints — which now include, mirabile dictu, an actual health care reform proposal! — and argued that their core weaknesses is an unwillingness to endorse new spending. Thus Danny Vinik, in a fair-minded post for Business Insider:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Challenge for Reform Conservatism', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T21:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc57db8a-64d1-5149-8eed-36ceebb63a97', 'word_count': 971, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc57db8a-64d1-5149-8eed-36ceebb63a97'}, {'abstract': 'The plan includes “an opportunity for legal residence and citizenship” for young immigrants brought here illegally by their parents, but it does not offer citizenship to many undocumented immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/us/politics/house-gop-issues-immigration-plan-with-path-to-legal-status.html', 'snippet': 'The plan includes “an opportunity for legal residence and citizenship” for young immigrants brought here illegally by their parents, but it does not offer citizenship to many undocumented immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, Md. — The House Republican leadership’s call on Thursday to provide legal status for 11 million undocumented workers, and possible citizenship for those brought to this country as children, caused sharp division within the party even as it provided a starting point for negotiations with Democrats on overhauling the nation’s immigration system. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/REPUBS-1/REPUBS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/31/us/REPUBS-1/REPUBS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/REPUBS-1/REPUBS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/us/REPUBS-1/REPUBS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'supe