ganization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/034b6d23-b91a-54c6-9229-f47db19dd269', 'word_count': 14, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034b6d23-b91a-54c6-9229-f47db19dd269'}, {'abstract': 'The 50 Yard Lounge, in a tent wedged between two restaurants in Midtown Manhattan, is a weeklong event intended to bring together the worlds of food and sports.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/nocturnalist-at-the-super-bowl-when-food-not-football-is-the-star/', 'snippet': 'The 50 Yard Lounge, in a tent wedged between two restaurants in Midtown Manhattan, is a weeklong event intended to bring together the worlds of food and sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was billed as an evening fusing football with flavors of New York, but the pastrami on rye could have been a monarch’s take on that city signature – a jewel-like gobbet of meat with caraway-scented brown butter – the kegs were filled with wine, and the hot dogs (brace yourself, oh true New Yorkers) were of a variety from Puerto Rico.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nocturnalist at the Super Bowl | Where Food and Football Intersect', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berselius, Fredrik', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forgione, Marc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aska (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T21:54:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ac99a7-6c17-507b-8de7-f4071652b9ad', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ac99a7-6c17-507b-8de7-f4071652b9ad'}, {'abstract': 'The new restaurant, Barchetta, will open in the spring and emphasize seafood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/dining/dave-pasternack-to-open-a-restaurant-in-chelsea.html', 'snippet': 'The new restaurant, Barchetta, will open in the spring and emphasize seafood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave Pasternack, the chef and a partner at Esca, the Italian seafood restaurant in Hell’s Kitchen, is planning to open another restaurant come spring. This time it’s without B & B Hospitality, the Bastianich-Batali group, which owns Esca.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/dining/31pasternack/31pasternack-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/31/dining/31pasternack/31pasternack-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/dining/31pasternack/31pasternack-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/dining/31pasternack/31pasternack-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/dining/31pasternack/31pasternack-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height