ract': 'Two economists of different persuasions see opportunities for bipartisan progress – and some areas of contention — in President Obama’s speech.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/30/finding-common-ground-on-the-state-of-the-union/', 'snippet': 'Two economists of different persuasions see opportunities for bipartisan progress – and some areas of contention — in President Obama’s speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jared Bernstein is a senior fellow at the Center on Budget and Policy Priorities in Washington and a former chief economist to Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. Phillip Swagel is a professor at the School of Public Policy at the University of Maryland and was assistant Treasury secretary for economic policy from 2006 to 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Common Ground on the State of the Union', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T22:20:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jared Bernstein and Phillip Swagel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jared', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstnam