ower East Side gastropub that ushered in a new epoch of American comfort food and rustic, taxidermy-heavy restaurant design. Since then, he’s launched several other restaurants and expanded his atavistic men’s wear line, Freemans Sporting Club. The man once described as the “patron saint of hipsters” also became a dad, trimmed his beard, began spending more time at his farmhouse upstate and loudly proclaimed his distaste for the culture he’d come to represent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/t-magazine/30isa-hartman2/30isa-hartman2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/30/t-magazine/30isa-hartman2/30isa-hartman2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/t-magazine/30isa-hartman2/30isa-hartman2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/t-magazine/30isa-hartman2/30isa-hartman2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1100, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/t-magazine/30isa-hartman2/30isa-hartman2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/30/t-magazine/30isa-hartman2/30isa-hartman2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/30/t-magazine/30isa-hartman2/30isa-hartman2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Matters | The Godfather of Hipster American Dining Serves Up a Fresh Dish: Enlightenment', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somer, Taavo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freemans (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Isa (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T23:21:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd447452-5625-5542-9658-24e792c8ee1d', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd447452-5625-5542-9658-24e792c8ee1d'}, {'abstract': 'Lincoln Center’s Dance on Camera festival revisits the choreographic glories of the old ice-skating extravaganzas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/arts/dance/the-glories-of-ice-shows-recalled-at-dance-on-camera.html', 'snippet': 'Lincoln Center’s Dance on Camera festival revisits the choreographic glories of the old ice-skating extravaganzas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before she directed “The Fabulous Ice Age,” Keri Pickett was a photographer who had never contemplated making a film. Her uncle, the former figure skater Roy Blakey — an avid collector of ice-show memorabilia — changed all that. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'r