ours before the president’s arrival here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Reaches Out After Shooting of Nashville Student', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T23:47:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40e4c8c1-5210-5b4d-bbb9-beea4c58cb5b', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40e4c8c1-5210-5b4d-bbb9-beea4c58cb5b'}, {'abstract': 'The operatic tenor Lawrence Brownlee performed works from his “Spiritual Sketches” album on Wednesday at the Allen Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/arts/music/lawrence-brownlee-elevates-the-spiritual.html', 'snippet': 'The operatic tenor Lawrence Brownlee performed works from his “Spiritual Sketches” album on Wednesday at the Allen Room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone unfamiliar with the traditional African-American spirituals that the great operatic tenor Lawrence Brownlee performed on Wednesday at the Allen Room can be forgiven for mistaking them for concert art songs. If Mr. Brownlee and his accompanist and arranger Damien Sneed didn’t tell you, you might not realize that beloved spirituals like “There Is a Balm in Gilead,” “Sometimes I Feel Like a Motherless Child” and “Down by the Riverside” belong to an oral tradition of gospel music distinct from carefully notated classical art songs. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gospel Without Hallelujahs', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gospel Without Hallelujahs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gospel Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brownlee, Lawrence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-30T23:49:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b485bed-689a-5f13-9cac-73d44fe1253a', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b485bed-689a-5f13-9cac-73d44fe1253a'}, {'abstract': 'Traffic jams and a clog of pedestrians on the sidewalks this week are frustrating drivers, delaying students and costing vendors business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/nyregion/super-bowl-fever-hits-midtown-but-not-everyone-has-caught-it.html', 'snippet': 'Traffic jams and a clog of pedestrians on the sidewalks this week are frustrating drivers, delaying students and costing vendors business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The orchids are dying, and Cliff Jacobs blames the Super Bowl.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/31/nyregion/cranky-2/cranky-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/31/nyreg