triggered a torrent of hatred on line is coming back for the Super Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/cheerios-hard-for-racists-to-swallow/', 'snippet': 'A cereal ad that triggered a torrent of hatred on line is coming back for the Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never mind the point-spread, New Jersey weather, momentum shifts and Newtonian replays. Just keep an eye out for the Super Bowl’s first unscheduled time out, when the huge television audience can catch that famous Cheerios commercial family — the one that so enraged racist Americans several months ago, featuring a manly black actor as father, a serene white mother and their charming interracial seven-year-old, Gracie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cheerios: Hard for Racists to Swallow', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Mills Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T16:51:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd23bd9-a742-5ec9-b276-6ad9e0e7b9ed', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd23bd9-a742-5ec9-b276-6ad9e0e7b9ed'}, {'abstract': 'No detail is left untouched for the Russian director Dmitri Tcherniakov, who makes his Metropolitan Opera debut on Thursday with Borodin’s “Prince Igor.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/arts/music/dmitri-tcherniakov-tackles-prince-igor-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'No detail is left untouched for the Russian director Dmitri Tcherniakov, who makes his Metropolitan Opera debut on Thursday with Borodin’s “Prince Igor.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every once in a while, the Russian stage director Dmitri Tcherniakov has a nightmare. He’s ready to go to the theater and run a rehearsal when he realizes he has forgotten what he is supposed to do there, what he wants to tell the performers.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02IGOR1_SPAN/02IGOR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02IGOR1_SPAN/02IGOR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02IGOR1_SPAN/02IGOR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02IGOR1_SPAN/02IGOR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02IGOR1_SPAN/02IGOR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02IGOR1_SPAN/02IGOR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02IGOR1_SPAN/02IGOR1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Perfectionist Does Opera His Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Perfectionist Does Opera His Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tcherniakov, Dmitri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Prince Igor (Opera)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T17:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bbfe468-5446-524b-8ced-f7e9cf67a1b7', 'word_count': 1831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bbfe468-5446-524b-8ced-f7e9cf67a1b7'}, {'abstract': 'The composer Leonid Desyatnikov and the choreographer Alexei Ratmansky have been collaborators four times — and counting, they hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/arts/dance/alexei-ratmansky-and-leonid-desyatnikov-on-collaborating.html', 'snippet': 'The composer Leonid Desyatnikov and the choreographer Alexei Ratmansky have been collaborators four times — and counting, they hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The choreographer Alexei Ratmansky has created four ballets to music by Leonid Desyatnikov: “Russian Seasons” (New York City Ballet, 2006), “Old Ladies Falling Out” (Territory festival in Moscow, 2007), “Lost Illusions” (Bolshoi Ballet, 2011) and “Opera” (La Scala Ballet, 2013). Both men are Russian, and both have worked at the Bolshoi in Moscow, where Mr. Ratmansky, 45, now artist in residence at American Ballet Theater, was the artistic director of the Bolshoi Ballet from 2004 to 2008, and Mr. Desyatnikov, 58, was music director from 2009 to 2010. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02ILLUSIONS2_SPAN/02ILLUSIONS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02ILLUSIONS2_SPAN/02ILLUSIONS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02ILLUSIONS2_SPAN/02ILLUSIONS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02ILLUSIONS2_SPAN/02ILLUSIONS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02ILLUSIONS2_SPAN/02ILLUSIONS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02ILLUSIONS2_SPAN/02ILLUSIONS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02ILLUSIONS2_SPAN/02ILLUSIONS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Easygoing, and Not Sure About a Donkey', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Easygoing, and Not Sure About a Donkey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulcas, Roslyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Desyatnikov, Leonid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T17:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97723d36-3c20-5f14-856a-39f417588ba5', 'word_count': 1308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97723d36-3c20-5f14-856a-39f417588ba5'}, {'abstract': 'The mezzo-soprano Sasha Cooke talks about self-image and the value of family and gut instincts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/arts/music/sasha-cooke-talks-about-self-image-family-and-gut-instincts.html', 'snippet': 'The mezzo-soprano Sasha Cooke talks about self-image and the value of family and gut instincts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While other students at Juilliard wanted to sing Verdi and Rossini, the mezzo-soprano Sasha Cooke, 31, gained a reputation as a quick study willing to learn new pieces written by her composer colleagues. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1171, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/02SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1171}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/arts/02SNAPSHOT/0