urce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Minute | Tray Tables Up', 'kicker': 'The New York Times News Minute', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T17:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quyn Do', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Do', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90fd7bb6-07a2-5c8e-935a-c067dde4093a', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90fd7bb6-07a2-5c8e-935a-c067dde4093a'}, {'abstract': 'Though the new farm bill passed, it did so without the help of the Kansas congressional delegation, which voted unanimously against it.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/no-help-for-farm-bill-from-miffed-kansans-in-the-house/', 'snippet': 'Though the new farm bill passed, it did so without the help of the Kansas congressional delegation, which voted unanimously against it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few states are as identified with farming as Kansas. Among its nicknames are the “The Wheat State” and “American’s Bread Basket.” And Kansas’s lawmakers are quick to point out the importance of agriculture to the state’s economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Help for Farm Bill From Miffed Kansans in the House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huelskamp, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Lynn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pompeo, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoder, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T17:24:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon and Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5350e67-5e97-5130-ba5f-c70b5363a94b', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5350e67-5e97-5130-ba5f-c70b5363a94b'}, {'abstract': 'A couple from Interlaken, N.J., refueled over lunch at Forty Ate, a pop-up restaurant in the Renaissance New York Times Square Hotel, overlooking the Super Bowl festivities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/nyregion/days-before-the-kickoff-a-timeout-at-forty-ate.html', 'snippet': 'A couple from Interlaken, N.J., refueled over lunch at Forty Ate, a pop-up restaurant in the Renaissance New York Times Square Hotel, overlooking the Super Bowl festivities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were moments last week, during the run-up to Sunday’s Super Bowl, when the hordes of football fans thronging Broadway for the N.F.L.’s pregame festivities appeared to outnumber even the characters handing out fliers and asking, “Do you like comedy?” During one such moment, as others rode toboggans down a snowless slope, a couple from Interlaken, N.J., made their way to the second floor of the Renaissance New York Times Square Hotel, overlooking the madness, to refuel over lunch at Forty Ate, a pop-up restaurant conceived by the football league and the restaurateur Danny Meyer’s Union Square Hospitality Group. The hosts offered Thursday-to-Saturday ownership of choice tables for $50,000 (drinks not included), but found only four takers. The rest of the restaurant’s 72 seats went to ordinary reservation-makers and walk-ins.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02TABLE1_SPAN/02TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02TABLE1_SPAN/02TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02TABLE1_SPAN/02TABLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02TABLE1_SPAN/02TABLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02TABLE1_SPAN/02TABLE1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02TABLE1_SPAN/02TABLE1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02TABLE1_SPAN/02TABLE1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', '