 Jets games for 22 years, said her job is like being a performer. “When you go in there, it’s showtime,” she said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/nyregion/a-concession-worker-is-ready-for-super-bowl-duty.html', 'snippet': 'Inez Keyes, who has been working at Giants and Jets games for 22 years, said her job is like being a performer. “When you go in there, it’s showtime,” she said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not everyone in a uniform at MetLife Stadium on Super Bowl Sunday will wear a helmet. Inez Keyes will wear a smile. High-fiving fans and co-workers while serving beer, she is the Peyton Manning of hospitality. (“Go Beertenders!”) Ms. Keyes, 55, one of nearly 3,000 concession workers for Delaware North Companies, has brought her A-game to Giants and Jets games in the Meadowlands for 22 years, going from counter worker to cashier to beertender on the 100 Concourse. (She also supervises a concession stand at the Izod Center.) Ms. Keyes commutes two hours from Canarsie, Brooklyn, taking two subways and two buses to New Jersey; her routine will vary slightly on Super Bowl Sunday, but despite the later kickoff, she will still leave the house early to be in place for the big game.\xa0', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE1/02ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE1/02ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE1/02ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '