s, giraffes and wildebeests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/travel/in-east-africa-safaris-that-leave-a-lighter-footprint.html', 'snippet': 'On visits to eco-friendly camps in Kenya and Tanzania, the author has lunch with the elephants and takes in scenes dotted with zebras, giraffes and wildebeests.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Want to have lunch with the elephants?” That sounded like an offer we couldn’t refuse — even if at least half the menu was bound to consist of hunks of grass and splintered acacia branches. Luckily, the human side of the invitation included gazpacho, zucchini frittata and salad. My husband and I did mind our manners, keeping our picnic well inside the Land Rover while a herd of our multi-ton hostesses grazed peacefully a few yards away, surrounded by children of all sizes. Introductions were made by our guide, Seronoi, and his spotter, Jackson, who identified our companions by the distinctive shape of their heads, ears and tusks. What better welcome to Samburu National Park, and to the sort of experience we’d hoped to find on safari in East Africa.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02PERSONAL5/02PERSONAL5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02PERSONAL5/02PERSONAL5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02PERSONAL5/02PERSONAL5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02PERSONAL5/02PERSONAL5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02PERSONAL5/02PERSONAL5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02PERSONAL5/02PERSONAL5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02PERSONAL5/02PERSONAL5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In East Africa, Safaris That Leave a Lighter Footprint', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safaris That Leave a Lighter Footprint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eco-Tourism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Safaris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tanzania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T18:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alida Becker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Becker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc9c19a0-9895-5164-b3f9-f7587bdec675', 'word_count': 1543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc9c19a0-9895-5164-b3f9-f7587bdec675'}, {'abstract': 'A mile from downtown, this newly fashionable arts district is home to everything from cafes to carwashes, bookstores to barbecue joints.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/travel/eclectic-east-austin.html', 'snippet': 'A mile from downtown, this newly fashionable arts district is home to everything from cafes to carwashes, bookstores to barbecue joints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mile from downtown, East Austin has historically been a working-class neighborhood, a vibrant enclave heavily populated by African-Americans because of an earlier era of segregationist laws — and later, a home to Mexican-American residents. These days, it’s also the city’s newly fashionable arts district, with studios, galleries, cocktail bars, cafes and all manner of food trucks popping up on most every block. Beloved taquerias and barbecue joints, ramshackle carwashes and Christian outreach ministries now jostle against shiny condos, fancy restaurants and, in refurbished bungalows, groovy hair salons with names like Peacock and Orbit.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02HEADS4/02HEADS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02HEADS4/02HEADS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02HEADS4/02HEADS4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02HEADS4/02HEADS4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/travel/02HEA