nflation rate well above current levels, this is a disastrous report:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Low-inflationary Trap', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T20:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43e7a1a1-e2b3-5290-b40d-6de43720f2e4', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43e7a1a1-e2b3-5290-b40d-6de43720f2e4'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Coffey and Adam Riff fell in love while working on Bloomberg’s 2009 re-election campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/02/fashion/weddings/a-campaign-for-mayor-and-for-a-mate.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Coffey and Adam Riff fell in love while working on Bloomberg’s 2009 re-election campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Chris Coffey talks about love, he often talks about New York.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/fashion/weddings/02VOWS1/02VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/fashion/weddings/02VOWS1/02VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 471}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/fashion/weddings/02VOWS1/02VOWS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non