or fear of it, in turn leads to an intensified idealization of homeownership — though the ownership rate in the city, at just over 30 percent, is less than half the figure for the country over all — a sense that there could be few problems immune to solution had one had the foresight (and resourcefulness) to a buy a brownstone in Brooklyn for $400,000 in 1995. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02BIGCITY_SPAN/02BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02BIGCITY_SPAN/02BIGCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02BIGCITY_SPAN/02BIGCITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02BIGCITY_SPAN/02BIGCITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02BIGCITY_SPAN/02BIGCITY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02BIGCITY_SPAN/02BIGCITY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/nyregion/02BIGCITY_SPAN/02BIGCITY_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'lega