nnounced that the reward was being offered for information that leads to the safe return of a 1715 Stradivarius violin stolen from the orchestra’s concertmaster.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/100000-reward-is-set-for-stolen-stradivarius-violin/', 'snippet': 'The Milwaukee Symphony Orchestra announced that the reward was being offered for information that leads to the safe return of a 1715 Stradivarius violin stolen from the orchestra’s concertmaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Milwaukee Symphony Orchestra announced late Friday afternoon that a $100,000 reward was being offered to anyone who provides information that leads to the safe return of the 1715 Stradivarius violin stolen from the orchestra’s concertmaster, Frank Almond, after a chamber concert in Milwaukee on Monday evening. Susan Loris, a spokeswoman for the orchestra said she was unable to identify the source of the reward money. It could be the orchestra, the anonymous owner of the violin (it was given to Mr. Almond as a permanent loan in 2008) or others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$100,000 Reward Is Set for Stolen Stradivarius Violin', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Violins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T22:17:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/325f5ce8-068c-53b0-b5e0-dda43c70bd32', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/325f5ce8-068c-53b0-b5e0-dda43c70bd32'}, {'abstract': 'The Focus! Festival at the Juilliard School continued its celebration of Alfred Schnittke with works by him and members of his circle, including Arvo Pärt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/01/arts/music/more-alfred-schnittke-at-juilliards-focus-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Focus! Festival at the Juilliard School continued its celebration of Alfred Schnittke with works by him and members of his circle, including Arvo Pärt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The notion of stealing a show through simplicity and understatement may seem counterintuitive if not oxymoronic. But your intuition and mine are not Arvo Pärt’s, and this is a feat Mr. Pärt achieves with some regularity, as he did on Wednesday evening in the fourth program of the annual Focus! festival of contemporary music at the Juilliard School.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/arts/01SCHNITTKE/01SCHNITTKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/01/arts/01SCHNITTKE/01SCHNITTKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/arts/01SCHNITTKE/01SCHNITTKE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/arts/01SCHNITTKE/01SCHNITTKE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url