of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c90316f0-9fe7-5553-9eb9-a044e4abe23c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c90316f0-9fe7-5553-9eb9-a044e4abe23c'}, {'abstract': 'Purchases of Morgan Stanley stock made by the firm’s chief executive years ago, when the Wall Street bank’s shares was trading far lower, have paid off extremely well for his portfolio.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/morgan-stanleys-stock-bet-yields-windfall-on-paper/', 'snippet': 'Purchases of Morgan Stanley stock made by the firm’s chief executive years ago, when the Wall Street bank’s shares was trading far lower, have paid off extremely well for his portfolio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Morgan Stanley’s share price fell to $20 in 2011, the bank’s chief executive, James P. Gorman, and several of his top lieutenants tried to encourage investors by buying up stock with their own money. Now, that put-your-money-where-your-mouth-is approach appears to have paid off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/dbpix-gorman/dbpix-gorman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 459, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/01/business/dbpix-gorman/dbpix-gorman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 459}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/dbpix-gorman/dbpix-gorman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/dbpix-gorman/dbpix-gorman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1568, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '