ps://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/01/business/media/super-bowl-sideshows-starring-puppies-kittens-and-fish.html', 'snippet': 'The Puppy Bowl, now in its 10th year as counterprogramming to the Super Bowl, is joined this year by the Kitten Bowl and the Fish Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Puppy Bowl has long been the big dog when it comes to alternative programming during the Super Bowl. When the stadium lights went out at the big game last year, more than a million viewers filled the time by flocking to the canine contest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/01puppy/01puppy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/01/business/01puppy/01puppy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/01puppy/01puppy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/01puppy/01puppy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1286, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/01puppy/01puppy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/01/business/01puppy/01puppy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/business/01puppy/01puppy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Super Bowl Sideshows Starring Puppies, Kittens and Fish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Geographic Wild', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hallmark Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANIMAL PLANET', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T23:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Frink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21c910d7-24dc-5989-b440-4fd010441388', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21c910d7-24dc-5989-b440-4fd010441388'}, {'abstract': 'Stripped down in Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/01/31/friday-night-music-arcade-fire-normal-person/', 'snippet': 'Stripped down in Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have to admit, I had a hard time warming up to Arcade Fire’s new album. It was a break from the previous sound, and it’s taken me a while to find the thread of continuity. But I have been listening, and am increasingly getting it. As I mentioned on WNYC (btw, I start at around the 25-minute mark) my appreciation of their music grows when I get a chance to hear them do stripped-down performances, like this one just up, which among other things shows that the intensity and commitment is undiminished. Also that they’re having fun:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Arcade Fire, Normal Person', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-01-31T23:18:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/809bf044-7037-5525-8aaf-93970efceead', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/809bf044-7037-5525-8aaf-93970efceead'}, {'abstract': 'President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner has said very little about the crisis that has led the nation’s currency to plunge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/01/world/americas/as-argentine-economic-crisis-swirls-president-keeps-low-profile.html', 'snippet': 'President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner has said very little about the crisis that has led the nation’s currency to plunge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — As Argentines stew over a currency crisis that has shaken markets around the world, many residents here are asking the same question: Where is the president?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/world/americas/ARGENTINA/ARGENTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/01/world/americas/ARGENTINA/ARGENTINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/01/world/americas/ARGENTINA/ARGENTINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subT